{"parentUuid":"3c9a7ccd-0be3-4086-8117-8fc4bf1e0ef5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e99f9aec-cde8-464a-a7d0-d96f0ee8f669","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"我不想再放到同一个二进制里了。按照这些观点我们拆成几个二进制？要记得考虑我们后续做Windows端。后续选择tauri作为gui,tui也要保留"},"uuid":"2f22b297-2be6-48c6-8bea-528a3afd69ce","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:03:27.246Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master"}
{"parentUuid":"2f22b297-2be6-48c6-8bea-528a3afd69ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"dff12075-2def-4781-aa08-d4df8596b22a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to think about how to split the project into multiple binaries, considering:\n1. They don't want everything in one binary anymore\n2. Cross-platform support (including Windows)\n3. Tauri as the future GUI, but TUI must be preserved\n4. Following the 4-layer architecture discussed\n\nLet me think carefully about the binary split and IPC strategy.\n\nKey considerations:\n- Windows doesn't have Unix domain sockets (well, Windows 10+ has them but they work differently)\n- Need to support both TUI (ratatui) and GUI (tauri) as frontends\n- hp-daemon needs to be a truly separate process\n- tools-server should be separate for sandbox isolation\n- Cross-platform IPC: named pipes work on both, TCP localhost works everywhere, Unix sockets on Linux/macOS need alternative on Windows\n\nLet me think about what makes sense:\n\n1. **hp-daemon** - Independent daemon process. Must run first. Monitors all others.\n2. **agent-core** - The brain. Context, memory, orchestrator, session, router, tokenizer, prompt, skills. Could be a library used by both TUI and Tauri, OR a separate process.\n3. **tools-server** - Tool execution sandbox. exec, file, git, web, explore.\n4. **Frontends** - TUI (ratatui binary) and GUI (tauri binary) - both connect to agent-core\n\nWait, should agent-core be a library or a process? If it's a library, both TUI and Tauri link it in. If it's a process, they communicate via IPC.\n\nIf agent-core is a library:\n- TUI binary links it directly (fast, simple)\n- Tauri binary links it directly\n- But then hp-daemon can't independently monitor agent-core's health... unless the library reports to hp-daemon\n\nIf agent-core is a process:\n- Both TUI and Tauri communicate via IPC\n- hp-daemon can independently monitor agent-core's process\n- Clearer boundaries\n- But more IPC overhead\n\nThe user said \"我不想再放到同一个二进制里了\" - so they want separate processes. Let me go with agent-core as a separate process.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user's original 4-layer design:\n\nLayer 4: UI (TUI / Tauri)\nLayer 3: Agent Core (context, memory, orchestrator, session, router, tokenizer, prompt, skills)\nLayer 2a: tools-server (tool execution, exec sandbox)\nLayer 2b: hp-daemon (health monitoring, circuit breaker, sentinel, liveness)\nLayer 1: Communication (API client)\n\nSo binaries would be:\n1. `dsx-tui` - TUI frontend\n2. `dsx-gui` - Tauri frontend (future)\n3. `dsxd` (or `dsx-agent`) - Agent core daemon\n4. `dsx-tools` - Tools server\n5. `dsx-hp` - Health platform daemon\n\nWait, should Layer 1 (API communication) be part of agent-core or separate? It makes sense to keep it in agent-core since that's who talks to the API.\n\nNow about IPC:\n- Windows support means we can't rely solely on Unix domain sockets\n- Options:\n  - TCP localhost: works everywhere, but port conflicts, firewall issues\n  - Named pipes: Windows has them, Unix has them (different APIs though)\n  - Use a library that abstracts this: `interprocess` crate on Rust, or `tokio` with TCP\n  - gRPC via tonic: works everywhere, well-supported, but heavy\n  - Simple HTTP/WebSocket: lightweight, works everywhere\n\nFor simplicity and cross-platform, I'd suggest:\n- Between frontend ↔ agent-core: WebSocket or simple HTTP (REST-ish), or use a Rust IPC library\n- Between agent-core ↔ tools-server: could be same process initially, or use the same IPC mechanism\n- Between hp-daemon ↔ all others: simple heartbeat + command protocol\n\nActually, let me think about this more practically. The user wants:\n1. Cross-platform (including Windows)\n2. Tauri for GUI, TUI preserved\n3. Separate binaries\n\nThe simplest cross-platform IPC approach that works well:\n- Use `tokio` with TCP localhost + a known port, or better yet, use a library\n- Actually, `interprocess` crate supports both Unix domain sockets and Windows named pipes\n- Or use stdin/stdout for simpler cases\n\nBut actually, for a more practical approach:\n- Agent-core could expose a simple JSON-RPC or MessagePack interface over stdin/stdout or TCP\n- TUI and Tauri both talk to it the same way\n\nLet me think about how many binaries is the right number:\n\nMinimum viable split:\n1. **dsx-hp** (health daemon) - starts first, monitors everything\n2. **dsx-agent** (agent core + tools + API) - the main agent process  \n3. **dsx-tui** (TUI frontend)\n4. **dsx-gui** (Tauri frontend, future)\n\nBut wait, the whole point was to separate tools-server from agent-core for sandboxing. And to keep hp-daemon truly independent.\n\nSo:\n1. **dsx-hp** - Health platform daemon (liveness, sentinel, circuit_breaker, platform, emotion, quality, report, assessment) + API gateway (gate, checks, audit)\n2. **dsx-agent** - Agent core (orchestrator, context, memory, session, router, tokenizer, prompt, skills, types, conversation, config, dsc_log)\n3. **dsx-tools** - Tools server (all tools/* + exec sandbox)\n4. **dsx-tui** - TUI frontend (tui/*)\n5. **dsx-gui** - Tauri frontend (future)\n\nHmm, but the user mentioned that the API gateway/checking should be in hp-daemon so it can physically enforce gates. Let me re-read...\n\n\"api请求必须走IPC经过hp-daemon的gate，物理上无法绕过\" - so hp-daemon should also proxy API requests, or at least be in the API call path.\n\nSo hp-daemon's role: health monitoring + API gateway (pre-checks, error classification, retry logic)\n\nThen agent-core talks to the API through hp-daemon, not directly.\n\nLet me finalize:\n\n### Binary Split\n\n1. **dsx-hp** — Health Platform Daemon\n   - Files from health/: mod, platform, liveness, sentinel, circuit_breaker, emotion, quality, report, assessment, gate, checks, audit, monitor\n   - API gateway: pre-request gate checking, error retry/block decision\n   - Monitors all other processes (heartbeat, resource, crash detection)\n   - Starts first, other processes register with it\n   - Exposes health-check endpoint + API proxy endpoint\n\n2. **dsx-agent** — Agent Core\n   - orchestrator/*, context, memory/*, session/*, router, tokenizer, prompt, skills, types, conversation, config, dsc_log\n   - Connects to hp-daemon to proxy API calls (no direct API access)\n   - Connects to tools-server for tool execution\n   - Exposes agent API for frontends (TUI/GUI)\n\n3. **dsx-tools** — Tools Server\n   - tools/* (ToolManager + all tool implementations)\n   - exec sandbox isolation\n   - Registers with hp-daemon\n   - Tool calls must be registered/audited\n\n4. **dsx-tui** — Terminal UI\n   - tui/* + tui_text\n   - Connects to dsx-agent via IPC\n   - Ratatui-based, full TUI experience\n\n5. **dsx** (future) — Tauri GUI\n   - New code, Tauri-based\n   - Connects to dsx-agent via same IPC protocol\n   - Can be developed independently\n\n### IPC Strategy (Cross-platform)\n\nFor cross-platform (Linux + macOS + Windows):\n- **Primary IPC**: TCP localhost with a well-defined port range, or use Unix sockets on unix + named pipes on Windows\n- **Best approach**: Use `tokio` with a simple JSON-RPC or custom binary protocol over TCP 127.0.0.1\n  - Works everywhere\n  - No external dependencies\n  - Easy to debug\n  - Can secure with a random token\n- **Alternative**: gRPC via `tonic` — more structured but heavier\n\nI think a simple approach:\n- Each process listens on a random localhost port and registers its address with hp-daemon (or uses a well-known discovery mechanism)\n- Or use a simpler model: hp-daemon is the hub, all communication routes through it\n- Actually, even simpler: use a shared config file or environment variables for port discovery\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Having all IPC go through hp-daemon creates a single point of failure and a bottleneck. Better to have:\n- hp-daemon: only for health monitoring + API proxying\n- Direct connections between agent ↔ tools, agent ↔ frontends\n- hp-daemon gets heartbeat pings from all processes, can issue kill/restart commands\n\nFor discovery: hp-daemon listens on a well-known port (or writes its port to a file). Agent registers, gets back a session token. Agent then starts its own listener, tells hp-daemon its port. Tools server and frontends ask hp-daemon \"where's the agent?\" and connect directly.\n\nActually this is getting complex. Let me simplify:\n\nFor now, a practical approach:\n- Use a **shared directory** (like `~/.config/dsx/run/`) for IPC endpoint discovery — each process writes its port to a file there\n- On Windows, use `%APPDATA%\\dsx\\run\\`\n- Communication protocol: simple length-prefixed JSON messages over TCP\n\nOr even simpler: **use stdin/stdout** for the TUI → agent communication (spawn agent as child process), and have tools-server also be a child process. hp-daemon is the only truly independent process.\n\nHmm, but the user said \"我不想再放到同一个二进制里了\" — separate binaries but child processes is still a valid architecture. The key is separate process spaces.\n\nLet me go with this simpler model:\n\n- **dsx-hp**: system service/daemon, runs independently, monitors all\n- **dsx-agent**: started by the frontend as a child process (or independently for headless mode), communicates via stdin/stdout or TCP\n- **dsx-tools**: started by dsx-agent as a child process, communicates via stdin/stdout\n- **dsx-tui**: the TUI frontend, starts dsx-agent as child\n- **dsx-gui**: the Tauri frontend, starts dsx-agent as child\n\nThis is actually much more practical! The frontend owns the lifecycle of agent and tools. hp-daemon is the only truly independent process.\n\nIPC between frontend ↔ agent: stdin/stdout (simplest) or localhost TCP\nIPC between agent ↔ tools: stdin/stdout (tools is spawned by agent)\nIPC between hp-daemon ↔ all: localhost TCP (for heartbeats and commands)\n\nActually wait, if agent and tools communicate via stdin/stdout, that means tools is a child process of agent. That's fine for process isolation. And frontend ↔ agent via stdin/stdout means frontend spawns agent.\n\nThis is clean. Let me present this.\n\nNow, for the tool calling flow with API gating:\n1. agent receives user message from frontend\n2. agent builds context, sends to hp-daemon's API proxy\n3. hp-daemon checks the context (gate/checks), if pass, forwards to DeepSeek API\n4. hp-daemon streams response back to agent\n5. agent processes response, extracts tool calls\n6. agent sends tool calls to tools-server (stdin/stdout or TCP)\n7. tools-server executes, sends results back\n8. agent builds next turn, goes back to step 2\n\nThis way hp-daemon is physically in the API call path and CANNOT be bypassed.\n\nOK let me structure the answer now. I should present:\n1. How many binaries and what each contains\n2. IPC strategy with Windows consideration\n3. How the data flow works\n4. A clear diagram\n\nLet me write this up.","signature":"dff12075-2def-4781-aa08-d4df8596b22a"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":43520,"output_tokens":4476,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2e9978b5-2c80-4d3a-ab85-499b03cc53dd","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:04:53.416Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master"}
{"parentUuid":"2e9978b5-2c80-4d3a-ab85-499b03cc53dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"dff12075-2def-4781-aa08-d4df8596b22a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"好问题。让我们从三个约束出发推导：**多进程隔离**、**跨平台（含 Windows）**、**TUI + Tauri 双前端**。\n\n---\n\n## 拆成 5 个二进制\n\n```\ndsx-hp      — 健康守护进程（系统级，最先启动，独立存活）\ndsx-agent   — Agent 核心（无界面，可 headless 运行）\ndsx-tools   — 工具执行服务器（沙箱隔离）\ndsx-tui     — 终端界面（ratatui）\ndsx         — 桌面 GUI（tauri，未来）\n```\n\n### 各二进制包含的模块\n\n| 二进制 | 模块 | 文件数 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **dsx-hp** | `health/` 全部 14 文件 + `api/client.rs`（作为 API 代理网关） | ~15 |\n| **dsx-agent** | `orchestrator/` 全部 + `context.rs` + `conversation.rs` + `memory/` 全部 + `session/` 全部 + `router.rs` + `tokenizer.rs` + `prompt.rs` + `skills.rs` + `types.rs` + `config.rs` + `dsc_log.rs` | ~35 |\n| **dsx-tools** | `tools/` 全部 14 文件 | ~14 |\n| **dsx-tui** | `tui/` 全部 18 文件 + `tui_text.rs` | ~18 |\n| **dsx** | 全新 Tauri 项目，复用与 dsx-tui 相同的 IPC 协议 | 0（新建） |\n\n### 为什么 api/client.rs 放在 dsx-hp 而不是 dsx-agent\n\n这是你上次分析的核心洞察——**API 请求必须物理上经过 hp-daemon 的 gate，不能在同一调用栈里被绕过**。所以：\n\n- dsx-agent **不持有 API key**，不直接调 DeepSeek API\n- dsx-agent 把构建好的 context 发给 dsx-hp，dsx-hp 做 gate 检查后代理转发\n- API key 只存在于 dsx-hp 进程中\n\n---\n\n## IPC 策略（跨平台第一原则）\n\nWindows 不支持 Unix domain socket（Windows 10 1803+ 有实验性支持但不稳定），所以策略：\n\n| 通信对 | IPC 方式 | 理由 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 前端 → dsx-agent | **stdin/stdout**（子进程模式） | 前端 spawn agent 作为子进程，天然跨平台，无需端口管理 |\n| dsx-agent → dsx-tools | **stdin/stdout**（子进程模式） | agent spawn tools 作为子进程，exec 沙箱隔离，tools 崩溃不影响 agent |\n| 所有进程 → dsx-hp | **TCP localhost**（127.0.0.1） | dsx-hp 是独立守护进程，不是任何人的子进程；TCP 在 Windows/Linux/macOS 行为完全一致 |\n| dsx-hp → 外部 API | **HTTPS** | 只有 dsx-hp 持有 API key |\n\n关键设计：\n- 子进程模式的 IPC 用 **length-prefixed JSON**（4 字节大端长度 + JSON 载荷），最简单，调试友好\n- dsx-hp 的 TCP 端口写到共享文件 `~/.config/dsx/run/hp.port`（Windows: `%APPDATA%\\dsx\\run\\hp.port`），其他进程启动时读这个文件发现 hp-daemon 地址\n- 全部异步，基于 tokio\n\n---\n\n## 进程启动与生命周期\n\n```\n系统启动 / 用户登录\n        │\n        ▼\n   [dsx-hp]  ─────────────── 守护进程，持续运行 ─────────────►\n   TCP :9001\n        │\n        │  用户打开终端 / 点击桌面图标\n        ▼\n   [dsx-tui] 或 [dsx]  ───── 前端进程\n        │ spawn(stdin/stdout)\n        ▼\n   [dsx-agent]  ──────────── Agent 核心\n        │ spawn(stdin/stdout)\n        ▼\n   [dsx-tools]  ──────────── 工具服务器\n```\n\n- dsx-hp **独立存活**，不随前端关闭而退出\n- 前端退出 → agent + tools 随之退出（子进程）\n- dsx-hp 监控 agent 和 tools 的心跳，超时无响应可重启或告警\n- 多个前端实例可以同时存在（每个 spawn 自己的 agent + tools），共享同一个 dsx-hp\n\n---\n\n## 数据流（一次完整的用户对话轮次）\n\n```\n 1. [dsx-tui] 用户输入 \"重构 config.rs\"\n       │  stdin JSON\n       ▼\n 2. [dsx-agent] orchestrator 接收，构建 context\n       │  TCP: 发送候选 context 给 hp-daemon\n       ▼\n 3. [dsx-hp] gate.rs 检查消息交替性/孤儿 tool_use\n       │  checks.rs 验证结构完整性\n       │  sentinel.rs 决定是否放行\n       │  通过 → 代理转发 POST /v1/messages 到 DeepSeek\n       │  SSE 流式返回\n       ▼\n 4. [dsx-agent] stream_handler 处理流事件\n       │  response_processor 提取 tool_call\n       │  gates.rs 检查工具合规性\n       │  stdin JSON: 发送工具调用\n       ▼\n 5. [dsx-tools] ToolManager 执行工具\n       │  circuit_breaker 检测循环/重复\n       │  执行结果 → stdin JSON 返回 agent\n       ▼\n 6. [dsx-agent] learning.rs 提取经验\n       │  context_compactor 准备下一轮\n       │  session_persistence 保存快照\n       │  stdin JSON: 流式结果推给前端\n       ▼\n 7. [dsx-tui] render/chat.rs 渲染响应\n```\n\n每一步 dsx-agent 和 dsx-tools 都向 dsx-hp 发送心跳。hp-daemon 在任何一步检测到异常（agent 无响应、tools 循环、API 错误率飙升）都有独立权限发出 kill/restart 指令。\n\n---\n\n## 共享 crate（不单独成为二进制，被多个二进制依赖）\n\n```\ndsx-proto     — IPC 消息类型定义（所有进程共享）\ndsx-types     — 核心数据类型（SafetyLevel, Message, ToolCall, TaskPhase 等）\n```\n\n这两个作为库 crate，不独立运行，被 5 个二进制共同依赖。放在 workspace 里统一编译。\n\n---\n\n## Cargo workspace 结构\n\n```\ndsx/\n├── Cargo.toml          (workspace)\n├── crates/\n│   ├── dsx-proto/      (共享 IPC 消息定义)\n│   ├── dsx-types/      (共享类型)\n│   ├── dsx-hp/         (健康守护进程)\n│   ├── dsx-agent/      (Agent 核心)\n│   ├── dsx-tools/      (工具服务器)\n│   ├── dsx-tui/        (终端界面)\n│   └── dsx/            (Tauri GUI，未来)\n├── src/                (当前 80 个原子文件，等待分配到各 crate)\n└── explore.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 总结\n\n| 问题 | 答案 |\n|---|---|\n| 几个二进制？ | **5 个**（dsx-hp、dsx-agent、dsx-tools、dsx-tui、dsx） |\n| 哪两个是共享库？ | **2 个**（dsx-proto、dsx-types） |\n| IPC 用啥？ | 父子进程间 **stdin/stdout** + 守护进程间 **TCP localhost** |\n| Windows 兼容？ | stdin/stdout + TCP 127.0.0.1，全部跨平台，零平台特定代码 |\n| Tauri 怎么接入？ | 与 dsx-tui 使用完全相同的 IPC 协议 spawn dsx-agent，TUI 和 GUI 可以并存 |\n\n这个拆分方案的核心：**dsx-hp 物理上独立于所有被监控进程，且是唯一持有 API key 的进程**——gate 不再能被绕过。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":43520,"output_tokens":4476,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2c25d035-fe37-4c4f-af4b-76e46957c53f","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:05:50.732Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master"}
