{"parentUuid":"36abdce0-e0d9-4a55-a78d-962ae01db1b2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"8ce34dfc-71d1-42c1-92d0-b1482fc67de3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01_d5IHqULPDNVWsNYnrE5o6829","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Team C: dsx-agent Orchestrator Design\n2\t\n3\t## 1. Overview\n4\t\n5\tThe orchestrator is the central nervous system of dsx-agent. It owns the main agent loop: receiving user input, building context, sending API requests, processing streaming responses, dispatching tool calls, and managing turn-level safety gates.\n6\t\n7\t**Architectural role** (from IPC Protocol, A02):\n8\t\n9\t```\n10\tTUI --(stdin/stdout)--> Agent --(stdin/stdout)--> Tools\n11\t                            |\n12\t                      (TCP IPC)\n13\t                            |\n14\t                           HP\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\tThe orchestrator lives in the Agent process. It does NOT call the API directly in the new architecture — it delegates to HP via TCP IPC for API calls, and to Tools via stdin/stdout for tool execution.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## 2. Twelve Modules — Pub API\n22\t\n23\t### 2.1 `mod.rs` — Module declarations\n24\t\n25\tNo change needed. Re-exports of public types if any.\n26\t\n27\t### 2.2 `agent_loop.rs` — Core agent loop\n28\t\n29\t**Current functions:**\n30\t- `handle_start_agent_loop(app: &mut App, stream_tx)`\n31\t  - Syncs messages, guards (streaming/confirm/exec-pending), pre-flight gate check, compact context, configure model/tools, spawn API request\n32\t- `handle_send_message(app, tx)` — Process user input, skill match, then start loop\n33\t\n34\t**New design — pub API:**\n35\t\n36\t```rust\n37\t// Called by TUI (stdin handler) when user submits input\n38\tpub fn handle_user_input(state: &mut AgentState, input: &str) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n39\t\n40\t// Called internally to start/fork the agent loop\n41\tpub fn start_agent_loop(state: &mut AgentState) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n42\t\n43\t// Called by HP response handler when streaming is done + tools processed\n44\tpub fn continue_agent_loop(state: &mut AgentState) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t**Flow:**\n48\t1. `handle_user_input` — guard checks, skill matching, session init, balance refresh, call `start_agent_loop`\n49\t2. `start_agent_loop` — message sync, gate check (via HP IPC), context compact, send API request to HP via TCP\n50\t3. HP streams back → `stream_handler` processes → tool calls → `continue_agent_loop` → back to step 2\n51\t\n52\t### 2.3 `stream_handler.rs` — Stream event dispatch\n53\t\n54\t**Current functions:**\n55\t- `handle_stream_event(app, event, tx)` — match StreamEvent variants\n56\t\n57\t**New design — pub API:**\n58\t\n59\t```rust\n60\t// Called by the HP TCP IPC receiver thread for each event"}]},"uuid":"79e7f318-497a-47f2-a630-72a23396d1e9","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:52:15.743Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/src/dsx-agent/orchestrator/DESIGN.md","content":"# Team C: dsx-agent Orchestrator Design\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThe orchestrator is the central nervous system of dsx-agent. It owns the main agent loop: receiving user input, building context, sending API requests, processing streaming responses, dispatching tool calls, and managing turn-level safety gates.\n\n**Architectural role** (from IPC Protocol, A02):\n\n```\nTUI --(stdin/stdout)--> Agent --(stdin/stdout)--> Tools\n                            |\n                      (TCP IPC)\n                            |\n                           HP\n```\n\nThe orchestrator lives in the Agent process. It does NOT call the API directly in the new architecture — it delegates to HP via TCP IPC for API calls, and to Tools via stdin/stdout for tool execution.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Twelve Modules — Pub API\n\n### 2.1 `mod.rs` — Module declarations\n\nNo change needed. Re-exports of public types if any.\n\n### 2.2 `agent_loop.rs` — Core agent loop\n\n**Current functions:**\n- `handle_start_agent_loop(app: &mut App, stream_tx)`\n  - Syncs messages, guards (streaming/confirm/exec-pending), pre-flight gate check, compact context, configure model/tools, spawn API request\n- `handle_send_message(app, tx)` — Process user input, skill match, then start loop\n\n**New design — pub API:**\n\n```rust\n// Called by TUI (stdin handler) when user submits input\npub fn handle_user_input(state: &mut AgentState, input: &str) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n\n// Called internally to start/fork the agent loop\npub fn start_agent_loop(state: &mut AgentState) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n\n// Called by HP response handler when streaming is done + tools processed\npub fn continue_agent_loop(state: &mut AgentState) -> Result<(), OrchestratorError>;\n```\n\n**Flow:**\n1. `handle_user_input` — guard checks, skill matching, session init, balance refresh, call `start_agent_loop`\n2. `start_agent_loop` — message sync, gate check (via HP IPC), context compact, send API request to HP via TCP\n3. HP streams back → `stream_handler` processes → tool calls → `continue_agent_loop` → back to step 2\n\n### 2.3 `stream_handler.rs` — Stream event dispatch\n\n**Current functions:**\n- `handle_stream_event(app, event, tx)` — match StreamEvent variants\n\n**New design — pub API:**\n\n```rust\n// Called by the HP TCP IPC receiver thread for each event","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":490}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"36abdce0-e0d9-4a55-a78d-962ae01db1b2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
