{"parentUuid":"05b876db-28b7-41d3-a0af-b0289e480266","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"8ce34dfc-71d1-42c1-92d0-b1482fc67de3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_04_G1dzmZr5Iwzhc8f6JhCo0922","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Design: D03 — Task, Plan, Memory, Ask, Status Tools\n2\t\n3\t**Owner:** Team D member D03\n4\t**Date:** 2026-05-14\n5\t**Status:** Draft for review\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Scope\n10\t\n11\t| File | Tool(s) | Role |\n12\t|------|---------|------|\n13\t| `task.rs` | `task_create`, `task_update`, `task_list` | Task CRUD + status workflow |\n14\t| `plan.rs` | `plan_create`, `plan_update`, `plan_read`, `plan_list` | Plan CRUD + status workflow |\n15\t| `memory.rs` | `mem_save`, `mem_read`, `mem_forget`, `recall`, `pitfall_save`, `pitfall_guide` | Memory read/write/search + cross-session learning |\n16\t| `ask.rs` | `ask_user` | User clarification (stub — handled by TUI) |\n17\t| `status.rs` | `status` | Working mode declaration |\n18\t\n19\tAll are registered under the combined `agent` tool in `agent.rs:exec_agent()`. The AI calls `agent` with an `action` parameter, which dispatches to the appropriate sub-module.\n20\t\n21\t---\n22\t\n23\t## 2. Architecture: Single-Process (No IPC)\n24\t\n25\t### 2.1 Current Architecture\n26\t\n27\tThe entire DSX system is a **single binary, single process**. The directory grouping (`dsx-tools/`, `dsx-agent/`, etc.) is organizational only — all modules are `mod` declarations in `main.rs`.\n28\t\n29\t```\n30\t┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n31\t│                     dsx (single process)                     │\n32\t│                                                              │\n33\t│  TUI ─→ tool_dispatch ─→ execute_tool() ─→ exec_agent()     │\n34\t│  (dsx-tui)   (dsx-agent/         (dsx-tools/      ─→ task.rs │\n35\t│              orchestrator)        mod.rs)           plan.rs  │\n36\t│                                                     memory.rs│\n37\t│                                                       status │\n38\t│                                                         │    │\n39\t│                    ┌────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n40\t│                    ▼                                         │\n41\t│              session::append_memory()                        │\n42\t│              session::read_memory()                          │\n43\t│              (dsx-agent/session/memory_io.rs)                │\n44\t│                    │                                         │\n45\t│                    ▼                                         │\n46\t│              std::fs::write/read  (filesystem)               │\n47\t└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t**Key insight:** Tools modules call `session::` functions via **direct function calls** within the same process. The `session/memory_io.rs` module (owned by Team C) provides the actual file I/O. There is no IPC, no RPC, no message passing.\n51\t\n52\t### 2.2 Data Flow for Each Tool Group\n53\t\n54\t| Tool Group | Calls | Receives From |\n55\t|-----------|-------|---------------|\n56\t| task.rs | `session::append_memory()`, `read_memory()`, `write_memory()` | `CURRENT_SESSION` OnceLock (set by TUI) |\n57\t| plan.rs | `session::write_plan()`, `update_plan_status()`, `read_plan_content()`, `list_plans()` | Same |\n58\t| memory.rs | `session::read_memory()`, `write_memory()`, `append_memory()`, `forget_memory_key()`, `load_pitfalls()`, `save_pitfalls()` | Same |\n59\t| ask.rs | (stub — returns error) | N/A — intercepted by TUI |\n60\t| status.rs | `router::parse_status_args()`, `router::set_phase()` | `AtomicU8` in `router.rs` |"}]},"uuid":"b925875a-4f3e-49b3-98f7-66fcbe6ad615","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:52:21.698Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/src/dsx-tools/DESIGN-D03.md","content":"# Design: D03 — Task, Plan, Memory, Ask, Status Tools\n\n**Owner:** Team D member D03\n**Date:** 2026-05-14\n**Status:** Draft for review\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\n| File | Tool(s) | Role |\n|------|---------|------|\n| `task.rs` | `task_create`, `task_update`, `task_list` | Task CRUD + status workflow |\n| `plan.rs` | `plan_create`, `plan_update`, `plan_read`, `plan_list` | Plan CRUD + status workflow |\n| `memory.rs` | `mem_save`, `mem_read`, `mem_forget`, `recall`, `pitfall_save`, `pitfall_guide` | Memory read/write/search + cross-session learning |\n| `ask.rs` | `ask_user` | User clarification (stub — handled by TUI) |\n| `status.rs` | `status` | Working mode declaration |\n\nAll are registered under the combined `agent` tool in `agent.rs:exec_agent()`. The AI calls `agent` with an `action` parameter, which dispatches to the appropriate sub-module.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture: Single-Process (No IPC)\n\n### 2.1 Current Architecture\n\nThe entire DSX system is a **single binary, single process**. The directory grouping (`dsx-tools/`, `dsx-agent/`, etc.) is organizational only — all modules are `mod` declarations in `main.rs`.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     dsx (single process)                     │\n│                                                              │\n│  TUI ─→ tool_dispatch ─→ execute_tool() ─→ exec_agent()     │\n│  (dsx-tui)   (dsx-agent/         (dsx-tools/      ─→ task.rs │\n│              orchestrator)        mod.rs)           plan.rs  │\n│                                                     memory.rs│\n│                                                       status │\n│                                                         │    │\n│                    ┌────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n│                    ▼                                         │\n│              session::append_memory()                        │\n│              session::read_memory()                          │\n│              (dsx-agent/session/memory_io.rs)                │\n│                    │                                         │\n│                    ▼                                         │\n│              std::fs::write/read  (filesystem)               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Key insight:** Tools modules call `session::` functions via **direct function calls** within the same process. The `session/memory_io.rs` module (owned by Team C) provides the actual file I/O. There is no IPC, no RPC, no message passing.\n\n### 2.2 Data Flow for Each Tool Group\n\n| Tool Group | Calls | Receives From |\n|-----------|-------|---------------|\n| task.rs | `session::append_memory()`, `read_memory()`, `write_memory()` | `CURRENT_SESSION` OnceLock (set by TUI) |\n| plan.rs | `session::write_plan()`, `update_plan_status()`, `read_plan_content()`, `list_plans()` | Same |\n| memory.rs | `session::read_memory()`, `write_memory()`, `append_memory()`, `forget_memory_key()`, `load_pitfalls()`, `save_pitfalls()` | Same |\n| ask.rs | (stub — returns error) | N/A — intercepted by TUI |\n| status.rs | `router::parse_status_args()`, `router::set_phase()` | `AtomicU8` in `router.rs` |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":451}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"05b876db-28b7-41d3-a0af-b0289e480266","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
