{"parentUuid":"aca0719b-3d0f-4db7-ab68-4805d66b06b1","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"8ce34dfc-71d1-42c1-92d0-b1482fc67de3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_06_wdp1w2cT1KDvSV8dstuu5602","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Input Processing Subsystem Design\n2\t\n3\t## E02 — Input Processing\n4\t\n5\t### 1. Problem Statement\n6\t\n7\tCurrently, input handlers are tightly coupled to the monolithic `App` struct. Each handler (`handle_chat_key`, `handle_confirm_key`, etc.) takes `&mut App` and directly mutates anything — state, side effects, spawning tasks. This makes testing impossible, mode transitions fragile, and the event loop (`mod.rs:103-137`) is cluttered with inline exit handling and mode-specific logic.\n8\t\n9\t### 2. Architecture: State Machine + Action Queue\n10\t\n11\tThe core idea: **input handlers are pure(ish) state machines**. They receive `(&mut InputState, KeyEvent)`, update input-level state, and return `InputAction`. The event loop (or AppState owner, E01) maps actions to App-level side effects.\n12\t\n13\t```\n14\t[KeyEvent]\n15\t    |\n16\t    v\n17\tInputHandler[mode]  ── mutates ──>  InputState\n18\t    |\n19\t    v\n20\tInputAction  ── consumed by ──>  EventLoop / AppState\n21\t                                        |\n22\t                                        v\n23\t                                  Side effects:\n24\t                                  - send_message(tx, ...)\n25\t                                  - start_agent_loop(tx)\n26\t                                  - load_session(...)\n27\t                                  - switch mode\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\t### 3. InputState — All input-mode-local state in one struct\n31\t\n32\t```rust\n33\t// File: input/state.rs (NEW)\n34\t\n35\tuse crate::types::SessionMeta;\n36\tuse super::mode::InputMode;\n37\t\n38\t/// All input-mode-local state, extracted from the monolithic App.\n39\t/// Lives inside AppState (E01's domain).\n40\tpub struct InputState {\n41\t    pub active_mode: InputMode,\n42\t\n43\t    // ── Chat mode ──\n44\t    pub chat: ChatState,\n45\t\n46\t    // ── Slash menu (embedded in chat) ──\n47\t    pub slash: SlashState,\n48\t\n49\t    // ── Picker modes ──\n50\t    pub intent: IntentPickerState,\n51\t    pub session: SessionPickerState,\n52\t\n53\t    // ── Sudo mode ──\n54\t    pub sudo: SudoState,\n55\t\n56\t    // ── Exit confirmation ──\n57\t    pub exit_prompt: bool,\n58\t}\n59\t\n60\t// ── Per-mode state structs ──"}]},"uuid":"7671a09b-53fc-434b-9655-b5bc6f99ae8e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:52:25.853Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/src/dsx-tui/input/DESIGN.md","content":"# Input Processing Subsystem Design\n\n## E02 — Input Processing\n\n### 1. Problem Statement\n\nCurrently, input handlers are tightly coupled to the monolithic `App` struct. Each handler (`handle_chat_key`, `handle_confirm_key`, etc.) takes `&mut App` and directly mutates anything — state, side effects, spawning tasks. This makes testing impossible, mode transitions fragile, and the event loop (`mod.rs:103-137`) is cluttered with inline exit handling and mode-specific logic.\n\n### 2. Architecture: State Machine + Action Queue\n\nThe core idea: **input handlers are pure(ish) state machines**. They receive `(&mut InputState, KeyEvent)`, update input-level state, and return `InputAction`. The event loop (or AppState owner, E01) maps actions to App-level side effects.\n\n```\n[KeyEvent]\n    |\n    v\nInputHandler[mode]  ── mutates ──>  InputState\n    |\n    v\nInputAction  ── consumed by ──>  EventLoop / AppState\n                                        |\n                                        v\n                                  Side effects:\n                                  - send_message(tx, ...)\n                                  - start_agent_loop(tx)\n                                  - load_session(...)\n                                  - switch mode\n```\n\n### 3. InputState — All input-mode-local state in one struct\n\n```rust\n// File: input/state.rs (NEW)\n\nuse crate::types::SessionMeta;\nuse super::mode::InputMode;\n\n/// All input-mode-local state, extracted from the monolithic App.\n/// Lives inside AppState (E01's domain).\npub struct InputState {\n    pub active_mode: InputMode,\n\n    // ── Chat mode ──\n    pub chat: ChatState,\n\n    // ── Slash menu (embedded in chat) ──\n    pub slash: SlashState,\n\n    // ── Picker modes ──\n    pub intent: IntentPickerState,\n    pub session: SessionPickerState,\n\n    // ── Sudo mode ──\n    pub sudo: SudoState,\n\n    // ── Exit confirmation ──\n    pub exit_prompt: bool,\n}\n\n// ── Per-mode state structs ──","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":390}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aca0719b-3d0f-4db7-ab68-4805d66b06b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
