{"parentUuid":"88ac3faa-279b-42d9-bd62-8bf17f8eceb4","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"9d74668c-3e37-4fcd-b03d-ee1c5ae0fb2d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_02_4GVQHlOvqermTURZKeyK8967","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# dsc Tool Design Declaration\n2\t\n3\t## Contract\n4\t\n5\tEvery tool is a `ToolEntry`:\n6\t\n7\t```rust\n8\tpub struct ToolEntry {\n9\t    pub name: &'static str,   // snake_case, globally unique\n10\t    pub def: fn() -> ToolDef, // schema + description sent to the model\n11\t    pub safety: fn(args: &str) -> SafetyLevel,  // Safe | Confirm | Danger\n12\t    pub exec: fn(args: &str) -> String,         // actual implementation\n13\t}\n14\t```\n15\t\n16\t## Writing a Tool — 4 Steps\n17\t\n18\t### 1. Definition (`fn xxx_def()`)\n19\t\n20\tDescribe what the tool does AND when to use it. The model reads this.\n21\t\n22\t```rust\n23\tfn read_file_def() -> ToolDef {\n24\t    ToolDef {\n25\t        call_type: \"function\".into(),\n26\t        function: ToolFunction {\n27\t            name: \"read_file\".into(),\n28\t            description: \"Read a file. Max 500 lines per call. Use start_line/end_line to page.\".into(),\n29\t            parameters: serde_json::json!({\n30\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n31\t                \"properties\": {\n32\t                    \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"File path, relative to project root\"},\n33\t                    \"start_line\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"First line (1-indexed, optional)\"},\n34\t                    \"end_line\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"Last line (inclusive, optional)\"},\n35\t                },\n36\t                \"required\": [\"path\"],\n37\t                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n38\t            }),\n39\t        },\n40\t    }\n41\t}\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\t**Rules**:\n45\t- `name` must be snake_case, ≤ 40 chars, unique\n46\t- `description` must include: what it does, constraints (max lines, timeouts), and when to use it\n47\t- JSON Schema: use `\"description\"` on every field. The model reads these.\n48\t- Always set `\"additionalProperties\": false` — or the model will invent params.\n49\t\n50\t### 2. Execution (`fn exec_xxx(args: &str) -> String`)\n51\t\n52\tPure synchronous function. Parse args, do work, return result.\n53\t\n54\t```rust\n55\tfn exec_read_file(args: &str) -> String {\n56\t    let path = parse_arg(args, \"path\");\n57\t    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&path) {\n58\t        Ok(c) => c,\n59\t        Err(e) => return format!(\"[ERROR] Cannot read {}: {}\", path, e),\n60\t    };\n61\t    format!(\"[OK]\\n{}\", content)\n62\t}\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t**Result Protocol** — every result MUST start with one of:\n66\t\n67\t| Prefix | Meaning | Follow-up |\n68\t|--------|---------|-----------|\n69\t| `[OK]` | Success | None |\n70\t| `[PARTIAL]` | Truncated | Include `[HINT]` explaining how to get more |\n71\t| `[ERROR]` | Failure | Include `[HINT]` with fix |\n72\t| `[FAIL]` | Command ran but exited non-zero | Show stdout+stderr |\n73\t| `[SUDO_REQUIRED]` | exec needs sudo | TUI handles password prompt |\n74\t| `[PROJECT_MAP]` | explore output | Persisted across compaction |\n75\t\n76\tThe model is trained to read the prefix first and follow HINTs.\n77\t\n78\t### 3. Safety (`fn xxx_safety(args: &str) -> SafetyLevel`)\n79\t\n80\t```rust"}]},"uuid":"d4ffc123-58f4-4739-86d2-7b536f3dc313","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:10:24.872Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/docs/tool-design.md","content":"# dsc Tool Design Declaration\n\n## Contract\n\nEvery tool is a `ToolEntry`:\n\n```rust\npub struct ToolEntry {\n    pub name: &'static str,   // snake_case, globally unique\n    pub def: fn() -> ToolDef, // schema + description sent to the model\n    pub safety: fn(args: &str) -> SafetyLevel,  // Safe | Confirm | Danger\n    pub exec: fn(args: &str) -> String,         // actual implementation\n}\n```\n\n## Writing a Tool — 4 Steps\n\n### 1. Definition (`fn xxx_def()`)\n\nDescribe what the tool does AND when to use it. The model reads this.\n\n```rust\nfn read_file_def() -> ToolDef {\n    ToolDef {\n        call_type: \"function\".into(),\n        function: ToolFunction {\n            name: \"read_file\".into(),\n            description: \"Read a file. Max 500 lines per call. Use start_line/end_line to page.\".into(),\n            parameters: serde_json::json!({\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"File path, relative to project root\"},\n                    \"start_line\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"First line (1-indexed, optional)\"},\n                    \"end_line\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"description\": \"Last line (inclusive, optional)\"},\n                },\n                \"required\": [\"path\"],\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n            }),\n        },\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Rules**:\n- `name` must be snake_case, ≤ 40 chars, unique\n- `description` must include: what it does, constraints (max lines, timeouts), and when to use it\n- JSON Schema: use `\"description\"` on every field. The model reads these.\n- Always set `\"additionalProperties\": false` — or the model will invent params.\n\n### 2. Execution (`fn exec_xxx(args: &str) -> String`)\n\nPure synchronous function. Parse args, do work, return result.\n\n```rust\nfn exec_read_file(args: &str) -> String {\n    let path = parse_arg(args, \"path\");\n    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(&path) {\n        Ok(c) => c,\n        Err(e) => return format!(\"[ERROR] Cannot read {}: {}\", path, e),\n    };\n    format!(\"[OK]\\n{}\", content)\n}\n```\n\n**Result Protocol** — every result MUST start with one of:\n\n| Prefix | Meaning | Follow-up |\n|--------|---------|-----------|\n| `[OK]` | Success | None |\n| `[PARTIAL]` | Truncated | Include `[HINT]` explaining how to get more |\n| `[ERROR]` | Failure | Include `[HINT]` with fix |\n| `[FAIL]` | Command ran but exited non-zero | Show stdout+stderr |\n| `[SUDO_REQUIRED]` | exec needs sudo | TUI handles password prompt |\n| `[PROJECT_MAP]` | explore output | Persisted across compaction |\n\nThe model is trained to read the prefix first and follow HINTs.\n\n### 3. Safety (`fn xxx_safety(args: &str) -> SafetyLevel`)\n\n```rust","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":198}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"88ac3faa-279b-42d9-bd62-8bf17f8eceb4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
