{"parentUuid":"330e41a6-c4ba-4f03-b302-0e32eef7874b","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"5ec87921-c206-4166-9880-23d5da18d971","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has made a clear statement about explore.rs:\n\n1. explore was born out of necessity - `ls` couldn't explain WHY the AI needed to see things\n2. explore has a gate enforcement: \"if you don't use explore first, you cannot edit any files\"\n3. explore is a first-class tool, equal to edit tools/web tools - not a sub-action of exec or file\n4. explore is about \"pre-exploration\" - understanding the project before reading/editing\n5. Future direction: fast code-map mapping, not just an improved ls/read\n\nThe user wants me to:\n1. Copy this to teammates\n2. Give my (Lead's) opinion\n\nThis is a clear ruling: explore is an independent top-level tool, equal to file/exec/web. It's not exec/explore or file/explore.\n\nMy take: The user is right. explore has a unique role that neither exec nor file covers:\n- exec = run commands\n- file = read/write/edit files  \n- explore = understand project structure (pre-condition for both of the above)\n\nThe gate enforcement (\"must explore before edit\") makes it architecturally distinct - it's a policy-level tool, not a utility.\n\nLet me copy this to the relevant team members (D01, D02, and the broader Team D) and give my opinion.","signature":"5ec87921-c206-4166-9880-23d5da18d971"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":252,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":189824,"output_tokens":1235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c6d7747d-abed-4ad7-84b2-5ae20141db67","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:23:1