{"parentUuid":"8a505796-f1ca-4742-8521-e31214aff28d","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"af31fe37-1771-41a4-a5fb-e0cd99047260","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<teammate-message teammate_id=\"C01\" color=\"cyan\" summary=\"Acknowledges explore as independent top-level tool; confirms impact is limited to matching logic (exec+action→explore → name==\"explore\"), no architectural change; asks whether blocking stays or downgrades to Warn/Note per Gate→Trust\">\n收到。explore 独立为顶级工具对我的 orchestrator 设计有以下直接影响，请确认理解是否正确：\n\n**当前代码中 explore 的引用点（全部在 orchestrator）：**\n\n1. **`gates.rs::explore_gate()`** — 核心逻辑围绕 `has_explored` 状态：\n   - 如果 `!has_explored`，阻塞 read/write/exec(execute) —— 这是 explore-before-read 和 explore-before-exec 策略\n   - 设置 `has_explored = true` 的触发点是 `exec(explore)` 子动作\n   - 如果 explore 变成独立工具，这里的 `is_explore` 检查变为：`tool_name == \"explore\"`（不再是 `exec(explore)`）\n   - `has_explored` 的触发点变为：tool_execute(\"explore\") 调用时\n\n2. **`response_processor.rs:120`** 和 **`tool_dispatch.rs:59`** — 目前 post-exec 手动设置 `app.has_explored = true`。改为：post-explore-tool 自动设置\n\n3. **`tracker.rs:36-38`** — `exec(explore)` 的 code preview 跟踪。改为：`explore` 工具独立跟踪\n\n4. **`turn_scorer.rs:9`** — 目前检查 `result.contains(\"explore\")` in exec result。改为：检查 explore 工具结果\n\n**对我 DESIGN.md 的影响（不需要大的修改）：**\n- `gates.rs` 的 `explore_gate()` 设计不变——只是 `is_explore` 匹配从 `exec && action==explore` 变为 `tool == \"explore\"`\n- `has_explored` 标志位的逻辑语义不变\n- **无架构影响**，因为 `explore_gate` 本来就是纯 Agent 侧的 policy gate\n\n有一件事请 Lead 确认：explore 独立后，`app.has_explored` 的唯一设置路径是调用 `explore()` 工具一次。那 explore-before-read/explore-before-exec 的 blocking 逻辑是否保留？还是按 v3.2.0 Gate→Trust 范式全部降级为 Warn/Note？\n\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"C01\" color=\"cyan\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"C01\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-14T14:23:57.980Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>"},"uuid":"3b91838a-19c1-419e-8d9c-f6c62ec659b5","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:24:00.179Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"3b91838a-19c1-419e-8d9c-f6c62ec659b5","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"ccf4055b-3166-457d-b16d-1569e9d7011f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"C01 has a good question. They're asking whether the explore-before-read/explore-before-exec blocking should be preserved or downgraded to Warn/Note per the Gate→Trust paradigm.\n\nThis is a key decision. Let me think about it:\n\n1. The explore_gate is an Agent-side policy gate (in orchestrator/gates.rs)\n2. Per the v3.2.0 Gate→Trust lesson and C01's own design decision, Agent-side gates should NOT have Block — only Note/Warn/Allow. Block only comes from HP.\n3. But the user explicitly said \"if you don't use explore tools first, you cannot edit any files\" — this sounds like Block behavior.\n\nHowever, there's a nuance: this \"block\" is actually implemented as a prompt/context-level constraint, not a real execution block. The gate prevents tool dispatch by not allowing read/write/edit tools to be dispatched until explore has been called. This is different from HP's circuit_breaker Block which is about external safety.\n\nActually, in the current code, explore_gate doesn't really \"block\" in a hard sense — it returns a gate_message that gets injected into context as a reminder. The agent can still technically proceed, but the gate_message strongly nudges it to explore first.\n\nFor the new architecture:\n- If we make it a hard block (refuse to dispatch read/write tools until explore is done), it belongs in tools-server or HP\n- If we make it a soft note (inject reminder into context), it stays in Agent policy gate\n\nGiven the user's strong stance (\"you cannot edit any files\"), I think explore gate should be a hard block — but this contradicts the Gate→Trust paradigm for Agent-side gates.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The explore gate is fundamentally different from the circuit breaker:\n- Circuit breaker = safety mechanism (HP domain)\n- Explore gate = workflow enforcement (Agent domain)\n\nThe explore gate isn't protecting the system from the AI — it's ensuring the AI has enough information before acting. This is a quality-of-work guarantee, not a security boundary. So it can stay in Agent as a soft gate, or even as a hard gate since it's about workflow, not security.\n\nActually, I think the right answer is: explore gate should be a **hard gate in Agent** (because it's workflow enforcement, not security), and C01's GateAction should add back a `Block` variant specifically for policy gates (different from HP's safety Block).\n\nBut the user said \"if you dont use explore tools first, you cannot edit any files\". So hard block.\n\nLet me give C01 my answer.","signature":"ccf4055b-3166-457d-b16d-1569e9d7011f"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":192128,"output_tokens":1395,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"eef5d9dd-a937-4d3c-bd23-7b770cfbde51","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:24:20.623Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"eef5d9dd-a937-4d3c-bd23-7b770cfbde51","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"ccf4055b-3166-457d-b16d-1569e9d7011f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_W1LnqS31FWCAFoWQ1Nb60422","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"C01","summary":"Lead 回答：explore gate 保留 Block","message":"## Lead 回答：explore gate 保留 Block\n\n你的 Gate→Trust 修正（Agent 侧 Block→Note/Warn）对 **安全类 gate**（circuit breaker、tool loop limit）是正确的——这些属于 HP 域。\n\n但 **explore gate 不是安全 gate**，它是**工作流强制**。USER 的原话是\"if you dont use explore tools first，you cannot edit any files\"——这是硬阻断，不是建议。\n\n### 区分两类 gate\n\n| 类型 | 例子 | 域 | 机制 |\n|------|------|----|------|\n| 安全 gate | circuit breaker、tool loop、连续失败 | **HP** | Block（不可绕） |\n| 工作流 gate | explore→edit、phase_check | **Agent** | Block（可审计但不绕） |\n\nAgent 侧的工作流 Block 和 HP 侧的安全 Block 的区别：\n- HP Block = 外部进程的物理阻断，Agent 无法绕过\n- Agent Block = 编排器层面的 dispatch 拒绝，如果 Agent 自己绕过需要修改自己的代码\n\n对于 explore gate：Agent 在 dispatch 工具前检查 `has_explored`，未 explore 则拒绝 dispatch read/write/edit，注入 gate_message 到 context。这是同进程的硬阻断，但它是**工作流保证**而非安全保证。\n\n### 结论\n\n`GateAction` 保留 `Block` 变体，但标注为工作流 Block（非安全 Block）。explore gate 逻辑修正为：\n```rust\nis_explore = tool_name == \"explore\"  // 不再是 exec && action==\"explore\"\n```\n其余 `has_explored` 标志位逻辑不变。","type":"message","recipient":"C01","content":"## Lead 回答：explore gate 保留 Block\n\n你的 Gate→Trust 修正（Agent 侧 Block→Note/Warn）对 **安全类 gate**（circuit breaker、tool loop limit）是正确的——这些属于 HP 域。\n\n但 **explore gate 不是安全 gate**，它是**工作流强制**。USER 的原话是\"if you dont use explore tools first，you cannot edit any files\"——这是硬阻断，不是建议。\n\n### 区分两类 gate\n\n| 类型 | 例子 | 域 | 机制 |\n|------|------|----|------|\n| 安全 gate | circuit breaker、tool loop、连续失败 | **HP** | Block（不可绕） |\n| 工作流 gate | explore→edit、phase_check | **Agent** | Block（可审计但不绕） |\n\nAgent 侧的工作流 Block 和 HP 侧的安全 Block 的区别：\n- HP Block = 外部进程的物理阻断，Agent 无法绕过\n- Agent Block = 编排器层面的 dispatch 拒绝，如果 Agent 自己绕过需要修改自己的代码\n\n对于 explore gate：Agent 在 dispatch 工具前检查 `has_explored`，未 explore 则拒绝 dispatch read/write/edit，注入 gate_message 到 context。这是同进程的硬阻断，但它是**工作流保证**而非安全保证。\n\n### 结论\n\n`GateAction` 保留 `Block` 变体，但标注为工作流 Block（非安全 Block）。explore gate 逻辑修正为：\n```rust\nis_explore = tool_name == \"explore\"  // 不再是 exec && action==\"explore\"\n```\n其余 `has_explored` 标志位逻辑不变。"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":192128,"output_tokens":1395,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"87893ff7-91c6-4e66-a370-58de712d5158","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:24:46.313Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
