{"parentUuid":"36a86010-a8f7-4536-a919-859965f59965","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","promptId":"0706e0e9-4e9e-4fbd-ace8-d83c8cd04ff9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_xEiyexkOVLQntzcpZzkN4542","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Alternation gate + sandbox pre-flight validation module.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Before any context is sent to the API, it passes through this gate.\n4\t//! The gate validates message alternation, checks for orphans, simulates the\n5\t//! Anthropic format conversion, and either:\n6\t//!\n7\t//! - **Pass**: context is clean, proceed to API\n8\t//! - **Block**: violation found, real context is untouched\n9\t//!\n10\t//! This is the key architectural improvement over v3.x: the real message\n11\t//! state is NEVER polluted by a failed validation. We validate a candidate,\n12\t//! not the live state.\n13\t\n14\tuse crate::conversation::ContextAssembler;\n15\tuse crate::types::{AnthropicContent, Message};\n16\t\n17\t/// Context for the gate check.\n18\tpub struct GateContext<'a> {\n19\t    pub assembler: &'a ContextAssembler,\n20\t    pub has_orphan_tool_uses: bool,\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\t/// Result of a gate check.\n24\t#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n25\tpub enum GateResult {\n26\t    /// Context is clean — proceed to API.\n27\t    Pass,\n28\t    /// Block the request. Contains a user-facing reason and whether /fix can repair.\n29\t    Block {\n30\t        reason: String,\n31\t        /// Whether /fix can repair this issue.\n32\t        repairable: bool,\n33\t    },\n34\t}\n35\t\n36\timpl GateResult {\n37\t    pub fn is_pass(&self) -> bool {\n38\t        matches!(self, GateResult::Pass)\n39\t    }\n40\t\n41\t    pub fn is_block(&self) -> bool {\n42\t        matches!(self, GateResult::Block { .. })\n43\t    }\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t/// Run full pre-flight validation on a candidate context.\n47\t///\n48\t/// This does NOT mutate the assembler or any health state.\n49\t/// It only reads the candidate and reports findings.\n50\tpub fn check_gate(ctx: &GateContext) -> GateResult {\n51\t    // 1. Assembler self-validation (structural checks)\n52\t    if let Err(reason) = ctx.assembler.validate() {\n53\t        return GateResult::Block {\n54\t            reason: format!(\"Context integrity error: {}\", reason),\n55\t            repairable: true,\n56\t        };\n57\t    }\n58\t\n59\t    // 2. Check ready_for_api (must have complete turns, no pending tools)\n60\t    if let Err(reason) = ctx.assembler.ready_for_api() {\n61\t        return GateResult::Block {\n62\t            reason: format!(\"Not ready for API: {}\", reason),\n63\t            repairable: false,\n64\t        };\n65\t    }\n66\t\n67\t    // 3. Simulate Anthropic conversion (dry run) and validate alternation\n68\t    let (_, anthropic_msgs) = ctx.assembler.to_anthropic_messages();\n69\t    if let Err(result) = validate_anthropic_messages(&anthropic_msgs) {\n70\t        return result;\n71\t    }\n72\t\n73\t    // 4. Check orphan tool_use flag from health platform\n74\t    if ctx.has_orphan_tool_uses {\n75\t        return GateResult::Block {\n76\t            reason: \"Session has orphan tool_use entries — repair with /fix before sending to API\"\n77\t                .into(),\n78\t            repairable: true,\n79\t        };\n80\t    }"}]},"uuid":"e0536d38-3a41-4691-9e31-23abc9be9451","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:50:05.802Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/src/dsx-hp/gate.rs","content":"//! Alternation gate + sandbox pre-flight validation module.\n//!\n//! Before any context is sent to the API, it passes through this gate.\n//! The gate validates message alternation, checks for orphans, simulates the\n//! Anthropic format conversion, and either:\n//!\n//! - **Pass**: context is clean, proceed to API\n//! - **Block**: violation found, real context is untouched\n//!\n//! This is the key architectural improvement over v3.x: the real message\n//! state is NEVER polluted by a failed validation. We validate a candidate,\n//! not the live state.\n\nuse crate::conversation::ContextAssembler;\nuse crate::types::{AnthropicContent, Message};\n\n/// Context for the gate check.\npub struct GateContext<'a> {\n    pub assembler: &'a ContextAssembler,\n    pub has_orphan_tool_uses: bool,\n}\n\n/// Result of a gate check.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub enum GateResult {\n    /// Context is clean — proceed to API.\n    Pass,\n    /// Block the request. Contains a user-facing reason and whether /fix can repair.\n    Block {\n        reason: String,\n        /// Whether /fix can repair this issue.\n        repairable: bool,\n    },\n}\n\nimpl GateResult {\n    pub fn is_pass(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, GateResult::Pass)\n    }\n\n    pub fn is_block(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, GateResult::Block { .. })\n    }\n}\n\n/// Run full pre-flight validation on a candidate context.\n///\n/// This does NOT mutate the assembler or any health state.\n/// It only reads the candidate and reports findings.\npub fn check_gate(ctx: &GateContext) -> GateResult {\n    // 1. Assembler self-validation (structural checks)\n    if let Err(reason) = ctx.assembler.validate() {\n        return GateResult::Block {\n            reason: format!(\"Context integrity error: {}\", reason),\n            repairable: true,\n        };\n    }\n\n    // 2. Check ready_for_api (must have complete turns, no pending tools)\n    if let Err(reason) = ctx.assembler.ready_for_api() {\n        return GateResult::Block {\n            reason: format!(\"Not ready for API: {}\", reason),\n            repairable: false,\n        };\n    }\n\n    // 3. Simulate Anthropic conversion (dry run) and validate alternation\n    let (_, anthropic_msgs) = ctx.assembler.to_anthropic_messages();\n    if let Err(result) = validate_anthropic_messages(&anthropic_msgs) {\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    // 4. Check orphan tool_use flag from health platform\n    if ctx.has_orphan_tool_uses {\n        return GateResult::Block {\n            reason: \"Session has orphan tool_use entries — repair with /fix before sending to API\"\n                .into(),\n            repairable: true,\n        };\n    }","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":220}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"36a86010-a8f7-4536-a919-859965f59965","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"e0536d38-3a41-4691-9e31-23abc9be9451","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"dff0b2bc-8cc2-4e48-be4e-2e9bffcc2897","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can give an accurate answer. gate.rs is NOT a \"conversion\" layer. It's a **pre-flight security checkpoint** that:\n\n1. Validates message integrity (assembler.validate())\n2. Checks if API-ready (ready_for_api())\n3. Dry-runs Anthropic format conversion (to_anthropic_messages()) and validates alternation\n4. Checks for orphan tool_use flag from health platform\n\nIt returns Pass or Block. It does NOT mutate anything - \"the real message state is NEVER polluted by a failed validation.\"\n\nThe user is right to question this - team members have been conflating gate.rs with the mock server / conversion layer. gate.rs is the EXISTING pre-API validation gate, and USER's mock server proposal is essentially formalizing and strengthening what gate.rs already does (steps 1-3) while keeping it read-only.\n\nLet me explain this clearly to the user.\n</previous>\n\ngate.rs 不是\"转化层\"。它是 **预 API 安全检查门**。\n\n```rust\ncheck_gate(ctx)  // 纯读，不写任何状态\n  ├─ 1. assembler.validate()       // 结构完整性\n  ├─ 2. assembler.ready_for_api()  // 轮次是否完成\n  ├─ 3. validate_anthropic_messages() // dry-run Anthropic 格式 + 交替性\n  └─ 4. has_orphan_tool_uses      // 健康平台标记\n```\n\n返回 `Pass` 或 `Block { reason, repairable }`。**不修改任何东西。**\n\n这正是 USER 方案 3（模拟伺服器）已经在做的事情——gate 的第 3 步就是 dry-run Anthropic 转换并校验。USER 的提案本质上是**把 gate 的第 3 步形式化、独立化**，让它从 API spec 推导 invariant 而非人工积累规则。\n\n团队成员之前把 gate 叫\"转化\"是不准确的——gate 是**检查门**，不是转化器。转化在 `converter.rs`（即将删除）和 `ContextAssembler::to_anthropic_messages()` 里。","signature":"dff0b2bc-8cc2-4e48-be4e-2e9bffcc2897"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":226432,"output_tokens":453,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_f