{"type":"file-history-snapshot","messageId":"c974b7dc-6f15-418f-8dba-fdbe5e2bf734","snapshot":{"messageId":"c974b7dc-6f15-418f-8dba-fdbe5e2bf734","trackedFileBackups":{"explore.md":{"backupFileName":"50cba2b5c9f9b5ac@v5","version":5,"backupTime":"2026-05-14T14:30:06.452Z"},"/home/qaqtamsy/.claude/plans/gentle-orbiting-karp.md":{"backupFileName":"8983a722ed3c512c@v2","version":2,"backupTime":"2026-05-14T13:54:50.050Z"},"/home/qaqtamsy/.claude/settings.json":{"backupFileName":"8036358f25755b3c@v2","version":2,"backupTime":"2026-05-14T13:27:22.854Z"}},"timestamp":"2026-05-14T15:14:02.228Z"},"isSnapshotUpdate":false}
{"parentUuid":"c974b7dc-6f15-418f-8dba-fdbe5e2bf734","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"ec7bfcd5-a045-4ac9-baa2-bd4cc743529a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to:\n\n1. Completely eliminate app.rs - dismantle its 80+ fields and 24 methods into their proper modules\n2. Each module first assembles itself into its own binary\n3. Then they connect/interact\n\nThe question is: which crates become independent binaries, and which are libraries? Let me think about this based on our 5-binary + 2-shared-crate architecture:\n\nCurrent planned architecture:\n- `dsx-types` — shared library (types only)\n- `dsx-proto` — shared library (IPC message types)\n- `dsx-hp` — binary (health daemon + API gateway)\n- `dsx-agent` — binary (agent core)\n- `dsx-tools` — binary (tool server)\n- `dsx-tui` — binary (terminal UI)\n- `dsx` — binary (Tauri GUI, future)\n\nBut now with app.rs being dismantled, the question is what goes where.\n\nThe key insight: app.rs currently holds the \"glue\" that connects everything. When we dismantle it, the glue needs to go somewhere. Let me think about where each piece of app.rs goes:\n\nFrom app.rs's 24 methods:\n- **Orchestrator (16 methods)**: These should go into dsx-agent's orchestrator module. They ARE the agent loop logic.\n- **UI (8 methods)**: tokens_used(), tt(), context_pct(), system_note(), flush_notes(), read_active_plan(), tool_action(), new() - these are UI concerns for dsx-tui.\n\nBut wait - when we move prepare_and_compact and other orchestrator methods to dsx-agent, what data do they need access to? The ContextAssembler, memories, health platform, etc. These are all agent-level state.\n\nThe challenge: currently `App` holds everything. When we dismantle it:\n1. Agent-level state (ContextAssembler, memories, health, session) → dsx-agent binary\n2. UI-level state (input, scrolling, mode, slash menu) → dsx-tui binary\n3. The connection between them → IPC (stdin/stdout as A02 designed)\n\nSo the answer about binaries:\n\n**Before dismantling app.rs:**\n- All crates are just file groupings, no binaries exist yet\n- main.rs is in dsx-tui/ but it creates the monolithic App\n\n**After dismantling app.rs:**\n- We need to create real binaries for each crate\n- dsx-agent needs its own main.rs that owns AgentState (extracted from App)\n- dsx-tui needs a main.rs that owns UI state and spawns dsx-agent as child process\n- dsx-tools needs a main.rs that listens on stdin/stdout for tool requests\n- dsx-hp needs a main.rs that listens on TCP for API requests\n\nThe question is: can we build them in parallel, or do we need to sequence them?\n\nDependencies:\n- dsx-types: no dependencies on other crates → can build first\n- dsx-proto: depends on dsx-types → after types\n- dsx-hp: depends on dsx-types, dsx-proto → after types+proto\n- dsx-agent: depends on dsx-types, dsx-proto → after types+proto\n- dsx-tools: depends on dsx-types, dsx-proto → after types+proto\n- dsx-tui: depends on dsx-types, dsx-proto → after types+proto\n\nActually, dsx-agent, dsx-tools, dsx-tui, and dsx-hp can all be built in parallel once dsx-types and dsx-proto are done.\n\nBut there's a chicken-and-egg problem: to test binaries, they need each other. dsx-tui needs dsx-agent to be running. dsx-agent needs dsx-tools and dsx-hp to be running.\n\nRealistic approach:\n1. Step 1: dsx-types (shared lib) — define all types\n2. Step 2: dsx-proto (shared lib) — define IPC messages\n3. Step 3: Build all 4 binaries in parallel (they can compile independently since they only depend on types+proto)\n4. Step 4: Integration test (start HP → start Tools → start Agent → start TUI)\n\nNow, about the dismantling of app.rs specifically:\n\nThe 80+ fields of App need to be distributed:\n\n**→ dsx-agent/src/agent_state.rs (new file):**\n- ctx: ContextAssembler\n- messages: Vec<Message> (or eliminate)\n- semantic_memory, long_mem, short_mem, pitfall_guide\n- health: DsAgentsHealthPlatform\n- monitor: MonitorState\n- has_explored, turns_since_last_read\n- tool_failures, tool_calls_this_turn, consecutive_tool_turns\n- pending_tools, tool_results\n- exec_buffer, exec_pending, exec_started_at, exec_child_pids\n- sudo_pending, sudo_password\n- files_written_this_turn\n- skip_all, gate_message\n- turn_scores, auto_verify\n- project_map\n- phase, phase_count, current_task_phase\n- session_seed, session_start, dirty, last_snapshot\n- token_estimate, token_breakdown, api_usage, session_tokens\n- balance, cache_hit_pct, reasoning_tokens\n\nPlus methods:\n- sync_messages, push_tool, prepare_and_compact\n- start_agent_loop, send_message\n- phase_check_tool, explore_gate, pre/post_tool_health_check\n- track_file_written, track_tool_code\n- extract_reasoning_insights, auto_extract_memory\n- repair_messages, maybe_save_session, update_phase\n- read_active_plan\n\n**→ dsx-tui/src/tui_state.rs (new file):**\n- input, input_cursor\n- scroll_offset, auto_scroll, last_max_scroll\n- mode: Mode\n- slash_open, slash_filter, slash_idx, slash_items, slash_submenu\n- esc_just_closed_menu, exit_prompt\n- stream_content, stream_reasoning, stream_tool_progress, stream_cancelled\n- last_activity\n- session_list, session_pick_idx\n- tool_code_path, tool_code_content, tool_code_action, tool_code_status\n- exec_scroll_offset, health_status_line, pending_notes\n- skill_index, active_skill_bodies\n- intent_question, intent_options\n- tools_enabled\n- status_msg\n\nPlus methods:\n- new, tokens_used, tt, context_pct, system_note, flush_notes, tool_action\n\n**→ dsx-tui/src/main.rs (stays):**\n- Creates TuiState\n- Spawns dsx-agent as child process (stdin/stdout)\n- Event loop: keyboard → IPC → render\n\n**→ dsx-agent/src/main.rs (new):**\n- Creates AgentState\n- Listens on stdin/stdout from parent (TUI)\n- Connects to HP via TCP\n- Spawns dsx-tools as child process\n\nLet me think about whether this is realistic for the team to do now. We have 9 active members (B01-B03, C01-C03, D01-D03). And we recalled E01 might be needed for tui_state.rs.\n\nFor the dismantling:\n- C01: Create AgentState, AgentState's main.rs, migrate orchestrator methods from App\n- C02: Migrate context methods, memory fields\n- C03: Migrate session/phase/config fields and methods\n- C01/C02/C03 together: Wire up IPC with TUI and Tools\n- D01: Create dsx-tools main.rs (IPC server listening on stdin/stdout)\n- B01: Create dsx-hp main.rs (TCP server)\n- B02: Wire up API gateway in HP\n\nFor TUI:\n- E01 needs to be recalled for tui_state.rs\n- Or C01 can do it temporarily\n\nLet me present this plan clearly.","signature":"ec7bfcd5-a045-4ac9-baa2-bd4cc743529a"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":267776,"output_tokens":2580,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"80137855-fd13-4233-adf2-1f1f98e59dba","timestamp":"2026-05-14T15:14:58.585Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"80137855-fd13-4233-adf2-1f1f98e59dba","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx","message":{"id":"ec7bfcd5-a045-4ac9-baa2-bd4cc743529a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"正确。分两步想：\n\n---\n\n## 第一步：哪些是二进制，哪些是库\n\n```\ndsx-types    → lib   (共享类型，不独立运行)\ndsx-proto    → lib   (IPC 消息定义，不独立运行)\n\ndsx-hp       → bin   (TCP 守护进程)\ndsx-agent    → bin   (核心，stdin/stdout 子进程)\ndsx-tools    → bin   (工具服务器，stdin/stdout 子进程)\ndsx-tui      → bin   (终端界面，父进程)\ndsx          → bin   (Tauri GUI，未来)\n```\n\n**没有\"一个模块分散到多个二进制\"的情况。** 4 个 bin 各自独立，每个有自己的 main.rs。\n\n---\n\n## 第二步：app.rs 80+ 字段怎么分配\n\n```\napp.rs (80+ 字段，24 方法，510 行)\n        │\n        │  拆\n        │\n        ├── 🔴 编排/记忆/健康/会话/配置 (60+ 字段, 16 方法)\n        │       → dsx-agent/src/agent.rs   (新建)\n        │       → dsx-agent/src/main.rs    (新建)\n        │       归: C01 + C02 + C03\n        │\n        └── 🟢 UI 态 (20 字段, 8 方法)\n                → dsx-tui/src/state.rs     (新建，替换 app.rs)\n                → dsx-tui/src/main.rs      (改：spawn agent 子进程)\n                归: 需召回 E01（或 C01 代）\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第三步：可以并行的\n\n**先建共享库（A 组已解散，由 C01 代）：**\n- dsx-types：枚举/结构体全部不动（STABILITY.md Frozen），只 pub use 重组\n- dsx-proto：IPC 消息枚举，A02 已设计好\n\n**然后 4 个 bin 可以并行：**\n\n| bin | main.rs 要做什么 | 谁做 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **dsx-hp** | TCP :9001 监听，收 ApiRequest → gate → POST API → SSE 返回 | B01+B02+B03 |\n| **dsx-agent** | stdin 读 TUI 消息，TCP 连 HP，stdin/stdout spawn Tools，主循环 | C01+C02+C03 |\n| **dsx-tools** | stdin 读 ToolCallReq → 执行 → stdout 写 ToolResult | D01+D02+D03 |\n| **dsx-tui** | spawn Agent 子进程，键盘事件 → IPC 帧 → 渲染 | E01（召回）或 C01 代 |\n\n4 个都可以**先在自己的 crate 内编译通过**，不需要其他 bin 存在——因为 IPC 边界在编译期只是 trait/类型引用（来自 dsx-proto），运行时才是 TCP/stdin 连接。\n\n---\n\n## 第四步：联动\n\n都编译通了之后，启动顺序：\n```\ndsx-hp 启动（TCP 守护）\n  → dsx-tui 启动\n    → spawn dsx-agent（stdin/stdout）\n      → dsx-agent spawn dsx-tools（stdin/stdout）\n      → dsx-agent 连 dsx-hp（TCP）\n```\n\n---\n\n## 要不要召回 E01？\n\n`dsx-tui/src/state.rs`（20 个 UI 字段 + 8 个方法）不复杂，但需要懂 ratatui。两个选择：\n\n| 召回 E01 | 不召回，C01 代 |\n|---|---|\n| 熟悉自己设计的 AppState 方案 | 省一次召回 |\n| 但同时需召回 E02/E03（input/render 各有依赖） | C01 需额外读 ratatui 代码 |\n\n建议召回 E01——state.rs 是它的设计，而且后续 render 改动也需要它协调。你怎么说？"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":267776,"output_tokens":2580,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"634ba5f1-aaba-4831-9459-9d39bed6f3de","timestamp":"2026-05-14T15:15:25.753Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
