{"parentUuid":"46c1bb0c-5f25-4189-94b2-06079f3b6478","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"465a413c-cf65-462a-a430-54e2aa52cc91","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"TUI started, printed the welcome message, but the agent didn't seem to output anything. The exit was 124 (timeout), meaning it was waiting for input. But wait - \"hello\" was piped via stdin - so it should have read it. Let me check the TUI and agent logs.\n\nThe TUI says it's waiting for input: `> ` prompt, then timeout. That suggests that the TUI's readline loop started but the `hello` on stdin was consumed somewhere. Actually, looking at the TUI code:\n\n```rust\nloop {\n    input.clear();\n    print!(\"> \");\n    let _ = std::io::stdout().flush();\n    if stdin.read_line(&mut input).is_err() || input.trim().is_empty() {\n        continue;\n    }\n```\n\nThe `print!(\"> \")` writes to stdout which is connected to the terminal/pipe. The `stdin.read_line()` reads from stdin.\n\nWhen we do `echo \"hello\" | timeout 5 ./dsx-tui`, the stdin pipe gets \"hello\\n\", then EOF. So:\n1. Print prompt \"> \" (to stdout, goes to terminal)\n2. Read line -> \"hello\"\n3. Check if empty -> no\n4. Send frame to agent: `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}`\n5. Read from agent_reader in a loop until \"done\" or \"error\"\n6. But agent just echoes back, which doesn't contain \"done\" or \"error\"\n7. So the loop hangs forever -> timeout\n\nThat's the issue. The agent's echo response doesn't contain \"done\" or \"error\", so the TUI's read loop never breaks.\n\nLet me check the TUI's response loop logic:\n\n```rust\nsend(&mut agent_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"{}\"}}\"#, msg));\nwhile let Some(resp) = read_line(&mut agent_reader) {\n    println!(\"  ← {resp}\");\n    if resp.contains(\"\\\"done\\\"\") || resp.contains(\"\\\"error\\\"\") { break; }\n}\n```\n\nAnd in the agent, the echo branch:\n```rust\nwrite_frame(&mut tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"echo\",\"data\":{frame}}}\"#));\n```\n\nThe agent sends back: `{\"type\":\"echo\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}}`\nThis contains neither `\"done\"` nor `\"error\"`, so the TUI loop spins forever.\n\nSo the pipeline IS working (TUI sends → Agent receives and responds), but the TUI's response loop doesn't know how to handle the echo response gracefully.\n\nThis is a minor TUI-side issue. The fix is either:\n1. Agent should respond with `\"done\"` in the echo case\n2. Or TUI's response loop should break on any non-stream response type\n3. Or TUI should just read one response and then break\n\nLet me look at the TUI code more carefully and make it work with the agent's echo response.\n\nActually, let me check the stderr logs to confirm the agent connected and spawned tools.","signature":"465a413c-cf65-462a-a430-54e2aa52cc91"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":54528,"output_tokens":773,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"74ec70c2-69a0-4db3-ae96-9d491af0f7fe","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:15:13.914Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
