{"parentUuid":"a4996cc5-a76c-4983-8cce-ba38a7a2d4d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"41309640-e225-4ac8-8995-97d6485dc7f4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I think the issue is that the agent's stdout is being captured by the TUI, so the `write_frame` to TUI might be blocking. But when running the agent directly (not via TUI), stdout IS the terminal.\n\nWait, let me re-think. When I ran `echo '{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}' | XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/tmp timeout 5 ./target/release/dsx-agent 2>&1`:\n- Agent stdin = pipe from echo\n- Agent stdout = terminal (via 2>&1, stderr is merged with stdout)\n- Agent stderr = terminal\n\nSo the agent:\n1. Prints \"dsx-agent starting\" to stderr ✅ \n2. Connects to HP via TCP \n3. Sends register frame\n4. Spawns tools\n5. Reads ToolsReady... \n\nHmm, let me think about what could hang. The `read_frame` for ToolsReady:\n```rust\nlet ready = read_frame(&mut tools_reader).unwrap_or_default();\n```\n\nIf tools doesn't output anything, this would block. But we know tools sends `{\"type\":\"tools_ready\",\"tools\":[]}` on stdin. But wait — tools' stdin is piped from the agent, and its stdin stays empty (the agent never sent an Init frame). So tools might be waiting for Init on stdin and not sending Ready.\n\nLet me look at the tools IPC code again:\n\n```rust\npub fn ipc_main_loop(manager: &mut ToolManager) {\n    let stdin = io::stdin();\n    let stdout = io::stdout();\n    let mut reader = io::BufReader::new(stdin.lock());\n    let mut writer = stdout.lock();\n\n    loop {\n        let frame = match read_frame(&mut reader) {\n            Ok(Some(f)) => f,\n            Ok(None) => break,  // EOF\n            Err(e) => { ... }\n        };\n\n        match frame {\n            InboundFrame::Init { ... } => {\n                manager.apply_init(...);\n                let tools = manager.filtered_defs();\n                if write_frame(&mut writer, &OutboundFrame::Ready { tools }).is_err() { break; }\n            }\n            ...\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe tools main loop reads a frame. If it gets EOF (stdin closed), it breaks. Otherwise it parses an InboundFrame. If the first frame is an Init, it calls apply_init and sends Ready.\n\nBut the agent spawns tools but never sends an Init frame to tools! The agent just:\n1. Spawns tools\n2. Reads ToolsReady from tools\n\nBut tools are waiting for Init before sending Ready! Deadlock!\n\nWait, that doesn't make sense. Let me re-read: the tools' `ipc_main_loop` reads a frame. If the stream is empty, it blocks on `read_line`. When echo sends 'hello' via pipe, the agent's stdin gets \"hello\". But tools' stdin is a separate pipe.\n\nSo tools' stdin is an empty pipe. `read_frame` → `read_line` will block waiting for input. The agent is also blocked reading tools' stdout for the Ready frame. Deadlock!\n\nThe fix is: the agent needs to send an Init frame to tools before waiting for Ready. Or the tools server should send Ready immediately on startup (like a \"ready\" handshake), without waiting for Init.\n\nThe current flow:\n```\nAgent spawns Tools\nAgent blocks reading Tools' stdout for \"Ready\" ← deadlock\nTools blocks reading stdin for \"Init\"\n```\n\nThe fix is either:\n1. Agent sends Init to tools first, then reads Ready\n2. Tools sends Ready immediately on startup, without waiting for Init\n\nOption 1 is more correct (the tools can't report their capabilities until they know what's allowed). Let me modify the agent to send Init before waiting for Ready.\n\nActually, look at the current code again:\n\n```rust\n// 2. Spawn dsx-tools\nlet exe = std::env::current_exe().unwrap();\nlet tools_path = exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-tools\");\nlet mut tools_child = Command::new(&tools_path)\n    .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n    .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n    .spawn()\n    .expect(\"dsx-agent: failed to spawn dsx-tools\");\n\nlet tools_stdin = tools_child.stdin.take().unwrap();\nlet tools_stdout = tools_child.stdout.take().unwrap();\nlet mut tools_reader = BufReader::new(tools_stdout);\nlet mut tools_writer = tools_stdin;\n\n// Read ToolsReady  ← BUG: should send Init FIRST\nlet ready = read_frame(&mut tools_reader).unwrap_or_default();\n```\n\nFix: Send Init frame to tools before reading Ready. The Init needs `allowed_tools`, `session_seed`, and `auto_mode`. Since we're in a minimal pipe mode, let me send empty allowed_tools and a generated seed.","signature":"41309640-e225-4ac8-8995-97d6485dc7f4"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1348,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":58368,"output_tokens":1416,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d43e63ff-efcf-42c1-bbf3-486ea39bf29d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:16:06.129Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
