{"parentUuid":"444a188d-6675-40d0-9e0e-81bfb700c9cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"78a4dbbc-52f9-4e28-84a6-9ce06ae4dd1d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fix: `drop(agent_writer)` before `child.wait()`. But I also need to send a shutdown if it's an intentional quit. Let me also handle the case where the loop breaks normally (EOF on stdin).\n\nActually, looking at the code structure, when the user types `/quit` or `/exit`:\n1. Send shutdown to agent\n2. Break from loop\n3. Falls through to `child.wait()`\n\nThe agent processes the shutdown frame and sends `shutdown_ack`, then breaks its loop.\n\nWhen the loop breaks due to EOF:\n1. No shutdown sent to agent\n2. Falls through to `child.wait()`\n3. But agent_writer is still alive, so agent's stdin isn't closed yet\n4. Deadlock\n\nFix: drop agent_writer before child.wait():\n```rust\ndrop(agent_writer);\nlet _ = child.wait();\n```\n\nBut wait, could dropping agent_writer cause issues for the /quit case? When we send shutdown via `send(&mut agent_writer, ...)`, that writes to the pipe. Then the agent reads it, processes it, sends shutdown_ack. Then the agent breaks its loop. Then the agent's main function does cleanup (unregister from HP, wait for tools, etc.) and exits.\n\nBut the TUI's response loop (while let Some(resp) = read_line(...)) reads the shutdown_ack frame and exits (it doesn't contain \"done\" or \"error\"... wait, does it? Let me check).\n\nThe shutdown path:\n1. TUI sends `{\"type\":\"shutdown\"}` to agent\n2. Agent receives it, matches `frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\"\")`\n3. Agent sends `{\"type\":\"shutdown_ack\"}` to TUI\n4. Agent breaks its main loop\n5. TUI's response loop: `resp.contains(\"\\\"done\\\"\") || resp.contains(\"\\\"error\\\"\")` — shutdown_ack contains neither \"done\" nor \"error\"!\n\nSo the TUI hangs even with /quit! The response loop never breaks.\n\nFix: add `\"shutdown_ack\"` to the break conditions:\n```rust\nif resp.contains(\"\\\"done\\\"\") || resp.contains(\"\\\"error\\\"\") || resp.contains(\"\\\"shutdown_ack\\\"\") { \n    break; \n}\n```\n\nOr just break unconditionally after sending shutdown (since we know what response to expect).\n\nLet me fix both issues properly:\n\n```rust\nif msg == \"/quit\" || msg == \"/exit\" {\n    send(&mut agent_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"shutdown\"}\"#);\n    // Read one response (should be shutdown_ack)\n    let _ = read_line(&mut agent_reader);\n    break;\n}\n```\n\nActually, the simplest fix that covers all cases:\n```rust\nif msg == \"/quit\" || msg == \"/exit\" {\n    send(&mut agent_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"shutdown\"}\"#);\n    while let Some(resp) = read_line(&mut agent_reader) {\n        println!(\"  ← {resp}\");\n        if resp.contains(\"\\\"shutdown_ack\\\"\") { break; }\n    }\n    break;\n}\n```\n\nAnd for the normal EOF exit:\n```rust\n// Drop agent_writer to close stdin pipe, so agent sees EOF and exits\ndrop(agent_writer);\nlet _ = child.wait();\n```\n\nLet me implement both fixes.","signature":"78a4dbbc-52f9-4e28-84a6-9ce06ae4dd1d"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":69760,"output_tokens":1122,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"41200be2-0a74-4391-b721-4b0f6d9d64c7","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:18:14.407Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
