s sync.\n\nActually, this is more involved than \"收尾\". The actual API calling, conversation management, streaming, etc. is all stubbed out. Making it work would require implementing the real API client.\n\nLet me think about what the most practical \"今天可以正常使用\" path is:\n\n1. The HP daemon has the `client.rs` module which might have real HTTP client code\n2. The agent's `api.rs` is a stub with Phase 4 TODO\n3. The actual API is called from HP (since only HP has API key)\n\nSo the flow would be:\n1. Agent receives user input\n2. Agent builds conversation with ContextAssembler\n3. Agent sends API request to HP via IPC\n4. HP makes real HTTP call to Anthropic API\n5. HP returns response to Agent\n6. Agent returns response to TUI\n\nBut this requires:\n1. Real API client in HP (not stub) — check if it exists\n2. Real conversation management in Agent (ContextAssembler exists, but assembly flow needs wiring)\n3. IPC protocol for API request/response between Agent and HP\n\nThis is substantial work. Let me check if the HP has a real API client already.","signature":"5684ba79-0942-49ce-8ee9-5608ed27ee85"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":83840,"output_tokens":772,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d436dea3-bee7-41cc-9558-965670a5310a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:20:10.321Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
