{"parentUuid":"4c8d75b0-403a-4f26-9ee1-0bfa2db2ffbe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ddf8f9ab-d801-42d7-9251-c7fccf1f1f0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_iAEfzoWSNuxsRlrkyjtd6707","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! HTTP client: request building, retry loop, SSE streaming to StreamEvent channel.\n2\t\n3\tuse dsx_types::*;\n4\tuse crate::{AccumulatedToolCall, StreamEvent};\n5\tuse crate::config::Config;\n6\tuse futures_util::StreamExt;\n7\tuse reqwest::Client as HttpClient;\n8\tuse std::collections::HashMap;\n9\tuse std::time::Duration;\n10\tuse tokio::sync::mpsc;\n11\t\n12\tuse crate::converter::{anthropic_url, request_to_provider};\n13\t\n14\t/// Streaming chat via Anthropic Messages endpoint.\n15\t///\n16\t/// Takes pre-validated Anthropic-format messages from the ContextAssembler.\n17\t/// The conversion and validation are done upstream — this function only handles\n18\t/// the HTTP request and SSE parsing.\n19\tpub async fn chat_stream(\n20\t    config: &Config,\n21\t    model: &str,\n22\t    system: Option<String>,\n23\t    anthropic_msgs: Vec<AnthropicMessage>,\n24\t    _thinking: bool,\n25\t    effort: Option<&str>,\n26\t    tools: Option<Vec<ToolDef>>,\n27\t    tool_choice: Option<&str>,\n28\t    max_tokens: u32,\n29\t    _temperature: Option<f64>,\n30\t    _top_p: Option<f64>,\n31\t    _user_id: Option<&str>,\n32\t    tx: mpsc::Sender<StreamEvent>,\n33\t) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n34\t    // Messages are already converted by ContextAssembler — no convert_messages() call needed\n35\t\n36\t    // Convert tools to Anthropic format\n37\t    let anthropic_tools: Option<Vec<AnthropicTool>> = tools.map(|tds| {\n38\t        tds.into_iter()\n39\t            .map(|td| AnthropicTool {\n40\t                name: td.function.name,\n41\t                description: td.function.description,\n42\t                input_schema: td.function.parameters,\n43\t            })\n44\t            .collect()\n45\t    });\n46\t\n47\t    // Build tool_choice\n48\t    let tc = tool_choice.map(|s| {\n49\t        if s == \"auto\" {\n50\t            serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"auto\"})"}]},"uuid":"c3a2a3d8-bcd9-4aed-8056-8302fe0f736c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:20:10.729Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/client.rs","content":"//! HTTP client: request building, retry loop, SSE streaming to StreamEvent channel.\n\nuse dsx_types::*;\nuse crate::{AccumulatedToolCall, StreamEvent};\nuse crate::config::Config;\nuse futures_util::StreamExt;\nuse reqwest::Client as HttpClient;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\nuse std::time::Duration;\nuse tokio::sync::mpsc;\n\nuse crate::converter::{anthropic_url, request_to_provider};\n\n/// Streaming chat via Anthropic Messages endpoint.\n///\n/// Takes pre-validated Anthropic-format messages from the ContextAssembler.\n/// The conversion and validation are done upstream — this function only handles\n/// the HTTP request and SSE parsing.\npub async fn chat_stream(\n    config: &Config,\n    model: &str,\n    system: Option<String>,\n    anthropic_msgs: Vec<AnthropicMessage>,\n    _thinking: bool,\n    effort: Option<&str>,\n    tools: Option<Vec<ToolDef>>,\n    tool_choice: Option<&str>,\n    max_tokens: u32,\n    _temperature: Option<f64>,\n    _top_p: Option<f64>,\n    _user_id: Option<&str>,\n    tx: mpsc::Sender<StreamEvent>,\n) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // Messages are already converted by ContextAssembler — no convert_messages() call needed\n\n    // Convert tools to Anthropic format\n    let anthropic_tools: Option<Vec<AnthropicTool>> = tools.map(|tds| {\n        tds.into_iter()\n            .map(|td| AnthropicTool {\n                name: td.function.name,\n                description: td.function.description,\n                input_schema: td.function.parameters,\n            })\n            .collect()\n    });\n\n    // Build tool_choice\n    let tc = tool_choice.map(|s| {\n        if s == \"auto\" {\n            serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"auto\"})","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":528}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c8d75b0-403a-4f26-9ee1-0bfa2db2ffbe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"c3a2a3d8-bcd9-4aed-8056-8302fe0f736c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"b435cfd1-8a0d-47c8-8f2b-d8f9a50848fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HP has a REAL `chat_stream` function that makes actual HTTP calls to the Anthropic API! It takes AnthropicMessage, converts tools, builds the request, and streams the response.\n\nAnd the HP's main.rs has a TCP accept loop that handles frames. But the current frame types only handle health-related frames (register, heartbeat, judge, etc.). There's no frame type for API requests.\n\nSo the wiring that needs to happen:\n\n1. **HP side**: Add a new frame type like `api_chat` that takes the conversation messages and calls the real `client::chat_stream` \n2. **Agent side**: In the main loop, when receiving `user_input`, build the conversation using ContextAssembler, send it to HP as an `api_chat` frame, and stream the response back to TUI\n\nBut this is a significant amount of work. And the user said \"不动底层逻辑\". The HP main.rs already has the server infrastructure. Adding a new frame type is extending, not refactoring.\n\nLet me think about the minimum viable path:\n\n**Minimum: single-round API call via the existing pipeline**\n\n1. Add `chat` frame to HP dispatch_frame that:\n   - Receives `{\"type\":\"chat\",\"messages\":[...],\"system\":\"...\",\"model\":\"...\"}`\n   - Calls `client::chat_stream` \n   - Returns response as a frame\n\n2. In the agent, when receiving `user_input`:\n   - Forward to HP as a chat request\n   - Return response to TUI\n\nBut `client::chat_stream` is async/tokio, and the HP main loop is synchronous (thread-based). I'd need to either:\n- Use `tokio::runtime::Runtime::block_on` to call the async function synchronously\n- Or convert the HP to use tokio (big change)\n\nActually, HP depends on tokio already (it's in Cargo.toml). Let me check...\n\nActually, the HP's main.rs doesn't use tokio at the top level. It's thread-based. But the `client.rs` uses tokio. We could create a small tokio runtime for the API calls.\n\nWait, let me re-think. The agent flow would be:\n1. Agent receives `user_input` from TUI\n2. Agent needs to build the conversation, call the API, get response\n3. But the API key is in HP, not in agent\n\nSo the flow must be:\n```\nTUI → Agent → HP (API call) → Agent → TUI\n```\n\nThe simplest implementation:\n1. Agent receives user_input frame\n2. Agent wraps it as an API request and sends to HP via TCP\n3. HP receives the API request, calls the real Anthropic API\n4. HP returns the response to Agent\n5. Agent forwards to TUI\n\nFor step 2, the agent needs:\n- System prompt (from config)\n- Conversation history (currently none, since agent doesn't maintain state)\n- User's message\n\nThe current agent is stateless — it just forwards frames. To make it stateful, it needs to maintain conversation history.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me take a step back and think about what \"正常使用\" really means to the user.\n\nActually, I think the most practical approach for today is to make the **TUI work as a standalone binary** that directly uses the agent library (AgentState, ContextAssembler, HP client via IPC). Instead of piping through a separate agent process, the TUI could manage everything inline.\n\nBut that changes the architecture we just built (5 processes).\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. Maybe the user's expectation is different. Let me just explain what's working and what needs more work for full AI interaction, and let them decide.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read what the user said: \"早。今天在不动底层逻辑的情况下收一下尾确保今天可以正常使用\"\n\n\"收尾\" = wrap up/finish\n\"不动底层逻辑\" = don't touch underlying logic\n\"确保今天可以正常使用\" = ensure it can be used normally today\n\nSo they want me to finish up the remaining tasks and make it usable. The \"底层逻辑\" presumably refers to the architecture we already built (5-process, IPC, types etc.).\n\nLet me think about what \"正常使用\" means in context. Given that the project is DSX and the user has been working on it for days, I think it means: being able to launch DSX and have it respond to user input with AI-generated responses.\n\nTo achieve this, I need:\n1. A real API call path from user input → AI response\n2. Conversation management (at least basic)\n\nThe quickest way is to add an `api_chat` handler in HP that the agent's main loop can call.\n\nLet me check the HP's configuration to see if it has the API key set up.\n\nActually, let me look at how `hp.rs` in the HP crate works — specifically the config.","signature":"b435cfd1-8a0d-47c8-8f2b-d8f9a50848fd"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":550,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":85120,"output_tokens":1239,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b55af00c-e3d6-4c6b-ade0-d1f554a8b5a0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:20:24.905Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
