{"parentUuid":"d77fe822-c306-4f5c-9eb9-f47f759d6515","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"efed3e39-7385-4e3d-a5a2-cbc574fadd0f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`AnthropicMessage` and `AnthropicContent` are re-exported from `dsx_types`. I can use `dsx_types::AnthropicMessage` and `dsx_types::AnthropicContent`.\n\nNow let me implement the changes. I'll do both HP and agent in parallel.\n\nLet me start with the HP's dispatch_frame. I'll rewrite the function to:\n1. Not lock the service at the top\n2. Add api_chat handler\n\nHere's the full new dispatch_frame:\n\n```rust\nfn dispatch_frame(\n    line: &str,\n    service: &Mutex<HealthService>,\n) -> String {\n    let frame_type: String = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(line)\n        .ok()\n        .and_then(|v| v.get(\"type\").and_then(|v| v.as_str().map(String::from)))\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n\n    match frame_type.as_str() {\n        \"api_chat\" => handle_api_chat(line),\n        _ => {\n            let mut svc = service.lock().unwrap();\n            match frame_type.as_str() {\n                \"register\" => {\n                    ...\n                }\n                ...\n                _ => json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"unknown frame type: {frame_type}\")),\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nActually, I realize that moving the lock inside each match arm will be quite a bit of restructuring. Let me think about whether there's a simpler approach that minimizes changes.\n\nAlternative: keep the existing structure, but wrap the api_chat handler in a way that doesn't hold the lock. \n\n```rust\nfn dispatch_frame(line: &str, service: &Mutex<HealthService>) -> String {\n    let frame_type = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(line)...;\n\n    match frame_type.as_str() {\n        \"api_chat\" => {\n            return handle_api_chat(line);\n        }\n        _ => {}\n    }\n\n    let mut svc = service.lock().unwrap();\n    match frame_type.as_str() {\n        \"register\" => { ... }\n        ...\n        _ => json_response(\"error\", ...)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis way:\n- api_chat returns early before the lock\n- All other handlers work as before with the lock held at the top\n\nThis is the minimal change. Let me do this.\n\nWait, but I also need to add the config loading. Let me add a `static HP_CONFIG` and initialize it in main().\n\nLet me also build the api_chat handler function:\n\n```rust\nfn handle_api_chat(line: &str) -> String {\n    use dsx_types::{AnthropicContent, AnthropicMessage};\n    \n    let config = match HP_CONFIG.get() {\n        Some(c) => c.clone(),\n        None => return json_response(\"error\", \"HP not configured (no API key/enabled)\"),\n    };\n    \n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(line) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(e) => return json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"invalid api_chat frame: {e}\")),\n    };\n    \n    let model = v.get(\"model\").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"deepseek-v4-flash\");\n    let system = v.get(\"system\").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).map(String::from);\n    \n    let messages_val = match v.get(\"messages\").and_then(|v| v.as_array()) {\n        Some(arr) => arr,\n        None => return json_response(\"error\", \"api_chat: missing messages array\"),\n    };\n    \n    let anthropic_msgs: Vec<AnthropicMessage> = messages_val.iter().filter_map(|m| {\n        let role = m.get(\"role\")?.as_str()?;\n        // Support both string content and content array\n        let content = if let Some(text) = m.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            vec![AnthropicContent::Text { text: text.to_string() }]\n        } else if let Some(arr) = m.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_array()) {\n            // Pass through as-is — let serde handle it\n            return Some(AnthropicMessage {\n                role: role.to_string(),\n                content: serde_json::from_value(m.get(\"content\")?.clone()).ok()?,\n            });\n        } else {\n            return None;\n        };\n        Some(AnthropicMessage {\n            role: role.to_string(),\n            content,\n        })\n    }).collect();\n    \n    if anthropic_msgs.is_empty() {\n        return json_response(\"error\", \"api_chat: no valid messages\");\n    }\n    \n    let rt = match tokio::runtime::Runtime::new() {\n        Ok(r) => r,\n        Err(e) => return json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"runtime error: {e}\")),\n    };\n    \n    let (content, error): (String, Option<String>) = rt.block_on(async {\n        let (tx, mut rx) = tokio::sync::mpsc::channel::<StreamEvent>(64);\n        let cfg = config.clone();\n        let model_o = model.to_string();\n        let sys = system.clone();\n        let msgs = anthropic_msgs;\n        \n        tokio::spawn(async move {\n            let _ = client::chat_stream(\n                &cfg, &model_o, sys, msgs,\n                false, None, None, None, 4096,\n                None, None, None, tx,\n            ).await;\n        });\n        \n        let mut content = String::new();\n        let mut error = None;\n        while let Some(event) = rx.recv().await {\n            match event {\n                StreamEvent::ContentDelta(delta) => content.push_str(&delta),\n                StreamEvent::Done { .. } => break,\n                StreamEvent::Error(e) => { error = Some(e); break; }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n        (content, error)\n    });\n    \n    match error {\n        Some(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e),\n        None => format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"api_response\\\",\\\"content\\\":{}}}\",\n            serde_json::to_string(&content).unwrap_or_default()),\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis is ~60 lines. Let me clean it up and add it to main.rs.\n\nNow for the agent side, I need to modify the main loop to:\n1. On startup: build an initial conversation with system prompt\n2. On user_input: append user message to conversation, send api_chat to HP, get response, append to conversation, forward to TUI\n\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    // ... existing startup code (HP connection, tools spawn) ...\n    \n    // Conversation tracking\n    let mut conversation: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n    let system_prompt = \"You are DSX (DeepSeek X Agents), an AI-powered coding assistant.\";\n    // system prompt is sent with each api_chat request, not tracked in conversation\n    \n    loop {\n        match read_frame(&mut tui_reader) {\n            Some(frame) => {\n                eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tui ← {frame}\");\n                \n                if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\"\") {\n                    // Forward to tools (existing)\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"api_request\\\"\") && hp.is_some() {\n                    // Forward to HP (existing)\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\"\") {\n                    // Shutdown (existing)\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_input\\\"\") {\n                    // NEW: process user input through HP API\n                    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&frame) {\n                        Ok(v) => v,\n                        Err(_) => { write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &frame); continue; }\n                    };\n                    let text = v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    if text.is_empty() { continue; }\n                    \n                    // Add user message to conversation\n                    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":text}));\n                    \n                    // Build api_chat request\n                    let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n                        \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n                        \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\",\n                        \"system\": system_prompt,\n                        \"messages\": conversation,\n                    });\n                    \n                    // Send to HP\n                    if let Some(ref hp_conn) = hp {\n                        let mut hp_w = hp_conn.try_clone().unwrap();\n                        write_frame(&mut hp_w, &chat_req.to_string());\n                        let mut hp_r = BufReader::new(hp_conn.try_clone().unwrap());\n                        if let Some(resp) = read_frame(&mut hp_r) {\n                            // Parse response\n                            let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n                                Ok(v) => v,\n                                Err(_) => { write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp); continue; }\n                            };\n                            if resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) == Some(\"api_response\") {\n                                let content = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                                // Add assistant response to conversation\n                                conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":content}));\n                                // Forward to TUI\n                                write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp);\n                            } else {\n                                // Error or unknown\n                                write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp);\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                } else {\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"echo\",\"data\":{frame}}}\"#));\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                }\n            }\n            None => break,\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Cleanup\n    drop(tools_writer);\n    let _ = tools_child.wait();\n    if let Some(ref hp) = hp {\n        let mut hp_w = hp.try_clone().unwrap();\n        let frame = format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"unregister\",\"pid\":{}}}\"#, std::process::id());\n        write_frame(&mut hp_w, &frame);\n    }\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: shutdown complete\");\n}\n```\n\nWait, there's a problem. The HP connection handler reads frames from the TCP connection. But the agent's `hp` variable is a single TcpStream. When I clone it and write a frame, the HP side reads it. But then I clone it AGAIN to read the response. However, the response from the HP is written to the same TCP stream. \n\nThe issue is that we're creating a new `BufReader` each time, which might miss data that's already buffered. Better to reuse the reader.\n\nBut actually, the current api_request forwarding code does the same thing:\n```rust\nlet mut hp_w = hp.as_ref().unwrap().try_clone().unwrap();\nwrite_frame(&mut hp_w, &frame);\nlet mut hp_r = BufReader::new(hp.as_ref().unwrap().try_clone().unwrap());\nif let Some(resp) = read_frame(&mut hp_r) {\n```\n\nThis clones the TCP stream twice — once for writing, once for reading. When we write a frame, it goes to HP. HP dispatches it and writes a response. Then we read from another clone of the stream. Since TCP is ordered, the response should arrive after the request.\n\nBut with our current api_chat approach, the HP will process the API call (which takes seconds) before writing the response. During that time, the agent might send more frames on the same TCP connection (like heartbeats). This would cause the HP to process those frames before the API response.\n\nFor now, since the agent only uses the HP connection for api_chat (not for regular health stuff), this shouldn't be an issue. The HP processes the api_chat frame, then any other frames received afterward.\n\nWait, this is actually a problem. The HP reads frames from a single connection in a loop:\n```\nread line → dispatch → write response → read next line → ...\n```\n\nIf we send api_chat, the HP blocks on the API call inside dispatch_frame. During that time, no other frames on that connection are processed. But the agent doesn't send other frames on this connection (register was sent at startup, and api_chat is sent now).\n\nAfter the API call, the HP writes the response and reads the next line (blocking). The agent reads the response. This should work fine for a single request-response cycle.\n\nBut for the agent model, the agent sends api_chat and waits for the response. The HP blocks inside dispatch_frame during the API call. Then writes the response. Then reads the next frame (blocking on the agent to send something). This is correct for our usage pattern.\n\nOK so the approach works. Let me implement it.\n\nNow let me think about potential issues:\n1. The `rx.recv()` inside `block_on` might deadlock if the channel is full. The channel capacity is 64, and chat_stream sends content deltas, so it should be fine. Worst case, if the model returns a very long response, the channel buffers up to 64 messages, then awaits tx.send(). But since rx is being drained by the recv loop, this shouldn't deadlock.\n\nActually wait, there's a real issue: `tokio::spawn` requires a `'static` lifetime for the future. But the `cfg` variable... hmm, let me use `cfg.clone()` to pass owned data into the async block.\n\n2. The `line` variable in `handle_api_chat` might have large content (many messages). But since it's over TCP, it's already been read into memory.\n\n3. The `conversation` Vec in the agent grows unbounded. For now, it's fine for testing. We can add truncation later.\n\nOK let me just implement it. Let me write the HP changes first, then the agent changes.\n\nFor the agent, I also need to handle an edge case: the HP connection might fail during api_chat. I should handle that gracefully.\n\nAlso, I notice that the agent uses `hp` as `Option<TcpStream>`. If HP is not running, we fall back to echo mode. That's the current behavior and should be preserved.\n\nLet me finalize and write the code.\n\nOne more thing: the system prompt. I said \"You are DSX...\". Let me use a simple default or read from the agent config. For now, a hardcoded default is fine.\n\nOK let me write the final implementation now. I'll write the HP main.rs changes and agent main.rs changes.\n\nFor the HP, the key changes:\n1. Add `use std::sync::OnceLock;`\n2. Add `static HP_CONFIG: OnceLock<Config> = OnceLock::new();`\n3. In `main()`: initialize HP_CONFIG\n4. Change `dispatch_frame` to check for api_chat before locking\n5. Add `handle_api_chat` function\n\nFor the agent:\n1. Add conversation tracking\n2. Handle `user_input` by sending to HP\n\nLet me write this now.","signature":"efed3e39-7385-4e3d-a5a2-cbc574fadd0f"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":109440,"output_tokens":3768,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"18c14254-18f1-4371-9165-1c4aa08f314d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:29:10.266Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
