ink about what the user actually wants.\n\nI think the simplest answer is:\n1. Yes, we can use musl for static linking\n2. For single binary, we can restructure to use subcommands\n\nBut both have caveats:\n- musl: some crates might not compile with musl (openssl-sys, etc.)\n- Single binary: the architecture was designed for process isolation\n\nLet me just be direct with the user and explain the options. Actually, let me try the musl target first to see if it compiles, and then propose the single-binary approach.\n\nLet me check if musl target is available.","signature":"8064e249-ae39-4fcf-a685-32e87cee4ffd"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":134144,"output_tokens":1338,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"113404e9-4a18-4088-82a7-b296b3e9b91e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:34:36.495Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
