based on argv[1].**\n\nLet me trace through what each crate needs:\n\n**dsx-hp**: Move main() logic to `dsx_hp::run()`. Main.rs becomes:\n```rust\nfn main() { dsx_hp::run(); }\n```\n\n**dsx-agent**: Move main() logic to `dsx_agent::run()`. \n\n**dsx-tools**: Already has `dsx_tools::ipc::ipc_main_loop()` exposed. Add `dsx_tools::run()`.\n\n**dsx-tui**: Move main() logic to `dsx_tui::run()`.\n\nThen create `crates/dsx/` with:\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    let subcommand = std::env::args().nth(1).unwrap_or_default();\n    match subcommand.as_str() {\n        \"hp\" => dsx_hp::run(),\n        \"agent\" => dsx_agent::run(),\n        \"tools\" => dsx_tools::run(),\n        _ => dsx_tui::run(), // default: tui mode\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAnd the TUI's spawn code changes from `exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-agent\")` to `Command::new(&exe).arg(\"agent\")`.\n\nSame for agent → tools: `Command::new(&exe).arg(\"tools\")`.\n\nLet me implement this. But first, let me see how big these changes are.\n\nFor dsx-tools, the current main.rs is just:\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    dsx_tools::ipc::ipc_main_loop(&mut dsx_tools::registration::build_tool_manager());\n}\n```\n\nSo I just need to add a `pub fn run()` in lib.rs that does the same.\n\nFor dsx-hp and dsx-agent, their main functions are in main.rs, not in the library. I need to extract the logic.\n\nActually, for the smallest change: I'll create a `pub fn run()` in each library that just duplicates the main logic. Then the original main.rs calls the library function. No structural changes needed.\n\nBut wait, main.rs in dsx-hp and dsx-agent imports things like `use std::net::TcpListener` and has its own struct definitions (like `HealthService`). Moving all of that into lib.rs requires restructuring the lib.\n\nAn alternative: don't move the code. Instead, have the umbrella binary use `std::process::Command` to spawn the REAL binaries (dsx-hp, dsx-agent, etc.) that exist alongside the umbrella binary. This is the `exec` approach:\n\n```\ntarget/re