--list-sessions\"]`. Combined: `[\"dsx\", \"--list-sessions\"]`. That's correct.\n\nWhat about the agent spawn? When agent spawns tools via `Command::new(&exe).arg(\"tools\")`, the child's argv is `[\"dsx\", \"tools\"]`. The umbrella dispatches \"tools\" to dsx_tools::run(). dsx_tools doesn't parse CLI args, so it's fine.\n\nFor the HP: `Command::new(&exe).arg(\"hp\")` → child argv is `[\"dsx\", \"hp\"]` → umbrella dispatches \"hp\" to dsx_hp::runner::run(). HP doesn't parse CLI args (uses env vars). Fine.\n\nOK, the approach works. Let me implement it.\n\nFor dsx-tui's run function, I'll use `parse_from` to skip the first arg if it's \"tui\" (or any unknown role):\n\n```rust\nuse clap::Parser;\n\npub fn run() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // Strip role prefix if present (umbrella binary adds it)\n    let raw: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\n    let args: Vec<String> = if raw.len() > 1 && !raw[1].starts_with('-') {\n        // First non-flag arg is a role — skip it\n        std::env::args().take(1).chain(std::env::args().skip(2)).collect()\n    } else {\n        raw\n    };\n    let cli = Cli::parse_from(args);\n    // ... rest of main\n}\n```\n\nBut I can't use Cli inside lib.rs because it's defined in main.rs. I need to move Cli to lib.rs or redefine it there.\n\nHmm, let me just take a different approach: have the TUI's run function handle the arg skipping internally:\n\n```rust\n// In lib.rs\npub fn run() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // Parse args, skipping argv[1] if it looks like a subcommand (not a flag)\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\n    let skip = args.get(1).map_or(false, |a| !a.starts_with('-'));\n    let cli = Cli::parse_from(\n        std::env::args().take(1).chain(std::env::args().skip(if skip { 2 } else { 1 }))\n    );\n    run_with_cli(cli)\n}\n```\n\nBut I still need the Cli struct and run_with_cli to be in lib.rs. Let me move the relevant code from main.rs to lib.rs.\n\nActually, the most practical: extract main