{"parentUuid":"1cd6012f-3c6e-4b9a-a010-15625758490e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"f64ac9f4-fd26-438c-a99e-9a68acab8f8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, now I need to create the dsx-tui lib's `run()` function and the umbrella binary. Let me do this efficiently.\n\nFor dsx-tui, I'll add a `pub fn run()` at the end of lib.rs that contains the main logic, and update main.rs to call it. But the issue with Cli parsing... Let me think.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: Since the umbrella dispatches via subcommands, and the TUI is the default role, when the umbrella calls `dsx_tui::run()`, the args might be:\n- `[\"dsx\"]` (no args, umbrella default) \n- `[\"dsx\", \"--list-sessions\"]` (with flags)\n- `[\"dsx\", \"tui\", \"--list-sessions\"]` (with explicit subcommand + flags, but umbrella strips the subcommand)\n\nWait, in my umbrella design, when the user runs `dsx --list-sessions`, the umbrella sees role=None, matches default `_ =>`, and calls `dsx_tui::run()`. The argv is `[\"dsx\", \"--list-sessions\"]`. Cli parses this correctly.\n\nWhen the user runs `dsx tui --list-sessions`, the umbrella sees role=\"tui\", matches default, calls `dsx_tui::run()`. The argv is `[\"dsx\", \"tui\", \"--list-sessions\"]`. Cli sees \"tui\" as an unexpected positional arg and errors.\n\nSo the umbrella needs to strip argv[1] when dispatching to a subcommand. I can modify env args or use `parse_from`.\n\nFor the TUI's run function, I'll accept the role stripping:\n\n```rust\npub fn run() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // Strip subcommand prefix if present (used by umbrella binary)\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\n    let offset = if args.get(1).map_or(false, |a| !a.starts_with('-')) { 2 } else { 1 };\n    let cli = Cli::parse_from(\n        std::env::args().take(1).chain(std::env::args().skip(offset))\n    );\n    run_impl(cli)\n}\n```\n\nBut `Cli` is defined in main.rs... Let me just move it to lib.rs.\n\nLet me create a function `run_impl(cli: Cli)` in lib.rs and have `run()` parse args with role stripping.\n\nWait, I'll keep it simple. I'll add Cargo.toml for the umbrella crate, then update everything.\n\nLet me:\n1. Add run function for dsx-tui\n2. Create umbrella crate\n3. Update spawning code\n4. Build and test","signature":"f64ac9f4-fd26-438c-a99e-9a68acab8f8f"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":540,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":160128,"output_tokens":1580,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fc1e43a6-899c-412e-badb-4db48f67aab0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:43:15.167Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
