{"parentUuid":"c060251a-b7bb-41bc-8726-31e7e11c0e0a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"c11a42b8-f5f3-4248-947a-0fd79b1268e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`cross` install is running in background. This will take a while.\n\nLet me try yet another approach in the meantime — maybe there's a simpler way to get a statically linked binary without the C++ compilation:\n\n1. Check if `esaxx-rs` can be avoided by using different features\n2. Or try pre-building the C++ dependency\n\nActually, let me take a step back. The user asked for \"静态链接\" (static linking). A binary that's statically linked means it has no external library dependencies. The musl target achieves this.\n\nBut there's another approach: **static-pie binary**. Using `RUSTFLAGS=\"-C target-feature=+crt-static -C relocation-model=pie\"` should work for the gnu target without the proc-macro issue.\n\nWait, the issue with `+crt-static` was that proc-macro crates don't support it. Let me try a different approach:\n\n```bash\ncargo build --release -p dsx --config 'target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.rustflags=[\"-C\", \"target-feature=+crt-static\"]'\n```\n\nOr use a `.cargo/config.toml` with target-specific flags that exclude proc-macros.\n\nActually, this is a well-known issue. The solution is to build with a cargo config that applies `+crt-static` only to non-proc-macro targets:\n\n```toml\n# .cargo/config.toml\n[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\nrustflags = [\"-C\", \"target-feature=+crt-static\"]\n```\n\nBut there's a workaround: use `cargo build --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` with the env var `RUSTFLAGS=\"-C target-feature=+crt-static\"`. The trick is to build with the `--target` flag, which disables proc-macro host-target issues.\n\nWait, I already tried `RUSTFLAGS` with the gnu target and it failed with the proc-macro error. The issue is that when you set `RUSTFLAGS`, it applies to ALL crates including proc-macros, but proc-macros need to be compiled for the HOST (not the target). So `+crt-static` tries to statically link a proc-macro library which doesn't make sense.\n\nThe fix is to use cargo's `[env]` section or build host dependencies separately:\n```\ncargo build --release -p dsx --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\nCARGO_TARGET_X86_64_UNKNOWN_LINUX_GNU_RUSTFLAGS=\"-C target-feature=+crt-static\"\n```\n\nLet me try this approach.","signature":"c11a42b8-f5f3-4248-947a-0fd79b1268e2"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":188800,"output_tokens":775,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"4a4f649f-38d4-4dd4-9a3e-8c842af74f97","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:51:06.225Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
