33.001Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/state.rs","content":"        if let Some(ref mut stdin) = self.stdin {\n            let mut line = serde_json::to_string(&frame)\n                .unwrap_or_else(|_| r#\"{\"t\":\"error\",\"message\":\"serialize failed\"}\"#.into());\n            line.push('\\n');\n            if let Err(e) = stdin.write_all(line.as_bytes()) {\n                log::warn!(\"agent: stdin write error: {}\", e);\n            }\n            if let Err(e) = stdin.flush() {\n                log::warn!(\"agent: stdin flush error: {}\", e);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Non-blocking: returns the next available Agent frame, if any.\n    pub fn try_recv(&self) -> Option<AgentFrame> {\n        self.frame_rx.try_recv().ok()\n    }\n\n    /// Drain all available frames (non-blocking).\n    pub fn drain_frames(&self) -> Vec<AgentFrame> {\n        let mut frames = Vec::new();\n        while let Ok(frame) = self.frame_rx.try_recv() {\n            frames.push(frame);\n        }\n        frames\n    }\n\n    /// Read-only access to config.\n    pub fn config(&self) -> &Config {\n        &self.config\n    }\n\n    /// Mutable config access (for slash commands that modify settings).\n    pub fn config_mut(&mut self) -> &mut Config {\n        &mut self.config\n    }\n\n    /// Forward config updates to the Agent subprocess.\n    pub fn send_config_update(&mut self) {\n        self.send_frame(TuiFrame::ModeChange {\n            mode: format!(\"config/{}\", self.config.model),\n        });\n    }\n\n    /// Shutdown the Agent subprocess gracefully.\n    pub fn shutdown(&mut self) {\n        self.send_frame(TuiFrame::Shutdown);\n        if let Some(mut child) = self.child.take() {\n            let _ = child.wait();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Drop for AgentConnection {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        self.send_frame(TuiFrame::Shutdown);\n        if let Some(mut child) = self.child.take() {\n            let _ = child.wait();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ─── StreamBuffer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/// Accumulates streaming content from the Agent.\n///\n/// Owned by the event loop; provides the source of truth for all\n/// in-progress streaming output displayed by the render layer.\npub(crate) struct StreamBuffer {\n    pub content: String,\n    pub reasoning: String,\n    pub tool_progress: Vec<(String, String)>,\n    pub cancelled: bool,\n    pub last_activity: Instant,\n    /// Accumulated reasoning insights extracted during streaming\n    pub reasoning_insights: Vec<String>,\n}\n\nimpl StreamBuffer {\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            content: String::new(),\n            reasoning: String::new(),\n            tool_progress: Vec::new(),\n            cancelled: false,\n            last_activity: Instant::now(),\n            reasoning_insights: Vec::new(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Reset all streaming state for a new response.\n    pub fn clear(&mut self) {\n        self.content.clear();\n        self.reasoning.clear();\n        self.tool_progress.clear();\n        self.cancelled = false;\n        self.last_activity = Instant::now();\n    }\n\n    /// Apply an Agent StreamPayload frame to the buffer.","numLines":100,"startLine":200,"totalLines":595}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"321fdf5b-89a4-4b62-be4a-c7f3a40ad882","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"a695bced-b8f5-49af-a74d-95e70506d340","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"c796e8de-1984-4896-9ce1-149521fcbc57","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. The TUI architecture has:\n1. `AgentConnection` — IPC layer (spawns agent, sends/receives JSON-LP)\n2. `StreamBuffer` — streaming state\n3. `App` — full UI state with ContextAssembler, but uses stubs\n\nThe challenge: `App` uses stubbed ContextAssembler, config, etc. In the 5-process architecture, the real ContextAssembler is in dsx-agent, not in the TUI.\n\nThere are two approaches:\n\n**Approach A: Simplify App to be just display state**\n- Remove ContextAssembler from App\n- Messages come from AgentConnection as AgentFrame events\n- App just tracks what to display\n- Cleaner architecture but more refactoring\n\n**Approach B: Use App as-is with stubs**\n- Keep ContextAssembler stub as is (it's a thin wrapper)\n- When streaming responses, messages arrive from AgentConnection\n- The stub ContextAssembler is a placeholder, doesn't need to be functional\n- Less refactoring, works with IPC architecture\n\nActually, looking at the `App` struct more carefully, it has `ctx: ContextAssembler` and `messages: Vec<Message>`. In the IPC architecture, the TUI doesn't own the conversation — the agent does. The TUI just displays messages received from the agent.\n\nFor the simplest working ratatui TUI, I need:\n1. Simplified AppUI state (display messages, input, scroll, mode)\n2. AgentConnection for IPC\n3. StreamBuffer for streaming\n4. Event loop: poll keyboard + poll agent frames → update state → render\n\nLet me create a minimal but functional ratatui setup. I'll:\n1. Create a simple event loop in `run_impl()` that replaces the readline loop\n2. Use crossterm for terminal management\n3. Use ratatui for rendering\n4. Show messages in a scrollable chat panel\n5. Use AgentConnection for agent communication\n\nActually, the `App` struct in `app.rs` is massive (80+ fields). Let me simplify by creating a minimal UI state. Or better yet, let me use the existing `App` but strip it down.\n\nLooking at the code more carefully, the `App` struct has:\n- ContextAssembler, messages, streaming state\n- Config, health, memory\n- Tool tracking, phase detection\n- UI state (input, scroll, mode)\n\nFor the IPC architecture, many of these fields should be removed (memory, health, ctx, etc.) since they live in dsx-agent. But that's a lot of refactoring.\n\nLet me take the practical approach: create a new lightweight `AppUi` struct that's purely UI state. The event loop is:\n1. Init: start AgentConnection, terminal, ratatui\n2. Loop:\n   a. Poll keyboard events (crossterm)\n   b. Poll AgentConnection frames\n   c. Update UI state (messages, streaming)\n   d. Render with ratatui\n3. On quit: shutdown cleanly\n\nFor rendering, I'll use ratatui with:\n- A chat panel (scrollable message list)\n- An input box\n- A status bar\n\nLet me also look at the existing render modules to see what's there.","signature":"c796e8de-1984-4896-9ce1-149521fcbc57"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":207232,"output_tokens":873,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"62e37b86-9761-4012-9268-b16cfe44d7a2","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:00:43.027Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
