{"parentUuid":"de45795f-3f1e-4358-beaf-321ba8a3d245","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"580e08fe-f25c-425b-af09-e8c37d8eae55","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. The architecture is already well-designed:\n\n1. **`AppState`** (state.rs) — pure UI state (~25 fields, no agent logic)\n2. **`StreamBuffer`** (state.rs) — streaming content accumulator\n3. **`AgentConnection`** (state.rs) — IPC layer to agent subprocess\n4. **`RenderContext`** (state.rs) — snapshot assembled once per render cycle\n5. **Render modules** (render/) — ratatui rendering\n6. **Input modules** (input/) — keyboard input handling\n\nThe `App` struct in `app.rs` is the old monolithic state — it's NOT what we need. The new architecture uses `AppState` in `state.rs`.\n\nThe challenge: `AgentConnection` uses `TuiFrame`/`AgentFrame` enums for IPC. But our current agent main.rs uses a different frame format. Let me check:\n\nCurrent agent frame format:\n- TUI → Agent: `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}`\n- Agent → TUI: `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}` and `{\"type\":\"done\"}`\n\nBut `AgentConnection` sends `TuiFrame` (serde-tagged with `\"t\"` field) and receives `AgentFrame` (serde-tagged with `\"t\"` field). \n\n`TuiFrame` has `#[serde(tag = \"t\")]`, so `TuiFrame::UserInput { text: \"hello\", tools_enabled: true }` serializes to `{\"t\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\",\"tools_enabled\":true}`.\n\nBut the agent expects `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}` — different field name for the tag!\n\nThere's a mismatch between the TUI's frame format and the agent's frame format. I'd need to either:\n1. Fix the TUI's frame format to match what the agent expects\n2. Or fix the agent to understand the TUI's format\n\nThe simplest approach: fix the TUI's `TuiFrame` to use `\"type\"` instead of `\"t\"` as the tag, and fix the field names to match what the agent sends/receives.\n\nActually, let me look at what the agent currently sends and what AgentFrame expects:\n\nAgentFrame:\n- `StreamPayload { delta, reasoning, tool_progress }` → `{\"t\":\"payload\",\"delta\":\"...\",\"reasoning\":...,\"tool_progress\":[...]}`\n- `StreamDone { usage }` → `{\"t\":\"done\",\"usage\":...}`\n- `StreamError { message }` → `{\"t\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}`\n\nBut the agent currently sends:\n- `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}`\n- `{\"type\":\"done\"}`\n- `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}`\n\nThese don't match AT ALL. The agent sends flat JSON-LP, but AgentFrame expects serde-tagged enums.\n\nThis means I need to either:\n1. Change the agent to send AgentFrame-format frames\n2. Change AgentFrame to match what the agent sends\n3. Or create a translation layer\n\nOption 1 is the cleanest: make the agent communicate using the `AgentFrame` format. But the agent is a general-purpose IPC process — it should be format-agnostic. Actually, the agent is OUR process, so we control the format.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the current agent's communication is:\n```\nAgent → TUI: {\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"...\"} / {\"type\":\"done\"} / {\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}\nTUI → Agent: {\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"...\"} / {\"type\":\"shutdown\"}\n```\n\nAnd `AgentFrame`/`TuiFrame` use serde tag `\"t\"` with different variant names.\n\nThe simplest path: update the agent's runner.rs to use the `AgentFrame` / `TuiFrame` format. But that requires importing those types or matching their serialization format.\n\nActually, even simpler: change `TuiFrame` and `AgentFrame` to use `\"type\"` as the tag and match the agent's format. Then the existing `AgentConnection` code will work with the agent's current output.\n\nLet me think about what changes:\n\n**TuiFrame** (what TUI sends to agent):\n- `UserInput` → `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"...\",\"tools_enabled\":true}` — currently has tag `\"t\"`, needs `\"type\"`. Field: `text` matches what agent expects.\n- `Shutdown` → `{\"type\":\"shutdown\"}` — matches\n\n**AgentFrame** (what TUI receives from agent):\n- `StreamPayload` → but agent sends `api_response` not `payload`\n- `StreamDone` → but agent sends `{\"type\":\"done\"}` — matches variant name! But what content?\n- `StreamError` → agent sends `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}` — matches variant name!\n\nCurrently the agent sends:\n- Response: `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}`\n- Done: `{\"type\":\"done\"}`\n- Error: `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}`\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Change `TuiFrame` tag from `\"t\"` to `\"type\"`\n2. Change `AgentFrame` tag from `\"t\"` to `\"type\"`\n3. Fix `StreamPayload` to match the agent's response format\n\nActually wait, looking at this from a different angle. The `AgentConnection::try_recv()` receives `AgentFrame` via serde deserialization. If the agent sends `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}`, but `AgentFrame` has variant `StreamPayload { delta, reasoning, tool_progress }`, they won't match.\n\nI need to either:\nA. Change the agent to send AgentFrame-format frames\nB. Change AgentFrame to match what the agent sends  \nC. Use raw JSON (not typed enums) and parse manually\n\nFor simplicity, let me go with option A: **change the agent to send/receive frames in the format that AgentConnection/TuiFrame expect**.\n\nBut that means modifying the agent runner.rs to use different frame formats. Let me update both sides:\n\n1. Update `TuiFrame` to serialize with `\"type\"` tag\n2. Update the agent runner.rs to deserialize `TuiFrame` and serialize `AgentFrame`\n3. This way, the agent becomes a proper IPC server that understands the TUI's protocol\n\nActually, there's an even simpler path: since the agent currently uses simple JSON matching (`frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_input\\\"\")`), I can just update the TUI frame format to match what the agent currently expects, and update AgentFrame to deserialize what the agent sends.\n\nLet me do option B since it requires fewer changes to the agent (which is already working):\n1. Change `TuiFrame` tag from `\"t\"` to `\"type\"`\n2. Fix variant serialization names to match agent's expectations\n3. Change `AgentFrame` tag from `\"t\"` to `\"type\"`\n4. Fix variant deserialization names to match what agent sends\n5. Handle the content field mapping\n\nWait, but the agent's current frame format is different from what AgentFrame expects. The agent sends `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"...\"}` but AgentFrame expects streaming events like `StreamPayload`. \n\nFor the minimal viable ratatui TUI, let me take a pragmatic approach:\n\n**Just make the TUI event loop work, using raw JSON-LP (the current format) initially. Then iterate.**\n\nActually, I think the right approach is:\n\n1. Update `TuiFrame` to use `\"type\"` tag and match agent's current expectations\n2. Update `AgentFrame` to deserialize from the agent's current output format\n3. Build the ratatui event loop\n\nFor `AgentFrame`, the agent currently sends:\n- `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}` → map to `AgentFrame` variant for content\n- `{\"type\":\"done\"}` → map to `AgentFrame::StreamDone`\n- `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}` → map to `AgentFrame::StreamError`\n\nLet me just update `AgentFrame` to match:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(tag = \"type\")]\npub(crate) enum AgentFrame {\n    #[serde(rename = \"api_response\")]\n    StreamPayload {\n        content: String,\n        #[serde(default)]\n        reasoning: Option<String>,\n    },\n    #[serde(rename = \"done\")]\n    StreamDone,\n    #[serde(rename = \"error\")]\n    StreamError {\n        message: String,\n    },\n    #[serde(rename = \"shutdown_ack\")]\n    ShutdownAck,\n}\n```\n\nAnd `TuiFrame`:\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize)]\n#[serde(tag = \"type\")]\npub(crate) enum TuiFrame {\n    #[serde(rename = \"user_input\")]\n    UserInput { text: String },\n    #[serde(rename = \"shutdown\")]\n    Shutdown,\n}\n```\n\nWait, but the TUI's `AgentConnection::send_frame` uses `TuiFrame` with `\"t\"` tag. If I change the tag to `\"type\"`, the serialized JSON will match what the agent expects. But I also need to remove `tools_enabled` since the agent doesn't expect that field in the user_input frame.\n\nActually, looking at the agent's main loop, it checks `frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_input\\\"\")`. If TuiFrame serializes to `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"hello\"}`, the agent will match it as user_input. But then the agent's `handle_user_input` function extracts `text` from the frame — and the TUI sends `text` field. So this should work.\n\nLet me also check: does the agent currently send `api_response` with `content` field? Yes: `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}`.\n\nFor AgentFrame deserialization, the field is `content`, not `delta`. But `StreamBuffer::apply_payload` takes `delta`. Let me adjust.\n\nOK, I think the simplest approach is:\n\n1. Fix `TuiFrame` and `AgentFrame` serialization to match the agent's protocol\n2. Replace the readline loop in `run_impl()` with the ratatui event loop\n3. The event loop uses `crossterm` for keyboard, `ratatui` for render, `AgentConnection` for IPC\n\nLet me now implement this. The key file to change is `dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (the `run_impl()` function) and the frame serialization in `state.rs`.\n\nLet me now write the full implementation. I'll:\n\n1. Update `TuiFrame` in state.rs to use \"type\" tag\n2. Update `AgentFrame` in state.rs to match agent's output\n3. Rewrite `run_impl()` in lib.rs with the ratatui event loop\n4. Add InputAction handling for keyboard events\n\nThis is a significant rewrite but it's what the user asked for.\n\nLet me plan the event loop:\n\n```rust\nfn run_tui() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    ensure_hp_running();\n    \n    // Setup terminal\n    let mut terminal = ratatui::init();\n    \n    // Setup agent connection\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe()?;\n    let agent_bin = if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n        exe.to_str().map(|s| s.to_string())\n    } else {\n        exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-agent\").to_str().map(|s| s.to_string())\n    };\n    \n    let config = Config::load()?;\n    let mut conn = AgentConnection::spawn(agent_bin.as_deref(), config.clone())?;\n    let mut state = AppState::new(Mode::Normal);\n    let mut stream = StreamBuffer::new();\n    \n    // Main loop\n    loop {\n        // Poll keyboard\n        if let Some(action) = poll_input()? {\n            match action {\n                InputAction::Quit => break,\n                InputAction::Submit(text) => {\n                    // Send to agent\n                    conn.send_frame(TuiFrame::UserInput { text: text.clone() });\n                    state.push_message(Message::user(&text));\n                    stream.clear();\n                }\n                InputAction::ScrollUp => state.scroll_offset += 1,\n                InputAction::ScrollDown => state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(1),\n                // ... more actions\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Poll agent frames\n        for frame in conn.drain_frames() {\n            match frame {\n                AgentFrame::StreamPayload { content, reasoning } => {\n                    stream.apply_payload(&content, reasoning.as_deref(), &[]);\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamDone { .. } => {\n                    let msg = stream.to_message();\n                    state.push_message(msg);\n                    stream.clear();\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamError { message } => {\n                    state.status_msg = message;\n                    stream.clear();\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Render\n        terminal.draw(|f| {\n            let ctx = RenderContext::from_parts(&state, &stream, &conn);\n            render_main(f, ctx);\n        })?;\n        \n        // Throttle\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(16)); // ~60fps\n    }\n    \n    // Cleanup\n    ratatui::restore();\n    conn.shutdown();\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\nBut I need `poll_input()` which uses crossterm. Let me check the input modules.","signature":"580e08fe-f25c-425b-af09-e8c37d8eae55"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2703,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":209408,"output_tokens":3210,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"760f86c1-75fb-49f2-9de7-20f58ab96415","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:01:20.516Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
