{"parentUuid":"7b5ee086-a967-4551-8223-e5937b3a03bd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"a766d544-0386-4a79-b9ba-1f3802263dea","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture. The TUI stubs are already in place for all the agent-side modules (Config, ContextAssembler, health, session, etc.). The `AgentConnection` takes a `Config` from these stubs.\n\nNow I need to replace the readline `run_impl()` with a proper ratatui event loop. Let me plan the exact changes:\n\n1. **Fix `TuiFrame` and `AgentFrame` in `state.rs`** — change serde tag from `\"t\"` to `\"type\"`, fix field names to match what the agent sends/receives\n\n2. **Rewrite `run_impl()` in `lib.rs`** — replace readline loop with ratatui event loop:\n   - Init terminal (crossterm + ratatui)\n   - Init AgentConnection\n   - Init AppState + StreamBuffer\n   - Main loop: poll keyboard → poll agent frames → render\n   - Clean shutdown\n\nThe event loop will use:\n- `crossterm::event::poll()` for non-blocking keyboard polling\n- `handle_chat_key()` for chat input handling\n- `AgentConnection::drain_frames()` for agent responses\n- `StreamBuffer` for streaming content\n- `ratatui::Terminal::draw()` for rendering\n\nLet me now write the code. I'll focus on getting the event loop working with basic chat and streaming display.\n\nFor `TuiFrame` and `AgentFrame`, I need to match the agent's wire format. The current agent:\n- Receives: `{\"type\":\"user_input\",\"text\":\"...\"}`\n- Sends: `{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"...\"}` or `{\"type\":\"done\"}` or `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}`\n\nSo I'll update:\n- `TuiFrame` to serialize with `#[serde(tag = \"type\")]` \n- `AgentFrame` to deserialize with `#[serde(tag = \"type\")]` and match the agent's variants\n\nBut there's a complication: the TUI's input handler produces `InputAction`s like `SendMessage(text)`. I need to map these to `TuiFrame`s.\n\nAlso, the streaming: when the agent sends `api_response`, content is streamed. But the agent currently sends the FULL response at once (non-streaming), followed by `done`. So there's no incremental streaming — but that's OK for now, we can add it later.\n\nLet me write the implementation.\n\nActually, thinking about this more carefully, I realize the `run_impl()` function needs to be completely rewritten. The current version handles agent IPC directly (creating child, reading/writing frames). The new version should use `AgentConnection` which already encapsulates this.\n\nBut wait — `AgentConnection::spawn()` takes `agent_bin: Option<&str>`. In the current readline version, we pass the raw binary path. In the ratatui version, we'll use AgentConnection.\n\nLet me write the new `run_impl()`:\n\n```rust\nfn run_impl(cli: Cli) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    ensure_hp_running();\n    \n    // Determine agent binary path\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe()?;\n    let agent_bin = if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n        exe.to_str().map(|s| s.to_string())\n    } else {\n        exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-agent\").to_str().map(|s| s.to_string())\n    };\n    \n    // Load config\n    let config = stubs::config::Config::load()?;\n    \n    // Spawn agent\n    let mut conn = AgentConnection::spawn(agent_bin.as_deref(), config)?;\n    let mut state = AppState::new(Mode::Chat);\n    let mut stream = StreamBuffer::new();\n    \n    // Setup terminal\n    crossterm::terminal::enable_raw_mode()?;\n    let mut stdout = std::io::stdout();\n    crossterm::execute!(stdout, crossterm::terminal::EnterAlternateScreen)?;\n    let mut terminal = ratatui::Terminal::new(ratatui::backend::CrosstermBackend::new(stdout))?;\n    \n    // Commands list for slash menu\n    let commands: Vec<(String, String)> = vec![\n        (\"/quit\".into(), \"Exit DSX\".into()),\n        (\"/exit\".into(), \"Exit DSX\".into()),\n        (\"/model\".into(), \"Switch model\".into()),\n        (\"/effort\".into(), \"Set reasoning effort\".into()),\n        (\"/lang\".into(), \"Change language\".into()),\n    ];\n    \n    // Main event loop\n    let res = loop {\n        // Poll keyboard (non-blocking, 16ms timeout = ~60fps)\n        if crossterm::event::poll(std::time::Duration::from_millis(16))? {\n            let event = crossterm::event::read()?;\n            match event {\n                crossterm::event::Event::Key(key) => {\n                    let action = handle_chat_key(&mut state.input_state, key, &commands);\n                    match action {\n                        InputAction::SendMessage(text) => {\n                            if !text.is_empty() {\n                                state.push_message(Message::user(&text));\n                                conn.send_frame(TuiFrame::UserInput { text: text.clone(), tools_enabled: true });\n                                stream.clear();\n                                state.mode = Mode::Streaming;\n                            }\n                        }\n                        InputAction::None => {}\n                        _ => {} // TODO: handle more actions\n                    }\n                }\n                crossterm::event::Event::Resize(_, _) => {}\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Poll agent frames\n        for frame in conn.drain_frames() {\n            match frame {\n                AgentFrame::StreamPayload { content, reasoning, tool_progress } => {\n                    stream.apply_payload(&content, reasoning.as_deref(), &tool_progress);\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamDone { usage } => {\n                    let msg = stream.to_message();\n                    state.push_message(msg);\n                    state.api_usage = usage;\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.status_msg.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamError { message } => {\n                    state.status_msg = message;\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Check for quit condition\n        if state.input_state.exit_prompt {\n            // TODO: handle exit\n        }\n        \n        // Render\n        terminal.draw(|f| {\n            let ctx = RenderContext::from_parts(&state, &stream, &conn);\n            render::main::render_main(f, ctx);\n        })?;\n    };\n    \n    // Cleanup\n    terminal.clear()?;\n    crossterm::execute!(std::io::stdout(), crossterm::terminal::LeaveAlternateScreen)?;\n    crossterm::terminal::disable_raw_mode()?;\n    conn.shutdown();\n    \n    res\n}\n```\n\nWait, I need to check what `render::main::render_main` looks like. Let me check the render module.\n\nAlso, I need to handle the `InputAction::None` case — this is returned by most key presses (typing characters). The `InputAction::None` just means \"key was consumed but no app-level effect needed\" — the state is already updated by `handle_chat_key()`.\n\nFor the quit action, `handle_chat_key` returns `InputAction::None` for Esc key. There's no explicit `Quit` action in `InputAction`. The user would type `/quit` in the chat buffer and press Enter, which sends it as a message. The agent would handle it as a shutdown command... but wait, in the current readline version, `/quit` is handled locally (sends shutdown frame and breaks the loop). In the ratatui version, `/quit` needs to be handled too.\n\nFor the minimal version, I'll handle `/quit` and `/exit` as text commands in the input: when the user sends `/quit` or `/exit`, break the loop.\n\nLet me also check the render module for the main render function.","signature":"a766d544-0386-4a79-b9ba-1f3802263dea"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2579,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":221952,"outpu