\n\nfn run_event_loop(\n    terminal: &mut ratatui::Terminal<ratatui::backend::CrosstermBackend<std::io::Stdout>>,\n    conn: &mut AgentConnection,\n    state: &mut AppState,\n    stream: &mut StreamBuffer,\n    commands: &[(String, String)],\n) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    loop {\n        // Poll keyboard (16ms = ~60fps)\n        if crossterm::event::poll(std::time::Duration::from_millis(16))? {\n            let event = crossterm::event::read()?;\n            if let crossterm::event::Event::Key(key) = event {\n                let action = handle_chat_key(&mut state.input_state, key, commands);\n                match action {\n                    InputAction::SendMessage(text) => {\n                        let trimmed = text.trim().to_string();\n                        if trimmed.is_empty() { continue; }\n                        \n                        // Check for local commands\n                        if trimmed == \"/quit\" || trimmed == \"/exit\" {\n                            return Ok(());\n                        }\n                        \n                        // Send to agent\n                        state.push_message(Message::user(&trimmed));\n                        conn.send_frame(TuiFrame::UserInput { text: trimmed });\n                        stream.clear();\n                        state.mode = Mode::Streaming;\n                    }\n                    _ => {}\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Poll agent frames\n        for frame in conn.drain_frames() {\n            match frame {\n                AgentFrame::StreamPayload { content } => {\n                    stream.apply_payload(&content, None, &[]);\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamDone => {\n                    let msg = stream.to_message();\n                    state.push_message(msg);\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamError { message } => {\n                    state.status_msg = message;\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::ShutdownAck => {\n                    return Ok(());\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Render\n        terminal.draw(|f| {\n            render_all(f, state, conn, stream);\n        })?;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait, but `handle_chat_key` is async-free and modifies `state.input_state` in-place. It returns `InputAction`. The `InputAction::SendMessage` carries the text to send.\n\nBut there's an issue: `handle_chat_key` expects `state: &mut InputState`, not `&mut AppState`. And `AppState` has `input_state: InputState`. So I need to pass `&mut state.input_state`.\n\nAlso, `InputAction::None` means the key was consumed (e.g., typing a character). No app-level action needed.\n\nFor the quit flow: when user types `/quit` and presses Enter, `handle_chat_key` returns `InputAction::SendMessage(\"/quit\")`. The event loop detects the `/quit` prefix and breaks.\n\nLet me also handle Ctrl+C and Ctrl+D for quitting.\n\nActually, I also need to handle more actions from `handle_chat_key`. For example:\n- `InputAction::ScrollUp(n)` → `state.scroll_offset += n`\n- `InputAction::ScrollDown(n)` → `state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(n)`\n\nLet me add these.\n\nAlso, I need to think about what happens when stream is active (mode = Streaming). During streaming, the user should still be able to type, but pressing Enter would send a new message while the agent is still responding. This is a design choice — for now, I'll just accept new messages and append them.\n\nLet me also handle the `render_all` function — it takes `(&mut Frame, &AppState, &AgentConnection, &StreamBuffer)`.\n\nOne potential issue: `terminal.draw()` takes a closure that borrows `state`, `conn`, `stream`. But `terminal.draw()` borrows `self` (terminal) mutably, and I also borrow `state`,