{"parentUuid":"7449abfb-8d84-4a45-ad7a-7572112be280","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"d4042207-0c07-492f-afb6-c9a5b15dde66","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issues are:\n\n1. **CPU 100%**: The loop has no throttle when poll returns immediately. `poll(16ms)` might always return true in some terminals (Mouse events, focus events, etc.), causing the loop to spin at max speed.\n\n2. **Can't type**: The `_ => {}` catch-all for keyboard events handles `InputAction::None` quietly. But the state IS updated by `handle_chat_key` before it returns `None`. So the input buffer should be updating but the user doesn't see it? Or maybe the render isn't showing the input properly?\n\nWait, let me think again. The user said \"无法输入任何字段\" — \"can't type any field\". This means pressing keys does nothing. The most likely cause:\n\nThe `crossterm` event system might not be properly initialized. In some terminal environments, `event::poll()` and `event::read()` don't work without calling `crossterm::terminal::enable_raw_mode()` (which we do) AND potentially having an event reader initialized.\n\nActually, I think I know the issue. `crossterm::event::poll()` and `event::read()` work with stdin. But in raw mode, the terminal might be in a special state. Some implementations need to use `crossterm::event::read()` in a loop.\n\nWait, I just realized there might be a simpler issue. When `poll()` returns `true` but `read()` returns an event type we don't handle (like `Event::Mouse` or `Event::FocusGained`), we fall into the `_ => {}` catch-all. If the terminal is constantly sending these events, the loop never sleeps (poll returns immediately) but also doesn't process keyboard events meaningfully.\n\nBut even with `_ => {}`, the keyboard events SHOULD still be processed — when a key IS pressed, `read()` returns `Event::Key(key)` and we process it.\n\nThe real problem is likely the CPU spin preventing timely rendering. If the loop is spinning at 100%, the render might not show updates.\n\nLet me make two changes:\n1. Add a mandatory sleep (16ms) in each loop iteration, regardless of poll\n2. Also poll with a shorter timeout and throttle unconditionally\n\nActually, let me just make the loop properly throttled:\n\n```rust\nloop {\n    // Throttle: never spin faster than ~60fps even if poll spuriously returns\n    let poll_start = std::time::Instant::now();\n    \n    if crossterm::event::poll(std::time::Duration::from_millis(10))? {\n        if let Event::Key(key) = crossterm::event::read()? {\n            // handle key\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Agent frames\n    for frame in conn.drain_frames() { ... }\n    \n    // Render\n    terminal.draw(...)?;\n    \n    // Ensure minimum frame time to prevent CPU spinning\n    let elapsed = poll_start.elapsed();\n    if elapsed < std::time::Duration::from_millis(16) {\n        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(16) - elapsed);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n1. The loop runs at most ~60fps (16ms per iteration)\n2. Even if poll() returns immediately, we sleep to throttle\n3. The render only happens once per throttle tick\n\nThis should fix the CPU 100% issue.\n\nFor the typing issue, let me also add `crossterm::event::PushKeyboardEnhancementFlags` or some other keyboard setup. Actually, the simplest is to just make sure the event handling works.\n\nWait, I think I may have found another issue. Looking at the code:\n\n```rust\nEvent::Key(key) => {\n    // Ctrl+C / Ctrl+D to quit\n    if key.code == KeyCode::Char('c') && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL\n        || key.code == KeyCode::Char('d') && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL\n    {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n\n    let action = crate::input::chat::handle_chat_key(\n        &mut state.input_state,\n        key,\n        commands,\n    );\n    use crate::input::action::InputAction;\n    match action {\n```\n\nThere's no issue in the code that would prevent typing. `handle_chat_key` is called for every Key event, and for typing characters, it returns `InputAction::None` after updating the buffer.\n\nUnless... `handle_chat_key` is not being called at all because `poll()` is blocking or returning events that aren't keyboard events.\n\nActually, I think the CPU issue IS the typing issue. If the loop is spinning at 100% CPU, the terminal might not process keyboard events correctly (the OS might throttle input). So fixing the CPU spin should fix both.\n\nLet me apply the fix.","signature":"d4042207-0c07-492f-afb6-c9a5b15dde66"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":247424,"output_tokens":2610,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"32e7903f-32ed-40a4-9245-1051ef32c6e3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:12:22.207Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"32e7903f-32ed-40a4-9245-1051ef32c6e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"d4042207-0c07-492f-afb6-c9a5b15dde66","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_QsqbEbCt34DYO5SvNT7c0593","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs","old_string":"/// Main ratatui event loop: poll keyboard → handle input → poll agent → render.\nfn event_loop(\n    terminal: &mut ratatui::Terminal<ratatui::backend::CrosstermBackend<std::io::Stdout>>,\n    conn: &mut AgentConnection,\n    state: &mut AppState,\n    stream: &mut StreamBuffer,\n    commands: &[(String, String)],\n) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    use crossterm::event::{Event, KeyCode, KeyModifiers};\n\n    loop {\n        // ── Poll keyboard ──\n        if crossterm::event::poll(std::time::Duration::from_millis(16))? {\n            match crossterm::event::read()? {\n                Event::Key(key) => {\n                    // Ctrl+C / Ctrl+D to quit\n                    if key.code == KeyCode::Char('c') && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL\n                        || key.code == KeyCode::Char('d') && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL\n                    {\n                        return Ok(());\n                    }\n\n                    let action = crate::input::chat::handle_chat_key(\n                        &mut state.input_state,\n                        key,\n                        commands,\n                    );\n                    use crate::input::action::InputAction;\n                    match action {\n                        InputAction::SendMessage(text) => {\n                            let trimmed = text.trim().to_string();\n                            if trimmed.is_empty() {\n                                continue;\n                            }\n                            // Local commands\n                            if trimmed == \"/quit\" || trimmed == \"/exit\" {\n                                return Ok(());\n                            }\n                            // Send to agent\n                            state.push_message(Message::user(&trimmed));\n                            conn.send_frame(TuiFrame::UserInput { text: trimmed });\n                            stream.clear();\n                            state.mode = Mode::Streaming;\n                        }\n                        InputAction::ScrollUp(n) => {\n                            state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_add(n);\n                            state.auto_scroll = false;\n                        }\n                        InputAction::ScrollDown(n) => {\n                            state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(n);\n                        }\n                        _ => {}\n                    }\n                }\n                Event::Resize(w, h) => {\n                    let _ = (w, h);\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ── Poll agent frames ──\n        for frame in conn.drain_frames() {\n            match frame {\n                AgentFrame::StreamPayload { content } => {\n                    stream.apply_payload(&content, None, &[]);\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamDone => {\n                    let msg = stream.to_message();\n                    state.push_message(msg);\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamError { message } => {\n                    state.status_msg = message;\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::ShutdownAck => {\n                    return Ok(());\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ── Render ──\n        terminal.draw(|f| {\n            crate::render::render_all(f, state, conn, stream);\n        })?;\n    }\n}","new_string":"/// Main ratatui event loop: poll keyboard → handle input → poll agent → render.\nfn event_loop(\n    terminal: &mut ratatui::Terminal<ratatui::backend::CrosstermBackend<std::io::Stdout>>,\n    conn: &mut AgentConnection,\n    state: &mut AppState,\n    stream: &mut StreamBuffer,\n    commands: &[(String, String)],\n) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    use crossterm::event::{Event, KeyCode, KeyModifiers};\n    use crate::input::action::InputAction;\n\n    // Initialize event polling\n    let _ = crossterm::event::read(); // drain any buffered events\n\n    loop {\n        let frame_start = std::time::Instant::now();\n\n        // ── Poll keyboard ──\n        if crossterm::event::poll(std::time::Duration::from_millis(10))? {\n            match crossterm::event::read()? {\n                Event::Key(key) => {\n                    // Ctrl+C / Ctrl+D to quit\n                    if (key.code == KeyCode::Char('c') || key.code == KeyCode::Char('d'))\n                        && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL\n                    {\n                        return Ok(());\n                    }\n\n                    let action = handle_chat_key(\n                        &mut state.input_state,\n                        key,\n                        commands,\n                    );\n                    match action {\n                        InputAction::SendMessage(text) => {\n                            let trimmed = text.trim().to_string();\n                            if !trimmed.is_empty() {\n                                // Local commands\n                                if trimmed == \"/quit\" || trimmed == \"/exit\" {\n                                    return Ok(());\n                                }\n                                // Send to agent\n                                state.push_message(Message::user(&trimmed));\n                                conn.send_frame(TuiFrame::UserInput { text: trimmed });\n                                stream.clear();\n                                state.mode = Mode::Streaming;\n                            }\n                        }\n                        InputAction::ScrollUp(n) => {\n                            state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_add(n);\n                            state.auto_scroll = false;\n                        }\n                        InputAction::ScrollDown(n) => {\n                            state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(n);\n                        }\n                        _ => {}\n                    }\n                }\n                Event::Resize(w, h) => {\n                    let _ = (w, h);\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ── Poll agent frames ──\n        for frame in conn.drain_frames() {\n            match frame {\n                AgentFrame::StreamPayload { content } => {\n                    stream.apply_payload(&content, None, &[]);\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamDone => {\n                    let msg = stream.to_message();\n                    state.push_message(msg);\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::StreamError { message } => {\n                    state.status_msg = message;\n                    stream.clear();\n                    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n                }\n                AgentFrame::ShutdownAck => {\n                    return Ok(());\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ── Render ──\n        terminal.draw(|f| {\n            crate::render::render_all(f, state, conn, stream);\n        })?;\n\n        // ── Throttle: ensure at most ~60fps, prevents CPU spin ──\n        let elapsed = frame_start.elapsed();\n        let min_frame = std::time::Duration::from_millis(16);\n        if elapsed < min_frame {\n            std::thread::sleep(min_frame - elapsed);\n        }\n    }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":247424,"output_tokens":2610,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"0fa55a4b-49b7-480b-9d76-6da891e7812f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:12:30.557Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
