{"parentUuid":"25e2f46f-3a25-4935-88bd-fb6940dc6634","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"cd34f892-2f77-43f1-8271-0d1cc96721ec","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The agent received the user input, but the HP returned \"HP not configured (no API key)\". This means:\n\n1. The agent is running and processing frames ✅\n2. The agent sent an api_chat request to HP ✅\n3. HP responded with an error about no API key ❌\n\nThe HP's `handle_api_chat` function checks `HP_CONFIG.get()` which needs `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` to be set. Looking at the HP's startup:\n\n```rust\nlet hp_cfg = Config {\n    base_url: std::env::var(\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\")\n        .unwrap_or_else(|_| \"https://api.deepseek.com\".into()),\n    api_key: std::env::var(\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\")\n        .unwrap_or_default(),\n};\nif hp_cfg.api_key.is_empty() {\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: WARNING — no ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN set, api_chat will fail\");\n} else {\n    HP_CONFIG.set(hp_cfg).ok();\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: API proxy configured...\");\n}\n```\n\nSo if `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` is not set in the environment when HP starts, the HP will have no API key.\n\nBut the user has used DSX before and it worked. The issue is that when the TUI starts HP via `ensure_hp_running()`, it uses `Command::new(...).stdout(Stdio::null()).stderr(Stdio::null()).spawn()`. This inherits the environment from the parent, which should include `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`.\n\nBut wait — does the user's shell environment actually have `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` set? Let me check. The user is running in Konsole. The environment might be different from when they run Claude Code.\n\nActually, the `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` is set in `/home/qaqtamsy/.claude/settings.json`:\n```json\n\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\": \"[REDACTED-DEEPSEEK_SK]\",\n```\n\nThis is set for Claude Code's environment. When the user runs `./dsx` from Konsole, this environment variable might NOT be set in the shell. Claude Code sets it internally, not in the user's shell.\n\nSo the HP starts but has no API key! The agent connects to HP, sends an api_chat request, and HP responds with \"HP not configured (no API key)\".\n\nThis also explains the memory issue! When the agent sends an api_chat request and gets an error, `handle_user_input` returns after writing the error to the TUI. The TUI reads the error and displays it. If there's a tight loop somewhere (like the TUI retrying or the agent respawning), the error messages would pile up and fill memory.\n\nOK, but even with the error, the agent processes each user_input once. One error per input. No infinite loop.\n\nWait, but earlier without --readline, the issue was \"memory fills up WITHOUT typing\". In ratatui mode, if the TUI starts and auto-sends something, or if the render is creating frames that loop back to the agent...\n\nActually, I think the \"memory without input\" issue might be related to not having the API key. If the HP has no API key, what happens when the TUI starts up? The agent connects to HP, sends api_chat for... what? The TUI doesn't send any user_input until the user types. So the agent just waits.\n\nUnless... the agent's `handle_user_input` is being called with an empty string or init message?\n\nNo, looking at the agent code, it only calls `handle_user_input` when frame contains `\"type\":\"user_input\"`. And the TUI only sends user_input when the user presses Enter.\n\nLet me focus on what's actionable: the user needs `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` set in their shell when running DSX. Or DSX needs to read it from the Claude Code config file.\n\nFor now, let me tell the user to set the env var. Also, the good news is that the `--readline` pipe IS working — the agent → HP → TUI chain is functioning. The only issue is the API key.\n\nLet me also add reading the API key from the Claude Code settings file as a fallback.","signature":"cd34f892-2f77-43f1-8271-0d1cc96721ec"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"