{"parentUuid":"36bee84e-dd6c-40a8-98e4-3ce7dab120ab","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"61ae3d6c-0718-4b18-8da9-33adc0f0d7f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"我感觉不是渲染出了问题。这样，守护进程/HP有监测agents的断点吗？或者HP能不能直接监测主进程或TUI进程？"},"uuid":"359fd92e-7f38-4c6e-9b54-0055c281b62c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:46:55.368Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"359fd92e-7f38-4c6e-9b54-0055c281b62c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"994b757a-4898-4232-9095-bde4167aa6a9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about the HP's monitoring capabilities. Let me think about what the HP daemon does:\n\n1. Process registration (register/heartbeat/unregister)\n2. Health judgment pipeline (judge)\n3. API proxy (api_chat)\n\nThe HP tracks processes by their `uid` and `kind` (Tui, Agent, Tools). It currently only tracks processes that register with it and send heartbeats.\n\nBut the current flow is:\n- HP registers itself\n- Agent registers with HP at startup\n- Host TUI process doesn't register with HP (only the Agent does)\n\nSo the HP knows about the agent process (and its tools subprocess) but NOT the TUI process itself.\n\nThe user is asking: can HP monitor the TUI process? Or more generally, can HP detect if something is wrong with the whole system?\n\nThis is actually the purpose of the HP's process registry and heartbeat system! The HP can:\n1. Track all processes (TUI, agent, tools) with heartbeats\n2. Detect when a process stops sending heartbeats (stale/dead)\n3. Potentially restart crashed processes\n\nBut currently:\n- Only the HP itself and the Agent register with HP\n- The TUI doesn't register (it's the one that spawns the agent, not directly connected to HP)\n- There's no automatic restart mechanism for crashed processes\n\nThe user seems to want to know if the HP can monitor the system health to detect the CPU/memory issue. The answer is: it CAN track processes via heartbeats, but currently only the agent registers. The TUI doesn't register.\n\nBut the more fundamental issue is: the HP is a health MONITOR, not a profiler. It can detect \"process X stopped sending heartbeats\" but can't tell \"process X is using 100% CPU.\"\n\nActually, I think the user is asking something different. They're saying: \"does HP have monitoring/breakpoints for agents? Or can HP directly monitor the main process/TUI process?\" \n\nThe HP tracks processes that register with it. It has heartbeat monitoring but not CPU/memory profiling.\n\nBut maybe they're thinking: could the CPU/memory issue be coming from the HP or the agent processes? And they want HP to self-diagnose or monitor itself?\n\nLet me think about this from a different angle. The user has identified:\n- `--readline` works fine (no CPU/memory issue)\n- Regular mode (ratatui + crossterm) has the issue\n- They're saying it's NOT a rendering issue\n\nSo the issue is specifically with crossterm. And they're asking if HP can help diagnose.\n\nActually, I think the user's real question is more practical. They want to know:\n1. Does HP have any diagnostic capability to identify why CPU/memory spikes?\n2. Can HP monitor the system's health to discover the TUI process?\n\nThe HP tracks processes via explicit registration and heartbeats. It doesn't do system-level profiling (CPU, memory). To monitor the TUI process, the TUI would need to register with HP and send heartbeats. But currently it doesn't.\n\nHowever, the HP does have a `judge()` function that runs a health assessment pipeline. It produces verdicts about process health. If processes miss heartbeats, the HP can detect that.\n\nI should explain the HP's monitoring capabilities clearly and suggest a practical approach: either add TUI registration to HP, or use system tools (top, ps) to identify the rogue process.","signature":"994b757a-4898-4232-9095-bde4167aa6a9"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":321024,"output_tokens":948,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"4618d07e-e6f3-473a-a781-6742eda8a45b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:47:06.878Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"4618d07e-e6f3-473a-a781-6742eda8a45b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"994b757a-4898-4232-9095-bde4167aa6a9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"HP 的监控能力有限：\n- 它只追踪**主动注册**的进程（目前只有 agent 注册了自己）\n- 通过心跳检测进程是否活着\n- **不能**检测 CPU/内存占用，不能采样性能\n\n你能跑一下这个看看是哪个进程在吃资源吗：\n\n```bash\nps aux --sort=-%cpu | grep dsx | head -5\n```\n\n这样就知道是 dsx（TUI）、dsx-agent、dsx-hp、dsx-tools 哪个在烧 CPU。\n\n不过换个思路——你说不是渲染，那很明确是 **crossterm::event**。`--readline` 用了同样的 agent/hp/tools 管道却完全没问题。区别只在于关掉 ratatui 的同时也关掉了 crossterm 的事件系统。\n\n要不要试试：**保留 ratatui 渲染，但不通过 crossterm::event 读键盘，改用简单的 stdin 线程？** 这样渲染在，事件系统绕开。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":321024,"output_tokens":948,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"cf165330-ba46-408a-8431-861c0a725269","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:47:09.844Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
