{"parentUuid":"e3739185-5bde-4f10-b214-5c11cbdb6b94","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dd88f82d-1b12-496b-9e03-797e1451f328","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"就没了，TUI也没有。cpu和内存没啥问题"},"uuid":"6e31213d-1c36-470b-b1ab-3d69ca387521","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:58:06.022Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"6e31213d-1c36-470b-b1ab-3d69ca387521","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"3c3944b7-ac50-468a-a77b-0b74d4c70cff","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `--demo` mode:\n1. Agent started and connected to HP and tools ✅\n2. CPU/memory fine ✅\n3. But ratatui TUI didn't show - just the stderr messages on terminal, no alternate screen rendering\n\nThis means the ratatui init probably failed silently. The stderr messages are from the agent (inherited stderr). But the TUI should have entered alternate screen mode and started rendering.\n\nWait - the TUI DID run the `--demo` code path. It printed \"dsx-tui: agent started (pid=...)\" somewhere? No, I removed that in the current code. But the agent's stderr messages are showing because the agent inherits stderr from the TUI.\n\nThe issue is that the terminal is showing agent stderr messages on top of where the TUI should be rendering. Maybe:\n1. The `terminal.clear()` failed\n2. Or the alternate screen wasn't entered properly\n3. Or the agent's stderr output corrupted the terminal\n\nBut the user said \"TUI也没有\" - no TUI display. And CPU/memory are fine. This means the TUI DID start (we see agent stderr), but the alternate screen didn't show properly.\n\nWait - this might be a race condition. The agent prints \"dsx-agent starting\" to stderr. But in raw mode, these prints might interfere with the terminal rendering.\n\nActually, the key issue: the TUI's `crossterm::terminal::enable_raw_mode()` might be competing with the inherited agent stderr. When the agent writes to stderr, it goes to the same terminal that's in raw mode. Raw mode means newlines don't cause carriage returns, etc. The agent's output would corrupt the display.\n\nThis is actually the same as the readline mode - the agent's stderr shows on the terminal. But in readline mode, the terminal isn't in raw mode, so the output is fine.\n\nHmm, but in the regular ratatui mode (not --demo), the agent's stderr ALSO goes to the terminal via `Stdio::inherit()`. So this should be the same.\n\nLet me think... actually, the `--demo` mode output just shows the agent stderr messages. This means:\n1. Terminal raw mode was entered (otherwise the messages would look different)\n2. But the alternate screen wasn't properly set up\n3. The render loop didn't draw anything visible\n\nMaybe the issue is that `terminal.clear()` was called after `execute!(EnterAlternateScreen)`, which should work. But then the event loop's first draw also clears. The agent's stderr messages would be printed BEFORE the terminal setup (during AgentConnection::spawn etc.), not after.\n\nWait, looking at the code flow:\n```rust\n// 1. Create stub connection\nlet mut conn = AgentConnection::spawn(None, config)?;\n\n// 2. Spawn agent directly\nlet mut child = Command::new(&agent_bin).arg(\"agent\")...\n// AGENT PRINTS TO STDERR HERE\n\n// 3. Terminal setup\ncrossterm::terminal::enable_raw_mode()?;\ncrossterm::execute!(EnterAlternateScreen, Hide)?;\n\n// 4. Event loop\n```\n\nThe agent spawns (step 2) and starts printing to stderr (inherited). THEN terminal setup (step 3) enters raw mode. By the time the terminal is in alternate screen, the agent's messages have already been printed to the normal terminal. The alternate screen should be clean.\n\nBut in the user's output, the messages appear AFTER the alternate screen should have been entered. This is strange.\n\nUnless the terminal setup is FAILING but not returning an error. `enable_raw_mode()` and `execute!` could fail on some terminals. But the code uses `?`, so errors would propagate.\n\nActually, maybe the issue is simpler. The user sees the agent messages BECAUSE the terminal is in raw mode. In raw mode, output from the agent's stderr (which goes to the same terminal) gets displayed without normal terminal processing. The messages appear on top of the alternate screen.\n\nBut the alternate screen should be separate from the normal screen. In raw mode, writes to stdout go to the alternate screen. But agent's stderr also goes to the alternate screen (it's the same terminal).\n\nSo the alternate screen IS showing, but the agent's stderr messages are ALSO appearing on it (because stderr is inherited). The agent prints to stderr, which goes to the terminal, which is the alternate screen.\n\nThe fix: redirect agent's stderr to a file or null, not inherit. Or silence the agent's startup messages.\n\nBut wait - the regular `--readline` mode has the same configuration (agent stderr inherit) and it works fine with no corruption. The difference is that readline mode doesn't use raw mode, so the stderr output is properly handled by the terminal.\n\nIn raw mode, when the agent writes `dsx-agent starting\\n` to stderr, the `\\n` doesn't cause a carriage return. So the cursor goes to the next line (newline) but stays at the current column (no carriage return). This causes the display to \"staircase\" down.\n\nThis might be what's happening. The TUI IS rendering, but the agent's stderr output corrupts the raw mode display.\n\nActually, you know what, in the --demo mode, `conn.shutdown()` is called in the cleanup. But `conn.shutdown()` sends `TuiFrame::Shutdown` to the AGENT PROCESS THAT WAS SPAWNED BY `--demo`. But `conn` is a STUB connection (spawned with None). So `conn.shutdown()` does nothing (stdin is None).\n\nThis means the agent process is never sent a shutdown! It keeps running, waiting for input on stdin.\n\nThe user's output shows the agent starting messages. Then the TUI should start rendering. But the user says no TUI display. Maybe the TUI IS rendering but the agent's stderr messages are on top.\n\nLet me ask the user: is the screen completely blank/terminal, or can they see the alternate screen with messages on top? And does keyboard work?\n\nActually, I think the user's output tells me: they see the stderr messages and nothing else. The TUI is probably not rendering because of the issue with agent_reader.read_line() blocking the render loop.\n\nLooking at the --demo event loop:\n```rust\n// Agent frames: read one line\nloop {\n    let mut line = String::new();\n    match agent_reader.read_line(&mut line) {\n```\n\nThis inner loop blocks on `read_line()`! If the agent hasn't sent a response (it's waiting for user input), `read_line()` blocks. The entire event loop blocks, never rendering.\n\nThis is the bug. I'm reading from agent_reader in a blocking way inside the render loop. The agent hasn't sent anything because no user_input was sent yet. The read blocks.\n\nFix: make the agent read non-blocking. I need to check if there's data available before reading.\n\nIn Rust, I can't easily do non-blocking reads on a BufReader. I need to use the file descriptor directly. One approach: set the fd to non-blocking mode.\n\nLet me just change the agent reading to use `std::io::stdin().lock()` or check for available bytes.\n\nActually, the simplest fix for this specific test: only try to read agent responses AFTER we've sent a message. Before sending, skip the agent reading.","signature":"3c3944b7-ac50-468a-a77b-0b74d4c70cff"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":338560,"output_tokens":2313,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b904238a-a243-4400-b666-45cd360b1767","timestamp":"2026-05-15T04:58:25.449Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
