{"parentUuid":"d299fc0b-ccee-4774-92f5-818c5f91383f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"8a96861e-a805-45dc-844f-cda8a25eb483","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user says \"基本恢复\" (basically restored) and wants me to continue adding other features. They mentioned earlier wanting tool calling, session persistence, etc. Let me ask what specific feature they want next, or should I just start with tool calling since that's the most impactful?\n\nActually, they said \"先接入其他的功能\" - connect other features. Let me start with the most impactful one: tool calling. But this requires changes in both HP and agent. Let me plan this properly.\n\nActually wait - the user said \"之后再扫尾\" (clean up later). So they want me to restore multiple features now and clean up later. Let me focus on:\n\n1. Tool calling (most impactful)\n2. Slash menu fix (the `/` menu popup)\n\nFor the slash menu, the issue is:\n- User types `/` → menu opens ✓ (handled by handle_chat_key)\n- User continues typing `/lang` → menu filters ✓\n- User presses Enter → SendMessage(\"/lang zh\") → our new code handles it locally ✓\n- But the issue is that the slash menu navigation (arrows, Enter to select) should work too\n\nActually, the slash menu IS handled by `handle_chat_key` - it handles arrow keys for navigation, Enter to select, etc. When the user selects an item, the buffer is set to `\"/lang \"` and the user can continue typing. This should work.\n\nThe original issue was that when Enter is pressed with a slash command in the buffer, it gets sent to the agent instead of handled locally. Our fix addresses that.\n\nLet me focus on tool calling. This is the most complex feature to restore.\n\nFor tool calling, I need to:\n\n1. **HP side**: Modify `handle_api_chat()` to return tool_calls in the response\n2. **Agent side**: Add tool calling loop in `handle_user_input()`\n3. **TUI side**: Display tool calls and results in the chat\n\nLet me