{"parentUuid":"91e1132a-9b68-4e35-aa56-96a70df04807","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"da41ca5b-fc83-4b48-8a52-eda0139f3f14","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I need to update the agent's `handle_user_input` to handle tool_calls in the response. The flow should be:\n\n1. Send api_chat to HP\n2. Get response with possible tool_calls\n3. If tool_calls present:\n   a. Forward to tools process\n   b. Get results\n   c. Build new conversation with tool results\n   d. Send new api_chat to HP\n   e. Go back to step 2\n4. If no tool_calls: forward response to TUI\n\nBut wait — the agent's `handle_user_input` function receives the HP response synchronously (one frame sent, one frame received). The `handle_user_input` is called from the main loop's match on `user_input`.\n\nFor the tool calling loop, I need to:\n1. Send api_chat to HP\n2. Read response\n3. If tool_calls: \n   a. Forward `tool_call_req` to tools\n   b. Read tool result\n   c. Build updated conversation\n   d. Send new api_chat\n   e. Read response\n   f. Loop\n4. Send final response to TUI\n\nThis means I can't use the current `handle_user_input` which sends one api_chat and reads one response. I need a loop.\n\nActually, looking at the current code, `handle_user_input` already sends one api_chat and reads one response. I just need to add a loop after reading the response:\n\n```rust\n// After reading the first HP response\nif resp has tool_calls {\n    loop {\n        // Forward tool_calls to tools\n        for tc in tool_calls {\n            write tools frame\n            read tools result\n        }\n        // Build new api_chat with tool results\n        send api_chat to HP\n        read response\n        if no tool_calls { break; }\n    }\n}\n// Send final response to TUI\nwrite_frame(tui_writer, &final_resp);\n```\n\nThe tricky part is building the conversation for subsequent rounds. I need to append:\n- Assistant message with tool_calls\n- User message with tool_results\n\nThen the next api_chat request sends the full conversation.\n\nLet me also look at how the tools process expects tool calls. Looking at the IPC protocol in dsx-tools:\n\n```rust\nInboundFrame::CallReq { id, name, action, args, timeout_secs }\n```\n\nThe agent needs to send `tool_call_req` frames to the tools process. But the current agent main loop already handles forwarding tool_call frames from TUI to tools:\n\n```rust\nif frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\"\") {\n    write_frame(&mut tools_writer, &frame);\n    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(&mut tools_reader) {\n        write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp);\n    }\n    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n}\n```\n\nFor agent-driven tool calling (not TUI-driven), the agent directly sends to tools and reads results, without going through TUI.\n\nThe tool_call_req format:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_call_req\",\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"read\",\"action\":\"read\",\"args\":{\"path\":\"...\"},\"timeout_secs\":30}\n```\n\nAnd the response from tools:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"id\":\"...\",\"success\":true,\"content\":\"...\"}\n```\n\nOK, let me now modify the agent's `handle_user_input` to support tool calling.\n\nActually, the modification is significant. Let me rewrite the function to have a tool-calling loop. I'll modify the conversation building too.\n\nActually, I think the cleanest approach is to:\n1. Build the initial api_chat with the user message\n2. Send to HP\n3. Read response\n4. If tool_calls in response:\n   a. Forward each to tools\n   b. Collect results\n   c. Append tool calls and results to conversation\n   d. Send new api_chat\n   e. Read response\n   f. Loop back to 4\n5. Send final response to TUI\n\nThe conversation for the second round needs to be:\n```\n[\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"original user message\"},\n  {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"I'll read that file\", \"tool_calls\": [...]},\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"tool_result content\"}\n]\n```\n\nBut the HP's `handle_api_chat` currently only handles `{role, content}` messages. I need to also handle `{role, content, tool_calls}` and `{role, content_with_tool_results}`.\n\nThe HP converts messages to AnthropicMessage using a filter_map. I need to extend it to handle tool-related content.\n\nActually, let me extend the HP's message conversion to handle tool_calls and tool_results. For tool_calls, the assistant message has `tool_calls` field. For tool_results, we need a separate message format.\n\nLet me think about the conversation format for tool rounds:\n\nRound 1:\n```json\n{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"read file foo.txt\"}\n```\n→ HP calls API → response has tool_calls\n\nRound 2 conversation:\n```json\n[\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"read file foo.txt\"},\n  {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"\", \"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"tu1\", \"name\": \"read\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"foo.txt\\\"}\"}]},\n  {\"role\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_call_id\": \"tu1\", \"content\": \"file contents\"}\n]\n```\n→ HP calls API → response could be final content\n\nFor the HP, I need to add handling for:\n1. Messages with `tool_calls` → convert to AnthropicContent::ToolUse\n2. Messages with `tool_call_id` → convert to AnthropicContent::ToolResult\n\nLet me update `handle_api_chat` in HP to handle these.\n\nActually, looking at the existing code, the message conversion in `handle_api_chat` is:\n```rust\nlet blocks = if let Some(text) = content.as_str() {\n    vec![AnthropicContent::Text { text: text.to_string() }]\n} else if let Some(arr) = content.as_array() {\n    serde_json::from_value(content.clone()).ok()?\n} else {\n    return None;\n};\n```\n\nThe `else if let Some(arr)` branch handles array content — if the content is an array of AnthropicContent blocks, it deserializes directly. This is the path for complex content with tool uses and tool results.\n\nSo if I