{"parentUuid":"4fa642a5-3ea6-4991-927c-96e29f6e41ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"02170392-7a89-4447-b13c-f855599f5a3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to update both the function signature and the call site. Let me rewrite `handle_user_input` to include tools support. This is going to be a significant rewrite.\n\nThe new flow:\n1. Extract user text\n2. Add to conversation\n3. Loop:\n   a. Build api_chat with conversation\n   b. Send to HP\n   c. Read HP response\n   d. If error → break, forward error\n   e. If has tool_calls:\n      - Save assistant message with tool_calls to conversation\n      - Forward each tool_call to tools\n      - Read tool result for each\n      - Add tool_result to conversation\n      - Continue loop (next api_chat will include tool results)\n   f. If no tool_calls → break, forward final response\n4. Send done\n\nFor the conversation, between rounds I need to add:\n1. Assistant response with tool_calls\n2. Tool results (as separate tool_result role messages)\n\nThe next api_chat request sends the full conversation including these.\n\nLet me implement this now. I'll also need to import the tools IPC types. The tools process uses JSON-LP with specific frame formats. Let me check what the tool_call_req frame format is.\n\nFrom dsx-tools/ipc.rs:\n```rust\nInboundFrame::CallReq { id, name, action, args, timeout_secs }\n```\n\nSerialized with `#[serde(tag = \"type\")]`:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_call_req\",\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"read\",\"action\":\"read\",\"args\":{...},\"timeout_secs\":30}\n```\n\nAnd the response:\n```rust\nOutboundFrame::Result { id, success, content }\n```\n\nSerialized:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"id\":\"...\",\"success\":true,\"content\":\"...\"}\n```\n\nLet me now implement the full function.","signature":"02170392-7a89-4447-b13c-f855599f5a3a"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":377344,"output_tokens":2660,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"87740cf5-09c0-48d9-9847-63ba459e16f3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:14:54.734Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"87740cf5-09c0-48d9-9847-63ba459e16f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"02170392-7a89-4447-b13c-f855599f5a3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_midjzNWhq02UAmmFzsho0719","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs","old_string":"/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n\n    // Add user message to conversation\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    // If no HP connection, fall back to echo\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Build api_chat request with full conversation\n    let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n        \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n        \"model\": read_model(),\n        \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n        \"messages\": conversation,\n    });\n\n    write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n    // Read response (one line — HP responds with a single JSON frame)\n    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(reader) {\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                }\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            _ => {\n                // Unknown response type — forward as-is\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}","new_string":"/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\n/// Supports multi-round tool calling: detects tool_calls in HP response, dispatches to\n/// tools process, sends tool results back to HP, repeats until final text response.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    tools_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    tools_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    let t_reader = match tools_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools not available, skipping tool dispatch\"); &mut BufReader::new(std::io::empty()) }\n    };\n    let t_writer = match tools_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools not available, skipping tool dispatch\"); return; }\n    };\n\n    // Tool-calling loop: up to 10 rounds to prevent infinite loops\n    for _round in 0..10 {\n        // Send api_chat with current conversation\n        let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n            \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n            \"model\": read_model(),\n            \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n            \"messages\": conversation,\n        });\n        write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n        // Read HP response\n        let resp = match read_frame(reader) {\n            Some(r) => r,\n            None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: HP connection lost\"); return; }\n        };\n\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                let has_tools = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\")\n                    .and_then(|t| t.as_array())\n                    .map(|a| !a.is_empty())\n                    .unwrap_or(false);\n\n                if !has_tools {\n                    // Final response — no more tool calls\n                    if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                    }\n                    write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                    return;\n                }\n\n                // Tool call round — save assistant message with tool_calls\n                let content = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                let tool_calls = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\").unwrap().clone();\n                conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": content,\n                    \"tool_calls\": tool_calls,\n                }));\n\n                // Forward each tool call to tools process\n                let tcs = tool_calls.as_array().unwrap().clone();\n                for tc in &tcs {\n                    let id = tc.get(\"id\").and_then(|i| i.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let name = tc.get(\"name\").and_then(|n| n.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let raw_args = tc.get(\"arguments\").and_then(|a| a.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"{}\");\n                    let args_val: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(raw_args).unwrap_or_default();\n                    let args_str = serde_json::to_string(&args_val).unwrap_or_else(|_| \"{}\".into());\n\n                    // Build tool_call_req frame (matching dsx-tools IPC protocol)\n                    let req = format!(\n                        r#\"{{\"type\":\"tool_call_req\",\"id\":\"{}\",\"name\":\"{}\",\"action\":\"{}\",\"args\":{},\"timeout_secs\":30}}\"#,\n                        id, name, name, args_str,\n                    );\n                    write_frame(t_writer, &req);\n\n                    // Read tool result\n                    if let Some(tool_resp) = read_frame(t_reader) {\n                        let tr_v: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&tool_resp).unwrap_or_default();\n                        let success = tr_v.get(\"success\").and_then(|s| s.as_bool()).unwrap_or(false);\n                        let tr_content = tr_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"error\");\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                            \"role\": \"tool_result\",\n                            \"tool_call_id\": id,\n                            \"content\": tr_content,\n                            \"is_error\": !success,\n                        }));\n                    } else {\n                        // Tools process closed — abort tool round\n                        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools process closed\");\n                        write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"tool process lost\"}}\"#));\n                        return;\n                    }\n                }\n                // Continue loop: next api_chat round includes tool results\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n            _ => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // Max rounds reached\n    write_frame(tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"exceeded max tool rounds\"}\"#);\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":377344,"output_tokens":2660,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8494545a-ef01-414a-b2dd-271f3657132c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:15:08.496Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"8494545a-ef01-414a-b2dd-271f3657132c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"348c2d62-c264-4bdd-8a72-5c551f98a6f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_midjzNWhq02UAmmFzsho0719","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"3a7c1dfa-938b-4c50-a8cd-3b655602fa11","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:15:08.567Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs","oldString":"/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n\n    // Add user message to conversation\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    // If no HP connection, fall back to echo\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Build api_chat request with full conversation\n    let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n        \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n        \"model\": read_model(),\n        \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n        \"messages\": conversation,\n    });\n\n    write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n    // Read response (one line — HP responds with a single JSON frame)\n    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(reader) {\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                }\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            _ => {\n                // Unknown response type — forward as-is\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}","newString":"/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\n/// Supports multi-round tool calling: detects tool_calls in HP response, dispatches to\n/// tools process, sends tool results back to HP, repeats until final text response.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    tools_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    tools_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    let t_reader = match tools_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools not available, skipping tool dispatch\"); &mut BufReader::new(std::io::empty()) }\n    };\n    let t_writer = match tools_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools not available, skipping tool dispatch\"); return; }\n    };\n\n    // Tool-calling loop: up to 10 rounds to prevent infinite loops\n    for _round in 0..10 {\n        // Send api_chat with current conversation\n        let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n            \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n            \"model\": read_model(),\n            \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n            \"messages\": conversation,\n        });\n        write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n        // Read HP response\n        let resp = match read_frame(reader) {\n            Some(r) => r,\n            None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: HP connection lost\"); return; }\n        };\n\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                let has_tools = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\")\n                    .and_then(|t| t.as_array())\n                    .map(|a| !a.is_empty())\n                    .unwrap_or(false);\n\n                if !has_tools {\n                    // Final response — no more tool calls\n                    if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                    }\n                    write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                    return;\n                }\n\n                // Tool call round — save assistant message with tool_calls\n                let content = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                let tool_calls = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\").unwrap().clone();\n                conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": content,\n                    \"tool_calls\": tool_calls,\n                }));\n\n                // Forward each tool call to tools process\n                let tcs = tool_calls.as_array().unwrap().clone();\n                for tc in &tcs {\n                    let id = tc.get(\"id\").and_then(|i| i.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let name = tc.get(\"name\").and_then(|n| n.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let raw_args = tc.get(\"arguments\").and_then(|a| a.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"{}\");\n                    let args_val: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(raw_args).unwrap_or_default();\n                    let args_str = serde_json::to_string(&args_val).unwrap_or_else(|_| \"{}\".into());\n\n                    // Build tool_call_req frame (matching dsx-tools IPC protocol)\n                    let req = format!(\n                        r#\"{{\"type\":\"tool_call_req\",\"id\":\"{}\",\"name\":\"{}\",\"action\":\"{}\",\"args\":{},\"timeout_secs\":30}}\"#,\n                        id, name, name, args_str,\n                    );\n                    write_frame(t_writer, &req);\n\n                    // Read tool result\n                    if let Some(tool_resp) = read_frame(t_reader) {\n                        let tr_v: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&tool_resp).unwrap_or_default();\n                        let success = tr_v.get(\"success\").and_then(|s| s.as_bool()).unwrap_or(false);\n                        let tr_content = tr_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"error\");\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                            \"role\": \"tool_result\",\n                            \"tool_call_id\": id,\n                            \"content\": tr_content,\n                            \"is_error\": !success,\n                        }));\n                    } else {\n                        // Tools process closed — abort tool round\n                        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools process closed\");\n                        write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"tool process lost\"}}\"#));\n                        return;\n                    }\n                }\n                // Continue loop: next api_chat round includes tool results\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n            _ => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // Max rounds reached\n    write_frame(tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"exceeded max tool rounds\"}\"#);\n}","originalFile":"//! dsx-agent — central process. Connects TUI ↔ Agent ↔ Tools ↔ HP.\n\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Write};\nuse std::net::TcpStream;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\n\n// ── JSON-LP helpers ──\n\nfn read_frame(reader: &mut BufReader<impl std::io::Read>) -> Option<String> {\n    let mut line = String::new();\n    reader.read_line(&mut line).ok().filter(|n| *n > 0).map(|_| line.trim().to_string())\n}\n\nfn write_frame(writer: &mut impl Write, frame: &str) {\n    let _ = writeln!(writer, \"{frame}\");\n    let _ = writer.flush();\n}\n\n// ── HP connection ──\n\nfn hp_port() -> u16 {\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    let path = std::path::PathBuf::from(home).join(\".dsx\").join(\"hp.port\");\n    std::fs::read_to_string(&path).ok().and_then(|s| s.trim().parse().ok()).unwrap_or(0)\n}\n\n// ── Conversation helpers ──\n\n/// Default system prompt for DSX.\nconst SYSTEM_PROMPT: &str = \"\\\nYou are DSX (DeepSeek X Agents), an AI-powered coding assistant running in the terminal. \\\nYou help users with software engineering tasks: writing code, debugging, refactoring, \\\nand answering technical questions. Keep responses concise and accurate.\";\n\n/// Read model name from ~/.dsx/config.json, fallback to deepseek-v4-flash.\nfn read_model() -> String {\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    let path = std::path::PathBuf::from(home).join(\".dsx\").join(\"config.json\");\n    if let Ok(data) = std::fs::read_to_string(&path) {\n        if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&data) {\n            if let Some(model) = v.get(\"model\").and_then(|m| m.as_str()) {\n                return model.to_string();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \"deepseek-v4-flash\".into()\n}\n\n/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n\n    // Add user message to conversation\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    // If no HP connection, fall back to echo\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => {\n            write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\"));\n            return;\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Build api_chat request with full conversation\n    let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n        \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n        \"model\": read_model(),\n        \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n        \"messages\": conversation,\n    });\n\n    write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n    // Read response (one line — HP responds with a single JSON frame)\n    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(reader) {\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                }\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n            _ => {\n                // Unknown response type — forward as-is\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ── HP connection helpers ──\n\n/// Connect to HP, register, and return (read_handle, write_handle).\nfn connect_hp() -> (Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>, Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>) {\n    let port = hp_port();\n    if port == 0 {\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: HP not running (no hp.port) — continuing without AI\");\n        return (None, None);\n    }\n\n    let stream = match TcpStream::connect(format!(\"127.0.0.1:{port}\")) {\n        Ok(s) => s,\n        Err(e) => {\n            eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: cannot connect HP: {e}\");\n            return (None, None);\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Register with HP\n    let pid = std::process::id();\n    let reg_frame = format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"register\",\"kind\":\"Agent\",\"name\":\"dsx-agent\",\"pid\":{pid}}}\"#);\n    let mut writer = stream.try_clone().unwrap();\n    write_frame(&mut writer, &reg_frame);\n\n    // Create reader and drain register response\n    let reader = BufReader::new(Box::new(stream.try_clone().unwrap()) as Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>);\n    // Note: We don't drain here — the handle_user_input function first reads\n    // from the HP socket, which will get the register response.\n    // Instead, we use a persistent reader that tracks position.\n    // But since BufReader is stateful, we need to flush the stale data.\n\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: connected to HP on port {port}\");\n    (Some(reader), Some(Box::new(writer) as Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>))\n}\n\n// ── Main ──\n\npub fn run() {\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent starting\");\n\n    // 1. Connect to HP — get persistent read/write handles\n    let (mut hp_reader, mut hp_writer) = connect_hp();\n\n    // Drain the register response from the HP connection\n    if let Some(ref mut r) = hp_reader {\n        let _ = read_frame(r);\n    }\n\n    // 2. Spawn dsx-tools\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().unwrap();\n    let mut tools_cmd = Command::new(\n        if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n            exe.to_path_buf()\n        } else {\n            exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-tools\")\n        }\n    );\n    if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n        tools_cmd.arg(\"tools\");\n    }\n    let mut tools_child = tools_cmd\n        .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n        .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n        .spawn()\n        .expect(\"dsx-agent: failed to spawn dsx-tools\");\n\n    let tools_stdin = tools_child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n    let tools_stdout = tools_child.stdout.take().unwrap();\n    let mut tools_reader = BufReader::new(tools_stdout);\n    let mut tools_writer = tools_stdin;\n\n    // Send Init first — tools waits for Init before sending ToolsReady\n    write_frame(&mut tools_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"tools_init\",\"allowed_tools\":[],\"session_seed\":\"pipe\",\"auto_mode\":true}\"#);\n    let ready = read_frame(&mut tools_reader).unwrap_or_default();\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools → {ready}\");\n\n    // 3. Conversation state\n    let mut conversation: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n\n    // 4. Main loop: read from TUI (stdin), forward to HP/Tools, write to TUI (stdout)\n    let stdin = std::io::stdin();\n    let mut tui_reader = BufReader::new(stdin.lock());\n    let mut tui_writer = std::io::stdout();\n\n    loop {\n        match read_frame(&mut tui_reader) {\n            Some(frame) => {\n                eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tui ← {frame}\");\n\n                if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\"\") {\n                    // Forward to Tools\n                    write_frame(&mut tools_writer, &frame);\n                    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(&mut tools_reader) {\n                        write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp);\n                    }\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_input\\\"\") {\n                    handle_user_input(&frame, &mut hp_reader, &mut hp_writer, &mut conversation, &mut tui_writer);\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\"\") {\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"shutdown_ack\"}\"#);\n                    break;\n                } else {\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"echo\",\"data\":{frame}}}\"#));\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                }\n            }\n            None => break,\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Cleanup: close tools stdin first so tools exits, THEN wait\n    drop(tools_writer);\n    let _ = tools_child.wait();\n    // Unregister from HP\n    if let Some(ref mut w) = hp_writer {\n        let frame = format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"unregister\",\"pid\":{}}}\"#, std::process::id());\n        write_frame(w, &frame);\n    }\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: shutdown complete\");\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":47,"oldLines":10,"newStart":47,"newLines":14,"lines":[" }"," "," /// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.","+/// Supports multi-round tool calling: detects tool_calls in HP response, dispatches to","+/// tools process, sends tool results back to HP, repeats until final text response."," fn handle_user_input(","     frame: &str,","     hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,","     hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,","+    tools_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,","+    tools_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,","     conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,","     tui_writer: &mut impl Write,"," ) {"]},{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":58,"