{"parentUuid":"c59e4ebd-1fac-4536-9b92-41616279208c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs","content":"//! dsx-agent — central process. Connects TUI ↔ Agent ↔ Tools ↔ HP.\n\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Write};\nuse std::net::TcpStream;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\n\n// ── JSON-LP helpers ──\n\nfn read_frame(reader: &mut impl std::io::BufRead) -> Option<String> {\n    let mut line = String::new();\n    reader.read_line(&mut line).ok().filter(|n| *n > 0).map(|_| line.trim().to_string())\n}\n\nfn write_frame(writer: &mut impl Write, frame: &str) {\n    let _ = writeln!(writer, \"{frame}\");\n    let _ = writer.flush();\n}\n\n// ── HP connection ──\n\nfn hp_port() -> u16 {\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    let path = std::path::PathBuf::from(home).join(\".dsx\").join(\"hp.port\");\n    std::fs::read_to_string(&path).ok().and_then(|s| s.trim().parse().ok()).unwrap_or(0)\n}\n\n// ── Conversation helpers ──\n\n/// Default system prompt for DSX.\nconst SYSTEM_PROMPT: &str = \"\\\nYou are DSX (DeepSeek X Agents), an AI-powered coding assistant running in the terminal. \\\nYou help users with software engineering tasks: writing code, debugging, refactoring, \\\nand answering technical questions. Keep responses concise and accurate.\";\n\n/// Read model name from ~/.dsx/config.json, fallback to deepseek-v4-flash.\nfn read_model() -> String {\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    let path = std::path::PathBuf::from(home).join(\".dsx\").join(\"config.json\");\n    if let Ok(data) = std::fs::read_to_string(&path) {\n        if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&data) {\n            if let Some(model) = v.get(\"model\").and_then(|m| m.as_str()) {\n                return model.to_string();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \"deepseek-v4-flash\".into()\n}\n\n/// Approximate token count of a JSON value.\nfn tok(val: &serde_json::Value) -> usize {\n    match val {\n        serde_json::Value::String(s) => s.len() / 4 + 1,\n        serde_json::Value::Object(m) => m.values().map(tok).sum(),\n        serde_json::Value::Array(a) => a.iter().map(tok).sum(),\n        _ => 1,\n    }\n}\nfn conv_tok(conv: &[serde_json::Value]) -> usize {\n    conv.iter().map(tok).sum()\n}\n\n/// Cache-friendly compaction: never delete messages (preserves cache prefix).\n/// Instead, truncate overly long tool_result content to ~300 chars.\n/// This keeps the message count and structure intact.\nfn compact_cache_friendly(conv: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>, limit: usize) {\n    if conv.iter().map(tok).sum::<usize>() <= limit { return; }\n    let mut trimmed = 0;\n\n    // Phase 1: truncate large tool_result content\n    for i in 0..conv.len() {\n        if tok(&conv[i]) < 5000 { continue; }\n        if conv[i].get(\"role\").and_then(|r| r.as_str()) != Some(\"tool_result\") { continue; }\n        if let Some(s) = conv[i].get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            if s.len() > 600 {\n                let short = format!(\"{}...[+{} bytes]\", &s[..300], s.len() - 300);\n                conv[i][\"content\"] = serde_json::json!(short);\n                trimmed += 1;\n                if conv.iter().map(tok).sum::<usize>() <= limit { return; }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Phase 2: if still over limit, truncate long assistant messages\n    for i in 0..conv.len() {\n        if tok(&conv[i]) < 5000 { continue; }\n        if conv[i].get(\"role\").and_then(|r| r.as_str()) != Some(\"assistant\") { continue; }\n        if let Some(s) = conv[i].get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            if s.len() > 600 {\n                let short = format!(\"{}...[+{} bytes]\", &s[..300], s.len() - 300);\n                conv[i][\"content\"] = serde_json::json!(short);\n                trimmed += 1;\n                if conv.iter().map(tok).sum::<usize>() <= limit { return; }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    if trimmed > 0 {\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: compacted {} long messages\", trimmed);\n    }\n}\n\n/// Handle a user_input frame: build conversation, call HP API, forward response to TUI.\n/// Supports multi-round tool calling: detects tool_calls in HP response, dispatches to\n/// tools process, sends tool results back to HP, repeats until final text response.\nfn handle_user_input(\n    frame: &str,\n    hp_reader: &mut Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>,\n    hp_writer: &mut Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>,\n    tools_reader: &mut impl std::io::BufRead,\n    tools_writer: &mut impl std::io::Write,\n    conversation: &mut Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n    tui_writer: &mut impl Write,\n) {\n    // Extract user text from frame\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(frame) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(_) => { let _ = writeln!(tui_writer, \"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"error\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"invalid frame\\\"}}\"); return; }\n    };\n    let text = match v.get(\"text\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n        Some(t) if !t.is_empty() => t,\n        _ => return,\n    };\n    conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}));\n\n    let reader = match hp_reader {\n        Some(r) => r,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    let writer = match hp_writer {\n        Some(w) => w,\n        None => { write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"echo\\\",\\\"data\\\":{frame}}}\")); return; }\n    };\n    // Tool-calling loop: up to 10 rounds to prevent infinite loops\n    for _round in 0..10 {\n        // Compact conversation if approaching context limit (~200K tokens ≈ 800K chars)\n        compact_cache_friendly(conversation, 200_000);\n\n        // Send api_chat with current conversation\n        let chat_req = serde_json::json!({\n            \"type\": \"api_chat\",\n            \"model\": read_model(),\n            \"system\": SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n            \"messages\": conversation,\n        });\n        write_frame(writer, &chat_req.to_string());\n\n        // Read HP response\n        let resp = match read_frame(reader) {\n            Some(r) => r,\n            None => { eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: HP connection lost\"); return; }\n        };\n\n        let resp_v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(&resp) {\n            Ok(v) => v,\n            Err(_) => { write_frame(tui_writer, &resp); return; }\n        };\n\n        match resp_v.get(\"type\").and_then(|t| t.as_str()) {\n            Some(\"api_response\") => {\n                let has_tools = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\")\n                    .and_then(|t| t.as_array())\n                    .map(|a| !a.is_empty())\n                    .unwrap_or(false);\n\n                if !has_tools {\n                    // Final response — no more tool calls\n                    if let Some(content) = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}));\n                    }\n                    write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                    return;\n                }\n\n                // Tool call round — save assistant message with tool_calls\n                let content = resp_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                let tool_calls = resp_v.get(\"tool_calls\").unwrap().clone();\n                conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": content,\n                    \"tool_calls\": tool_calls,\n                }));\n\n                // Forward each tool call to tools process\n                let tcs = tool_calls.as_array().unwrap().clone();\n                for tc in &tcs {\n                    let id = tc.get(\"id\").and_then(|i| i.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let name = tc.get(\"name\").and_then(|n| n.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let raw_args = tc.get(\"arguments\").and_then(|a| a.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"{}\");\n                    let args_val: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(raw_args).unwrap_or_default();\n                    let args_str = serde_json::to_string(&args_val).unwrap_or_else(|_| \"{}\".into());\n\n                    // Build tool_call_req frame (matching dsx-tools IPC protocol)\n                    let req = format!(\n                        r#\"{{\"type\":\"tool_call_req\",\"id\":\"{}\",\"name\":\"{}\",\"action\":\"{}\",\"args\":{},\"timeout_secs\":30}}\"#,\n                        id, name, name, args_str,\n                    );\n                    write_frame(tools_writer, &req);\n\n                    // Read tool result\n                    if let Some(tool_resp) = read_frame(tools_reader) {\n                        let tr_v: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&tool_resp).unwrap_or_default();\n                        let success = tr_v.get(\"success\").and_then(|s| s.as_bool()).unwrap_or(false);\n                        let tr_content = tr_v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"error\");\n                        conversation.push(serde_json::json!({\n                            \"role\": \"tool_result\",\n                            \"tool_call_id\": id,\n                            \"content\": tr_content,\n                            \"is_error\": !success,\n                        }));\n                        // Compact after potentially large tool results\n                        compact_cache_friendly(conversation, 200_000);\n                    } else {\n                        // Tools process closed — abort tool round\n                        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools process closed\");\n                        write_frame(tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"tool process lost\"}}\"#));\n                        return;\n                    }\n                }\n                // Continue loop: next api_chat round includes tool results\n            }\n            Some(\"error\") => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n            _ => {\n                write_frame(tui_writer, &resp);\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // Max rounds reached\n    write_frame(tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"exceeded max tool rounds\"}\"#);\n}\n\n// ── HP connection helpers ──\n\n/// Connect to HP, register, and return (read_handle, write_handle).\nfn connect_hp() -> (Option<BufReader<Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>>>, Option<Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>>) {\n    let port = hp_port();\n    if port == 0 {\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: HP not running (no hp.port) — continuing without AI\");\n        return (None, None);\n    }\n\n    let stream = match TcpStream::connect(format!(\"127.0.0.1:{port}\")) {\n        Ok(s) => s,\n        Err(e) => {\n            eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: cannot connect HP: {e}\");\n            return (None, None);\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Register with HP\n    let pid = std::process::id();\n    let reg_frame = format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"register\",\"kind\":\"Agent\",\"name\":\"dsx-agent\",\"pid\":{pid}}}\"#);\n    let mut writer = stream.try_clone().unwrap();\n    write_frame(&mut writer, &reg_frame);\n\n    // Create reader and drain register response\n    let reader = BufReader::new(Box::new(stream.try_clone().unwrap()) as Box<dyn std::io::Read + Send>);\n    // Note: We don't drain here — the handle_user_input function first reads\n    // from the HP socket, which will get the register response.\n    // Instead, we use a persistent reader that tracks position.\n    // But since BufReader is stateful, we need to flush the stale data.\n\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: connected to HP on port {port}\");\n    (Some(reader), Some(Box::new(writer) as Box<dyn std::io::Write + Send>))\n}\n\n// ── Main ──\n\npub fn run() {\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent starting\");\n\n    // 1. Connect to HP — get persistent read/write handles\n    let (mut hp_reader, mut hp_writer) = connect_hp();\n\n    // Drain the register response from the HP connection\n    if let Some(ref mut r) = hp_reader {\n        let _ = read_frame(r);\n    }\n\n    // 2. Spawn dsx-tools\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().unwrap();\n    let mut tools_cmd = Command::new(\n        if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n            exe.to_path_buf()\n        } else {\n            exe.with_file_name(\"dsx-tools\")\n        }\n    );\n    if std::env::var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\").is_ok() {\n        tools_cmd.arg(\"tools\");\n    }\n    let mut tools_child = tools_cmd\n        .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n        .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n        .spawn()\n        .expect(\"dsx-agent: failed to spawn dsx-tools\");\n\n    let tools_stdin = tools_child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n    let tools_stdout = tools_child.stdout.take().unwrap();\n    let mut tools_reader = BufReader::new(tools_stdout);\n    let mut tools_writer = tools_stdin;\n\n    // Send Init first — tools waits for Init before sending ToolsReady\n    write_frame(&mut tools_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"tools_init\",\"allowed_tools\":[],\"session_seed\":\"pipe\",\"auto_mode\":true}\"#);\n    let ready = read_frame(&mut tools_reader).unwrap_or_default();\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tools → {ready}\");\n\n    // 3. Conversation state\n    let mut conversation: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n\n    // 4. Main loop: read from TUI (stdin), forward to HP/Tools, write to TUI (stdout)\n    let stdin = std::io::stdin();\n    let mut tui_reader = BufReader::new(stdin.lock());\n    let mut tui_writer = std::io::stdout();\n\n    loop {\n        match read_frame(&mut tui_reader) {\n            Some(frame) => {\n                eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: tui ← {frame}\");\n\n                if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\"\") {\n                    // Forward to Tools\n                    write_frame(&mut tools_writer, &frame);\n                    if let Some(resp) = read_frame(&mut tools_reader) {\n                        write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &resp);\n                    }\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_input\\\"\") {\n                    handle_user_input(&frame, &mut hp_reader, &mut hp_writer, &mut tools_reader, &mut tools_writer, &mut conversation, &mut tui_writer);\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                } else if frame.contains(\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\"\") {\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"shutdown_ack\"}\"#);\n                    break;\n                } else {\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"echo\",\"data\":{frame}}}\"#));\n                    write_frame(&mut tui_writer, r#\"{\"type\":\"done\"}\"#);\n                }\n            }\n            None => break,\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Cleanup: close tools stdin first so tools exits, THEN wait\n    drop(tools_writer);\n    let _ = tools_child.wait();\n    // Unregister from HP\n    if let Some(ref mut w) = hp_writer {\n        let frame = format!(r#\"{{\"type\":\"unregister\",\"pid\":{}}}\"#, std::process::id());\n        write_frame(w, &frame);\n    }\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-agent: shutdown complete\");\n}\n","numLines":356,"startLine":1,"totalLines":356}},"displayPath":"crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"89ace863-2dd8-488c-87c0-f52b19f186e5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:31:09.638Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"89ace863-2dd8-488c-87c0-f52b19f186e5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs","content":"//! dsx-hp — Health Platform daemon.\n//!\n//! A lightweight daemon that tracks process liveness, runs the health\n//! judgment pipeline, and exposes a `HealthProbe` service over TCP.\n//!\n//! ## IPC protocol\n//!\n//! JSON-LP frames over TCP `localhost`. Port written to\n//! `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dsx/hp.port`.\n//!\n//! ## Build\n//!\n//! This is a separate binary target. Add to `Cargo.toml`:\n//!\n//! ```toml\n//! [[bin]]\n//! name = \"dsx-hp\"\n//! path = \"src/dsx-hp/main.rs\"\n//! ```\n//!\n//! ## Startup sequence\n//!\n//! 1. Parse CLI args (port, log level).\n//! 2. Bind TCP listener on `127.0.0.1:{port}`.\n//! 3. Write port to `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dsx/hp.port`.\n//! 4. Enter accept loop — one thread per connection.\n//! 5. On SIGTERM/SIGINT: write empty port file, drain connections, exit.\n\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Write};\nuse std::net::{TcpListener, TcpStream};\nuse std::sync::{mpsc, Arc, Mutex, OnceLock};\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::time::Duration;\n\nuse crate::client;\nuse crate::config::Config;\nuse crate::ipc_traits::HealthProbe;\nuse crate::monitor;\nuse crate::pipeline::judge;\nuse crate::registry::ProcessRegistry;\nuse crate::types::{HpError, ProcessKind, Verdict};\nuse crate::StreamEvent;\nuse dsx_types::{AnthropicContent, AnthropicMessage};\n\nstatic HP_CONFIG: OnceLock<Config> = OnceLock::new();\n\n// ── Health service implementation ──\n\n/// Concrete implementation of the `HealthProbe` trait.\n///\n/// Owns the process registry and delegates pipeline judgment.\n/// Runs synchronously; the IPC layer wraps calls in async tasks.\nstruct HealthService {\n    registry: ProcessRegistry,\n}\n\nimpl HealthService {\n    fn new(timeout_secs: u64) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            registry: ProcessRegistry::new(timeout_secs),\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl HealthProbe for HealthService {\n    fn register(\n        &mut self,\n        kind: ProcessKind,\n        name: &str,\n        pid: u32,\n    ) -> Result<(), HpError> {\n        self.registry.register(kind, name, pid)\n    }\n\n    fn heartbeat(&mut self, pid: u32) -> Result<(), HpError> {\n        self.registry.heartbeat(pid)\n    }\n\n    fn unregister(&mut self, pid: u32) -> Result<(), HpError> {\n        self.registry.unregister(pid)\n    }\n\n    fn judge(&self) -> Vec<Verdict> {\n        // monitor_state is placeholder — in production the Agent\n        // pushes MonitorState updates via IPC frames.\n        let monitor_state = monitor::MonitorState::new();\n        judge(&self.registry, &monitor_state)\n    }\n\n    fn query(&self, pid: u32) -> Result<crate::types::ProcessHealth, HpError> {\n        self.registry.health(pid)\n    }\n\n    fn list_processes(&self) -> Vec<crate::types::ProcessSummary> {\n        self.registry.summaries()\n    }\n}\n\n// ── Main ──\n\n/// Load API config: ~/.dsx/config.json, with env var override.\nfn load_hp_config() -> Config {\n    // Try env vars first\n    let env_key = std::env::var(\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\").unwrap_or_default();\n    let env_url = std::env::var(\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\").unwrap_or_default();\n\n    if !env_key.is_empty() {\n        return Config {\n            base_url: if env_url.is_empty() { \"https://api.deepseek.com\".into() } else { env_url },\n            api_key: env_key,\n        };\n    }\n\n    // Fall back to ~/.dsx/config.json\n    let cfg_path = std::path::PathBuf::from(\n        std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into()),\n    ).join(\".dsx\").join(\"config.json\");\n\n    if let Ok(data) = std::fs::read_to_string(&cfg_path) {\n        if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&data) {\n            let api_key = v.get(\"api_key\").and_then(|k| k.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n            let base_url = v.get(\"base_url\").and_then(|b| b.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"https://api.deepseek.com\").to_string();\n            if !api_key.is_empty() {\n                return Config { base_url, api_key };\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    Config { base_url: \"https://api.deepseek.com\".into(), api_key: String::new() }\n}\n\npub fn run() {\n    // 0. Load API config\n    let hp_cfg = load_hp_config();\n    if hp_cfg.api_key.is_empty() {\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: WARNING — no API key configured, run 'dsx config' to set up\");\n    } else {\n        let _ = HP_CONFIG.set(hp_cfg);\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: API proxy configured\");\n    }\n\n    // 1. CLI defaults\n    let port = std::env::var(\"DSX_HP_PORT\")\n        .ok()\n        .and_then(|v| v.parse::<u16>().ok())\n        .unwrap_or(0); // 0 = OS-assigned\n\n    let timeout_secs = std::env::var(\"DSX_HP_TIMEOUT\")\n        .ok()\n        .and_then(|v| v.parse::<u64>().ok())\n        .unwrap_or(30);\n\n    let addr = format!(\"127.0.0.1:{port}\");\n\n    // 2. Bind TCP listener\n    let listener = TcpListener::bind(&addr).expect(\"dsx-hp: failed to bind TCP listener\");\n    let actual_port = listener.local_addr().unwrap().port();\n\n    // 3. Write port file\n    write_port_file(actual_port);\n    eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: listening on 127.0.0.1:{actual_port} (timeout={timeout_secs}s)\");\n\n    // 4. Create health service\n    let service = Arc::new(Mutex::new(HealthService::new(timeout_secs)));\n\n    // 5. Accept loop\n    let (_shutdown_tx, shutdown_rx) = mpsc::channel::<()>();\n\n    // Register self as the HP process\n    {\n        let mut svc = service.lock().unwrap();\n        svc.register(ProcessKind::Tui, \"dsx-hp\", std::process::id())\n            .ok();\n    }\n\n    // Heartbeat ticker — self-heartbeat every 15s\n    let svc_heartbeat = service.clone();\n    let _hb_ticker = thread::spawn(move || loop {\n        thread::sleep(Duration::from_secs(15));\n        if shutdown_rx.try_recv().is_ok() {\n            break;\n        }\n        if let Ok(mut svc) = svc_heartbeat.lock() {\n            svc.heartbeat(std::process::id()).ok();\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Signal handler (SIGINT/SIGTERM) — write empty port file, then exit\n    let svc_shutdown = service.clone();\n    let _sig_handler = thread::spawn(move || {\n        // Read from stdin or use a simpler signal handling mechanism\n        // In production, use a signal library or tokio signal.\n        // For now, Ctrl+C will kill the process and port cleanup happens\n        // via the drop handler below.\n        let _ = svc_shutdown;\n        thread::park();\n    });\n\n    // Accept connections\n    for stream in listener.incoming() {\n        match stream {\n            Ok(stream) => {\n                let svc = service.clone();\n                thread::spawn(|| handle_connection(stream, svc));\n            }\n            Err(e) => {\n                eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: accept error: {e}\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Cleanup on exit\n    clear_port_file();\n}\n\n// ── Connection handler ──\n\n/// Process a single TCP connection.\n///\n/// Reads JSON-LP frames from the stream, dispatches to `HealthProbe`,\n/// writes JSON-LP response frames.\nfn handle_connection(\n    stream: TcpStream,\n    service: Arc<Mutex<HealthService>>,\n) {\n    let peer = stream.peer_addr().ok();\n    let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream.try_clone().unwrap());\n\n    let mut buf = String::new();\n    loop {\n        buf.clear();\n        match reader.read_line(&mut buf) {\n            Ok(0) => break, // EOF\n            Ok(_) => {\n                let trimmed = buf.trim();\n                if trimmed.is_empty() {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                let response = dispatch_frame(trimmed, &service);\n                if let Ok(mut w) = stream.try_clone() {\n                    let _ = writeln!(w, \"{response}\");\n                    let _ = w.flush();\n                }\n            }\n            Err(_) => break,\n        }\n    }\n\n    if let Some(addr) = peer {\n        eprintln!(\"dsx-hp: connection closed: {addr}\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// Parse a JSON-LP frame and dispatch to the health service.\n///\n/// Frame format (JSON one-line):\n/// ```json\n/// {\"type\": \"register\", \"kind\": \"Agent\", \"name\": \"...\", \"pid\": 1234}\n/// {\"type\": \"heartbeat\", \"pid\": 1234}\n/// {\"type\": \"unregister\", \"pid\": 1234}\n/// {\"type\": \"judge\"}\n/// {\"type\": \"query\", \"pid\": 1234}\n/// {\"type\": \"list\"}\n/// {\"type\":\"api_chat\",\"model\":\"...\",\"system\":\"...\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hello\"}]}\n/// ```\nfn dispatch_frame(\n    line: &str,\n    service: &Mutex<HealthService>,\n) -> String {\n    let frame_type: String = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(line)\n        .ok()\n        .and_then(|v| v.get(\"type\").and_then(|v| v.as_str().map(String::from)))\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n\n    // api_chat doesn't need the health lock (can block for 10+s on HTTP)\n    if frame_type == \"api_chat\" {\n        return handle_api_chat(line);\n    }\n\n    let mut svc = service.lock().unwrap();\n\n    match frame_type.as_str() {\n        \"register\" => {\n            // Minimal parsing — production should use serde\n            let kind = if line.contains(\"Agent\") {\n                ProcessKind::Agent\n            } else if line.contains(\"Tools\") {\n                ProcessKind::Tools\n            } else {\n                ProcessKind::Tui\n            };\n            let pid = extract_pid(line).unwrap_or(0);\n            let name = extract_name(line).unwrap_or(\"unknown\");\n\n            match svc.register(kind, name, pid) {\n                Ok(()) => json_response(\"ok\", \"registered\"),\n                Err(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e.to_string()),\n            }\n        }\n        \"heartbeat\" => {\n            let pid = extract_pid(line).unwrap_or(0);\n            match svc.heartbeat(pid) {\n                Ok(()) => json_response(\"ok\", \"heartbeat recorded\"),\n                Err(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e.to_string()),\n            }\n        }\n        \"unregister\" => {\n            let pid = extract_pid(line).unwrap_or(0);\n            match svc.unregister(pid) {\n                Ok(()) => json_response(\"ok\", \"unregistered\"),\n                Err(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e.to_string()),\n            }\n        }\n        \"judge\" => {\n            let verdicts = svc.judge();\n            let json = serde_json::to_string(&verdicts).unwrap_or_else(|_| \"[]\".into());\n            format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"verdicts\\\",\\\"data\\\":{json}}}\")\n        }\n        \"query\" => {\n            let pid = extract_pid(line).unwrap_or(0);\n            match svc.query(pid) {\n                Ok(health) => {\n                    let data = serde_json::to_string(&health).unwrap_or_default();\n                    format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"health\\\",\\\"data\\\":{data}}}\")\n                }\n                Err(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e.to_string()),\n            }\n        }\n        \"list\" => {\n            let summaries = svc.list_processes();\n            let json = serde_json::to_string(&summaries).unwrap_or_else(|_| \"[]\".into());\n            format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"process_list\\\",\\\"data\\\":{json}}}\")\n        }\n        _ => json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"unknown frame type: {frame_type}\")),\n    }\n}\n\n// ── Helpers ──\n\nfn json_response(status: &str, message: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"{status}\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"{message}\\\"}}\")\n}\n\n/// Handle an `api_chat` frame — makes a real HTTP call to the LLM API.\n///\n/// This runs outside the health-service lock so long API calls don't\n/// block heartbeats or process registration.\nfn handle_api_chat(line: &str) -> String {\n    let config = match HP_CONFIG.get() {\n        Some(c) => c.clone(),\n        None => return json_response(\"error\", \"HP not configured (no API key)\"),\n    };\n\n    let v: serde_json::Value = match serde_json::from_str(line) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(e) => return json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"invalid api_chat frame: {e}\")),\n    };\n\n    let model = v\n        .get(\"model\")\n        .and_then(|v| v.as_str())\n        .unwrap_or(\"deepseek-v4-flash\");\n    let system = v.get(\"system\").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).map(String::from);\n\n    let messages_val = match v.get(\"messages\").and_then(|v| v.as_array()) {\n        Some(arr) => arr,\n        None => return json_response(\"error\", \"api_chat: missing messages array\"),\n    };\n\n    // Convert plain {role, content} messages to AnthropicMessage\n    let anthropic_msgs: Vec<AnthropicMessage> = messages_val\n        .iter()\n        .filter_map(|m| {\n            let role = m.get(\"role\")?.as_str()?;\n            let content = m.get(\"content\")?;\n\n            // Handle tool_calls on assistant messages\n            if let Some(tcs) = m.get(\"tool_calls\").and_then(|t| t.as_array()) {\n                let mut blocks: Vec<AnthropicContent> = Vec::new();\n                // Add text content if present\n                if let Some(text) = content.as_str() {\n                    if !text.is_empty() {\n                        blocks.push(AnthropicContent::Text { text: text.to_string() });\n                    }\n                }\n                // Add tool_use blocks\n                for tc in tcs {\n                    let id = tc.get(\"id\").and_then(|i| i.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let name = tc.get(\"name\").and_then(|n| n.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                    let args = tc.get(\"arguments\").and_then(|a| a.as_str())\n                        .and_then(|s| serde_json::from_str(s).ok())\n                        .unwrap_or(serde_json::Value::Null);\n                    blocks.push(AnthropicContent::ToolUse {\n                        id: id.to_string(),\n                        name: name.to_string(),\n                        input: args,\n                    });\n                }\n                return Some(AnthropicMessage {\n                    role: role.to_string(),\n                    content: blocks,\n                });\n            }\n\n            // Handle tool_result messages\n            if role == \"tool_result\" {\n                if let Some(tool_call_id) = m.get(\"tool_call_id\").and_then(|i| i.as_str()) {\n                    let is_error = m.get(\"is_error\").and_then(|e| e.as_bool());\n                    return Some(AnthropicMessage {\n                        role: \"user\".to_string(),\n                        content: vec![AnthropicContent::ToolResult {\n                            tool_use_id: tool_call_id.to_string(),\n                            content: content.as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_string(),\n                            is_error,\n                        }],\n                    });\n                }\n            }\n\n            let blocks = if let Some(text) = content.as_str() {\n                vec![AnthropicContent::Text {\n                    text: text.to_string(),\n                }]\n            } else if let Some(arr) = content.as_array() {\n                serde_json::from_value(content.clone()).ok()?\n            } else {\n                return None;\n            };\n            Some(AnthropicMessage {\n                role: role.to_string(),\n                content: blocks,\n            })\n        })\n        .collect();\n\n    if anthropic_msgs.is_empty() {\n        return json_response(\"error\", \"api_chat: no valid messages\");\n    }\n\n    // Create a tokio runtime for the (entirely async) HTTP client\n    let rt = match tokio::runtime::Runtime::new() {\n        Ok(r) => r,\n        Err(e) => return json_response(\"error\", &format!(\"runtime error: {e}\")),\n    };\n\n    let (content, error, tool_calls, stop_reason): (String, Option<String>, Vec<serde_json::Value>, Option<String>) = rt.block_on(async {\n        let (tx, mut rx) = tokio::sync::mpsc::channel::<StreamEvent>(64);\n        let cfg = config;\n        let model_o = model.to_string();\n        let sys = system;\n        let msgs = anthropic_msgs;\n\n        tokio::spawn(async move {\n            let _ = client::chat_stream(\n                &cfg, &model_o, sys, msgs, false, None, None, None, 8192, None, None, None, tx,\n            )\n            .await;\n        });\n\n        let mut content = String::new();\n        let mut error = None;\n        let mut tool_calls: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n        let mut stop_reason: Option<String> = None;\n        while let Some(event) = rx.recv().await {\n            match event {\n                StreamEvent::ContentDelta(delta) => content.push_str(&delta),\n                StreamEvent::Done { raw_message, stop_reason: sr, .. } => {\n                    if let Some(text) = raw_message.content {\n                        content = text;\n                    }\n                    stop_reason = sr;\n                    if let Some(tcs) = raw_message.tool_calls {\n                        for tc in tcs {\n                            tool_calls.push(serde_json::json!({\n                                \"id\": tc.id,\n                                \"name\": tc.function.name,\n                                \"arguments\": tc.function.arguments,\n                            }));\n                        }\n                    }\n                    break;\n                }\n                StreamEvent::Error(e) => {\n                    error = Some(e);\n                    break;\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n        (content, error, tool_calls, stop_reason)\n    });\n\n    match error {\n        Some(e) => json_response(\"error\", &e),\n        None => {\n            let mut resp = serde_json::json!({\n                \"type\": \"api_response\",\n                \"content\": content,\n            });\n            if !tool_calls.is_empty() {\n                resp[\"tool_calls\"] = serde_json::Value::Array(tool_calls);\n            }\n            if let Some(sr) = stop_reason {\n                resp[\"stop_reason\"] = serde_json::json!(sr);\n            }\n            serde_json::to_string(&resp).unwrap_or_else(|_| json_response(\"error\", \"serialize failed\"))\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Extract `pid` field from a JSON-LP line (simple parser, no serde).\nfn extract_pid(line: &str) -> Option<u32> {\n    // Find `\"pid\":<digits>` or `\"pid\": <digits>`\n    let after = line.split(\"\\\"pid\\\"\").nth(1)?;\n    let after_colon = after.split(':').nth(1)?;\n    let trimmed = after_colon.trim_start();\n    let digits: String = trimmed.chars().take_while(|c| c.is_ascii_digit()).collect();\n    digits.parse().ok()\n}\n\n/// Extract `name` field from a JSON-LP line (simple parser).\nfn extract_name(line: &str) -> Option<&str> {\n    // Find `\"name\":\"<text>\"` or `\"name\": \"<text>\"`\n    let after = line.split(\"\\\"name\\\"\") .nth(1)?;\n    let after_colon = after.split(':').nth(1)?;\n    let trimmed = after_colon.trim();\n    let start = trimmed.find('\"')? + 1;\n    let end = trimmed[start..].find('\"')?;\n    Some(&trimmed[start..start + end])\n}\n\n// ── Port file management ──\n\nfn port_file_path() -> std::path::PathBuf {\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    std::path::PathBuf::from(home).join(\".dsx\").join(\"hp.port\")\n}\n\nfn write_port_file(port: u16) {\n    let path = port_file_path();\n    if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {\n        let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent);\n    }\n    let _ = std::fs::write(&path, port.to_string());\n}\n\nfn clear_port_file() {\n    let _ = std::fs::write(port_file_path(), \"\");\n}\n","numLines":550,"startLine":1,"totalLines":550}},"displayPath":"crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6466ebf5-14ee-4acb-b1a6-2bdf2b6d66e1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:31:08.748Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"6466ebf5-14ee-4acb-b1a6-2bdf2b6d66e1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/src/main.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/src/main.rs","content":"//! DSX — umbrella binary. All roles in one binary.\n//!\n//! Usage:\n//!   dsx           — interactive TUI (default)\n//!   dsx hp        — health platform daemon (API proxy + process registry)\n//!   dsx agent     — agent sub-process (conversation, tools dispatch)\n//!   dsx tools     — tool execution server (sandboxed)\n//!\n//! Each role is a separate OS process for isolation and fault containment.\n//! The same binary dispatches to the right implementation based on argv[1].\n\nfn main() {\n    let _ = std::env::set_var(\"DSX_SINGLE_BINARY\", \"1\");\n\n    let role = std::env::args().nth(1).unwrap_or_default();\n    match role.as_str() {\n        \"hp\" => dsx_hp::runner::run(),\n        \"agent\" => dsx_agent::runner::run(),\n        \"tools\" => dsx_tools::run(),\n        \"config\" => run_config(),\n        _ => {\n            if let Err(e) = dsx_tui::run() {\n                eprintln!(\"dsx: TUI error: {e}\");\n                std::process::exit(1);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Interactive config setup: writes ~/.dsx/config.json\nfn run_config() {\n    use std::io::Write;\n\n    let home = std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"/tmp\".into());\n    let dir = std::path::PathBuf::from(&home).join(\".dsx\");\n    let cfg_path = dir.join(\"config.json\");\n    let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir);\n\n    // Read existing\n    let mut api_key = String::new();\n    let mut base_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com\".to_string();\n    let mut model = \"deepseek-v4-flash\".to_string();\n    if let Ok(data) = std::fs::read_to_string(&cfg_path) {\n        if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&data) {\n            api_key = v.get(\"api_key\").and_then(|k| k.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n            base_url = v.get(\"base_url\").and_then(|b| b.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"https://api.deepseek.com\").to_string();\n            model = v.get(\"model\").and_then(|m| m.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"deepseek-v4-flash\").to_string();\n        }\n    }\n\n    println!(\"DSX Configuration\");\n    println!(\"(leave blank to keep current value)\");\n    println!();\n\n    print!(\"API key [{}]: \", if api_key.is_empty() { \"(none)\" } else { \"****\" });\n    std::io::stdout().flush().ok();\n    let mut input = String::new();\n    std::io::stdin().read_line(&mut input).ok();\n    let trimmed = input.trim().to_string();\n    if !trimmed.is_empty() { api_key = trimmed; }\n\n    if api_key.is_empty() {\n        eprintln!(\"Error: API key is required\");\n        std::process::exit(1);\n    }\n\n    print!(\"Base URL [{}]: \", base_url);\n    std::io::stdout().flush().ok();\n    input.clear();\n    std::io::stdin().read_line(&mut input).ok();\n    let trimmed = input.trim().to_string();\n    if !trimmed.is_empty() { base_url = trimmed; }\n\n    print!(\"Model [{}]: \", model);\n    std::io::stdout().flush().ok();\n    input.clear();\n    std::io::stdin().read_line(&mut input).ok();\n    let trimmed = input.trim().to_string();\n    if !trimmed.is_empty() { model = trimmed; }\n\n    let config = serde_json::json!({ \"api_key\": api_key, \"base_url\": base_url, \"model\": model });\n    match std::fs::write(&cfg_path, serde_json::to_string_pretty(&config).unwrap()) {\n        Ok(_) => println!(\"Saved to {}\", cfg_path.display()),\n        Err(e) => eprintln!(\"Error saving config: {e}\"),\n    }\n}\n","numLines":87,"startLine":1,"totalLines":87}},"displayPath":"crates/dsx/src/main.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d7867ef9-150e-4d9f-8e75-d03c7bc0cbfa","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:31:08.644Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"d7867ef9-150e-4d9f-8e75-d03c7bc0cbfa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/Cargo.toml","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/Cargo.toml","content":"[package]\nname = \"dsx\"\nversion = \"4.0.0-alpha1\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[dependencies]\ndsx-hp = { path = \"../dsx-hp\" }\ndsx-agent = { path = \"../dsx-agent\" }\ndsx-tools = { path = \"../dsx-tools\" }\ndsx-tui = { path = \"../dsx-tui\" }\nserde_json = \"1\"\nanyhow = \"1\"\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}},"displayPath":"crates/dsx/Cargo.toml"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"01d0cf71-f12b-43b0-960a-f6643bdbd8fb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:31:08.645Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"01d0cf71-f12b-43b0-960a-f6643bdbd8fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"plan_file_reference","planFilePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/.claude/plans/gentle-orbiting-karp.md","planContent":"# DSX Multi-Team Collaboration Plan\n\n## Context\n\nDSX 已从单体 binary 拆分为 7 crate（5 binary + 2 shared lib），80 个原子文件已按模块分类到位。现在需要 5 支 Team（A-E）并行完成各 crate 的接口设计、模块实现和集成测试。\n\nLead（Claude Opus）负责：制定 task → 点对点分发 → 收集报告 → 汇总分析 → 等待 User 解散指令。\n\n## Team 映射\n\n| Team | Crate | 职责 | 文件 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Team A** | dsx-types + dsx-proto | 核心类型 + IPC 消息协议 | 1 (+ 新建 proto) |\n| **Team B** | dsx-hp | 健康守护进程 + API 代理网关 | 15 |\n| **Team C** | dsx-agent | Agent 核心（无界面） | 32 |\n| **Team D** | dsx-tools | 工具执行服务器（沙箱） | 13 |\n| **Team E** | dsx-tui | 终端界面（ratatui） | 19 |\n\n## 通信规则\n\n```\n                    ┌──────────┐\n                    │   LEAD   │\n                    │ (Claude) │\n                    └────┬─────┘\n           ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n    p2p     │        p2p  │  p2p         │  p2p\n     ▼      ▼         ▼   ▼   ▼          ▼   ▼\n  ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐\n  │Team A│ │Team B│ │Team C│ │Team D│ │Team E│\n  │01 02 │ │01 02 │ │01 02 │ │01 02 │ │01 02 │\n  │  03  │ │  03  │ │  03  │ │  03  │ │  03  │\n  └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘\n     ↑          ↑          ↑          ↑          ↑\n     └──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┘\n              Team 间禁止通信\n```\n\n- **Team 内**：01/02/03 可互相通信协作\n- **Team 间**：严格隔离，禁止通信\n- **Lead → Member**：点对点分发 task，不允许广播\n- **Member → Lead**：完成任务后点对点报告\n- **解散**：仅 User 有权限命令解散\n\n## Team 成员分工\n\n### Team A — dsx-types + dsx-proto（基础层，优先完成）\n\n| 成员 | 分工 | 关键文件 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A01** | 核心类型定义 | `src/dsx-types/mod.rs`：SafetyLevel, Message, ToolCall, TaskPhase, AgentPhase, DebugLevel, PersistentConfig, SessionFile |\n| **A02** | IPC 消息协议 | `src/dsx-proto/`：定义全部跨进程消息枚举（Agent→HP、Agent→Tools、HP→Agent、Tools→Agent、TUI→Agent） |\n| **A03** | 共享工具函数 | token 计数接口、序列化/反序列化辅助、错误类型定义 |\n\n### Team B — dsx-hp（健康守护 + API 网关）\n\n| 成员 | 分工 | 关键文件 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **B01** | 守护核心 | `mod.rs`, `liveness.rs`, `platform.rs`, `monitor.rs`：进程注册、心跳检测、崩溃重启、健康平台 |\n| **B02** | API 代理网关 | `client.rs`, `converter.rs`, `sentinel.rs`, `gate.rs`：API 转发、消息格式转换、错误哨兵、预检门 |\n| **B03** | 熔断 + 质量 | `circuit_breaker.rs`, `quality.rs`, `emotion.rs`, `assessment.rs`, `audit.rs`, `checks.rs`, `report.rs` |\n\n### Team C — dsx-agent（Agent 核心）\n\n| 成员 | 分工 | 关键文件 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **C01** | 编排引擎 | `orchestrator/`（12 文件）：agent_loop, stream_handler, response_processor, tool_dispatch, context_compactor, gates, learning, tracker, turn_scorer, session_persistence |\n| **C02** | 上下文 + 记忆 | `context.rs`, `conversation.rs`, `memory/`（5 文件）：ContextBuilder, ContextAssembler, 长/短/语义/陷阱记忆 |\n| **C03** | 会话 + 路由 + 技能 | `session/`（7 文件）, `router.rs`, `tokenizer.rs`, `prompt.rs`, `skills.rs`, `config.rs`, `dsc_log.rs` |\n\n### Team D — dsx-tools（工具服务器）\n\n| 成员 | 分工 | 关键文件 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **D01** | 工具框架 + 系统工具 | `mod.rs`（ToolManager）, `exec.rs`, `explore.rs`, `git.rs`, `web.rs` |\n| **D02** | 文件 + 元数据工具 | `file.rs`, `meta.rs`, `agent.rs`：文件读写编辑搜索、技能/文件元数据、统一 agent 分发 |\n| **D03** | 任务/计划/记忆工具 | `task.rs`, `plan.rs`, `memory.rs`, `ask.rs`, `status.rs` |\n\n### Team E — dsx-tui（终端界面）\n\n| 成员 | 分工 | 关键文件 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **E01** | 应用核心 | `main.rs`, `mod.rs`, `app.rs`, `commands.rs`, `mode.rs`：事件循环、状态管理、斜杠命令、模式切换 |\n| **E02** | 输入处理 | `input/`（5 文件）, `utils.rs`, `tui_text.rs`：聊天输入、确认/选择器/sudo 模式 |\n| **E03** | 渲染引擎 | `render/`（7 文件）：聊天面板、输入框、弹窗、状态栏、工具预览、工作区面板 |\n\n## Task 执行流程\n\n```\nPhase 0: Lead 创建 5 Team + 15 Member（TeamCreate）\nPhase 1: Lead 点对点发送 task 给 A01-A03（Team A 优先）\n         → A 完成后各成员报告 Lead\nPhase 2: Lead 发送 task 给 B01-B03, C01-C03（B/C 并行）\n         → B/C 完成后各成员报告 Lead\nPhase 3: Lead 发送 task 给 D01-D03, E01-E03（D/E 并行）\n         → D/E 完成后各成员报告 Lead\nPhase 4: Lead 收集全部 15 份报告，汇总分析\nPhase 5: Lead 向 User 呈报分析结果\nPhase 6: 等待 User 命令解散\n```\n\n### 依赖关系\n\n```\nTeam A (types + proto)\n    │\n    ├──► Team B (hp) ── 可并行 ──►\n    │         │\n    ├──► Team C (agent) ─────────► Team D (tools)\n    │         │                         │\n    └──► Team E (tui) ◄─────────────────┘\n                                       (tui 通过 IPC 调 tools)\n```\n\n- A 是所有 crate 的依赖，必须最先完成\n- B 和 C 可并行（B 依赖 A 的 types，C 也依赖 A 的 types）\n- D 依赖 C 的 IPC 协议（tools 被 agent 调用）\n- E 依赖 A 的 types，可较早启动但完整集成需等 C/D\n\n## 每个 Member 的 Task 模板\n\n```\nTask: [模块名] 接口设计与实现\nContext: [所在 crate 的职责]\nInput: [分配给该成员的文件列表]\nRequirements:\n  1. 阅读全部分配文件，理解现有实现\n  2. 设计模块的 pub API（trait / struct / enum / fn 签名）\n  3. 定义与其他 crate 的 IPC 交互点（使用 Team A 定义的 proto）\n  4. 编写 Cargo.toml 依赖\n  5. 标注哪些现有代码可复用、哪些需重写/删除\n  6. 输出模块设计文档（Markdown）\nDeliverable: 1 份 Markdown 设计文档\n```\n\n## 通信协议\n\n- Lead → Member：`SendMessage(to=member, content=task)`\n- Member → Lead：成员完成后通过 `SendMessage(to=lead, content=report)` 报告\n- Team 内协作：成员间 `SendMessage(to=same_team_member, content=...)`\n- 解散：`TeamDelete(name)` — 仅 User 命令触发\n\n## 验证方式\n\n1. 每个 Team 完成时，Lead 检查成员报告完整性\n2. Lead 汇总分析后，对照 `explore.md` 确认无遗漏\n3. 最终由 User 审核各模块设计文档\n4. User 批准后执行 `TeamDelete` 逐一解散\n"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3fff69c0-4fbd-4c2b-a8ed-a9287629b5a0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:31:09.639Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
