`tool_call_req` -- tool call with id, name, action, args, timeout_secs\n- `tool_cancel` -- cancel specific or all tools\n- `tool_confirm_resp` -- user approval/denial for confirm requests\n- `tools_shutdown` -- shutdown signal\n\nOutbound frames (Tools -> Agent):\n- `tools_ready` -- ready signal with tool definitions\n- `tool_progress` -- streaming progress (stdout/stderr/progress)\n- `tool_result` -- legacy result (id, success, content)\n- `tool_result_message` -- structured result with error flag\n- `tool_error` -- error with code (UNKNOWN_TOOL, BLOCKED, TIMEOUT, PANIC, FORBIDDEN)\n- `tool_confirm_req` -- request user confirmation\n\n---\n\n### 7. `dsx-tui` -- Terminal UI\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/Cargo.toml`\n**main.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/main.rs`\n**lib.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`\n**Dependencies:** dsx-types, dsx-proto, tokio, serde, serde_json, ratatui (0.30, crossterm), crossterm (0.29), anyhow, tui-markdown, log, regex, clap\n\n**All source files (25):**\n\n| Path | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/main.rs` | Binary entry point, calls `dsx_tui::run()` |\n| `src/lib.rs` | Main TUI runtime: CLI parsing, agent spawning, event loop, readline/demo modes. Also contains ~300 lines of Phase 4 stubs (stubs module). |\n| `src/app.rs` | Application state/App struct |\n| `src/commands.rs` | Slash commands |\n| `src/mode.rs` | TUI mode enum (Chat, Streaming, etc.) |\n| `src/state.rs` | `AppState`, `AgentConnection`, `AgentFrame`, `StreamBuffer`, `RenderContext` |\n| `src/status.rs` | Status line rendering |\n| `src/tui_text.rs` | Internationalized text |\n| `src/utils.rs` | Utility functions including `textwrap` |\n| `src/workspace.rs` | Workspace panel state |\n\n**input/ module (7 files):**\n\n| Path | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/input/mod.rs` | Module declarations + re-exports |\n| `src/input/chat.rs` | `handle_chat_key` -- chat mode keyboard handler |\n| `src/input/confirm.rs` | `handle_confirm_key`, `handle_danger_key` |\n| `src/input/sudo.rs` | `handle_sudo_key` |\n| `src/input/picker.rs` | `handle_intent_picker_key`, `handle_session_picker_key` |\n| `src/input/action.rs` | `InputAction` enum |\n| `src/input/state.rs` | `InputState` |\n\n**render/ module (7 files):**\n\n| Path | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/render/mod.rs` | Main `render_all` dispatch, layout (horizontal/vertical), color palette, DS banner, `center_rect`, `truncate_path` |\n| `src/render/chat.rs` | Chat message rendering |\n| `src/render/input.rs` | Input area rendering |\n| `src/render/popups.rs` | Popup overlays |\n| `src/render/workspace.rs` | Workspace panel rendering |\n| `src/render/tool_code.rs` | Tool code/execution output rendering |\n\n---\n\n## CROSS-CRATE DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\ndsx-types      (no internal deps)\ndsx-proto      depends on: dsx-types\ndsx-hp         depends on: dsx-types, dsx-proto\ndsx-agent      depends on: dsx-types, dsx-proto\ndsx-tools      depends on: dsx-types, dsx-proto\ndsx-tui        depends on: dsx-types, dsx-proto\ndsx (umbrella) depends on: dsx-hp, dsx-agent, dsx-tools, dsx-tui\n```\n\n---\n\n## BINARY ROLES AND COMMUNICATION\n\n| Binary | Process Role | Communication Channel |\n|--------|-------------|----------------------|\n| `dsx-hp` | TCP daemon (port from `~/.dsx/hp.port`) | TCP localhost, JSON-LP |\n| `dsx-tui` | UI process | spawns agent via stdin/stdout pipes |\n| `dsx-agent` | Orchestrator | stdin/stdout to TUI, spawns tools, TCP to HP |\n| `dsx-tools` | Tool executor | stdin/stdout to agent |\n| `dsx` | Umbrella dispatcher | selects role via argv[1] |\n\n---\n\n## KEY NOTES\n\n- The project is at **Phase 4** (integration) of a major v3->v4 refactor. Many stub modules exist in `dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (the `stubs` module spanning ~340 lines) providing placeholder implementations for modules that will eventually be accessed via IPC from `dsx-agent`.\n- The changelog (`CHANGELOG-v4.0.0.md`) documents the reasoning: monolith was split into 5 processes + 2 shared libraries for fault isolation, sandboxing, and architectural clarity.\n- The `next-dev.md` lists remaining TODOs: 88 warnings (unused imports), stub replacements, cross-crate import path unification, and StreamEvent data flow.\n- `dsx-proto/src/lib.rs` is essentially empty -- IPC frame types are actually defined in `dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs`. This appears to be a design issue where the shared protocol crate was not populated with the frame definitions.\n- The `tokenizer.json` file is bundled at `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/tokenizer.json`.\n- Config is stored at `~/.dsx/config.json` with fields: `api_key`, `base_url`, `model`, `prompt_lang`."}]}]},"uuid":"a60ef80d-4bb1-4d75-a920-34d2eaada8f0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:33:29.241Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Very thorough exploration. I need to understand the full current state of this Rust project. \n\n1. List all files under crates/ recursively (use find or ls -R)\n2. For each crate, read its Cargo.toml and lib.rs/mod.rs to understand what modules exist\n3. Read the workspace Cargo.toml at the repo root\n4. Read crates/dsx/Cargo.toml\n\nThe project is at /home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx\n\nReport back ALL file paths and module structures. Be exhaustive.","agentId":"ab009cb9d79fe19a6","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the exhaustive report on the DSX Rust project.\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n**DSX (DeepSeek X Agents)** v4.0.0-alpha1 is a multi-process AI coding assistant. The workspace contains 7 crates (5 binaries + 2 libraries), totaling approximately 80 source files across 15 module teams.\n\nWorkspace root: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx`\nBuild target: `release`\n\n---\n\n## WORKSPACE CONFIGURATION\n\n`/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/Cargo.toml`\n\n- resolver = \"2\"\n- Edition 2021, MIT license\n- 7 members:\n  1. `crates/dsx-types` (lib)\n  2. `crates/dsx-proto` (lib)\n  3. `crates/dsx` (bin -- umbrella)\n  4. `crates/dsx-hp` (bin)\n  5. `crates/dsx-agent` (bin)\n  6. `crates/dsx-tools` (bin)\n  7. `crates/dsx-tui` (bin)\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURE (Multi-Process)\n\n```\ndsx-hp (TCP daemon, port 9001)\n  |-- Health platform, API proxy, process registry, sentinel\n  |-- Only process that holds the API key\n  |\n  +-- dsx-tui (ratatui terminal UI, parent process)\n       |-- Spawns dsx-agent via stdin/stdout JSON-LP\n       |\n       +-- dsx-agent (conversation orchestrator, stdin/stdout)\n            |-- Spawns dsx-tools via stdin/stdout JSON-LP\n            |-- Connects to dsx-hp via TCP JSON-LP\n            |\n            +-- dsx-tools (sandboxed tool execution, stdin/stdout)\n```\n\n---\n\n## CRATE DETAILS\n\n### 1. `dsx-types` -- Shared Type Library\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-types/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-types/Cargo.toml`\n**lib.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-types/src/lib.rs`\n**Dependencies:** serde, serde_json, thiserror\n\n**Public modules (9):**\n\n| Module | Source File | Description |\n|--------|------------|-------------|\n| `message` | `src/message.rs` | `Message`, `ToolCall`, `FunctionCall` |\n| `safety` | `src/safety.rs` | `SafetyLevel` |\n| `tool_def` | `src/tool_def.rs` | `ToolDef`, `ToolFunction` |\n| `state` | `src/state.rs` | `AgentPhase`, `TaskPhase`, `DebugLevel`, `RouterCommand` |\n| `config` | `src/config.rs` | `PersistentConfig`, `ProfileConfig`, `UserPreferences` |\n| `session` | `src/session.rs` | `SessionFile`, `SessionMeta`, `StreamState` |\n| `anthropic` | `src/anthropic.rs` | `AnthropicContent`, `AnthropicMessage`, `AnthropicTool`, `AnthropicThinking`, `AnthropicRequest`, `AnthropicStreamEvent`, and more |\n| `api_types` | `src/api_types.rs` | `UsageInfo`, `TokenDetails`, `ModelInfo`, `ModelList`, `BalanceInfo`, `BalanceEntry` |\n| `convert` | `src/convert.rs` | Conversion utilities |\n| `error` | `src/error.rs` | `DsxError`, `IpcError`, `ApiError`, `ToolError`, `HealthError` |\n| `serde` | `src/serde.rs` | `SerdeError`, `encode_msg`, `encode_msg_with_max`, `decode_msg`, `try_decode_msg`, `MAX_FRAME_SIZE` |\n| `token` | `src/token.rs` | `TokenCount`, `TokenBreakdown`, `estimate_messages_tokens`, `count_tokens`, `format_tokens`, `context_usage_ratio` |\n\n---\n\n### 2. `dsx-proto` -- IPC Protocol Library\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-proto/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-proto/Cargo.toml`\n**lib.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-proto/src/lib.rs`\n**Dependencies:** dsx-types, serde, serde_json\n\nCurrently the lib.rs only contains a doc comment `//! DSX IPC message protocol -- shared between all processes`. The actual IPC frame definitions live in `dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs` instead (see below).\n\n---\n\n### 3. `dsx` -- Umbrella Binary\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/Cargo.toml`\n**main.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx/src/main.rs`\n**Dependencies:** dsx-hp, dsx-agent, dsx-tools, dsx-tui, serde_json, anyhow\n\nThe single entry point that dispatches based on argv[1]:\n- `dsx hp` -> calls `dsx_hp::runner::run()`\n- `dsx agent` -> calls `dsx_agent::runner::run()`\n- `dsx tools` -> calls `dsx_tools::run()`\n- `dsx config` -> runs interactive config setup (writes `~/.dsx/config.json`)\n- `dsx` (default) -> calls `dsx_tui::run()`\n\nSets env var `DSX_SINGLE_BINARY=1` on startup.\n\n---\n\n### 4. `dsx-hp` -- Health Platform Daemon\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/Cargo.toml`\n**main.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/main.rs`\n**lib.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/lib.rs`\n**runner.rs:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs`\n**Dependencies:** dsx-types, dsx-proto, tokio, reqwest (rustls, json, stream), serde, serde_json, log, futures-util, anyhow\n\n**All source files (22):**\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/lib.rs` | Re-exports. Defines `StreamEvent` enum and `AccumulatedToolCall` struct. Public modules listed below. |\n| `src/main.rs` | Binary entry point, delegates to `runner::run()` |\n| `src/runner.rs` | TCP server loop, connection handler, frame dispatch, `api_chat` handler (HTTP to LLM API) |\n| `src/client.rs` | HTTP client for Anthropic API calls |\n| `src/config.rs` | API config (key, base_url) |\n| `src/converter.rs` | Message conversion utilities |\n| `src/types.rs` | HpError, ProcessKind, Verdict, ProcessHealth, ProcessSummary |\n| `src/registry.rs` | ProcessRegistry (heartbeat tracking) |\n| `src/pipeline.rs` | Health judgment pipeline |\n| `src/ipc_traits.rs` | HealthProbe trait definition |\n| `src/assessment.rs` | Health assessment logic |\n| `src/audit.rs` | Health audit trail |\n| `src/circuit_breaker.rs` | Circuit breaker pattern |\n| `src/emotion.rs` | Agent emotion inference |\n| `src/gate.rs` | Tool gate / safety checks |\n| `src/liveness.rs` | Liveness probing |\n| `src/monitor.rs` | MonitorState |\n| `src/platform.rs` | Platform abstractions |\n| `src/quality.rs` | Quality metrics |\n| `src/report.rs` | Report generation |\n| `src/sentinel.rs` | Error sentinel |\n| `src/session.rs` | Session stubs (Phase 4) |\n| `src/stubs.rs` | Phase 4 stubs |\n\n**Public modules in lib.rs:**\n`runner`, `client`, `config`, `types`, `registry`, `pipeline`, `ipc_traits`, `assessment`, `audit`, `circuit_breaker`, `emotion`, `gate`, `liveness`, `monitor`, `platform`, `quality`, `report`, `sentinel`, `session`, `stubs`\n\nPrivate modules: `converter`\n\nKey exports: `chat_stream`, `get_balance`, `list_models`, `anthropic_url`, `request_to_provider`\n\n---\n\n### 5. `dsx-agent` -- Conversation Orchestrator\n\n**Path:** `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/`\n**Cargo.toml:** `/home