mplemented. Strips umbrella subcommand, dispatches to `run_readline_direct`, `run_demo`, or `run_impl`.\n\n- **`run_impl()`** (line 140): The real TUI path. Spawns the agent binary with **raw pipes** (stdin/stdout), creates a **stubbed AgentConnection** (`AgentConnection::spawn(None, ...)` -- no real subprocess behind it), and runs a manual event loop inline (lines 212-338). The inline loop reads agent stdout directly, parses JSON-LP frames by string-matching (e.g., `contains(\"\\\"api_response\\\"\")`), and handles keyboard via a background reader thread. This is a **transitional implementation** -- the proper `AgentConnection` IPC abstraction is created but unused (stub mode), while real I/O goes through raw pipes.\n\n- **`run_demo()`** (line 341): Similar to `run_impl` but with sample messages pre-loaded. Also uses raw pipes + stub AgentConnection. Implemented.\n\n- **`run_readline_direct()`** (line 476): Simple line-by-line REPL. No ratatui. Fully implemented.\n\n- **`event_loop()`** (line 549): A properly refactored ratatui event loop using the real `AgentConnection::drain_frames()` API. **THIS IS DEAD CODE** -- it is never called. The `run_impl` function has its own inline equivalent. The comment at line 387 references \"same as event_loop\" but never calls it.\n\n- **`stubs` module** (line 659-999): ~340 lines of no-op and default-value implementations for every dependency that would normally live in `dsx-agent`:\n  - `stubs::tools`: Just an `AUTO_MODE` AtomicBool. Stub.\n  - `stubs::dsc_log`: `init()` and `set_level()` do nothing. Stub.\n  - `stubs::config`: `Config struct` with real fields + reads `~/.dsx/config.json`. Handlers like `handle_*_command()` return `None`. **Partial** -- the struct is real but all commands are no-ops.\n  - `stubs::session`: All functions return empty defaults. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::conversation`: `ContextAssembler` struct with all methods no-oped. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::api`: `StreamEvent` enum defined, `get_balance()` returns zero balance. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::tokenizer`: `format_tokens()` and `context_usage_ratio()` are real implementations. **Partial** -- only two functions, minimally useful.\n  - `stubs::context`: `ContextBuilder`, `CompactLevel`, `compact_context`, `force_compact` -- all no-ops. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::health`: `DsAgentsHealthPlatform`, `HealthLevel`, `ContextTier`, `AgentEmotion` structs defined but all logic stubbed. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::memory`: `SemanticMemory`, `LongTermMemory`, `ShortTermMemory`, `PitfallGuide` structs defined, methods are empty. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::skills`: `SkillIndex`, `GlobalSkills` with empty scan. **Stub**.\n  - `stubs::orchestrator`: 6 sub-submodules (agent_loop, gates, arg_parser, tracker, learning, phase_detector), all functions are no-ops returning defaults. **Stub**.\n\n**TODOs/Issues:**\n- `event_loop()` function is dead code (defined but never called).\n- stubs marked \"Phase 4\" -- they are placeholders for when IPC to `dsx-agent` is complete.\n- `save_dsx_config` persists only to JSON file, no IPC sync with agent.\n\n---\n\n### 3. `app.rs` (560 lines) -- LEGACY / BEING DEPRECATED\n\n**What it does:** The original monolithic `App` struct with **~80 fields** covering UI state, agent orchestration, health monitoring, memory, session management, tool chains, and more. Fully-built constructor, message repair, context preparation/compaction, learning extraction, phase detection, and session saving.\n\n**Implementation status:** **Complete** as a standalone struct, but it is a **legacy implementation slated for replacement**. The newer `AppState` in `state.rs` is the intended successor. Currently:\n- `commands.rs` still uses `&mut App` (old).\n- `workspace.rs` still takes `&App` (old).\n- All `render/*` modules use the new `RenderContext` (new).\n- `app.rs` defines helper types (`GateBlocked`, `ApiError`, `RetryProgress`, `RateLimitInfo`) also used by new `state.rs`.\n\n**TODOs/Issues:**\n- Lines 393, 400: `[MEMORY FROZEN]` comments indicating self-learning memory is disabled by default.\n- All actual work (context building, phase detection, etc.) delegates to `stubs::*` which are no-ops.\n- `prepare_and_compact` builds context through stubs -- produces empty result.\n- Should eventually be removed when migration to `AppState` + `AgentConnection` is complete.\n\n---\n\n### 4. `state.rs` (560 lines) -- COMPLETE (New Architecture)\n\n**What it does:** Defines the disaggregated state types for the new architecture:\n- `TuiFrame` / `AgentFrame` enums -- JSON-LP IPC frame types for agent communication.\n- `AgentConnection` -- spawns the agent binary, manages stdin/stdout via a background reader thread and `std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel`. Methods: `spawn()`, `send_frame()`, `try_recv()`, `drain_frames()`, `shutdown()`.\n- `StreamBuffer` -- accumulates streaming deltas (content, reasoning, tool_progress). Methods: `new()`, `clear()`, `apply_payload()`, `is_active()`, `to_message()`.\n- `AppState` -- pure UI state (~25 fields, no orchestration/health/memory). Fields: `input_state`, `mode`, `messages`, `scroll_offset`, `auto_scroll`, `tool_code_*`, `pending_tools`, `gate/error state`, etc.\n- `RenderContext` -- read-only snapshot assembled once per render cycle from `AppState` + `StreamBuffer` + `AgentConnection`. Has ~50 fields aggregating everything render functions need.\n\n**Implementation status:** Fully implemented. `AgentConnection` has a working background reader, frame parsing, backpressure via sync_channel, Drop handling for shutdown. `StreamBuffer` is fully functional. `AppState` and `RenderContext` are complete.\n\n**Issues:** None. This is the intended architecture.\n\n---\n\n### 5. `mode.rs` (22 lines) -- COMPLETE\n\n**What it does:** `Mode` enum with variants: `Chat`, `Streaming`, `ToolConfirm`, `DangerPrompt`, `SudoPrompt`, `ApiConfig`, `SessionPicker`, `IntentPicker`, `GateBlock`. Also `SubMenuState` struct.\n\n**Implementation status:** Complete, nothing missing.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `commands.rs` (126 lines) -- PARTIAL (Legacy API)\n\n**What it does:** `handle_slash_command(app: &mut App, input: &str, tx)` -- dispatches slash commands. Handles: `/reset`, `/reconfig`, `/effort`, `/lang`, `/model`, `/profile`, `/balance`, `/fix`, `/context`, `/clear`, `/tools`, `/auto`, `/skip-all`, `/dev`, `/compact`.\n\n**Implementation status:** All command branches are wired, but every command delegates to `stubs::*` handlers (which return `None` / empty). The actual effect for `/model`, `/effort`, `/lang` etc. relies on real config handlers not being implemented in stubs. The `/balance` command spawns a tokio task. The `/fix` command runs `repair_messages()`. The `/compact` command runs `compact_context()` which is a stub.\n\n**Issues:** Still uses the old `App` struct. Needs migration to work with `AppState` + `AgentConnection` IPC.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `status.rs` (27 lines) -- COMPLETE\n\n**What it does:** `render_status_line()` -- one-liner for narrow terminal fallback showing model, token usage, balance, auto-mode flag. Uses `RenderContext`.\n\n**Implementation status:** Complete.\n\n---\n\n### 8. `tui_text.rs` (194 lines) -- COMPLETE\n\n**What it does:** Two fully-populated `TuiText` bundles (English `TUI_EN` and Chinese `TUI_ZH`) with all UI labels, prompts, and help text (~60 fields each). `tui_text(lang)` returns the appropriate bundle.\n\n**Implementation status:** Complete. All strings are defined in both languages.\n\n---\n\n### 9. `utils.rs` (104 lines) -- COMPLETE\n\n**What it does:** Pure utility functions: `strip_ansi`, `display_width` (CJK-aware), `format_bytes`, `pad_to_width`, `textwrap` (CJK-aware line wrapping), `truncate` (with ellipsis), `char_boundary`, `prev_char_boundary`, `next_char_boundary`.\n\n**Implementation status:** Complete and correct. All functions handle CJK multi-byte characters properly.\n\n---\n\n### 10. `workspace.rs` (263 lines) -- COMPLETE (Legacy API)\n\n**What it does:** Two render functions using the old `App`:\n- `re