{"parentUuid":"b4e48bdc-a2aa-4fcf-81e5-1bfe20290471","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"9c8944ba-4043-4856-a981-0162eb332ee0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very comprehensive picture. Let me also check the dsx-agent's runner.rs more carefully to understand what's actually connected vs what exists but isn't wired. And let me check lib.rs of dsx-agent to see which modules are declared but not used.\n\nLet me also quickly check what the agent's current `runner.rs` actually does vs what modules exist but aren't called.\n\nNow I have enough information to present a comprehensive report. Let me organize it clearly.\n\nThe key findings are:\n\n### Already Working (end-to-end):\n1. Single static binary (`dsx`)\n2. TUI spawns agent via pipes\n3. Agent spawns tools via pipes\n4. Agent connects to HP via TCP\n5. HP proxies API calls to DeepSeek\n6. Basic conversation with tool calling (10 rounds max)\n7. Cache-friendly compaction\n8. Slash commands (locally intercepted: /model, /lang, /effort, /help)\n9. `dsx config` for setup\n10. Keyboard input, chat rendering, popups\n\n### Major Gaps (by impact):\n\n**1. Streaming responses missing** — HP streams internally via channels, but agent waits for complete response with `read_frame()`. User sees entire response at once instead of token-by-token.\n\n**2. dsx-proto crate is empty** — Shared IPC protocol definitions don't exist. Frame types are scattered: dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs has tool frames, dsx-tui/src/state.rs has TUI frames, dsx-hp runner has HP frames. No single source of truth.\n\n**3. Agent's rich modules are NOT wired into runner.rs** — 41 source files exist with full implementations for:\n   - Session persistence (save/restore conversations)\n   - Memory system (long-term, short-term, semantic, pitfall)\n   - Context management (ContextBuilder, ContextAssembler)\n   - Orchestrator modules (gates, learning, phase_detector, tracker, turn_scorer, context_compactor, stream_handler, response_processor, tool_dispatch, session_persistence)\n   - Skills system, Router, Health integration\n   \n   But `runner.rs` only does: basic conversation loop + tool dispatch + cache-friendly compaction. None of the above is used.\n\n**4. HP stubs blocking gate/audit** — The `ContextAssembler` in `dsx-hp/src/stubs.rs` is a no-op, so `gate.rs` and `audit.rs` can't actually validate anything. `session.rs` and `config.rs` are also stubs.\n\n**5. TUI render/workspace.rs is a TODO stub** — The workspace panel (plans, tasks, health, memory) and full info panel don't render.\n\n**6. TUI stubs (~340 lines)** — All cross-crate functionality (orchestrator, context, health, memory, skills, session, API balance, tokenizer) is no-ops.\n\n**7. Two parallel architectures in TUI** — Old `App` (80 fields) vs new `AppState` + `RenderContext`. `commands.rs` uses old App, `workspace.rs` (legacy) uses old App, but render layer uses new RenderContext.\n\n**8. Dead code** — `event_loop()` in lib.rs is properly implemented but never called.\n\n**9. Tools stubs** — `list_skills`, `read_skill_ref`, `glance` return placeholder data. Memory/plan/task tools rely on stub I/O.\n\n**10. 88 compiler warnings** (unused imports, dead code).\n\n**11. No auto_mode for tools** — Tool confirmation always required.\n\n**12. No health monitoring integration** — HP daemon and health platform code exist but agent doesn't push MonitorState updates.\n\nLet me present this clearly.","signature":"9c8944ba-4043-4856-a981-0162eb332ee0"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":64128,"output_tokens":2094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"1a