nding their APIs, and figuring out where to wire them in runner.rs is a massive task. Maybe I should split this into 2 agents?\n\nActually, let me split it differently:\n- Agent-rewire-1: Session + Memory + Context + Conversation (the data layer)\n- Agent-rewire-2: Orchestrator + Skills + Router + Tokenizer + Health + Prompt (the orchestration layer)\n\nHmm, but the user said 3 teammates. Let me just spawn 3 and give them clearly scoped work. The agent one is the biggest but a sonnet with 1M context should handle it.\n\nLet me finalize the spawns.\n\nActually wait, Task dependencies: Tasks 2-4 depend on Task 1 (dsx-proto). But I shouldn't make them wait for me to finish dsx-proto first. They should start reading code and understanding the existing types immediately. The dsx-proto changes will mostly affect import paths, which can be updated later.\n\nLet me spawn all 3 now and tell them to start reading/understanding while I work on dsx-proto.","signature":"be5372f5-df7e-4dcb-8486-f371c312fd60"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":76288,"output_tokens":4342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3e1ac047-deba-4ac4-a7f6-f8365ec168c6","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:41:51.871Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
