{"parentUuid":"a8f87e26-ad80-4074-8584-21012c0e7fc2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"be5372f5-df7e-4dcb-8486-f371c312fd60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_85iLF25P4qjrzMHaG9EN2579","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Agent runner 接入全部模块","subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"agent-rewire","team_name":"dsx-integration","prompt":"Your task: Wire all existing dsx-agent modules into runner.rs so the full intelligence layer works.\n\n## Context\n\nDSX v4.0.0-alpha1 is a 5-process AI coding assistant migrated from a monolith. The agent crate (`crates/dsx-agent/`) has 41 source files — 39 from the original monolith (fully implemented), plus `runner.rs` and `lib.rs` which were created fresh during the multi-process migration.\n\n**The problem**: `runner.rs` only implements a basic conversation loop with tool calling + cache-friendly compaction. It does NOT call any of the 39 existing modules. All the intelligence (session persistence, memory, context management, orchestrator, skills, router, tokenizer, health) is sitting there unused.\n\n**Your job**: Read the existing modules, understand their APIs, and wire them into `runner.rs`.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nTUI(stdin/stdout) → Agent(runner.rs) → HP(TCP) → DeepSeek API\n                       ↓\n                   Tools(stdin/stdout)\n```\n\nAll modules are in-process (direct function calls, no IPC needed between them).\n\n## What to do\n\n### Phase 1: READ and understand\nRead these key files first:\n- `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs` — the current main loop\n- `crates/dsx-agent/src/lib.rs` — module declarations\n- `crates/dsx-agent/src/agent.rs` — the Agent struct (389 lines, likely the central state)\n\nThen explore each subsystem to understand its public API:\n- `session/` (7 files): mod.rs, persist.rs, index.rs, plan_io.rs, memory_io.rs, restore.rs, snapshot.rs\n- `memory/` (5 files): mod.rs, long_term.rs, short_term.rs, semantic.rs, pitfall.rs  \n- `orchestrator/` (12 files): mod.rs, agent_loop.rs, stream_handler.rs, response_processor.rs, tool_dispatch.rs, context_compactor.rs, gates.rs, learning.rs, tracker.rs, turn_scorer.rs, session_persistence.rs, arg_parser.rs, phase_detector.rs\n- `context.rs` — ContextBuilder\n- `conversation.rs` — ContextAssembler\n- `skills.rs` — SkillIndex\n- `router.rs` — Message routing\n- `tokenizer.rs` — Token counting\n- `health.rs` — Health status\n- `prompt.rs` — System prompt building\n- `api.rs` — API integration\n- `config.rs` — Agent config\n- `dsc_log.rs` — Logging\n- `tools.rs` — Tool dispatch\n- `tui.rs` — TUI stubs (legacy)\n\n### Phase 2: WIRE them in\nModify `runner.rs` to:\n1. Initialize Agent struct (from agent.rs) at startup\n2. Use session persistence (save/restore conversations to disk)\n3. Use ContextBuilder/ContextAssembler for proper context assembly (replacing the raw `Vec<serde_json::Value>` conversation)\n4. Use the orchestrator's context_compactor instead of the inline compact_cache_friendly\n5. Call orchestrator gates before tool execution\n6. Call phase_detector to know what phase the agent is in\n7. Use tracker to track file operations\n8. Use turn_scorer after each turn\n9. Use learning module to extract learnings\n10. Use the memory system (long_term, short_term, semantic, pitfall)\n11. Use the real tokenizer instead of the approximate tok() function\n12. Use prompt.rs for system prompt building\n13. Use skills.rs for skill indexing\n14. Use router.rs for message routing decisions\n15. Integrate health.rs for health status reporting to HP\n\n### Phase 3: Ensure it compiles\n- `cargo build --release 2>&1 | head -50` to check\n- Fix any compilation errors\n- Do NOT create new modules — only modify runner.rs and maybe lib.rs\n\n## Important constraints\n- Do NOT run `cargo test` (user forbids it)\n- Do NOT modify the existing modules' internal logic — only call their public APIs from runner.rs\n- If a module's API doesn't fit the new architecture, note it in your report but don't redesign it\n- Keep runner.rs as the single entry point (don't create new binaries)\n- The existing conversation loop structure (TUI frame → HP → tools → response) should be preserved but enhanced with module calls\n\n## Deliverable\n1. Modified `runner.rs` that wires in as many modules as possible\n2. A brief report of what was wired, what couldn't be wired (and why), and any compilation issues\n\nStart by reading all the files. Take your time to understand before writing code.","run_in_background":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":76288,"output_tokens":4342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c44ddcd5-5bcd-4932-8a9b-580c1c2f48fe","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:42:28.191Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
