\n\n## Important constraints\n- Do NOT run `cargo test` (user forbids it)\n- Do NOT modify the existing modules' internal logic — only call their public APIs from runner.rs\n- If a module's API doesn't fit the new architecture, note it in your report but don't redesign it\n- Keep runner.rs as the single entry point (don't create new binaries)\n- The existing conversation loop structure (TUI frame → HP → tools → response) should be preserved but enhanced with module calls\n\n## Deliverable\n1. Modified `runner.rs` that wires in as many modules as possible\n2. A brief report of what was wired, what couldn't be wired (and why), and any compilation issues\n\nStart by reading all the files. Take your time to understand before writing code.","teammate_id":"agent-rewire@dsx-integration","agent_id":"agent-rewire@dsx-integration","agent_type":"sonnet","model":"claude-opus-4-7","name":"agent-rewire","color":"blue","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"dsx-integration","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c44ddcd5-5bcd-4932-8a9b-580c1c2f48fe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"13f348ff-1881-44f8-b0e3-b3db871d38e0","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"be5372f5-df7e-4dcb-8486-f371c312fd60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01_zfsY0huEoTfpbEkczzDl7394","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"消除 HP 和 Tools stubs","subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"stubs-eliminator","team_name":"dsx-integration","prompt":"Your task: Eliminate stub implementations in dsx-hp and dsx-tools, replacing them with real logic.\n\n## Context\n\nDSX v4.0.0-alpha1 is a 5-process AI coding assistant. Two crates have placeholder/stub code that was left during the multi-process migration and needs to be replaced with real implementations.\n\n## Part 1: dsx-hp stubs\n\nLocation: `crates/dsx-hp/src/`\n\n### stubs.rs\nContains a completely empty `ContextAssembler` struct. All methods return defaults:\n- `validate()` → always Ok\n- `ready_for_api()` → always Ok  \n- `to_anthropic_messages()` → returns None\n- `has_pending_tools()` → false\n- `pending_tool_count()` → 0\n- `last_turn()` → None\n- `from_legacy()` → (Self, empty vec)\n- `to_vec()` → empty vec\n\nThis causes `gate.rs` and `audit.rs` to be effectively no-ops. The REAL ContextAssembler exists in `crates/dsx-agent/src/conversation.rs`.\n\n**What to do**: \n- Read `crates/dsx-agent/src/conversation.rs` to understand the real ContextAssembler\n- Replace the HP stub with a real implementation, OR re-export/import from dsx-agent\n- Since dsx-hp already depends on dsx-types, and the ContextAssembler types should be shared via dsx-types or dsx-proto, you may need to move the ContextAssembler definition to a shared crate\n- Alternative: Make `gate.rs` and `audit.rs` work without depending on dsx-agent by implementing the needed validation logic directly in dsx-hp\n\n### session.rs\nContains empty stubs: `now_epoch()`, `sessions_dir()` returns None, `PitfallGuide` is empty, `load_pitfalls()` returns empty.\n\n**What to do**: Implement real session directory resolution and pitfall loading. The real implementations exist in `crates/dsx-agent/src/session/`.\n\n### config.rs  \nMarked as \"will be replaced by dsx-agent's config\". Currently a minimal Config struct with just base_url and api_key.\n\n**What to do**: Either keep as-is (it's functional for HP's needs) or add the fields HP needs. HP only needs api_key and base_url for API calls, so this may be fine.\n\n## Part 2: dsx-tools stubs\n\nLocation: `crates/dsx-tools/src/`\n\n### meta.rs — 3 TODO stubs\n- `list_skills` (line 55): Returns empty string. TODO says \"return actual skill list via IPC from agent\"\n- `read_skill_ref` (line 61): Returns hint message. TODO says \"read skill via IPC from agent\"  \n- `glance` (line 92): Returns \"no cached summary\". TODO says \"glance receives seed + semantic data via IPC from agent\"\n\n**What to do**: Since dsx-tools runs as a subprocess that communicates with dsx-agent via stdin/stdout JSON-LP, these tools CAN'T directly access agent data. Options:\n1. Add IPC frames for agent→tools to provide skill/semantic data at init time\n2. Make these tools send a request back to agent via a new IPC frame type\n3. Keep them as stubs with clear documentation\n\nRead `crates/dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs` to understand the IPC protocol first.\n\n### stubs.rs — Memory/Plan/Task I/O stubs\n`read_memory`, `write_memory`, `append_memory`, `forget_memory_key` all return empty/do nothing.\n`load_pitfalls`, `save_pitfalls` return empty guides.\n`write_plan`, `update_plan_status`, `read_plan_content`, `list_plans` all return None/empty.\n\n**What to do**: These are supposed to persist via the agent's session system. Implement real I/O:\n- Option A: Add IPC frames to forward memory/plan/task operations to agent\n- Option B: Give tools direct filesystem access to session data (simpler, faster)\n- Option C: Implement a lightweight local storage in tools\n\nRead the real implementations in `crates/dsx-agent/src/session/` to understand the data format.\n\n### registration.rs\nRead this to understand how all tool handlers are registered. You may need to update tool handler signatures.\n\n## Strategy\n1. First READ all relevant files to understand the current state\n2. For HP: The simplest approach is to implement ContextAssembler logic directly in dsx-hp (since it needs to validate messages before API calls)\n3. For Tools: Since tools can't directly call agent functions (separate process), either add IPC frames or implement local storage\n4. After making changes, run `cargo build --release 2>&1 | head -80` to verify\n\n## Important\n- Do NOT run `cargo test`\n- Prefer simple, direct solutions over complex IPC additions\n- The HP gate/audit must actually validate, not just return Ok\n- Tools that can't be fully implemented (need agent IPC) should be clearly documented\n\n## Deliverable\n1. Modified files with real implementations\n2. Report: what was replaced, what remains stub (and why), any issues found","run_in_background":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":76288,"output_tokens":4342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ea4daead-bd14-46ad-9f38-84f7a7446212","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:43:06.577Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
