needed validation logic directly in dsx-hp\n\n### session.rs\nContains empty stubs: `now_epoch()`, `sessions_dir()` returns None, `PitfallGuide` is empty, `load_pitfalls()` returns empty.\n\n**What to do**: Implement real session directory resolution and pitfall loading. The real implementations exist in `crates/dsx-agent/src/session/`.\n\n### config.rs  \nMarked as \"will be replaced by dsx-agent's config\". Currently a minimal Config struct with just base_url and api_key.\n\n**What to do**: Either keep as-is (it's functional for HP's needs) or add the fields HP needs. HP only needs api_key and base_url for API calls, so this may be fine.\n\n## Part 2: dsx-tools stubs\n\nLocation: `crates/dsx-tools/src/`\n\n### meta.rs — 3 TODO stubs\n- `list_skills` (line 55): Returns empty string. TODO says \"return actual skill list via IPC from agent\"\n- `read_skill_ref` (line 61): Returns hint message. TODO says \"read skill via IPC from agent\"  \n- `glance` (line 92): Returns \"no cached summary\". TODO says \"glance receives seed + semantic data via IPC from agent\"\n\n**What to do**: Since dsx-tools runs as a subprocess that communicates with dsx-agent via stdin/stdout JSON-LP, these tools CAN'T directly access agent data. Options:\n1. Add IPC frames for agent→tools to provide skill/semantic data at init time\n2. Make these tools send a request back to agent via a new IPC frame type\n3. Keep them as stubs with clear documentation\n\nRead `crates/dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs` to understand the IPC protocol first.\n\n### stubs.rs — Memory/Plan/Task I/O stubs\n`read_memory`, `write_memory`, `append_memory`, `forget_memory_key` all return empty/do nothing.\n`load_pitfalls`, `save_pitfalls` return empty guides.\n`write_plan`, `update_plan_status`, `read_plan_content`, `list_plans` all return None/empty.\n\n**What to do**: These are supposed to persist via the agent's session system. Implement real I/O:\n- Option A: Add IPC frames to forward memory/plan/task operations to agent\n- Option B: Give tools direct filesystem access to session data (simpler, faster)\n- Option C: Implement a lightweight local storage in tools\n\nRead the real implementations in `crates/dsx-agent/src/session/` to understand the data format.\n\n### registration.rs\nRead this to understand how all tool handlers are registered. You may need to update tool handler signatures.\n\n## Strategy\n1. First READ all relevant files to understand the current state\n2. For HP: The simplest approach is to implement ContextAssembler logic directly in dsx-hp (since it needs to validate messages before API calls)\n3. For Tools: Since tools can't directly call agent functions (separate process), either add IPC frames or implement local storage\n4. After making changes, run `cargo build --release 2>&1 | head -80` to verify\n\n## Important\n- Do NOT run `cargo test`\n- Prefer simple, direct solutions over complex IPC additions\n- The HP gate/audit must actually validate, not just return Ok\n- Tools that can't be fully implemented (need agent IPC) should be clearly documented\n\n## Deliverable\n1. Modified files with real implementations\n2. Report: what was replaced, what remains stub (and why), any issues found","teammate_id":"stubs-eliminator@dsx-integration","agent_id":"stubs-eliminator@dsx-integration","agent_type":"sonnet","model":"claude-opus-4-7","name":"stubs-eliminator","color":"green","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"dsx-integration","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea4daead-bd14-46ad-9f38-84f7a7446212","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
