{"parentUuid":"2ad66df5-bc33-40c2-8547-f0e9bce48250","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"810391b9-5323-475f-bba4-a07a5ea46856","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"dsx-proto is already a dependency for all three crates. Good. Now let me update dsx-tools/src/ipc.rs to use the shared frame types from dsx-proto instead of its own InboundFrame/OutboundFrame definitions.\n\nActually, wait - this is a delicate operation. The current `InboundFrame` and `OutboundFrame` in dsx-tools are used extensively in the IPC main loop and tool manager. If I replace them, I need to make sure the field names match.\n\nLet me compare:\n\nCurrent dsx-tools InboundFrame:\n- Init { allowed_tools, session_seed, auto_mode }\n- CallReq { id, name, action, args, timeout_secs }\n- Cancel { id }\n- ConfirmResp { id, approved }\n- Shutdown\n\nMy AgentToTools:\n- Init { allowed_tools, session_seed, auto_mode }\n- CallReq { id, name, action, args, timeout_secs }\n- Cancel { id }\n- ConfirmResp { id, approved }\n- Shutdown\n\nThese match. Good.\n\nCurrent dsx-tools OutboundFrame:\n- Ready { tools }\n- Progress { id, content, stream_type }\n- Result { id, success, content }\n- ToolResultMessage { id, name, action, success, content, is_error }\n- ToolError { id, error, code }\n- ToolConfirmReq { id, tool_name, action, danger_level, prompt }\n\nMy ToolsToAgent:\n- Ready { tools }\n- Progress { id, content, stream_type }\n- Result { id, success, content }\n- ToolResultMessage { id, name, action, success, content, is_error }\n- ToolError { id, error, code }\n- ToolConfirmReq { id, tool_name, action, danger_level, prompt }\n\nThese also match. \n\nNow for dsx-tui:\nCurrent TuiFrame:\n- UserInput { text }\n- Shutdown\n\nMy TuiToAgent:\n- UserInput { text }\n- ToolCall { id, name, action, args }\n- Shutdown\n\nCurrent AgentFrame:\n- StreamPayload { content }\n- StreamDone\n- StreamError { message }\n- ShutdownAck\n\nMy AgentToTui:\n- ContentDelta { delta, reasoning }\n- ToolProgress { id, content, stream_type }\n- ApiResponse { content, tool_calls, stop_reason, usage }\n- Echo { data }\n- Done\n- Error { message }\n- ShutdownAck\n\nThe TUI side is more different. The old AgentFrame had StreamPayload (full content) while the new one has ContentDelta (streaming deltas). This is actually part of the streaming feature (Task 5). For now, the TUI's `run_impl` uses raw pipe reads with string matching, not structured deserialization. So the TUI changes can wait.\n\nLet me update dsx-tools first since it's the cleanest migration.\n\nActually, I should think about whether to update the individual crate imports now or let the teammates do it. The teammates are reading code right now. If I change the foundation while they're reading, it could cause confusion.\n\nLet me take a different approach: just notify the teammates that dsx-proto is ready, and let them use the shared types as they work. The local type definitions still work (they're not conflicting). The migration can happen incrementally.\n\nFor now, let me focus on what adds the most value: writing the shared frame types was the key deliverable. The teammates can migrate imports as part of their work.\n\nLet me send them updates.","signature":"810391b9-5323-475f-bba4-a07a5ea46856"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":806,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":99072,"output_tokens":944,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"db3264d4-3814-46fe-bcb6-a23b64628ffc","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:47:49.351Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","