ontent":"                InputAction::SendMessage(state.chat.buffer.clone())\n            }\n        }\n        KeyCode::Char(c) if key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::CONTROL => match c {\n            'd' | '\\x04' => InputAction::ScrollDown(12),\n            'u' | '\\x15' => InputAction::ScrollUp(12),\n            _ => NO_ACTION,\n        },\n        KeyCode::Char(c) => {\n            let pos = char_boundary(&state.chat.buffer, state.chat.cursor);\n            state.chat.buffer.insert(pos, c);\n            state.chat.cursor = pos + c.len_utf8();\n            if c == '/' && state.chat.buffer.trim() == \"/\" {\n                state.slash.open = true;\n                state.slash.filter = state.chat.buffer.clone();\n                update_slash_items(state, commands);\n                state.slash.idx = 0;\n            }\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Backspace => {\n            if state.chat.cursor > 0 {\n                let prev = prev_char_boundary(&state.chat.buffer, state.chat.cursor);\n                state.chat.buffer.remove(prev);\n                state.chat.cursor = prev;\n            }\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Delete => {\n            if state.chat.cursor < state.chat.buffer.len() {\n                state.chat.buffer.remove(state.chat.cursor);\n            }\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Left => {\n            state.chat.cursor = prev_char_boundary(&state.chat.buffer, state.chat.cursor);\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Right => {\n            state.chat.cursor = next_char_boundary(&state.chat.buffer, state.chat.cursor);\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Home => {\n            state.chat.cursor = 0;\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::End => {\n            state.chat.cursor = state.chat.buffer.len();\n            NO_ACTION\n        }\n        KeyCode::Up => InputAction::ScrollUp(3),\n        KeyCode::Down => InputAction::ScrollDown(3),\n        KeyCode::PageUp => InputAction::ScrollPageUp,\n        KeyCode::PageDown => InputAction::ScrollPageDown,\n        KeyCode::Tab => NO_ACTION,\n        _ => NO_ACTION,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Filter the slash commands list against the current input filter.\nfn update_slash_items(state: &mut InputState, commands: &[(String, String)]) {\n    let filter = state.slash.filter.trim().to_lowercase();\n    state.slash.items = commands\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|(cmd, _)| cmd.to_lowercase().contains(&filter))\n        .map(|(c, d)| (c.to_string(), d.to_string()))\n        .collect();\n}\n\n/// Build submenu items for a given slash command (pure, static).\nfn build_submenu_items(cmd: &str) -> Option<Vec<(String, String)>> {\n    match cmd {\n        \"/effort\" => Some(vec![\n            (\"high\".into(), \"High reasoning effort\".into()),\n            (\"max\".into(), \"Maximum reasoning effort\".into()),\n        ]),\n        \"/model\" => Some(vec![\n            (\"deepseek-v4-flash\".into(), \"Fast, cost-effective\".into()),\n            (\"deepseek-v4-pro\".into(), \"High capability\".into()),\n        ]),","numLines":80,"startLine":140,"totalLines":227}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb80f76b-ba8c-45a1-9254-2a9a78e08faf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"552cb9b3-0404-445e-89b6-72f3701b6631","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"869082cd-1619-4b32-b8f3-0ce2969d0d23","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issues clearly:\n\n### Issue 1: 思考链 not showing\nThe rendering code for streaming reasoning IS there (chat.rs:180-184), but the check is `if *ctx.mode == Mode::Streaming`. The question is: is the mode set to `Mode::Streaming` when content_delta arrives?\n\nLooking at lib.rs:220-232, when `content_delta` or `api_response` arrives, the code doesn't explicitly set mode to `Mode::Streaming`. The mode is only set to `Mode::Chat` when `done` arrives.\n\nSo the streaming content is being accumulated in the StreamBuffer but the render code only shows it if mode == Streaming. The mode needs to be set to Streaming when content starts arriving.\n\nSimilarly, for the **already-finished messages** (from conversation history), the reasoning content should be displayed. Looking at chat.rs:147, it checks `if let Some(ref r) = msg.reasoning_content` and renders a thinking block. So completed messages with reasoning should show up. The issue might be that reasoning_content is not being set on the Message struct properly.\n\nLet me check the agent side: In runner.rs, when the assistant message is built:\n```rust\nlet assistant_msg = Message {\n    role: \"assistant\".into(),\n    content: ...,\n    reasoning_content,\n    thinking_signature,\n};\n```\n\nAnd `reasoning_content` is set in the loop from `HpToAgent::ApiResponse { reasoning_content: rc, ... }`. But wait — the streaming loop accumulates reasoning in `agent.stream_reasoning` but the `reasoning_content` value from ApiResponse comes from what the HP sends. In the HP's `handle_api_chat_streaming`, the `reasoning` string is accumulated locally and only sent in the final `api_response` frame. This should be correct.\n\nBUT — looking at the HP code more carefully:\n```rust\nlet mut reasoning = String::new();\n...\nStreamEvent::ReasoningDelta(delta) => {\n    reasoning.push_str(&delta);\n    ...\n}\nStreamEvent::Done { raw_message, ... } => {\n    ...\n    if !reasoning.is_empty() {\n        resp[\"reasoning_content\"] = serde_json::json!(reasoning);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `reasoning` is sent in the final `api_response`. The agent receives it as `reasoning_content: rc`, sets `reasoning_content = rc`, and then puts it in the Message. The TUI then checks `msg.reasoning_content` in chat.rs:147 and renders it. So completed messages should show thinking blocks.\n\nBut the LIVE STREAMING reasoning (while tokens are arriving) requires mode to be Streaming. Let me fix the TUI event loop to set mode to Streaming when content_delta arrives.\n\n### Issue 2: 工作区/终端/聊天 no i18n labels\nLooking at render/mod.rs lines 102-115:\n```rust\n// Chat border\nlet chat_border = Block::default().borders(Borders::ALL)...;\n// Workspace border\nlet ws_border = Block::default().borders(Borders::ALL)...;\n```\n\nNo titles are set on these blocks! The `.title()` method is not called. It should use `ctx.tt()` for localized titles.\n\n### Issue 3: Slash menu\nLooking at input/chat.rs, the slash menu exists, commands list is filtered and displayed. But:\n- Line 200-206: `update_slash_items` filters by text match\n- Line 210: `build_submenu_items` is hardcoded with only /effort and /model\n\nThe slash commands list comes from `commands` parameter. Let me check what commands are passed in. Let me find where `handle_chat_key` is called.\n\nAlso, the menu items have no Chinese translations for descriptions.\n\n### Issue 4: Auto mode\nLooking at runner.rs line 548: `auto_mode: true` is hardcoded in the tools Init frame. Let me check if it's also read from config.\n\nLet me also check if `agent.auto_mode` is initialized from config. Let me find the AgentState::new function.\n\nOK let me be systematic. Let me fix each issue. Let me start with the most impactf