{"parentUuid":"590684db-fe7d-4937-9409-b7b498be5c87","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"3807a967-7b51-4688-b644-83fd4b6b9b30","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issues clearly. Let me plan the fixes:\n\n### Issue 1: 思考链\n- In lib.rs line 278: `state.mode = Mode::Streaming;` is set when user sends a message. But when `content_delta` arrives, the mode should already be Streaming. Let me check if this is correct.\n\nLooking at lib.rs line 278: \n```rust\nif let InputAction::SendMessage(text) = action {\n    ...send to agent...\n    state.mode = Mode::Streaming;\n}\n```\n\nSo mode is set to Streaming when user sends. This should be fine. But let me check the `content_delta` handler (line 220-225):\n\n```rust\nif trimmed.contains(\"\\\"content_delta\\\"\") {\n    if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(trimmed) {\n        let delta = v.get(\"delta\").and_then(|d| d.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n        let reasoning = v.get(\"reasoning\").and_then(|r| r.as_str());\n        stream.apply_payload(delta, reasoning, &[]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis applies the payload but doesn't set mode. Mode is set at send time (line 278) so it should already be Streaming when content_delta arrives.\n\nBut wait — looking at the render check in chat.rs:179: `if *ctx.mode == Mode::Streaming`. If the first response from agent is a content_delta, and the mode was set to Streaming at send time, then it should render. The issue might be elsewhere...\n\nActually, let me re-read the flow:\n1. User sends message → mode = Streaming, awaiting = true\n2. Agent sends content_delta frames → stream accumulates, dirty = true, render shows thinking block\n3. Agent sends api_response → if stream.content is empty, fill it\n4. Agent sends done → mode = Chat, message finalized\n\nThe render in chat.rs line 180 checks `if !ctx.stream_reasoning.is_empty()` — this should show. The TUI event loop checks `if dirty { terminal.draw(...) }` at line 238.\n\nWait — I see a potential issue. Look at line 225-228:\n```rust\n} else if trimmed.contains(\"\\\"api_response\\\"\") {\n    if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(trimmed) {\n        if let Some(content) = v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            if stream.content.is_empty() {\n                stream.apply_payload(content, None, &[]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`api_response` only fills stream.content if it's empty. But if content_delta already accumulated content, it skips. Good.\n\nAnd then `done` finalizes: `let msg = stream.to_message(); state.push_message(msg); stream.clear(); awaiting = false; state.mode = Mode::Chat;`\n\nHmm, but the `to_message()` method builds a Message from accumulated content. Let me check if it includes reasoning:\n\n```rust\npub fn to_message(&self) -> Message {\n    let mut msg = Message::assistant_empty();\n    if !self.content.is_empty() {\n        msg.content = Some(self.content.clone());\n    }\n    if !self.reasoning.is_empty() {\n        msg.reasoning_content = Some(self.reasoning.clone());\n    }\n    msg\n}\n```\n\nThis does include reasoning. And in chat.rs:147, it checks `msg.reasoning_content`. So completed messages should show thinking blocks.\n\nHowever, I notice `stream.clear()` is called after `to_message()`, which clears the reasoning. So for completed messages, reasoning shows. For live streaming, reasoning shows if mode == Streaming.\n\nActually, I think the core issue with thinking chain might be simpler — the DeepSeek API may not be returning reasoning/thinking content for the model being used. DeepSeek models don't have visible thinking chains in the same way Claude does. The `reasoning_content` field is part of the DeepSeek API response for their \"deepseek-reasoner\" model, but for standard chat models (deepseek-v4-flash), there's no thinking/reasoning.\n\nActually, wait. DeepSeek v4 does support thinking. Let me check the HP client to see if thinking is enabled.\n\nActually, looking at the HP client call in runner.rs:\n```rust\nlet _ = client::chat_stream(\n    &cfg, &model_o, sys, msgs, false, None, None, None, 8192, None, None, None, tx,\n).await;\n```\n\nThe `false` is the `thinking` parameter — it's set to false! This disables the thinking/reasoning chain in DeepSeek. I need to change this to `true` to enable thinking.\n\n### Issue 2: Panel labels\nIn render/mod.rs, the chat and workspace blocks have no `.title()`. I need to add localized titles.\n\n### Issue 3: Slash menu\nThe commands list in lib.rs line 173 has only 5 commands, all with English descriptions. Need to:\n1. Add more commands (/auto, /compact, /balance, /clear, /context, etc.)\n2. Support Chinese descriptions via tui_text\n\n### Issue 4: Auto mode\nConfig has `auto_mode: false` by default (config.rs:35). But there's an `auto_mode: Some(self.auto_mode)` in config.rs:121. The agent's runner.rs line 548 hardcodes `auto_mode: true` for tools_init. But `agent.auto_mode` comes from config.\n\nActually looking more carefully:\n- config default: `auto_mode: false`\n- agent uses `config.auto_mode` → `agent.auto_mode = false` by default\n- runner.rs checks `if agent.auto_mode { ... }` for phase detection\n\nSo auto_mode is DISABLED by default. The user needs to enable it. But the phase detection logic IS there (lines 313-318 — detect_task_phase_from_reasoning). So the code is wired, it's just off by default.\n\nBut wait — the tools_init hardcodes `auto_mode: true` (line 548). That's for the tools process, not for the agent's own mode. These are separate flags:\n- `agent.auto_mode` — controls agent's phase detection\n- `tools::AUTO_MODE` — controls tools auto-execution without confirmation\n\nOK so the issue is: auto_mode defaults to false. The user can't toggle it via slash commands because it needs to go through the agent.\n\nLet me now fix everything. Let me plan:\n\n1. **思考链**: Change HP client call to enable thinking (`false` → `true`)\n2. **面板标签**: Add `.title()` with ctx.tt() to chat and workspace blocks\n3. **Slash菜单**: Add more commands with i18n, make submenu items use tui_text\n4. **Auto mode**: Wire /auto command to toggle, enable thinking\n\nLet me start fixing these now.","signature":"3807a967-7b51-4688-b644-83fd4b6b9b30"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":185856,"output_tokens":1624,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"76620bb6-8d27-41b3-af1d-282d1b54d867","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:18:55.338Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
