{"parentUuid":"f274cc80-d051-4caf-9768-782054944495","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"5306e0b5-4a75-4c93-a38d-a0f90f1fb9aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, that still won't work. The borrow checker will still complain because `state.messages.clear()` borrows `state` mutably while the `send_to_agent` closure (which also borrows `state` mutably) is alive.\n\nBut actually, looking at the original code more carefully, the ORIGINAL code already had this potential issue. The original slash handlers (/quit, /lang, /model, /effort, /help) all touch `state.status_msg` while `send_to_agent` is alive. And it compiled fine. Why? Because those handlers DON'T call `send_to_agent`.\n\nThe issue is only with `/auto` and `/clear` which both modify state AND call send_to_agent. Let me check `/auto`:\n\n```rust\n\"/auto\" => {\n    state.auto_mode = !state.auto_mode;\n    save_dsx_config(\"auto_mode\", ...);\n    state.status_msg = format!(...);\n    send_to_agent(&t);\n}\n```\n\nThis touches `state.auto_mode`, `state.status_msg` (in the closure). This is the conflict.\n\nAnd /clear touches `state.messages`, `stream`, `state.status_msg`.\n\nThe fix: for /auto, don't call send_to_agent (since the toggle is local and saved to file). For /clear, manage state after the closure is dropped.\n\nActually, the simplest approach is to scope the closure tightly. Let me wrap the send_to_agent closure so it's dropped before the slash handlers that need state/stream.","signature":"5306e0b5-4a75-4c93-a38d-a0f90f1fb9aa"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":208128,"output_tokens":1906,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"