{"parentUuid":"4819ed80-e307-4830-abaa-cab3cff48d4b","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8309eff9-e184-4126-8fa6-8faf392305df","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking two questions:\n\n1. Why didn't the 400 error trigger a popup/dialog in the TUI?\n2. Is the old error popup and sudo authorization popup still working?\n\nLet me trace the error flow:\n\n1. HP gets a 400 error from the API\n2. HP sends `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"API 400 Bad Request: ...\"}` to the agent\n3. The agent receives this as `HpToAgent::Error { message }` and writes `AgentToTui::Error { message }` to the TUI\n4. The TUI receives `{\"type\":\"error\",...}` and should show it\n\nBut looking at the TUI's event loop, it only handles these frame types:\n- `content_delta`\n- `tool_progress`\n- `api_response`\n- `done`\n\nThere's NO handler for `error` frames! So when the agent sends an error frame, the TUI ignores it.\n\nFor the sudo/confirm popups, let me check if those are still wired. The popup rendering code exists in `render/popups.rs`, and the confirm/sudo input handlers exist in `input/`. But the key question is: does the agent actually send tool_confirm_req frames, and does the TUI handle them?\n\nLooking at the agent runner, it uses gates to check tool safety:\n```rust\nif let Some(err_msg) = gates::pre_tool_health_check(agent, name) {\n    let _ = agent.ctx.push_tool_result(id, &err_msg);\n    agent.health.record_error(name, &err_msg);\n    agent.tool_failures += 1;\n    continue;\n}\n```\n\nThe gates module checks the tool but doesn't ask for user confirmation. The old system had a confirm flow where dangerous tools would trigger a popup.\n\nLet me check if the tools process sends `ToolConfirmReq` frames and if the agent handles them.\n\nLooking at dsx-tools/src/lib.rs `handle_req`:\n```rust\nSafetyVerdict::Confirm(prompt) => {\n    return ipc::OutboundFrame::ToolConfirmReq {\n        id, tool_name: name.into(), action: action.into(),\n        danger_level: \"confirm\".into(), prompt,\n    };\n}\n```\n\nSo tools CAN send ToolConfirmReq. But the agent's runner.rs handles tool results:\n```rust\nlet tool_result: ToolsToAgent = match dsx_proto::read_frame(tools_reader) {\n    ...\n};\nlet (tr_id, tr_success, tr_content) = match tool_result {\n    ToolsToAgent::Result { ... } => ...\n    ToolsToAgent::ToolResultMessage { ... } => ...\n    ToolsToAgent::ToolError { ... } => ...\n    _other => continue, // skip Ready/Progress/ConfirmReq in tool loop\n};\n```\n\nThe `_other => continue` arm SKIPS ToolConfirmReq frames! So when tools asks for confirmation, the agent ignores it and hangs.\n\nThis is a significant issue. The confirmation flow requires:\n1. Agent receives ToolConfirmReq from tools\n2. Agent forwards it to TUI (need a new frame type or use existing ones)\n3. TUI shows popup\n4. User approves/rejects\n5. TUI sends response to agent\n6. Agent forwards to tools\n\nThis flow doesn't exist in the current runner.rs. The agent-rewire's report noted this:\n\n> 4. **`orchestrator::tool_dispatch::handle_confirm_tools/reject_tools/cancel_stream()`** — User confirmation flow for dangerous tools. The runner currently auto-executes all tools. Confirmation mode requires TUI interaction (task #4).\n\nLet me give the user a clear answer about what needs to be done.","signature":"8309eff9-e184-4126-8fa6-8faf392305df"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":296064,"output_tokens":1166,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"1617b046-b14f-4cb1-b2b3-9e9586d851f7","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:19:46.374Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"1617b046-b14f-4cb1-b2b3-9e9586d851f7","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8309eff9-e184-4126-8fa6-8faf392305df","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"两个问题的根因是同一个：**错误和确认流在类型迁移时被遗漏了**。\n\n## 1. 400 错误为什么没弹窗\n\nTUI 的事件循环只处理了这些帧类型：\n\n```\ncontent_delta  ← 流式内容\ntool_progress  ← 工具进度\napi_response   ← 最终响应\ndone           ← 回合结束\n```\n\n`error` 帧 **没有 handler**。Agent 确实发了 `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"API 400 ...\"}`，但 TUI 读到后不匹配任何分支，被忽略。\n\n## 2. sudo/确认弹窗还在吗\n\n弹窗渲染代码在（`render/popups.rs`）、输入处理在（`input/confirm.rs` `input/sudo.rs`），但 **pipeline 断了**：\n\n- 工具进程发出 `ToolConfirmReq` → Agent 收到后 `_other => continue` **直接跳过**\n- 确认流需要：Agent → TUI 转发确认请求 → TUI 弹窗 → 用户选择 → TUI → Agent → Tools 回复\n- 当前 `runner.rs` 里这一步完全不存在\n\n## 修复需要的改动\n\n| 改动 | 位置 |\n|------|------|\n| TUI 处理 `error` 帧 → 显示错误弹窗/状态栏 | `lib.rs` 事件循环 |\n| Agent 处理 `ToolConfirmReq` → 转发给 TUI | `runner.rs` tool loop |\n| TUI 处理确认帧 → 弹窗 → 用户选择 → 回复 Agent | `lib.rs` + `state.rs` |\n| Agent 收到确认回复 → 转发给 Tools | `runner.rs` |\n\n要现在修吗？"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":296064,"output_tokens":1166,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b8a2d2a0-529a-4187-9615-5a72ad764072","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:19:57.562Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
