{"parentUuid":"0e0429f9-5fea-4ded-a49e-29dba023e9f3","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8cd35dd9-2492-4c8f-a7d4-45cc1c55007f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to design the fix plan and spawn a Sonnet agent to implement it. Let me create a clear design spec and spawn a subagent.\n\nThe two issues are:\n1. TUI doesn't handle `error` frames from agent → need to show error popup/status bar\n2. Tool confirmation flow (danger/sudo popups) is broken → need to wire Agent→TUI→Agent→Tools\n\nLet me design the fix and spawn a single Sonnet agent.","signature":"8cd35dd9-2492-4c8f-a7d4-45cc1c55007f"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":296064,"output_tokens":1228,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"47323d8c-17d7-4238-b78f-e121fd00c2b4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:20:36.446Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"47323d8c-17d7-4238-b78f-e121fd00c2b4","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8cd35dd9-2492-4c8f-a7d4-45cc1c55007f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_mH998fbwccup5fnwq2053860","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix TUI error/confirm flow","prompt":"Your task: fix two broken flows in the DSX TUI — error display and tool confirmation popups.\n\n## Context\n\nDSX is a 5-process AI coding assistant. The TUI (`crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`) reads Agent frames from stdout and renders them. Two flows are broken:\n\n### Issue 1: Error frames not handled by TUI\n\nAgent sends `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}` frames, but TUI ignores them. Need to handle them.\n\nThe TUI event loop is in `lib.rs` around line 220-235. It checks `trimmed.contains(\"\\\"content_delta\\\"\")`, `\"tool_progress\"`, `\"api_response\"`, `\"done\"`. Need to add `\"error\"` handling: set `state.status_msg` to the error message and `state.mode = Mode::Chat`.\n\n### Issue 2: Tool confirmation flow missing\n\nThe pipeline:\n```\nTools → Agent: ToolConfirmReq (danger/sudo prompt)\nAgent → TUI:  forward confirm request  \nTUI:          show popup, user picks yes/no\nTUI → Agent:  send confirm response\nAgent → Tools: forward confirm response\n```\n\nCurrent state:\n- Render code exists: `render/popups.rs` has `render_auth_popup`, `render_danger_popup`\n- Input code exists: `input/confirm.rs` has `handle_confirm_key`, `input/sudo.rs` has `handle_sudo_key`  \n- TUI state has: `state.pending_tools`, `state.sudo_password`, `state.mode` (ToolConfirm, DangerPrompt, SudoPrompt modes exist in `mode.rs`)\n- **Missing**: Agent runner (`runner.rs`) skips ToolConfirmReq frames with `_other => continue`\n\n### What to fix\n\n**File 1: `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`** — Event loop additions:\n1. Add `\"error\"` frame handling: set `state.status_msg` and `state.mode = Mode::Chat`\n2. Add `\"tool_confirm_req\"` frame handling: extract id, tool_name, action, danger_level, prompt → set `state.pending_tools`, switch `state.mode` to `Mode::ToolConfirm` or `Mode::DangerPrompt`\n3. In the keyboard handler (`handle_chat_key`), when mode is ToolConfirm/DangerPrompt/SudoPrompt, call the appropriate confirm handler instead of chat handler\n4. When user confirms/rejects: send a `tool_confirm_resp` JSON frame to agent_writer\n\n**File 2: `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`** — Tool loop additions:\n1. After reading `ToolsToAgent::ToolConfirmReq`, forward it to TUI as a custom JSON frame\n2. Read TUI response from stdin (the confirm/reject answer)\n3. Forward the answer to Tools as `AgentToTools::ConfirmResp`\n\n### Key types already exist\n\nIn `crates/dsx-proto/src/lib.rs`:\n- `AgentToTools::ConfirmResp { id, approved }` — send to tools\n- `ToolsToAgent::ToolConfirmReq { id, tool_name, action, danger_level, prompt }` — receive from tools\n\nIn `crates/dsx-tui/src/state.rs`:\n- `AppState.pending_tools: Vec<(ToolCall, SafetyLevel, String)>` \n- `AppState.sudo_password: String`\n\nIn `crates/dsx-tui/src/mode.rs`:\n- `Mode::ToolConfirm`, `Mode::DangerPrompt`, `Mode::SudoPrompt`\n\n### Design rules\n- Error frames: just show in status bar, no popup needed\n- Confirm flow: \n  - Agent receives ToolConfirmReq → forwards to TUI as `{\"type\":\"tool_confirm_req\",\"id\":\"...\",\"tool_name\":\"...\",\"action\":\"...\",\"danger_level\":\"confirm|danger\",\"prompt\":\"...\"}`\n  - TUI receives → sets state.pending_tools, switches to ToolConfirm/DangerPrompt mode, renders popup\n  - User presses Enter → TUI sends `{\"type\":\"tool_confirm_resp\",\"id\":\"...\",\"approved\":true}` to agent stdin\n  - User presses Esc → TUI sends `{\"type\":\"tool_confirm_resp\",\"id\":\"...\",\"approved\":false}`\n  - Agent reads the response → sends `AgentToTools::ConfirmResp { id, approved }` to tools\n- Do NOT create new modules, only modify existing files\n- Do NOT run cargo test\n- After changes, verify `cargo build --release` compiles\n\nRead the files first, then implement. Keep changes minimal and surgical.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"fix-error-confirm"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":296064,"output_tokens":1228,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"557fcb9d-20f5-420c-87ec-e51cbed0ff32","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:21:10.687Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
