{"parentUuid":"d08d8545-de0e-4fa3-af46-03c5827b43c3","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"f96811c5-d1a1-4e64-a5d0-29c2916490dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_BUOCkiEhfXOYhZyiL4bd3383","type":"tool_result","content":"89:                    std::time::Duration::from_millis(200),\n111:    for _ in 0..50 {\n113:        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(100));\n467:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(33));\n469:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50));\n620:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(33));\n622:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50));","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8d9ac9b5-fff4-4cd5-b1bc-958e9f9ab446","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:42:35.583Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"89:                    std::time::Duration::from_millis(200),\n111:    for _ in 0..50 {\n113:        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(100));\n467:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(33));\n469:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50));\n620:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(33));\n622:            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50));","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d08d8545-de0e-4fa3-af46-03c5827b43c3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"8d9ac9b5-fff4-4cd5-b1bc-958e9f9ab446","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"230eed53-fd30-4785-8f55-0d025fbc727c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The render loop sleeps 33ms when awaiting (actively waiting for a response) and 50ms when idle. That's ~30fps during streaming — more than enough for smooth streaming.\n\nOK so the thinking chain IS streaming, the render IS showing it, the timing IS fast enough. The issue must be something else.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the user's message: \"为什么思考链路不是流式的\" — \"why isn't the thinking chain streaming?\"\n\nMaybe the issue is that during my earlier tests, the reasoning deltas came BEFORE any content deltas, and the TUI shows \"Generating response...\" spinner until content arrives. The user might see:\n1. Reasoning deltas arrive → thinking block shows in streaming area\n2. No content yet → spinner also shows \"Generating response...\"\n3. Content deltas arrive → content shows below thinking block\n4. Done → everything moves to completed messages\n\nThis IS streaming. But maybe the issue is that the TUI only renders the LAST 12 lines of reasoning during streaming (line 183: `let start = rlines.len().saturating_sub(12)`). If the reasoning is very long, the user only sees the tail end.\n\nActually, I think the real issue might be simpler. Let me check if the DeepSeek API actually returns separate `reasoning_content` in the streaming response. The `thinking` parameter was set to `true`, but DeepSeek's API might handle reasoning differently.\n\nLet me check the streaming output format. In my test, I saw:\n```\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"\",\"reasoning\":\"我们\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"\",\"reasoning\":\"被\"}\n```\n\nThis means reasoning IS being sent as content_delta frames. The TUI processes them correctly. The render shows them.\n\nI think the pipeline is actually working correctly. The reasoning IS streaming. Let me just tell the user that and ask what specifically they're seeing (or not seeing).\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the chat.rs render code one more time:\n\n```rust\nif *ctx.mode == Mode::Streaming {\n    if !ctx.stream_reasoning.is_empty() {\n        ...\n        lines.extend(render_thinking_block(...));\n    }\n    if !ctx.stream_content.is_empty() {\n        let cd = if ctx.stream_content.len() > 2000 {\n            let cut = char_boundary(&ctx.stream_content, ctx.stream_content.len().saturating_sub(2000));\n            &ctx.stream_content[cut..]\n        } else { &ctx.stream_content };\n        lines.extend(render_message_content(cd, w));\n    }\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe thinking block is rendered BEFORE the content. Both are rendered. This should show reasoning at the top, then content below.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: the thinking block always appears. Even if reasoning is empty, as long as mode is Streaming. Wait no — it checks `if !ctx.stream_reasoning.is_empty()`.\n\nOK, I'm confident the pipeline is correct. The reasoning IS streaming. Let me just confirm with the user what they're seeing vs what they expect.\n\nActually, I just realized there might be an issue with the AGENT's forwarding of ContentDelta. Let me check: does the agent actually forward the reasoning in the ContentDelta to the TUI?\n\nFrom the agent runner:\n```rust\nHpToAgent::ContentDelta { delta, reasoning } => {\n    let _ = dsx_proto::write_frame(tui_writer, &AgentToTui::ContentDelta {\n        delta: delta.clone(),\n        reasoning: reasoning.clone(),\n    });\n    if let Some(ref r) = reasoning {\n        agent.stream_reasoning.push_str(r);\n    }\n    agent.stream_content.push_str(&delta);\n}\n```\n\nAnd `AgentToTui::ContentDelta`:\n```rust\n#[serde(rename = \"content_delta\")]\nContentDelta {\n    delta: String,\n    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    reasoning: Option<String>,\n},\n```\n\nThis serializes to `{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"\",\"reasoning\":\"我们\"}`. The TUI reads this:\n```rust\nlet delta = v.get(\"delta\").and_then(|d| d.as_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\nlet reasoning = v.get(\"reasoning\").and_then(|r| r.as_str());\nstream.apply_payload(delta, reasoning, &[]);\n```\n\nThis all looks correct.\n\nAnd in `apply_payload`:\n```rust\npub fn apply_payload(&mut self, delta: &str, reasoning: Option<&str>, progress: &[(String, String)]) {\n    self.content.push_str(delta);\n    if let Some(r) = reasoning {\n        self.reasoning.push_str(r);\n    }\n    self.tool_progress = progress.to_vec();\n    self.last_activity = Instant::now();\n}\n```\n\nThis pushes delta to content and reasoning to reasoning. Both accumulate.\n\nSo the reasoning IS streaming. The thinking block IS rendering. I think the pipeline is fully functional.\n\nLet me tell the user that the pipeline IS working — reasoning is being sent from the API, forwarded by HP and Agent, and rendered by TUI. The thinking block appears at the top of streaming content. If they're not seeing it, there might be a specific rendering issue or the thinking might be collapsed/obscured.\n\nWait, actually, maybe the user is asking a different question. Maybe they want the thinking to be shown in a DIFFERENT way — like as collapsed-by-default expandable sections in the final message, rather than always visible. That's how Claude Code shows thinking — it's collapsed with a \"Thinking\" header that you can expand.\n\nIn the current DSX TUI, the thinking block is always visible (it's not collapsible). Maybe the user wants collapsible thinking blocks.\n\nOr maybe the issue is that during streaming, the thinking block appears but the content area is empty (just spinner), so the user thinks nothing is happening. Actually, that's the RIGHT behavior — reasoning comes first, then content.\n\nI think the most productive thing is to just confirm that it IS working and ask what the user expects.","signature":"230eed53-fd30-4785-8f55-0d025fbc727c"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":234,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":312704,"output_tokens":1478,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c2d65459-3589-4027-ab37-35c4cc1a5631","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:43:17.345Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"c2d65459-3589-4027-ab37-35c4cc1a5631","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"230eed53-fd30-4785-8f55-0d025fbc727c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"推理链**是流式的**。225 条 `content_delta` 包含 reasoning 数据，逐 token 从 DeepSeek API → HP → Agent → TUI → `stream.reasoning` → 渲染为「Thinking」框。\n\n当前行为：\n1. 推理 token 到达 → 实时显示在「Thinking」框内（最后 12 行，MUTED+斜体样式）\n2. 内容 token 到达 → 显示在 Thinking 框下方\n3. `done` → 两条都存入已完成消息，Thinking 块保留\n\n你说的「不是流式的」是指：\n- **A**：完全看不到 Thinking 框？\n- **B**：Thinking 框出现了但是一次性出现（没有逐 token 展开）？\n- **C**：想要可折叠的 Thinking（像 Claude Code 那样默认收起）？\n\n确认一下我继续调。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":234,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":312704,"output_tokens":1478,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"60beec2c-421b-4253-bc87-5fd739d425e9","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:43:23.596Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
