{"parentUuid":"aef5f80c-f4ef-465b-a92c-605dedf18586","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"28919d18-d248-4244-81fa-1e8a02c1ec6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_KBiF1TjnqiAlW9TPF9yh4970","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix streaming render blocking","prompt":"Fix: TUI render doesn't update during content streaming — all content_delta frames are processed in a tight loop before one render.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`, the `run_impl` function's main event loop structure:\n\n```\nloop {\n    while awaiting {\n        read_line from agent  // processes ALL buffered frames without render\n        if content_delta { update stream; dirty = true }\n        if done { finalize; awaiting = false }\n    }\n    if dirty { draw; dirty = false }  // ONE render for ALL frames\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe `BufReader` on the agent's stdout pipe buffers multiple lines. When HP sends 50+ content_delta frames quickly, BufReader reads them all at once. The `while awaiting` loop processes all 50 without rendering once. User sees 50 frames of content pop in at once.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a render inside the `while awaiting` loop: after every few frames (say every frame or every 4ms), call `terminal.draw()`. \n\nThe simplest approach: after processing each content_delta/tool_progress/error frame (anything that sets dirty=true), call draw immediately:\n\n```rust\nif dirty {\n    if terminal.draw(|f| crate::render::render_all(f, &state, &conn, &stream)).is_err() {\n        break;\n    }\n    dirty = false;\n}\n```\n\nAdd this render block inside the `while awaiting` loop, right after updating stream and setting dirty=true. Do NOT add it for `api_response` or `done` frames (those are terminal frames).\n\nAlso, the TUI uses a separate `agent_reader` (raw BufReader from child stdout), and reads raw JSON lines. Make sure the render inside the loop doesn't conflict with the existing render outside the loop.\n\n## Files to modify\n\nOnly `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`:\n- Find the `while awaiting` loop\n- After each content_delta/tool_progress/error frame processing, add immediate render\n- Keep the existing render after the while loop for keyboard processing\n\n## Build verify\n\nAfter changes: `cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"fix-streaming-render"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":226,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":314368,"output_tokens":4222,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"28db2e7f-332f-4c47-b42e-d75cd05f1ef2","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:47:07.075Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"28db2e7f-332f-4c47-b42e-d75cd05f1ef2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"4727ce0c-eec9-47ff-8024-2d4e2558ccec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_KBiF1TjnqiAlW9TPF9yh4970","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully.\nagent_id: fix-streaming-render@dsx-integration\nname: fix-streaming-render\nteam_name: dsx-integration\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"6c6b9c20-25b5-4148-a363-4c72b90e7de6","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:47:07.097Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"Fix: TUI render doesn't update during content streaming — all content_delta frames are processed in a tight loop before one render.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`, the `run_impl` function's main event loop structure:\n\n```\nloop {\n    while awaiting {\n        read_line from agent  // processes ALL buffered frames without render\n        if content_delta { update stream; dirty = true }\n        if done { finalize; awaiting = false }\n    }\n    if dirty { draw; dirty = false }  // ONE render for ALL frames\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe `BufReader` on the agent's stdout pipe buffers multiple lines. When HP sends 50+ content_delta frames quickly, BufReader reads them all at once. The `while awaiting` loop processes all 50 without rendering once. User sees 50 frames of content pop in at once.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a render inside the `while awaiting` loop: after every few frames (say every frame or every 4ms), call `terminal.draw()`. \n\nThe simplest approach: after processing each content_delta/tool_progress/error frame (anything that sets dirty=true), call draw immediately:\n\n```rust\nif dirty {\n    if terminal.draw(|f| crate::render::render_all(f, &state, &conn, &stream)).is_err() {\n        break;\n    }\n    dirty = false;\n}\n```\n\nAdd this render block inside the `while awaiting` loop, right after updating stream and setting dirty=true. Do NOT add it for `api_response` or `done` frames (those are terminal frames).\n\nAlso, the TUI uses a separate `agent_reader` (raw BufReader from child stdout), and reads raw JSON lines. Make sure the render inside the loop doesn't conflict with the existing render outside the loop.\n\n## Files to modify\n\nOnly `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`:\n- Find the `while awaiting` loop\n- After each content_delta/tool_progress/error frame processing, add immediate render\n- Keep the existing render after the while loop for keyboard processing\n\n## Build verify\n\nAfter changes: `cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","teammate_id":"fix-streaming-render@dsx-integration","agent_id":"fix-streaming-render@dsx-integration","agent_type":"sonnet","model":"claude-opus-4-7","name":"fix-streaming-render","color":"orange","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"dsx-integration","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28db2e7f-332f-4c47-b42e-d75cd05f1ef2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"6c6b9c20-25b5-4148-a363-4c72b90e7de6","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"28919d18-d248-4244-81fa-1e8a02c1ec6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01_RQEMYxb2tjoKYuB9hhFx6054","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix session isolation","prompt":"Fix: New TUI windows don't create isolated sessions — old sessions are always restored.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`, the `init_session()` function:\n\n```rust\nfn init_session(agent: &mut AgentState) {\n    let lives = session::find_live_sessions();\n    if let Some(meta) = lives.first() {\n        // ALWAYS restore first live session\n        agent.session_seed = file.seed.clone();\n        ...\n    }\n    // Fresh session (only if no live sessions found)\n    agent.session_seed = session::generate_seed();\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nEvery time a new TUI window connects to the agent, it finds old live sessions and restores them. So opening 5 TUI windows gives you the same conversation in all 5.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **New session by default**: Always generate a fresh session. Don't auto-restore.\n2. **Session restore only via flag**: Only restore if `--resume` is passed (the CLI flag already exists in `dsx-tui` but isn't forwarded to the agent).\n3. **Session seed isolation**: Each new window should get a unique session seed. The session files at `~/.config/dsx/sessions/` should be separated by seed.\n\nImplementation:\n- In `runner.rs`, change `init_session()` to always create a fresh session\n- Move the restore logic to a separate function that's only called when a `TuiToAgent` resume frame is received\n- Or: add a simple flag/env var that the TUI passes to tell the agent \"this is a new window, don't restore\"\n\nSimplest approach: just always generate a new session seed. Remove the auto-restore logic from `init_session()`. Keep the restore code in a separate function for future use.\n\n## Files to modify\n\n`crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`:\n- Modify `init_session()` to always create fresh session (remove the `find_live_sessions` and restore block)\n- Keep the restore code but move it to a separate function `fn try_restore_session(agent: &mut AgentState) -> bool` for future `--resume` use\n\n## Build verify\n\n`cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"fix-session-isolation"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":226,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":314368,"output_tokens":4222,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8c8842c1-b19c-4425-9da5-f183b6deb784","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:47:24.900Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"8c8842c1-b19c-4425-9da5-f183b6deb784","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"4727ce0c-eec9-47ff-8024-2d4e2558ccec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01_RQEMYxb2tjoKYuB9hhFx6054","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully.\nagent_id: fix-session-isolation@dsx-integration\nname: fix-session-isolation\nteam_name: dsx-integration\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"d8212386-c85a-4b63-89b0-578bd03295bb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:47:24.926Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"Fix: New TUI windows don't create isolated sessions — old sessions are always restored.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`, the `init_session()` function:\n\n```rust\nfn init_session(agent: &mut AgentState) {\n    let lives = session::find_live_sessions();\n    if let Some(meta) = lives.first() {\n        // ALWAYS restore first live session\n        agent.session_seed = file.seed.clone();\n        ...\n    }\n    // Fresh session (only if no live sessions found)\n    agent.session_seed = session::generate_seed();\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nEvery time a new TUI window connects to the agent, it finds old live sessions and restores them. So opening 5 TUI windows gives you the same conversation in all 5.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **New session by default**: Always generate a fresh session. Don't auto-restore.\n2. **Session restore only via flag**: Only restore if `--resume` is passed (the CLI flag already exists in `dsx-tui` but isn't forwarded to the agent).\n3. **Session seed isolation**: Each new window should get a unique session seed. The session files at `~/.config/dsx/sessions/` should be separated by seed.\n\nImplementation:\n- In `runner.rs`, change `init_session()` to always create a fresh session\n- Move the restore logic to a separate function that's only called when a `TuiToAgent` resume frame is received\n- Or: add a simple flag/env var that the TUI passes to tell the agent \"this is a new window, don't restore\"\n\nSimplest approach: just always generate a new session seed. Remove the auto-restore logic from `init_session()`. Keep the restore code in a separate function for future use.\n\n## Files to modify\n\n`crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`:\n- Modify `init_session()` to always create fresh session (remove the `find_live_sessions` and restore block)\n- Keep the restore code but move it to a separate function `fn try_restore_session(agent: &mut AgentState) -> bool` for future `--resume` use\n\n## Build verify\n\n`cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","teammate_id":"fix-session-isolation@dsx-integration","agent_id":"fix-session-isolation@dsx-integration","agent_type":"sonnet","model":"claude-opus-4-7","name":"fix-session-isolation","color":"pink","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"dsx-integration","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c8842c1-b19c-4425-9da5-f183b6deb784","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
