{"parentUuid":"8d5380d7-deea-47cb-84e8-c04842562bf9","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"cfcc131a-e95f-4cb7-97b2-09c6c5052f77","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is showing a bug in the TUI display. The chat panel is showing garbled/overlapping content — it looks like tool definitions or system prompts are being rendered in the chat area where conversation messages should be. The right side \"Workspace\" panel shows fragments of text about tool calling rules.\n\nThe user suspects that tool descriptions are being injected into the messages array as non-system-role messages, or that the system prompt is being mixed into the conversation display.\n\nLet me check what's happening. The key clue is that the display shows text about tool calling rules, XML tool call syntax, etc. This looks like the system prompt or tool definitions being rendered in the chat area.\n\nThis is likely because:\n1. The `prepare_and_compact` function builds a system prompt that includes tool definitions\n2. The system prompt (or parts of it) might be leaking into `agent.messages` \n3. Or the TUI is somehow displaying system-level messages as chat messages\n\nLet me also check: the filter I added (`m.role != \"system\"`) only filters messages sent to HP. But `agent.messages` might still contain system-role messages from the context building. The TUI displays `state.messages` which is synced from the agent.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the agent code, after `push_user`, `sync_messages()` is called. This syncs `agent.messages` from `agent.ctx`. The ContextAssembler might include system messages. Then when the TUI receives messages (via Done), the completed messages include system messages.\n\nBut wait — the TUI doesn't receive messages from the agent. The TUI manages its own `state.messages` locally. The TUI pushes user messages and assistant messages locally. The agent maintains its own copy of messages for context management.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be different. The display shows text about tool descriptions and calling conventions. This suggests the system prompt is being shown in the chat panel. Let me check how the system prompt is built...\n\nThe `prepare_and_compact` function builds a system prompt string. This is sent to HP as the `system` field. But somehow it might be leaking into the display.\n\nLet me check the render_workspace function and the chat rendering to see if there's a mix-up.\n\nActually, looking at the user's screenshot description more carefully, they're seeing \"tool_use 和 tool_result 必须在消息中相邻\" — this is text about Anthropic API rules. This is likely part of the system prompt that's being displayed in the chat panel.\n\nHow would system prompts get into the chat panel? Let me trace:\n1. The TUI pushes user messages to `state.messages` \n2. The agent returns assistant messages that get pushed to `state.messages`\n3. The TUI renders `state.messages` in the chat panel\n\nSo if system prompt text appears in the chat, it must be in `state.messages`. This would happen if the agent sends back a response that includes system prompt text.\n\nOR — the issue might be that the agent is sending back TOOL CALLS in the api_response, and the TUI is rendering them in a weird way. The tool calls have function names and arguments that might look like system prompts.\n\nWait, actually, looking at the screen content again:\n- \"的一部分，没有工具调用上下文\" - \"part of it, no tool calling context\"\n- \"根据规则，我需要'直接调用工具，描述工具不是调用'\" - \"according to rules, I need to 'directly call tools, describing tools is not calling'\"\n- \"因此我需要实际调用一个工具\" - \"therefore I need to actually call a tool\"\n\nThis looks like the MODEL'S RESPONSE TEXT — the LLM is generating text about how to call tools, rather than actually calling tools. This is not a system prompt leak. This is the model's output!\n\nThe model seems to be in a weird state where it's talking ABOUT tool calling instead of actually calling tools. This could be:\n1. The system prompt tells the model to use tools but the model is confused\n2. The system prompt format is wrong (missing tool definitions)\n3. The model is `deepseek-v4-flash` which might not support tool calling well\n\nThe user asks: \"是不是把工具的简介拼凑到role不是system了？\"\n\nThis translates to: \"Did you put tool descriptions into a role that's not system?\"\n\nLet me check: the system prompt is built by `prepare_and_compact`. The tool definitions are NOT sent to the model (the `tools: None` in the api_chat request). So the model doesn't know what tools are available!\n\nThat's the bug! The agent sends `tools: None` in the api_chat:\n```rust\nlet chat = AgentToHp::ApiChat {\n    model: agent.config.model.clone(),\n    system: Some(system),\n    messages: messages_json,\n    effort: agent.config.effort.clone(),\n    max_tokens: Some(agent.config.max_tokens),\n    tools: None,  // <-- NO TOOLS!\n};\n```\n\nWithout tool definitions, the model might still try to \"call\" tools by describing them in text, which is what we see.\n\nBut wait, during the tool-calling loop, when the model needs to call tools, the agent should include tool definitions. Let me check if the tools field is populated...\n\nActually, looking at the code, `tools: None` is hardcoded. The agent should populate this with the actual tool definitions from `agent.tools` or from the tools process.\n\nBut the tools were initially registered — the agent sends `tools_init` and receives `tools_ready` with tool definitions. These should be available.\n\nLet me check if there's code to populate the tools field. Let me search.","signature":"cfcc131a-e95f-4cb7-97b2-09c6c5052f77"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":321792,"output_tokens":1326,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation