s tool calling format.\n\nActually, looking at the model output — the model is generating `<tool_use>` XML tags in the TEXT content. This is NOT how Anthropic tool use works. In Anthropic API, tool use is a separate content block type (`\"type\": \"tool_use\"`), not embedded in text.\n\nThe model is CONFUSED about the tool calling format. The system prompt tells it about `tool_use` and `tool_result` (which are Anthropic content block types) but doesn't explain the SYNTAX. The model might interpret this as \"use XML tags\".\n\nThe fix: update the system prompt to be clearer about the tool calling format, or check if DeepSeek's API actually supports Anthropic tool use correctly.\n\nActually, I think the real issue might be that DeepSeek's API does NOT properly support Anthropic's tool use format. Instead, DeepSeek uses OpenAI's function calling format, which is different.\n\nLet me check: what does the HP's client.rs do with tool calls in the response?","signature":"9dddcb42-ed9d-49d3-aed4-e60ef0073a5c"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":681,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":335104,"output_tokens":742,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"42492e5b-e619-4187-a604-3911555aac2b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:00:45.274Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
