{"parentUuid":"5fb88444-905d-4010-b4d7-e646db9a9e61","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"99a5b996-9384-4671-aece-8d1ecde61238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the URL for DeepSeek becomes `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic/messages`. This is the Anthropic-compatible endpoint.\n\nNow the question is: does DeepSeek's `/anthropic/messages` endpoint actually support Anthropic tool use (`tool_use` content blocks)?\n\nLooking at DeepSeek's API documentation, their anthropic-compatible endpoint does support tools in the request. But the response format might differ — they might return tool calls in OpenAI format instead of Anthropic format.\n\nActually, I think the issue is simpler. The model is receiving tool definitions but doesn't know HOW to return them. In the Anthropic protocol, the model emits `content` as an array of content blocks, where tool calls are `{\"type\": \"tool_use\", ...}` blocks. But DeepSeek might not train their models to use this format.\n\nLet me check: does the DeepSeek API actually return Anthropic-format tool use content blocks? The HP client expects `AnthropicStreamEvent::ContentBlockStart` with `AnthropicContentBlockStart::ToolUse`. If DeepSeek doesn't emit these, the HP would never see tool calls.\n\nWait, but the model is generating `<tool_use>` XML in the text content. That means the model is NOT using Anthropic content blocks. It's writing text.\n\nBut actually, the HP client parses SSE events. If the model uses Anthropic tool use, the SSE events would include `content_block_start` with type `tool_use`. If the model instead writes text, the SSE events would be `content_block_delta` with type `text`.\n\nSo the question is: does DeepSeek's model support Anthropic tool use? The answer might be NO for `deepseek-v4-flash`.\n\nBut wait — the deepseek chat API (non-Anthropic) supports function calling via `tool_calls` in the response. Maybe we need to use the non-Anthropic endpoint, or use a different tool format.\n\nHmm, actually, let me look at this from a different angle. The HP already has a converter (`converter.rs` + `client.rs`) that handles the DeepSeek API. Maybe we need to check if DeepSeek's response format includes `tool_calls` in the OpenAI format, and the converter needs to map that to Anthropic's `tool_use` format.\n\nActually, looking at the HP's StreamEvent processing in `handle_api_chat_streaming`:\n```rust\nStreamEvent::Done { raw_message, stop_reason: sr, usage } => {\n    if let Some(text) = raw_message.content {\n        full_content = text;\n    }\n    let mut tool_calls: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n    if let Some(tcs) = raw_message.tool_calls {\n        for tc in tcs {\n            tool_calls.push(serde_json::json!({\n                \"id\": tc.id,\n                \"name\": tc.function.name,\n                \"arguments\": tc.function.arguments,\n            }));\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nThe HP DOES check for `raw_message.tool_calls` (which is `Option<Vec<ToolCall>>` in the Message type). But the Message type has `tool_calls: Option<Vec<ToolCall>>` which is the OpenAI format.\n\nSo: the HP's client.rs parses SSE events into Anthropic content blocks, then assembles them into a Message with `tool_calls` in OpenAI format. This should work IF the model returns tool_use content blocks.\n\nBut if the model returns TEXT instead of tool_use content blocks (because it doesn't understand Anthropic tool calling), the content would just be text with `<tool_use>` XML, and no tool_calls would be populated.\n\nThe fix options:\n1. Switch the model to one that supports Anthropic tool use\n2. Add a parser that detects XML `<tool_use>` in text content and converts to proper tool calls\n3. Change the API endpoint to use OpenAI function calling format instead\n\nOption 2 is a good pragmatic solution. Let me check if the deepseek-chat (OpenAI-compatible) endpoint would work better.\n\nActually, looking at the user's config, the base URL is `https://api.deepseek.com` and the converter adds `/anthropic/messages`. This endpoint is an Anthropic-compatible wrapper. But DeepSeek's models are primarily trained for OpenAI function calling format.\n\nI think the best pragmatic fix is: the agent should detect when the model outputs XML-style tool calls in text, parse them out, and execute the tools. This way we don't depend on the model supporting Anthropic tool use.\n\nBut actually, let me first check: does the `deepseek-v4-pro` model support Anthropic tool use? Or does this need to be a deepseek-chat model?\n\nActually, I just realized something. The problem might be that the model name is wrong. The user uses `deepseek-v4-flash` which might be a chat model with limited tool use support. Let me check if there are better models available.\n\nHmm, but this is getting complex. Let me focus on the pragmatic fix: parse XML tool calls from text content.\n\nLet me spawn a sonnet agent to implement this.","signature":"99a5b996-9384-4671-aece-8d1ecde61238"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":337408,"output_tokens":1970,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"54baf50f-7c9e-4a93-a7ff-1b7af7fdaf29","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:01:45.676Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
