{"parentUuid":"e308c33b-5c60-45de-a81d-5f5e398dffe2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"99a5b996-9384-4671-aece-8d1ecde61238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_ju7eSYzNmiLAHWxMjqxJ3722","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Parse XML tool calls from text","prompt":"Fix: DeepSeek v4 models don't support Anthropic's native `tool_use` content blocks. Instead, they output tool calls as XML in the text content like:\n\n```xml\n<tool_use>\n<tool_name>context7_query</tool_name>\n最新内核变动\n</tool_use>\n```\n\nThe HP/Agent need to parse this XML format from the text response and convert to proper tool calls.\n\n## How it works now\n\nThe HP (`crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs`) receives API response via `StreamEvent::Done { raw_message }`. The `raw_message.content` contains text. `raw_message.tool_calls` is empty because DeepSeek didn't return proper Anthropic tool_use blocks.\n\nThe agent (`crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`) receives the HpToAgent response and processes it. Tool calls are expected in `HpToAgent::ApiResponse { tool_calls, ... }`.\n\n## Fix: Parse XML tool calls from text content\n\nIn the HP's `handle_api_chat_streaming` function, after receiving the final `api_response` (or in the agent after receiving HpToAgent::ApiResponse), parse the text content for XML tool calls.\n\nAdd a function `parse_xml_tool_calls(content: &str) -> Vec<serde_json::Value>` that:\n1. Finds `<tool_use>` ... `</tool_use>` blocks\n2. Extracts `<tool_name>NAME</tool_name>` \n3. The remaining text between `</tool_name>` and `</tool_use>` is the arguments (JSON or plain text)\n4. Generates unique IDs for each tool call\n5. Returns Vec of `{\"id\": \"...\", \"name\": \"NAME\", \"arguments\": \"...\"}` in anthropic flat format\n\nAlso strip the XML blocks from the visible content so users don't see the raw XML in the chat.\n\n### Where to add\n\nOption A (simpler): Add to `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs` in the api_response handler:\n- After `HpToAgent::ApiResponse { content, tool_calls, ... }`, if `tool_calls` is None/empty AND content contains `<tool_use>`, parse XML tool calls\n- Add parsed tool calls to the response\n- Strip XML blocks from content\n\nOption B: Add to `crates/dsx-hp/src/runner.rs` in both `handle_api_chat` and `handle_api_chat_streaming`\n\nDo Option A — it's simpler and in one place.\n\n### Implementation\n\nIn `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`, after the api_response is received:\n```rust\n// Parse XML tool calls if native tool_calls is empty\nlet parsed_tool_calls = if parsed.is_empty() && content.contains(\"<tool_use>\") {\n    parse_xml_tool_calls(&content)\n} else {\n    parsed\n};\n// Then use parsed_tool_calls instead of parsed\n```\n\nAnd strip XML blocks from the visible content before showing to user.\n\n### Files to modify\n- `crates/dsx-agent/src/runner.rs`: Add `parse_xml_tool_calls()` function + wire it into api_response handler\n\n### Build\n`cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"sonnet","name":"fix-xml-tool-calls"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":337408,"output_tokens":1970,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"a7382f82-9838-4842-aa9d-4a056b5fd808","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:02:12.170Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
