{"parentUuid":"3540af7f-2127-4647-80ea-2dfdad5331a2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"c33bf1dd-1149-46f0-8295-0472154b5bde","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01_RUhZc3i28CUPHa3VcRCU5706","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/api/create-chat-completion","prompt":"DeepSeek的原生chat completion API文档。提取：1. 工具调用(function calling)的请求格式 2. 响应格式（tool_calls字段结构） 3. 如何发送工具定义 4. 工具结果如何回传"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":343680,"output_tokens":288,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"640536db-824e-4ef6-8947-9e3db60aa56f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:09:40.267Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"3540af7f-2127-4647-80ea-2dfdad5331a2","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"3c322f2e-e8d0-4322-b3c0-e6e3c6a59c0c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_lhtsSxM9cWY8jbqiMgJw4784","type":"tool_result","content":"# DeepSeek Anthropic 兼容 API 要点\n\n## 1. 支持的端点\n\n文档中仅明确提及一个端点：messages endpoint。Base URL 为 `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic`。采用 Anthropic SDK 进行调用（`client.messages.create(...)`），未提及 /v1/chat/completions 或其他 Anthropic 专有端点（如 /v1/messages/batches）是否支持，也未列举完整端点列表。\n\n## 2. 工具调用 (Tool Use) 工作机制\n\n工具调用采用 Anthropic 原生格式，而非 OpenAI function calling 格式。具体表现为：\n\n- **tools 数组**：支持 `name`、`input_schema`、`description` 三个字段完全可用；`cache_control` 被忽略。\n- **tool_choice**：`none`、`auto`、`any`、`tool` 四种模式均标记为 \"Supported\"，但 `disable_parallel_tool_use` 在所有模式下均被忽略。\n- **消息中的 tool_use block**：`id`、`input`、`name` 三个子字段完全支持。\n- **tool_result block**：`tool_use_id` 和 `content` 完全支持；`is_error` 被忽略。\n\n## 3. 响应格式\n\n响应采用 **Anthropic 原生 content block 格式**，而非 OpenAI function call。证据如下：\n\n- 请求中传入的是 Anthropic 消息结构（`role` + `content` 数组含 `type`、`text` 等字段），SDK 也是 `anthropic.Anthropic()`。\n- 消息 content 支持的类型包括 `text`、`thinking`、`tool_use`，这些是 Anthropic 的 content block 类型。\n- 响应通过 `message.content` 获取，返回的也是 content block 数组（如 `print(message.content)`）。\n\n## 4. 限制与注意事项\n\n| 维度 | 限制 |\n|------|------|\n| **图像支持** | `type=\"image\"` 不支持 |\n| **文档支持** | `type=\"document\"` 不支持 |\n| **搜索/网络结果** | `search_result`、`web_search_tool_result`、`server_tool_use` 均不支持 |\n| **MCP 工具** | `mcp_tool_use`、`mcp_tool_result` 均不支持 |\n| **代码执行** | `code_execution_tool_result` 不支持 |\n| **容器上传** | `container_upload` 不支持 |\n| **缓存控制** | 所有 `cache_control` 字段均被忽略 |\n| **思考模式** | `thinking` block 支持，但 \"`budget_tokens` is ignored\" |\n| **输出配置** | 仅 `effort` 支持 |\n| **top_k** | 被忽略 |\n| **模型回退** | 传入不支持模型名时，API \"会自动将其映射到 `deepseek-v4-flash`\" |\n| **温度范围** | 限定 `[0.0 ~ 2.0]` |\n| **HTTP 头部** | `anthropic-beta` 和 `anthropic-version` 均被忽略 |\n\n此外，`redacted_thinking`、`citations`、`service_tier`、`mcp_servers`、`metadata`、`container` 等字段也未支持或直接被忽略。该兼容层本质上是将 Anthropic 请求格式翻译为 DeepSeek 自有模型调用，因此任何 Anthropic 独有功能（缓存、提示词缓存 beta、MCP 等）均不可用。"}]},"uuid":"57681d61-d04e-407d-af0e-d16698076675","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:09:48.329Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":30726,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# DeepSeek Anthropic 兼容 API 要点\n\n## 1. 支持的端点\n\n文档中仅明确提及一个端点：messages endpoint。Base URL 为 `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic`。采用 Anthropic SDK 进行调用（`client.messages.create(...)`），未提及 /v1/chat/completions 或其他 Anthropic 专有端点（如 /v1/messages/batches）是否支持，也未列举完整端点列表。\n\n## 2. 工具调用 (Tool Use) 工作机制\n\n工具调用采用 Anthropic 原生格式，而非 OpenAI function calling 格式。具体表现为：\n\n- **tools 数组**：支持 `name`、`input_schema`、`description` 三个字段完全可用；`cache_control` 被忽略。\n- **tool_choice**：`none`、`auto`、`any`、`tool` 四种模式均标记为 \"Supported\"，但 `disable_parallel_tool_use` 在所有模式下均被忽略。\n- **消息中的 tool_use block**：`id`、`input`、`name` 三个子字段完全支持。\n- **tool_result block**：`tool_use_id` 和 `content` 完全支持；`is_error` 被忽略。\n\n## 3. 响应格式\n\n响应采用 **Anthropic 原生 content block 格式**，而非 OpenAI function call。证据如下：\n\n- 请求中传入的是 Anthropic 消息结构（`role` + `content` 数组含 `type`、`text` 等字段），SDK 也是 `anthropic.Anthropic()`。\n- 消息 content 支持的类型包括 `text`、`thinking`、`tool_use`，这些是 Anthropic 的 content block 类型。\n- 响应通过 `message.content` 获取，返回的也是 content block 数组（如 `print(message.content)`）。\n\n## 4. 限制与注意事项\n\n| 维度 | 限制 |\n|------|------|\n| **图像支持** | `type=\"image\"` 不支持 |\n| **文档支持** | `type=\"document\"` 不支持 |\n| **搜索/网络结果** | `search_result`、`web_search_tool_result`、`server_tool_use` 均不支持 |\n| **MCP 工具** | `mcp_tool_use`、`mcp_tool_result` 均不支持 |\n| **代码执行** | `code_execution_tool_result` 不支持 |\n| **容器上传** | `container_upload` 不支持 |\n| **缓存控制** | 所有 `cache_control` 字段均被忽略 |\n| **思考模式** | `thinking` block 支持，但 \"`budget_tokens` is ignored\" |\n| **输出配置** | 仅 `effort` 支持 |\n| **top_k** | 被忽略 |\n| **模型回退** | 传入不支持模型名时，API \"会自动将其映射到 `deepseek-v4-flash`\" |\n| **温度范围** | 限定 `[0.0 ~ 2.0]` |\n| **HTTP 头部** | `anthropic-beta` 和 `anthropic-version` 均被忽略 |\n\n此外，`redacted_thinking`、`citations`、`service_tier`、`mcp_servers`、`metadata`、`container` 等字段也未支持或直接被忽略。该兼容层本质上是将 Anthropic 请求格式翻译为 DeepSeek 自有模型调用，因此任何 Anthropic 独有功能（缓存、提示词缓存 beta、MCP 等）均不可用。","durationMs":11370,"url":"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/guides/anthropic_api"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3540af7f-2127-4647-80ea-2dfdad5331a2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"640536db-824e-4ef6-8947-9e3db60aa56f","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"3c322f2e-e8d0-4322-b3c0-e6e3c6a59c0c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01_RUhZc3i28CUPHa3VcRCU5706","type":"tool_result","content":"# DeepSeek Chat Completion API — Tool Calling\n\n## 1. Tool Definitions (Request)\n\nTools are sent as a `tools` array in the request body. Each tool object requires:\n\n- **`type`**: Currently only `\"function\"` is supported\n- **`function`**: An object containing:\n  - **`name`** (required): \"Must be composed of a-z, A-Z, 0-9, underscores, and hyphens, max 64 characters\"\n  - **`description`**: Instructs the model on when/how to call the function\n  - **`parameters`** (optional): A JSON Schema object describing the inputs\n  - **`strict`** (default `false`): When true, forces strict schema adherence (Beta)\n\nUp to 128 functions are supported per request.\n\n## 2. Controlling Tool Selection\n\nThe `tool_choice` parameter accepts:\n\n| Value | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `\"none\"` | Model won't call any tool |\n| `\"auto\"` (default when tools exist) | Model may generate a message or call tools |\n| `\"required\"` | Model must call one or more tools |\n| `{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"my_function\"}}` | Forces a specific tool |\n\n## 3. Response Format — tool_calls\n\nWhen the model decides to call a tool, the response's `message` includes a `tool_calls` array. Each entry contains:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"string\",            // unique call ID\n  \"type\": \"function\",\n  \"function\": {\n    \"name\": \"string\",        // function name\n    \"arguments\": \"string\"    // JSON-encoded arguments\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Important caveat**: \"the model does not always generate valid JSON, and may invent parameters not defined in your schema.\" You must validate arguments before invoking the function.\n\nThe `finish_reason` will be `\"tool_calls\"` when the model decides to invoke tools.\n\n## 4. Returning Tool Results\n\nTool results are sent back as a new message in the `messages` array with:\n\n- **`role`**: `\"tool\"`\n- **`content`** (required): The result text\n- **`tool_call_id`** (required): Must match the `id` from the model's tool call\n\nThis is a multi-turn conversation pattern — after the assistant's response containing `tool_calls`, you append both the assistant message and then a tool message with the result, allowing the model to incorporate the outcome."}]},"uuid":"ee0d9a2e-ab73-45d1-8d94-d819f1e5031c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:09:49.710Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":115667,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# DeepSeek Chat Completion API — Tool Calling\n\n## 1. Tool Definitions (Request)\n\nTools are sent as a `tools` array in the request body. Each tool object requires:\n\n- **`type`**: Currently only `\"function\"` is supported\n- **`function`**: An object containing:\n  - **`name`** (required): \"Must be composed of a-z, A-Z, 0-9, underscores, and hyphens, max 64 characters\"\n  - **`description`**: Instructs the model on when/how to call the function\n  - **`parameters`** (optional): A JSON Schema object describing the inputs\n  - **`strict`** (default `false`): When true, forces strict schema adherence (Beta)\n\nUp to 128 functions are supported per request.\n\n## 2. Controlling Tool Selection\n\nThe `tool_choice` parameter accepts:\n\n| Value | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `\"none\"` | Model won't call any tool |\n| `\"auto\"` (default when tools exist) | Model may generate a message or call tools |\n| `\"required\"` | Model must call one or more tools |\n| `{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"my_function\"}}` | Forces a specific tool |\n\n## 3. Response Format — tool_calls\n\nWhen the model decides to call a tool, the response's `message` includes a `tool_calls` array. Each entry contains:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"string\",            // unique call ID\n  \"type\": \"function\",\n  \"function\": {\n    \"name\": \"string\",        // function name\n    \"arguments\": \"string\"    // JSON-encoded arguments\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Important caveat**: \"the model does not always generate valid JSON, and may invent parameters not defined in your schema.\" You must validate arguments before invoking the function.\n\nThe `finish_reason` will be `\"tool_calls\"` when the model decides to invoke tools.\n\n## 4. Returning Tool Results\n\nTool results are sent back as a new message in the `messages` array with:\n\n- **`role`**: `\"tool\"`\n- **`content`** (required): The result text\n- **`tool_call_id`** (required): Must match the `id` from the model's tool call\n\nThis is a multi-turn conversation pattern — after the assistant's response containing `tool_calls`, you append both the assistant message and then a tool message with the result, allowing the model to incorporate the outcome.","durationMs":9442,"url":"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/api/create-chat-completion"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"640536db-824e-4ef6-8947-9e3db60aa56f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
