ell the model the XML format for tool calls\n2. Make the XML parser more flexible — check for ANY XML tag that looks like a tool call\n\nActually, the better solution: tell the model the EXACT tool names and the EXACT XML format in the system prompt. Something like:\n\n```\nTOOL FORMAT: When you need to call a tool, use this exact format:\n<tool_use>\n<tool_name>EXACT_TOOL_NAME</tool_name>\n<arguments>{\"key\": \"value\"}</arguments>\n</tool_use>\n```\n\nAnd in the parser, recognize the `<tool_use>` tag.\n\nWait, the parser ALREADY handles `<tool_use>` format! The issue is that the model is generating `<read>` instead of `<tool_use>`. So I need to:\n1. Update the system prompt to tell the model to use `<tool_use>` format\n2. Also add fallback parsing for common tool-specific XML tags\n\nLet me also think about whether to include tool definitions in the system prompt explicitly. The Anthropic API sends tools separately, but maybe the model isn't processing them correctly. Including the tool list in the system prompt could help.\n\nActually, I think the real issue is that the Anthropic API's `tools` parameter might not be properly processed by DeepSeek's model. The documentation says it's SUPPORTED at the API level, but the MODEL might not be trained to use it.\n\nLet me take a pragmatic approach: update the system prompt to include tool definitions and the `<tool_use>` XML format, and update the parser.","signature":"fdd322ec-9949-4313-9593-1af175855195"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":233,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":347264,"output_tokens":837,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"bd1d2f65-c275-4be1-b616-ea033a095df1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:12:08.375Z","userType