{"parentUuid":"889a6750-acc3-4539-8a51-44bbca188af9","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"3c322f2e-e8d0-4322-b3c0-e6e3c6a59c0c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_f9RHV6NyOqYsUn4Bqxkd7009","type":"tool_result","content":"dsx-agent: tools → 0 definitions\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a880609c-af58-4dfc-be77-1db6ccd252c4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:17:39.634Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"dsx-agent: tools → 0 definitions\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}\n{\"type\":\"content_delta\",\"delta\":\"tool\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"889a6750-acc3-4539-8a51-44bbca188af9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"a880609c-af58-4dfc-be77-1db6ccd252c4","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"3a30dd89-f4a0-4dae-a54b-e5d503d69daf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"KEY FINDING: \"dsx-agent: tools → 0 definitions\" — the agent has ZERO tool definitions! This means the tools process isn't sending back any tools. Without tools, the model can't call any.\n\nThe root cause: when tools init is sent, the tools Ready response might not contain any tools. Let me check.\n\nThe agent sends `AgentToTools::Init { allowed_tools: vec![], ... }`. With `allowed_tools: vec![]`, the tools process might return an empty list.\n\nLooking at the tools code in `ipc.rs`:\n```rust\nInboundFrame::Init { allowed_tools, session_seed, auto_mode } => {\n    manager.apply_init(allowed_tools, &session_seed, auto_mode);\n    let tools = manager.filtered_defs();\n    if write_frame(&mut writer, &OutboundFrame::Ready { tools }).is_err() {\n```\n\nAnd `filtered_defs()`:\n```rust\npub fn filtered_defs(&self) -> Vec<ToolDef> {\n    match &self.allowed {\n        Some(allowed) => self.all_defs().into_iter()\n            .filter(|d| allowed.contains(&d.function.name))\n            .collect(),\n        None => self.all_defs(),\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAnd `apply_init`:\n```rust\npub fn apply_init(&mut self, allowed_tools: Vec<String>, session_seed: &str, auto_mode: bool) {\n    self.allowed = Some(allowed_tools);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nSo `self.allowed = Some(vec![])` — then `filtered_defs()` returns `Some(vec![])`, filtering to only tools in the empty list → ZERO tools!\n\nThat's the bug! The agent sends `allowed_tools: vec![]` which means \"allow no tools\". The tools process interprets this as \"only allow these tools\" and filters everything out.\n\nFix: change `allowed_tools: vec![]` to pass an empty Vec... wait, actually the issue is that `Some(vec![])` means \"allow nothing\" and `None` means \"allow all\".\n\nThe fix: in the agent's runner.rs init, don't pass an empty allowed list — either pass None or pass all tool names.\n\nBut looking at the code, `allowed_tools` is `Vec<String>`, not `Option<Vec<String>>`. If it's empty, it means \"no tools allowed\".\n\nFix: populate `allowed_tools` with all tool names from the tool_defs, or change the logic so that an empty list means \"all tools allowed\".\n\nActually, the simplest fix: change `apply_init` so that an empty allowed list means \"allow all\", not \"allow none\".","signature":"3a30dd89-f4a0-4dae-a54b-e5d503d69daf"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":355712,"output_tokens":697,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b166639d-6cea-49a5-a4eb-82bb1f712022","timestamp":"2026-05-15T08:17:59.790Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
