{"parentUuid":"b3bec32f-845e-458f-bdaa-cee793fb6be7","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"a637e7ed-3b1c-4da7-b38f-939068c4e159","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK the gateway's openai.rs assembles tool calls correctly in the Done event. The raw_message has `tool_calls: Some(assembled_tool_calls)`.\n\nNow let me check: does the HP's streaming loop handle the Done event correctly and include tool_calls in the api_response frame?\n\nLooking at the HP code I read earlier (lines 442-470 in runner.rs):\n```rust\nStreamEvent::Done { raw_message, stop_reason: sr, usage } => {\n    ...\n    let mut tool_calls: Vec<serde_json::Value> = Vec::new();\n    if let Some(tcs) = raw_message.tool_calls {\n        for tc in tcs {\n            tool_calls.push(serde_json::json!({\n                \"id\": tc.id,\n                \"name\": tc.function.name,\n                \"arguments\": tc.function.arguments,\n            }));\n        }\n    }\n    let mut resp = serde_json::json!({\n        \"type\": \"api_response\",\n        \"content\": full_content,\n    });\n    ...\n    if !tool_calls.is_empty() {\n        resp[\"tool_calls\"] = serde_json::Value::Array(tool_calls);\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct — it extracts tool_calls from the raw_message and includes them in the api_response frame. The agent should receive this.\n\nBut in my test, I didn't see the api_response frame. Let me check if maybe it's there but my grep didn't catch it.\n\nActually, looking at the test output again:\n```\n{\"type\":\"tool_progress\",\"id\":\"\",\"content\":\"read_file({\\\"path\\\":...})\",\"stream_type\":\"progress\"}\n...\n{\"type\":\"done\"}\n```\n\nThere's NO `api_response` frame between tool_progress and done. This means either:\n1. The gateway emitted Done without tool_calls\n2. The HP didn't include tool_calls in the api_response\n3. The api_response was sent but I'm not seeing it\n\nLet me check more carefully. The `tool_progress` frames have `\"id\":\"\"` (empty). This is from:\n```rust\nStreamEvent::ToolCallProgress { name, args_so_far } => {\n    let frame = serde_json::json!({\n        \"type\": \"tool_progress\",\n        \"id\": \"\",\n        \"content\": format!(\"{name}({args_so_far})\"),\n        \"stream_type\": \"progress\",\n    });\n```\n\nThe `id` is empty because the gateway's ToolCallProgress doesn't include an ID. But more importantly, CAN the gateway emit ToolCallProgress events? Let me check if openai.rs emits StreamEvent::ToolCallProgress.","signature":"a637e7ed-3b1c-4da7-b38f-939068c4e159"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":386688,"output_tokens":674,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5fc1723c-698d-4138-8fbd-f14518233694","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:09:00.568Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
