{"parentUuid":"7a24254e-0e19-475c-b28e-fe7dd183daa6","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"82a65656-a1c2-457c-aca0-13d39d1c1b4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Line 485: `return;` — The HP writes the api_response and then RETURNS from the function. It does NOT write a separate `done` frame after the api_response.\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. HP receives Done from gateway\n2. HP writes `api_response` frame to TCP\n3. HP returns from `handle_api_chat_streaming`\n4. Agent receives api_response... wait, but we said api_response was never received!\n\nLet me look more carefully. The agent output showed 0 api_response frames. But the HP code clearly writes api_response before returning.\n\nAh wait — the HP writes api_response and then returns. But `handle_api_chat_streaming` is called from `handle_connection`. After the function returns, `handle_connection` loops back to read the next frame. The HP does NOT write a `done` frame — the agent writes `done` to itself!\n\nActually no, let me re-read the agent code:\n```rust\nTuiToAgent::UserInput { text } => {\n    handle_user_input(...);\n    let _ = dsx_proto::write_frame(&mut tui_writer, &AgentToTui::Done);\n}\n```\n\nThe agent writes `done` to TUI after handle_user_input returns. But handle_user_input reads HP response and writes to TUI. So the sequence should be:\n1. Agent writes api_chat to HP\n2. Agent reads HP response (content_delta, tool_progress, api_response)\n3. Agent forwards frames to TUI (content_delta, tool_progress, api_response)\n4. Agent writes done to TUI\n\nBut the agent output shows tool_progress and done, but NO api_response. This means the agent's streaming loop reads content_delta and tool_progress from HP, but NOT api_response.\n\nWait — but the HP writes api_response before returning. So the agent's `dsx_proto::read_frame(hp_reader)` should read the api_response line.\n\nUNLESS... the agent's streaming loop handles the ToolProgress events and then exits without reading the api_response. Let me check the agent's streaming loop more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the agent output: there are 13 tool_progress events and then done. The api_response should be between the last tool_progress and done. But there's no api_response.\n\nCould it be that the HP's ToolCallProgress events are being generated by the gateway, but then the gateway crashes before sending Done? No — the HP wrote content back (the function returned), which means Done was received.\n\nWait, but the HP writes api_response and returns. Then `handle_connection` reads the next frame. The agent sends the next frame (or closes the connection). But meanwhile, the agent is reading the api_response.\n\nHmm, let me look at this from the agent's side. The agent's streaming loop:\n```rust\nloop {\n    let hp_resp: HpToAgent = match dsx_proto::read_frame(&mut hp_reader) {\n        Ok(Some(r)) => r,\n        Ok(None) => return,\n        Err(e) => { return; }\n    };\n    match hp_resp {\n        HpToAgent::ContentDelta { delta, reasoning } => { ... }\n        HpToAgent::ToolProgress { id, content, stream_type } => { ... }\n        HpToAgent::ApiResponse { ... } => { ... break; }\n        HpToAgent::Error { ... } => { ... return; }\n        _ => { ... }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `ToolProgress` arm should just forward to TUI and continue the loop. The `ApiResponse` arm should break. So the agent should read api_response and break.\n\nBut maybe the HP's api_response JSON isn't matching the `HpToAgent::ApiResponse` variant? If the JSON format is wrong, it might fall into the `_` arm and be ignored.\n\nLet me check what the HP actually writes as api_response. The HP writes:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"api_response\",\"content\":\"\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/tmp/test.txt\\\"}\"}]}\n```\n\nBut `HpToAgent::ApiResponse` expects:\n```rust\nHpToAgent::ApiResponse {\n    content: String,\n    tool_calls: Option<serde_json::Value>,\n    stop_reason: Option<String>,\n    reasoning_content: Option<String>,\n    thinking_signature: Option<String>,\n    usage: Option<dsx_types::UsageInfo>,\n}\n```\n\nThe `tool_calls` field is `Option<serde_json::Value>`, so it should accept the array. And all other fields are optional. This should parse correctly.\n\nHmm, but actually — let me check: does the agent's `_` arm just silently ignore frames? If the api_response doesn't deserialize, it would fall into `_ => { /* ignore */ }` and the agent would continue the loop, blocking on the next read. But HP closed the connection (no more frames), so the next read would return EOF, and the agent would return without writing api_response to TUI.\n\nWait, but that would mean the agent sees:\n1. content_delta with reasoning\n2. tool_progress ×13\n3. api_response (fails to parse → ignored)\n4. EOF (connection closed) → returns\n\nThe agent returns from handle_user_input, and then writes done to TUI. This matches what we see: tool_progress then done, no api_response.\n\nSo the api_response IS being sent by HP, but the AGENT can't parse it! Let me check why.\n\nActually wait, the HP returns after writing api_response. Then the connection handler reads the next frame. But the agent already read the api_response (and ignored it due to parse failure). So the agent blocks on the next read. The HP is waiting for the next frame from the agent. But the agent is waiting for the next frame from HP. DEADLOCK!\n\nNo wait, the agent's read would return EOF if HP closes. But HP doesn't close — it waits for the next frame. The agent blocks.\n\nUnless the agent's BufReader buffered extra data. When the BufReader reads, it fills its internal buffer with data from the TCP stream. If the api_response frame was split across TCP segments, the BufReader might have only part of it.\n\nActually, let me just check the REAL issue: what does the HP actually write as the api_response JSON? I'll check the exact JSON format the HP writes.","signature":"82a65656-a1c2-457c-aca0-13d39d1c1b4a"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":389248,"output_tokens":1486,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b37067ff-33eb-4f91-8bb3-cb05fa63b944","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:10:57.676Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
