tent: prog_content.clone(),\n                        stream_type: stream_type.clone(),\n                    });\n                }\n                HpToAgent::ApiResponse {\n                    content: c, tool_calls, stop_reason: _,\n                    reasoning_content: rc, thinking_signature: ts, usage: u,\n                } => {\n                    content = c;\n                    reasoning_content = rc;\n                    thinking_signature = ts;\n                    usage = u;\n                    tcs_raw = tool_calls.unwrap_or(serde_json::Value::Null);\n                    break;\n                }\n                HpToAgent::Error { message } => {\n                    let _ = dsx_proto::write_frame(tui_writer, &AgentToTui::Error { message: message.clone() });\n                    agent.health.record_api_error();\n                    return;\n                }\n                _ => { /* ignore non-stream frames during api_chat */ }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ── Process final api_response ──\n        agent.health.record_api_success(&agent.config.model);\n\n        // Parse tool calls (native Anthropic tool_use blocks)\n        let mut parsed: Vec<ToolCall> = parse_tool_calls(&tcs_raw);\n\n        // DeepSeek v4 outputs <tool_use> XML blocks in text content instead of\n        // native Anthropic tool_use blocks. Parse them as fallback.\n        if parsed.is_empty() && (content.contains(\"<tool_use>\") || content.contains(\"<read>\") || content.contains(\"<exec>\") || content.contains(\"<write>\") || content.contains(\"<search>\")) {\n            let (cleaned, xml_tcs) = parse_xml_tool_calls(&content);\n            content = cleaned;\n            parsed = xml_tcs;\n        }\n\n        let has_tools = !parsed.is_empty();\n\n                // Usage tracking\n                if let Some(ref u) = usage {\n                    agent.api_usage = Some(u.clone());\n                    agent.session_tokens += u.total_tokens as u64;\n                }\n                agent.token_estimate = breakdown.total;\n                agent.token_breakdown = Some(breakdown);\n                agent.health.context_tokens = agent.tokens_used();\n                agent.health.context_tier = crate::health::ContextTier::from_tokens(\n                    agent.health.context_tokens, agent.config.context_limit,\n                );\n\n                // Phase detection from reasoning\n                if let Some(ref r) = reasoning_content {\n                    agent.update_phase(r);\n                    if agent.auto_mode {\n                        let tp = phase_detector::detect_task_phase_from_reasoning(r);\n                        if tp != agent.current_task_phase {\n                            agent.current_task_phase = tp;\n                            router::set_phase(tp, router::read_debug_level());\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Build and push assistant Message\n                let assistant_msg = Message {\n                    role: \"assistant\".into(),\n                    content: if content.is_empty() && !parsed.is_empty() { None } else { Some(content.clone()) },\n                    name: None,\n                    tool_calls: if parsed.is_empty() { None } else { Some(parsed.clone()) },\n                    tool_call_id: None,\n                    reasoning_content,\n                    thinking_signature,\n                };\n\n                if let Err(e) = agent.ctx.push_assistant(assistant_msg.clone()) {\n                    log::error!(\"push_assistant failed: {:?} — repairing\", e);\n                    session_persistence::repair_messages(agent);\n                    agent.ctx.push_assistant_restore(assistant_msg.clone());\n                }\n                agent.sync_messages();\n\n                if !has_tools {\n                    // ── Final response ──\n                    agent.turn_scores.push(turn_scorer::score_current_turn(agent));\n                    agent.stream_content.clear();\n                    agent.stream_reasoning.clear();\n                    agent.phase = AgentPhase::Idle;\n\n                    agent.extract_reasoning_insights();\n                    learning::auto_extract_memory(agent, &assistant_msg);\n\n                    agent.health.record_turn(false);\n                    agent.health_status_line = health_status(agent);\n                    agent.health.reset_turn();\n\n                    session::save_live_snapshot(","numLines":100,"startLine":409,"totalLines":847}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f3389940-7357-4bbb-8157-cf8e1451d1e4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"b3864ce6-450d-4767-b12e-24bfd2b437fa","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"6de0436c-d41e-4cda-979a-44045e5897b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK I see the issue now. The agent correctly:\n1. Receives api_response with tool_calls from HP\n2. Sets `content = c` (empty string for tool-only responses)\n3. Sets `tcs_raw = tool_calls`\n4. Parses `tcs_raw` into `parsed` via `parse_tool_calls`\n5. `has_tools = !parsed.is_empty()` should be true\n\nThen the tool execution loop should execute each tool. But my test showed 0 api_response frames in the agent output. The agent wasn't forwarding the api_response to TUI!\n\nWait actually, looking at the code, the agent never sends the api_response to TUI. It sends content_delta and tool_progress to TUI during streaming. But after the streaming loop breaks (when api_response arrives), the agent processes tool calls and either:\n- Sends final api_response to TUI (if no tools)\n- Enters the tool execution loop (if tools)\n\nThe tool execution loop dispatches tools and continues. But the agent doesn't send a separate api_response to TUI when tools are present — it just dispatches tools.\n\nThat's the issue! The agent sends content_delta and tool_progress during streaming. When api_response arrives with tool calls, the agent breaks the streaming loop and enters the tool execution loop. The tool execution loop executes tools and then continues the API round. But the TUI still shows the old content (no update after api_response).\n\nBut wait — my test showed no `tool_call_req` frames either. The tools weren't executed. Let me check if `parse_tool_calls` actually parsed the tool calls.\n\nActually, the REAL issue might be that the api_response is not arriving at the agent at all. My test showed 0 api_response in the agent output. Let me verify: does the HP actually write the api_response?\n\nLet me add a stderr log to the