{"parentUuid":"0454920f-6911-4902-8427-7eeef49cdb62","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","promptId":"e1c70962-cfa1-407c-ad2e-e4be49537971","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_iTm97DobesiwILi0pqQK7963","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"95fc3de8-da08-4e01-af7c-6b081a5673e3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:11:47.834Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0454920f-6911-4902-8427-7eeef49cdb62","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"95fc3de8-da08-4e01-af7c-6b081a5673e3","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8a7c8854-30b7-45b8-98f3-016f9c44d763","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me just check: is the HP's api_response frame being written, and what does it look like? The issue might be that the frame is too long and gets truncated or mangled over TCP.\n\nActually, I think the real issue is simpler. Let me re-check: with `protocol=openai`, the gateway processes the OpenAI streaming response. The model generates tool_calls. The gateway emits ToolCallProgress events. But does the gateway also emit a ContentDelta for the text response?\n\nIn the OpenAI streaming format, when the model generates a tool call, the response contains ONLY tool call deltas, not text content. So the gateway:\n1. Emits ToolCallProgress events for each tool call delta\n2. Emits Done with the assembled tool_calls (and empty content)\n\nThe HP converts Done to api_response (with tool_calls) and writes it. The agent receives api_response with tool_calls and content=\"\".\n\nBut my test shows 0 api_response in the agent output. Let me check if maybe the api_response IS being sent but the agent isn't forwarding it to TUI.\n\nActually, looking at the agent output: the logs show 13 tool_progress events and then done. The api_response IS processed (because Done was written after handle_user_input returns). But the api_response is NOT forwarded to TUI.\n\nThat's the bug! The agent receives api_response, processes it internally, but never sends it to TUI. The TUI only sees:\n- content_delta (with reasoning)\n- tool_progress\n- done\n\nThe `api_response` frame (which contains the final content and tool calls) is consumed by the agent and never forwarded.\n\nWait, that's by design for the tool calling case. When tools are present, the agent enters a tool execution loop and then makes another API call. The TUI should see the tool calls being executed.\n\nBut in my test, there were NO tool_call_req frames. The tools weren't executed. Let me check if `parse_tool_calls` actually parsed them.\n\nActually, let me just check: in my test, what was the tcs_raw value? If tcs_raw was Null (no tool_calls in the api_response), then `parsed` would be empty and the agent would go to the \"no tools\" path.\n\nIf the HP's api_response has `tool_calls` as `null` or `None` instead of an array, the agent wouldn't see them. Let me check.\n\nThe HP writes: `resp[\"tool_calls\"] = serde_json::Value::Array(tool_calls)`. If `tool_calls` is empty (the HP's local vec), nothing is written, and the `tool_calls` field is omitted from the JSON.The agent deserializes `HpToAgent::ApiResponse { tool_calls: Option<serde_json::Value>, ... }`. If the field is missing, `tool_calls` is None, and `tcs_raw = tool_calls.unwrap_or(Null)` gives Null. Then `parse_tool_calls(&Null)` returns an empty vec. `has_tools = false`. The agent enters the \"no tools\" path, which sends api_response to TUI and returns.\n\nBUT — in my test, there's no api_response frame in the TUI output. So the agent is NOT entering the \"no tools\" path. It's entering the \"tools\" path (or crashing).\n\nWait, maybe the issue is something completely different. Let me just check if `content` is also empty. If both content and tool_calls are empty, the agent goes to the \"no tools\" path and writes api_response. But that should appear in the output.\n\nHmm, I'm overthinking this. Let me just run a direct test with `protocol=openai` and capture everything.","signature":"8a7c8854-30b7-45b8-98f3-016f9c44d763"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":394368,"output_tokens":1164,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ff59ff08-d29f-4fdc-b94c-96d5362f9403","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:12:15.019Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"ff59ff08-d29f-4fdc-b94c-96d5362f9403","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"8a7c8854-30b7-45b8-98f3-016f9c44d763","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_hvuyNyiAlgkCqeGbWCMG9089","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"# Direct HP test with openai protocol\necho '{\"type\":\"api_chat\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"system\":\"test\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"say hi\"}]}' | python3 -c \"\nimport socket, json\nport = int(open('/home/qaqtamsy/.dsx/hp.port').read().strip())\ns = socket.socket()\ns.connect(('127.0.0.1', port))\ns.send(b'{\\\"type\\\":\\\"register\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"Agent\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test\\\",\\\"pid\\\":99999}\\n')\ns.recv(4096)  # drain\n# Send api_chat\ns.send(b'{\\\"type\\\":\\\"api_chat\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"deepseek-v4-flash\\\",\\\"system\\\":\\\"test\\\",\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"say hi\\\"}]}\\n')\ns.settimeout(15)\nwhile True:\n    try:\n        line = b''\n        while True:\n            c = s.recv(1)\n            if not c: break\n            line += c\n            if c == b'\\n': break\n        if not line: break\n        print(line.decode().strip()[:120])\n    except: break\ns.close()\n\"","description":"Test HP directly with openai protocol","timeout":20000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":394368,"output_tokens":1164,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2a50065d-b643-4cb6-8dff-e670d2cb11c3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:12:25.018Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-44