{"parentUuid":"6287a921-7d52-4090-b096-c3d35408c223","isSidechain":false,"teamName":"dsx-integration","message":{"id":"49923a12-790e-4a01-98f7-ce5b4383367a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so `config::system_prompt` just re-exports `prompt::system_prompt`. The chain is:\n\n1. Agent's `prepare_and_compact()` calls `config::system_prompt(lang)` → gets base system prompt from `prompt.rs`\n2. ContextBuilder::new() takes the base prompt + empty semantic/long_mem blocks\n3. ContextBuilder::build() assembles the final system prompt with turns, cards, etc.\n4. Then pitfall guide and active skill bodies are appended\n\nThe key issue: `semantic_block` and `long_mem_block` are EMPTY. The ContextBuilder's build() function would include semantic memory and long-term memory if they were populated, but they're not.\n\nThis means:\n- Base system prompt (from prompt.rs) IS included\n- Turn history IS included (via ContextBuilder)\n- Pitfall guide IS appended\n- Active skill bodies ARE appended\n- BUT: semantic memory and long-term memory are NOT included (empty strings)\n\nThe prompt structure is:\n```\n[base system prompt from prompt.rs]\n[ContextBuilder output: backbone + compacted turns]\n[pitfall guide]\n[Active Skills]\n```\n\nThe base prompt from prompt.rs is what we updated earlier with the tool calling format. But the ContextBuilder might be generating a backbone that OVERRIDES or conflicts with our tool instructions.\n\nLet me check what ContextBuilder::build() actually produces.","signature":"49923a12-790e-4a01-98f7-ce5b4383367a"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":399744,"output_tokens":391,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"