{"parentUuid":"d4febff7-fada-41cf-9798-98365a71c8ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"b7e06a90-3c05-4300-b181-50acb57be21d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying that for the API (probably OpenAI), you can't filter tools — either you send all or none. If you send a subset and the model tries to call a tool that's not in the list, the API returns a 400 error.\n\nThis is a known behavior of the OpenAI API: the model can only call tools that were sent with the request. If the model calls a tool that wasn't included, it's an error.\n\nActually, wait. That's partially true. The model CAN only call tools that are in the `tools` parameter. If you filter tools, the model won't call the filtered-out ones (because it doesn't know they exist). So filtering should be safe — the model can't call what it doesn't know about.\n\nBut the user says \"不能过滤否则api会400\" — maybe they're thinking of a different scenario. Let me think about what could cause a 400:\n1. Sending a tool call with a tool name not in the tools list → this would be the API rejecting the response\n2. But if we filter the tools, the model won't call the filtered ones, so no issue\n\nActually, maybe the user is concerned about the opposite flow: what if the model already has a pending tool call from a previous round, and we filter a tool that was called? That could happen if we filter between rounds in a multi-turn conversation. But we only send tools with the request, not with the response.\n\nActually, I think the user might be referring to the fact that if you change the tool definitions between requests in a multi-turn conversation, the API can reject because it can't validate the tool call against the current schema. But that's a specific edge case.\n\nLet me re-read the user's message: \"不能过滤否则api会400,要么不传要么全传。每次发生变动会立刻报错\"\n\nOK so they're saying: you EITHER send no tools OR all tools. If you send a filtered subset, the API returns 400. And any change to the tool set causes immediate errors.\n\nThis doesn't match my understanding of how OpenAI/Anthropic APIs work. You CAN send a subset of tools. The model will only call the tools it knows about. But if the model has previously called a tool (in a multi-turn), and that tool is no longer in the list, it would be an issue.\n\nActually, for the multi-turn scenario:\n1. Turn 1: Send tools [A, B, C]. Model calls A.\n2. Turn 2: Send tools [A, B]. Model's previous call to A has a result. But A is still in the list, so tool_result for A is sent back. No issue.\n\nFor filtering to work correctly:\n- The tools list in each request should include ALL tools that have been called in the conversation history (because tool results need to reference the tool definition)\n- Plus any tools the model might need to call next\n\nSo if we filter tools turn-by-turn:\n- Turn 1: Send [explore, read_file]. Model calls explore.\n- Turn 2: Must still include explore in tools (because tool_result references it). Can add more tools.\n\nThis is more complex than just sending all tools. The user's point is valid: simpler to just send all tools than to maintain the dynamic tool set correctly.\n\nLet me accept the user's point and move on. They know their API better than me.","signature":"b7e06a90-3c05-4300-b181-50acb57be21d"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":393344,"output_tokens":777,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5467164c-6d86-4f2c-be51-530d2afa8add","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:00:16.138Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2