{"parentUuid":"9d627a97-743c-43df-940e-c045445b0773","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"91c6dbaf-1475-4568-ab22-dc36844596b4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_vj7DZjphKTGR5FJbaTqw8001","type":"tool_result","content":"260\t\n261\t    let http = HttpClient::builder()\n262\t        .connect_timeout(Duration::from_secs(10))\n263\t        .build()?;\n264\t\n265\t    let resp = http\n266\t        .post(&url)\n267\t        .header(\"Authorization\", format!(\"Bearer {}\", config.api_key))\n268\t        .header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n269\t        .json(&body_json)\n270\t        .send()\n271\t        .await;\n272\t\n273\t    let resp = match resp {\n274\t        Ok(r) => {\n275\t            if !r.status().is_success() {\n276\t                let status = r.status();\n277\t                let text = r.text().await.unwrap_or_default();\n278\t                let msg = format!(\"OpenAI API {}: {}\", status, text);\n279\t                let _ = tx.send(StreamEvent::Error(msg.clone())).await;"}]},"uuid":"28a466ca-4ba5-4d8d-8e30-c9e3d5e0c705","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:26:06.270Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-gateway/src/openai.rs","content":"\n    let http = HttpClient::builder()\n        .connect_timeout(Duration::from_secs(10))\n        .build()?;\n\n    let resp = http\n        .post(&url)\n        .header(\"Authorization\", format!(\"Bearer {}\", config.api_key))\n        .header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n        .json(&body_json)\n        .send()\n        .await;\n\n    let resp = match resp {\n        Ok(r) => {\n            if !r.status().is_success() {\n                let status = r.status();\n                let text = r.text().await.unwrap_or_default();\n                let msg = format!(\"OpenAI API {}: {}\", status, text);\n                let _ = tx.send(StreamEvent::Error(msg.clone())).await;","numLines":20,"startLine":260,"totalLines":474}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9d627a97-743c-43df-940e-c045445b0773","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"28a466ca-4ba5-4d8d-8e30-c9e3d5e0c705","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"4ad1a5b4-6e4c-4300-a4f5-6a40bf3d99c6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The gateway catches API errors and sends `StreamEvent::Error(msg)`. The HP receives this and writes to the TCP stream:\n\n```rust\nStreamEvent::Error(e) => {\n    let _ = writeln!(writer, \"{}\", json_response(\"error\", &e));\n    let _ = writer.flush();\n    return;\n}\n```\n\nThe HP writes `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}` to the TCP stream. Then the agent reads this:\n\n```rust\nHpToAgent::Error { message } => {\n    let _ = dsx_proto::write_frame(tui_writer, &AgentToTui::Error { ... });\n    agent.health.record_api_error();\n    return;\n}\n```\n\nBut the agent's output shows \"HP parse error\" — this is from the read_frame call, NOT from the Error handler. So the HP's error JSON can't be parsed as HpToAgent.\n\nWhat does the HP write? `json_response(\"error\", &e)` produces `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\"}`. The `message` contains the API error text, which might include characters that need JSON escaping.\n\nLet me check `json_response`:\n```rust\nfn json_response(status: &str, message: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"{{\\\"type\\\":\\\"{status}\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"{message}\\\"}}\")\n}\n```\n\nTHIS IS THE BUG! `format!(... \"{message}\" ...)` doesn't escape the `message` string for JSON! If the message contains `\"` or `\\` characters, the resulting JSON is malformed.\n\nFor example, if the API error is: \n```\nOpenAI API 400 Bad Request: {\"error\":{\"message\":\"...\",\"type\":\"...\",\"param\":null,\"code\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}\n```\n\nThen `json_response` produces: \n```\n{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"OpenAI API 400 Bad Request: {\"error\":{\"message\":\"...\",\"type\":\"...\",\"param\":null,\"code\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}\"}\n```\n\nThis is INVALID JSON because the embedded `\"` characters break the string.\n\nThe fix: use `serde_json::json!` for safe JSON serialization instead of string formatting.\n\nThis also explains why error popups don't work in the TUI — the HP sends broken JSON as the error frame, and the TUI's string matching might still work but the deserialization fails.\n\nLet me fix the `json_response` function to use serde_json.","signature":"4ad1a5b4-6e4c-4300-a4f5-6a40bf3d99c6"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":212,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":446848,"output_tokens":746,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"a0bbe369-6d3d-44dc-ad7c-103eb1672301","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:26:14.174Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
