{"parentUuid":"fa93389e-2da4-4102-af33-352e8c267b09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"8d10c397-f397-49c7-9351-adc4241136f6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"FOUND IT! The error message:\n\n```\n\"reasoning_content\" in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API.\n```\n\nThe DeepSeek API is saying: when the model returns reasoning_content (thinking mode is enabled), you MUST pass the reasoning_content back in subsequent messages. The assistant message in the second request has `content: \"\"` but doesn't include the `reasoning_content` field.\n\nThe model's first response had `reasoning_content` set. When the agent sends the second api_chat, the assistant message doesn't include `reasoning_content`. DeepSeek requires it.\n\nWait, but why would DeepSeek require reasoning_content in subsequent messages? This seems like a DeepSeek-specific requirement for thinking mode.\n\nLooking at the messages array in the second request:\n```json\n[\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"read /tmp/test.txt\"},\n  {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"\", \"tool_calls\": [...], \"reasoning_content\": null or missing},\n  {\"role\": \"tool\", \"content\": \"hello world\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call_001\"}\n]\n```\n\nThe assistant message has `reasoning_content` missing. But the first API response had reasoning_content. DeepSeek requires us to pass it back.\n\nFix: the agent should include `reasoning_content` in the assistant message when it's set. Currently, the agent's Message struct has `reasoning_content` but when converted to JSON for the HP request, it might be None.\n\nLet me check: in `messages_to_json` (which is now `serde_json::to_value(&msgs_no_system)`), the Message struct is serialized directly. The Message has:\n```rust\npub struct Message {\n    pub role: String,\n    pub content: Option<String>,\n    pub tool_calls: Option<Vec<ToolCall>>,\n    pub tool_call_id: Option<String>,\n    pub reasoning_content: Option<String>,\n    pub thinking_signature: Option<String>,\n}\n```\n\nWhen serialized, `reasoning_content` is present but might be `null` (None). The DeepSeek API might be strict about this being either present with the original value, or the key must not be present at all.\n\nWait, but the error says \"The `reasoning_content` in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API.\" This means DeepSeek requires the assistant's `reasoning_content` to be preserved and sent back in subsequent requests.\n\nWhen the agent serializes the Message, `reasoning_content` might be `null` (None) in the JSON. The OpenAI gateway should include it in the OpenAIMessage for assistant messages.\n\nLooking at the openai.rs converter:\n```rust\nOpenAIMessage {\n    role: \"assistant\".into(),\n    content: text,\n    tool_calls: if tcs.is_empty() { None } else { Some(tcs) },\n    tool_call_id: None,\n}\n```\n\nThere's NO `reasoning_content` field in `OpenAIMessage`! The raw JSON message has `reasoning_content` but the OpenAIMessage struct doesn't include it.\n\nFix: add `reasoning_content: Option<String>` to `OpenAIMessage` and pass it through.","signature":"8d10c397-f397-49c7-9351-adc4241136f6"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":449664,"output_tokens":1052,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"deb9648b-0179-4fb8-b677-2aeae08cf512","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:27:41.627Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
