{"parentUuid":"77993153-dc28-49bd-862e-f80a584441fd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ee2f0700-2140-4560-b2f5-8e83b5d90285","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"我很好奇，调用工具时是ai声明了什么才算是进入调用工具阶段？"},"uuid":"612427c3-b22d-4e22-b78b-734b84c1c4bf","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:35:35.321Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"612427c3-b22d-4e22-b78b-734b84c1c4bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"7594ad43-2e02-4a1c-b3f6-185259a5ac5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about how tool calling works in the API protocol — specifically, what does the model/AI return that signals it wants to call a tool?\n\nIn the OpenAI API (which we're now using), the model returns a `tool_calls` array in the response message when it wants to call a tool. The flow is:\n\n1. Request: We send `messages` + `tools` array with tool definitions\n2. Response: The model returns a message with `tool_calls` array instead of (or in addition to) `content`\n3. Each tool_call has: `id`, `type: \"function\"`, `function: {name, arguments}`\n4. The `finish_reason` is `\"tool_calls\"` when the model wants to call tools\n\nIn the OpenAI streaming format, the model sends tool call deltas progressively:\n- `delta.tool_calls[0].function.name` = \"read_file\"\n- `delta.tool_calls[0].function.arguments` = \"{\\\"path\\\": \\\"/tmp/test.txt\\\"}\"\n\nAnd in the final chunk, `finish_reason: \"tool_calls\"` signals the end.\n\nLet me also check if the user might be asking about how the HP/gateway detects this. In our code, the OpenAI gateway stream parser accumulates tool calls from deltas and when `finish_reason == \"tool_calls\"`, it assembles them into the final Message.tool_calls.\n\nBut actually, I think the user might be asking a more fundamental question: what determines whether the model enters the \"tool calling\" mode? The answer is: sending `tools` in the API request. If you send `tools`, the model knows it can call tools. The model decides which tool to call based on the user's request and the tool descriptions.\n\nBut there's also `tool_choice` parameter:\n- `\"auto\"` (default) — model can choose to use tools or not\n- `\"required\"` — model MUST use a tool\n- `\"none\"` — model should not use any tool\n- `{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"xxx\"}}` — force a specific tool\n\nIn our gateway, we don't set `tool_choice`, so it defaults to `\"auto\"` in the request. Let me check.","signature":"7594ad43-2e02-4a1c-b3f6-185259a5ac5c"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":460416,"output_tokens":580,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"77dc4cc0-136c-444a-afc4-db5c90ae1464","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:35:43.106Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
