{"parentUuid":"55e4308e-b7b3-434c-9c8d-81b810093059","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"e21acf6f-820d-491d-87a6-5bb7321783fe","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_4FbFPNGWHYQrcxs9UScQ5359","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix TUI missing keyboard and display","name":"fix-tui-keybinds","prompt":"Fix 4 TUI issues in DSX.\n\n## Issue 1: tool_progress floods display\n\n**File: `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`**\nCurrent code pushes EVERY chunk as a new entry:\n```rust\nstream.tool_progress.push((id.to_string(), content.to_string()));\n```\n\nChange to UPDATE the LAST entry if same tool name, or REPLACE the last entry. The progress builds up character by character (`read_file()`, `read_file({`, `read_file({\\\"path)`...). We only want ONE line showing the latest state.\n\nFix: `stream.tool_progress` is a `Vec<(String, String)>`. Instead of pushing, if the last entry starts with the same name, replace it:\n```rust\nlet entry = (id.to_string(), content.to_string());\nif let Some(last) = stream.tool_progress.last_mut() {\n    *last = entry;\n} else {\n    stream.tool_progress.push(entry);\n}\n```\n\n## Issue 2: Scrolling keys don't work\n\n**File: `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`**\nThe input handler returns actions like `ScrollUp(3)`, `ScrollDown(3)`, `ScrollPageUp`, `ScrollPageDown` but the event loop IGNORES them. It only checks `if let InputAction::SendMessage(text) = action`.\n\nIn the keyboard loop, after getting the action, add handling:\n```rust\nlet action = handle_chat_key(&mut state.input_state, key, &state.slash_commands);\nmatch action {\n    InputAction::SendMessage(text) => {\n        // existing send logic\n    }\n    InputAction::ScrollUp(n) => {\n        state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_add(n);\n    }\n    InputAction::ScrollDown(n) => {\n        state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(n);\n    }\n    InputAction::ScrollPageUp => {\n        state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_add(area_height);\n    }\n    InputAction::ScrollPageDown => {\n        state.scroll_offset = state.scroll_offset.saturating_sub(area_height);\n    }\n    InputAction::ScrollToTop => {\n        state.scroll_offset = 0;\n    }\n    InputAction::ToggleAutoScroll => {\n        state.auto_scroll = !state.auto_scroll;\n    }\n    _ => {}\n}\n```\n\nUse `state.scroll_offset` field (already exists on AppState). The area_height should come from the terminal area, but for simplicity use 20 lines as default page size.\n\nAlso need to check: `InputAction::CancelStream` should set `stream.cancelled = true`.\n\n## Issue 3: session_start not populated\n\n**File: `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`**\n`RenderContext::session_start` comes from `app.session_start` which defaults to 0. The workspace info panel checks this to show runtime. Need to set it when starting a session.\n\nWhen the first message is sent to agent, set `state.session_start = session::now_epoch()`:\n\n```rust\nif state.session_start == 0 {\n    state.session_start = std::time::SystemTime::now()\n        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n        .unwrap_or_default()\n        .as_secs();\n}\n```\n\nThis should go in the SendMessage handler, before or after writing to agent_writer.\n\nAlso check `render/workspace.rs` — the runtime display is already wired there but needs session_start to be non-zero.\n\n## Issue 4: Stream tool progress render should show only last entry\n\n**File: `crates/dsx-tui/src/render/chat.rs`**\nLines 194-197:\n```rust\nfor (name, args) in ctx.stream_tool_progress {\n    lines.push(Line::from(\"\"));\n    lines.extend(render_tool_call_block(name, args, w));\n}\n```\n\nThis renders ALL entries. With the fix in issue 1 (only one entry), this loop will have only one entry and display one line. Change `for` to show only the LAST entry:\n```rust\nif let Some((name, args)) = ctx.stream_tool_progress.last() {\n    lines.push(Line::from(\"\"));\n    lines.extend(render_tool_call_block(name, args, w));\n}\n```\n\n## Build\n`cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"sonnet"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":82,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":464640,"output_tokens":1084,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"47394cde-6971-498f-af1a-cf14ac102818","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:41:35.994Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
