{"parentUuid":"b78ae0e7-b372-40fa-a921-fdfedd21fba3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"d0ff6c36-ec27-4071-94e8-949ca533a0e4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is clear:\n1. Line 688: Annotates the context with \"Max tool rounds reached. Respond with what you have.\"\n2. Line 690-692: agent.sync_messages() + writes Error frame + returns\n\nBut the annotation is added but never used — the function returns immediately after writing the error. The annotation should trigger ANOTHER api_chat call so the model actually reads the annotation and generates a final response.\n\nThe fix: after the annotation, continue the for loop (make another api_chat call). The model will see the annotation and generate a final text response without tool calls.\n\nWait, but the for loop ends at 10 rounds. The annotation is done AFTER the loop exits. So we'd need to either:\n1. Change the structure to allow one more round after annotation\n2. Or break out of the loop at 10 rounds but DON'T send an error — instead annotate and let the loop exit, then continue to a FINAL text-only api call\n\nLet me restructure. The simplest fix:\n1. When the for loop exits (10 rounds done), don't send an error\n2. Instead, annotate, sync, and make ONE MORE api_chat call without tools (text-only)\n3. The model reads \"Max tool rounds reached. Respond with what you have.\" and generates a text response\n4. Forward the response to TUI\n\nThis is cleaner. Let me send a sonnet to implement it.","signature":"d0ff6c36-ec27-4071-94e8-949ca533a0e4"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":134,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":472320,"output_tokens":1045,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop