-|--------|\n| PageUp | exec_scroll_offset += 20 | **Sends ScrollPageUp** (chat scroll) | **REGRESSION** — exec scroll not handled anywhere |\n| PageDown | exec_scroll_offset -= 20 | **Sends ScrollPageDown** (chat scroll) | **REGRESSION** — exec scroll not handled anywhere |\n| End | Sets cursor + **enables auto_scroll** | Sets cursor only | **REGRESSION** — auto_scroll not re-enabled on End |\n| Esc (ApiConfig mode) | Handled in chat.rs | Not in chat handler (handled at higher level) | REFACTORED (acceptable) |\n| Enter (ApiConfig mode) | Handled in chat.rs (key verification logic) | Not in chat handler | **MISSING** — setup wizard key entry broken |\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/input/sudo.rs`\n\n| Feature | Old | New | Status |\n|---------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Esc = cancel sudo | Yes (with agent restart) | Yes (returns CancelSudo action) | PRESENT (action applied in event loop) |\n| Enter = submit password | Yes (with spawn_exec_async_with_sudo) | Yes (returns SubmitSudo) | PRESENT |\n| Character input | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Backspace | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n\nThe key difference: old `handle_sudo_key` did the actual work (spawning sudo exec, sending to agent). New version just returns actions. The event loop must handle `SubmitSudo` and `CancelSudo` — it does, but only sends a generic `tool_confirm_resp` approval, **NOT** spawning sudo exec with the password. So sudo password is collected but never actually used to execute commands.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 7: Event Loop Lifecycle Features Missing\n\n| Feature | Old (mod.rs) | New (lib.rs) | Status |\n|---------|-------------|-------------|--------|\n| Auto-query balance on startup | Yes (async `api::get_balance`) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Periodic crash recovery snapshot (every 3s) | Yes (`session::save_live_snapshot`) | Fields exist (`dirty`, `last_snapshot`) but no timer | **MISSING** |\n| Auto-save session on exit | Yes (`app.maybe_save_session()`) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Bracketed paste handling | Yes (`Event::Paste` handler with place at cursor) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Ctrl+C → exit prompt → second Ctrl+C → quit | Yes (full state machine) | Yes (basic) | PRESENT (simplified) |\n| `dsc_log` init | Yes (`crate::dsc_log::init()`) | No (stub is no-op) | STUBBED |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 8: Stubs That Should Be Real\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (lines 784-1120, `pub mod stubs`)\n\nAll stubs return empty/trivial values. The critical ones that affect UI behavior:\n\n| Stub Module | Dependency | Effect on UI |\n|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| `stubs::session::load_index()` | Returns `vec![]` | Session picker always shows \"No saved sessions found\" |\n| `stubs::session::find_live_sessions()` | Returns `vec![]` | Interrupted sessions never found |\n| `stubs::session::finalize_session()` | No-op | Sessions never saved to disk |\n| `stubs::session::list_plans()` | Returns `vec![]` | Workspace panel always shows \"No active plan\" |\n| `stubs::session::read_memory()` | Returns `\"\"` | Task summary always empty |\n| `stubs::session::load_pitfalls()` | Returns empty PitfallGuide | Pitfall invariants never injected |\n| `stubs::conversation::ContextAssembler` | All methods no-op | Message repair, annotation, and alternation checks disabled |\n| `stubs::health::DsAgentsHealthPlatform` | `infer_emotion()` returns empty, `check_alternation()` returns None | No agent health display in info panel, 400 detection broken |\n| `stubs::context::ContextBuilder::build()` | Returns empty messages | Token breakdown always \"0\" |\n| `stubs::api::get_balance()` | Returns empty BalanceInfo | Balance always blank |\n| `stubs::memory::SemanticMemory` | All methods no-op | Architecture decisions and error patterns never recorded |\n| `stubs::skills::SkillIndex::scan()` | Returns empty | Skill bodies never injected into context |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 9: Summary of Critical Regressions\n\n1. **Exec handling completely broken**: `ExecDone`, `ExecStarted`, and `ExecProgress` are never handled. Exec results are never displayed in the tool_code panel and never fed back to the agent.\n\n2. **Sudo password collected but never used**: The `SubmitSudo` action sends a generic `tool_confirm_resp` approval, not the actual password. Real sudo exec (with `spawn_exec_async_with_sudo`) is never called.\n\n3. **No session persistence**: `dirty`/`last_snapshot` fields exist but no periodic snapshot timer runs. `finalize_session` is stubbed. Sessions are never saved or resumed.\n\n4. **Gate/error/retry/rate-limit fields declared but never populated**: The event loop has no frame handlers for these types. The corresponding render blocks (`render_api_error_block`, `render_retry_progress_block`, `render_rate_limit_block`, `render_gate_popup`) will never trigger.\n\n5. **`/fix` slash command missing**: Users cannot repair orphaned tool_use/tool_result pairs, which would cause API 400 errors.\n\n6. **`/context` slash command missing**: Users cannot see detailed token breakdown.\n\n7. **`/tools`, `/skip-all`, `/dev` commands missing**: These toggles cannot be changed at runtime.\n\n8. **Exec panel scrolling broken**: `PageUp`/`PageDown` now scroll the chat panel instead of the exec panel (`exec_scroll_offset` is never modified by the event loop).\n\n9. **Auto-scroll not re-enabled on `End` key**: Old behavior: pressing End jumps to end and re-enables auto-scroll. New behavior: cursor moves but auto-scroll stays off.\n\n10. **No bracketed paste support**: The old handler inserted pasted text at the cursor position. No paste handling exists in the new event loop.\n\n11. **No auto-balance query on startup**: The old code queried API balance asynchronously on startup. New code does not.\n\n12. **No `auto_scroll` field in `RenderContext`?** — Checking RenderContext fields... actually `auto_scroll` IS in RenderContext (line 406). OK, that's fine.\n\n13. **Tool progress displays only latest instead of all**: Old code iterated all `stream_tool_progress` entries. New code only shows the last entry via `.last()`.</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>98877</total_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>127541</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
