ion&lt;String&gt;` | **MISSING** | Delayed safety gate interrupt |\n| 29 | `pending_notes` | `Vec&lt;String&gt;` | **MISSING** | System note queue flushed before agent loop |\n\nAdditionally, several fields that exist in AppState are **declared but never populated** by any event handler:\n- `last_gate_block` — never set by event loop (no `GateBlock` frame handler)\n- `last_api_error` — never set by event loop (no `ApiError` frame handler)\n- `retry_progress` — never set by event loop (no `RetryProgress` frame handler)\n- `rate_limit_info` — never set by event loop (no `RateLimitInfo` frame handler)\n- `file_changes` — never populated from IPC (no agent-to-tui frame carries this data)\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 2: Slash Commands\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (lines 416-483, inline handling in event loop)\n\nOld `commands.rs` handled **15 slash commands**. New code handles **9** inline (the rest forwarded to agent).\n\n| Command | Old Behavior | New Behavior | Status |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|--------|\n| `/help` | Not in old; old had config-based commands | Shows help text inline | **NEW** |\n| `/quit` / `/exit` | From old mod.rs event loop | Handled inline | PRESENT |\n| `/model` | `handle_model_command` | Handled inline + saves config | PRESENT |\n| `/lang` | `handle_lang_command` + rebuilds system prompt | Handled inline + saves config | PRESENT |\n| `/effort` | `handle_effort_command` | Handled inline | PRESENT |\n| `/auto` | Toggles locally + sets atomic | Toggles locally + forwarded to agent | PRESENT |\n| `/clear` | Full clear with ctx reassembly | Clears messages + stream | PRESENT |\n| `/compact` | Full local context compaction logic | Forwarded to agent as text | REGRESSION |\n| `/balance` | Async query to API with result handling | Forwarded to agent as text | REGRESSION |\n| `/tools` | Toggle `tools_enabled` locally | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n| `/skip-all` | Toggle `skip_all` locally | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n| `/dev` | Toggle `dev_mode` + debug logging | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n| `/reset` | `handle_reset_command` — reset config | **MISSING** (stub returns None) | **MISSING** |\n| `/reconfig` | `handle_reconfig_command` | **MISSING** (stub returns None) | **MISSING** |\n| `/profile` | `handle_profile_command` | **MISSING** (stub returns None) | **MISSING** |\n| `/fix` | Full message repair: detect orphan tools, check alternation | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n| `/context` | Show detailed token breakdown (system/semantic/backbone/episodic) | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n| `/compact force/now/hard` | Sub-options for aggressive compaction | **MISSING** (forwards basic `/compact` as raw text) | **MISSING** |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 3: Event Loop / IPC Frame Handling\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (event loop, lines 222-545)\n\nThe old event loop (`src/dsx-tui/mod.rs`) handled a rich `StreamEvent` enum. The new event loop parses raw JSON-LP strings with simple `.contains()` checks.\n\n**IPC frames handled in new event loop:**\n- `\"content_delta\"` -&gt; `stream.apply_payload()`\n- `\"tool_progress\"` -&gt; `stream.tool_progress` update\n- `\"api_response\"` -&gt; initial content display\n- `\"error\"` -&gt; `state.status_msg` + stream clear\n- `\"done\"` -&gt; push message + stream clear\n- `\"tool_confirm_req\"` -&gt; `pending_tools` + mode switch\n\n**IPC frames / StreamEvents MISSING from new event loop:**\n\n| Missing Handler | Old Behavior | Why It Matters |\n|----------------|-------------|----------------|\n| `ExecStarted(id, pid)` | Stores child PID for exec cancellation | Without this, exec cancellation cannot kill child processes |\n| `ExecDone(id, result)` | Finalizes exec: updates `tool_code_content`, pushes result via ContextAssembler, decrements `exec_pending`, restarts agent loop | **CRITICAL**: No exec results are ever displayed or fed back to the agent |\n| `ExecProgress(output)` | Streams exec output lines to `tool_code_content` in real-time | Live exec output never appears in bottom panel |\n| `SudoDone(results)` | Injects sudo exec results, continues agent loop | Sudo flow is completely broken |\n| `BalanceResult(balance)` | Updates `app.balance` field from async query | Balance never auto-updates on startup |\n| `ModelListResult(models)` | Updates model list for setup wizard | Setup wizard model selection broken |\n| `GateBlocked {reason, repairable, suggestion}` | Sets `last_gate_block` for popup render | Gate popup never shows — fields declared but never populated |\n| `ApiError {type, status, retry_count, ...}` | Sets `last_api_error` for render | Error blocks never appear in chat |\n| `RetryProgress {attempt, max_retries, ...}` | Sets `retry_progress` for render | Retry spinners never appear |\n| `RateLimitInfo {retry_after_secs, ...}` | Sets `rate_limit_info` for render | Rate limit countdown never appears |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 4: Render Differences\n\n#### 4a: Workspace Panel (`/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/render/workspace.rs`)\n\n| Feature | Old (`src/dsx-tui/workspace.rs`) | New | Status |\n|---------|------|-----|--------|\n| Section header | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Low balance warning | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Status message | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Active plan status | Yes (calls `session::list_plans`) | Yes (calls `stubs::session::list_plans`) | STUBBED — always returns no plans |\n| Task summary | Yes (calls `session::read_memory`) | Yes (calls `stubs::session::read_memory`) | STUBBED — always returns empty |\n| File changes this session | Yes (from `long_mem.file_changes`) | Yes (from `ctx.file_changes`) | PRESENT but `file_changes` never populated |\n| **Health errors block** | Shows `health.recent_errors.len()`, `health.overall_level`, `pitfall_count` | **MISSING** | **MISSING** |\n\n#### 4b: Info Panel (`workspace.rs::render_info_panel`)\n\n| Display Element | Old Format | New Format | Status |\n|-----------------|-----------|------------|--------|\n| Model line | `model auto_tag think phase_str **health_icon** **tier_str** **emotion_str** skip_tag exec_tag` | `model auto_tag think phase_str skip_tag exec_tag` | **MISSING** health_icon, tier_str, emotion_str |\n| Context bar | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Balance | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Session runtime | Yes (with local time) | Yes (without local time) | PRESENT |\n| Health status line | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n\nOld mode_line format:\n```\n\"{} {} {} {}{}{}{}{}{}\"  // model, auto_tag, think, phase_str, health_icon, tier_str, emotion_str, skip_tag, exec_tag\n```\nNew mode_line format:\n```\n\"{} {} {} {}{}{}\"         // model, auto_tag, think, phase_str, skip_tag, exec_tag\n```\n\nThe four missing components are:\n1. `health_icon` — derived from `health.overall_level` (Red=dot, Yellow=half-circle)\n2. `tier_str` — derived from `health.context_tier` (Danger=\"DGR\")\n3. `emotion_str` — derived from `health.infer_emotion()` (emoji + label)\n4. Local time (`local.format(\"%H:%M:%S\")`) on runtime line\n\n#### 4c: Chat Panel (`/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/render/chat.rs`)\n\n| Feature | Old | New | Status |\n|---------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Welcome banner | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Session picker | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Setup wizard | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Tool confirmations | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Message display | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Thinking blocks | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Tool call blocks | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Tool results | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| **Stream tool progress** | Shows ALL entries in loop | Shows only LAST entry | **REGRESSION** |\n| Stream content | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Stream reasoning | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Generating spinner | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Waiting spinner | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Esc cancel indicator | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| **API error block** | **MISSING** (new feature) | Yes | **NEW - IMPROVEMENT** |\n| **Retry progress block** | **MISSING** (new feature) | Yes | **NEW - IMPROVEMENT** |\n| **Rate limit block** | **MISSING** (new feature) | Yes | **NEW - IMPROVEMENT** |\n| Async exec indicator | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Scroll position | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n\n#### 4d: Tool Code Panel (`/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/render/tool_code.rs`)\n\n| Feature | Old | New | Status |\n|---------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Action label/color | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Running spinner | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Elapsed timer | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Exec output display | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Code view with line numbers | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Blinking cursor | Yes (uses `\\u{258a}`) | Yes (uses `\\u{258a}`) | PRESENT |\n\n#### 4e: Popups (`/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/render/popups.rs`)\n\n| Feature | Old | New | Status |\n|---------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Exit prompt | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Auth popup (confirm/danger/sudo) | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Intent picker | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Slash popup | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Submenu popup | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| **Gate blocked popup** | **MISSING** | Yes | **NEW** |\n| **Orphan tool_use warning** | From `app.health.has_orphan_tool_uses` | From `ctx.agent.health.has_orphan_tool_uses` | PRESENT |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 5: Mode Differences\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/mode.rs`\n\n| Mode | Old | New | Status |\n|------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Chat | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Streaming | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| ToolConfirm | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| DangerPrompt | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| SudoPrompt | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| ApiConfig | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| SessionPicker | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| IntentPicker | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| GateBlock | **MISSING** | Yes | **NEW** |\n\nNo modes are missing; `GateBlock` was added.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 6: Input Handler Differences\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/input/chat.rs`\n\n| Key | Old Behavior | New Behavior | Status |\n|-----|-------------|-------------|--------|\n| PageUp | exec_scroll_offset += 20 | **Sends ScrollPageUp** (chat scroll) | **REGRESSION** — exec scroll not handled anywhere |\n| PageDown | exec_scroll_offset -= 20 | **Sends ScrollPageDown** (chat scroll) | **REGRESSION** — exec scroll not handled anywhere |\n| End | Sets cursor + **enables auto_scroll** | Sets cursor only | **REGRESSION** — auto_scroll not re-enabled on End |\n| Esc (ApiConfig mode) | Handled in chat.rs | Not in chat handler (handled at higher level) | REFACTORED (acceptable) |\n| Enter (ApiConfig mode) | Handled in chat.rs (key verification logic) | Not in chat handler | **MISSING** — setup wizard key entry broken |\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/input/sudo.rs`\n\n| Feature | Old | New | Status |\n|---------|-----|-----|--------|\n| Esc = cancel sudo | Yes (with agent restart) | Yes (returns CancelSudo action) | PRESENT (action applied in event loop) |\n| Enter = submit password | Yes (with spawn_exec_async_with_sudo) | Yes (returns SubmitSudo) | PRESENT |\n| Character input | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n| Backspace | Yes | Yes | PRESENT |\n\nThe key difference: old `handle_sudo_key` did the actual work (spawning sudo exec, sending to agent). New version just returns actions. The event loop must handle `SubmitSudo` and `CancelSudo` — it does, but only sends a generic `tool_confirm_resp` approval, **NOT** spawning sudo exec with the password. So sudo password is collected but never actually used to execute commands.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 7: Event Loop Lifecycle Features Missing\n\n| Feature | Old (mod.rs) | New (lib.rs) | Status |\n|---------|-------------|-------------|--------|\n| Auto-query balance on startup | Yes (async `api::get_balance`) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Periodic crash recovery snapshot (every 3s) | Yes (`session::save_live_snapshot`) | Fields exist (`dirty`, `last_snapshot`) but no timer | **MISSING** |\n| Auto-save session on exit | Yes (`app.maybe_save_session()`) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Bracketed paste handling | Yes (`Event::Paste` handler with place at cursor) | No | **MISSING** |\n| Ctrl+C → exit prompt → second Ctrl+C → quit | Yes (full state machine) | Yes (basic) | PRESENT (simplified) |\n| `dsc_log` init | Yes (`crate::dsc_log::init()`) | No (stub is no-op) | STUBBED |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 8: Stubs That Should Be Real\n\nFile: `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` (lines 784-1120, `pub mod stubs`)\n\nAll stubs return empty/trivial values. The critical ones that affect UI behavior:\n\n| Stub Module | Dependency | Effect on UI |\n|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| `stubs::session::load_index()` | Returns `vec![]` | Session picker always shows \"No saved sessions found\" |\n| `stubs::session::find_live_sessions()` | Returns `vec![]` | Interrupted sessions never found |\n| `stubs::session::finalize_session()` | No-op | Sessions never saved to disk |\n| `stubs::session::list_plans()` | Returns `vec![]` | Workspace panel always shows \"No active plan\" |\n| `stubs::session::read_memory()` | Returns `\"\"` | Task summary always empty |\n| `stubs::session::load_pitfalls()` | Returns empty PitfallGuide | Pitfall invariants never injected |\n| `stubs::conversation::ContextAssembler` | All methods no-op | Message repair, annotation, and alternation checks disabled |\n| `stubs::health::DsAgentsHealthPlatform` | `infer_emotion()` returns empty, `check_alternation()` returns None | No agent health display in info panel, 400 detection broken |\n| `stubs::context::ContextBuilder::build()` | Returns empty messages | Token breakdown always \"0\" |\n| `stubs::api::get_balance()` | Returns empty BalanceInfo | Balance always blank |\n| `stubs::memory::SemanticMemory` | All methods no-op | Architecture decisions and error patterns never recorded |\n| `stubs::skills::SkillIndex::scan()` | Returns empty | Skill bodies never injected into context |\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 9: Summary of Critical Regressions\n\n1. **Exec handling completely broken**: `ExecDone`, `ExecStarted`, and `ExecProgress` are never handled. Exec results are never displayed in the tool_code panel and never fed back to the agent.\n\n2. **Sudo password collected but never used**: The `SubmitSudo` action sends a generic `tool_confirm_resp` approval, not the actual password. Real sudo exec (with `spawn_exec_async_with_sudo`) is never called.\n\n3. **No session persistence**: `dirty`/`last_snapshot` fields exist but no periodic snapshot timer runs. `finalize_session` is stubbed. Sessions are never saved or resumed.\n\n4. **Gate/error/retry/rate-limit fields declared but never populated**: The event loop has no frame handlers for these types. The corresponding render blocks (`render_api_error_block`, `render_retry_progress_block`, `render_rate_limit_block`, `render_gate_popup`) will never trigger.\n\n5. **`/fix` slash command missing**: Users cannot repair orphaned tool_use/tool_result pairs, which would cause API 400 errors.\n\n6. **`/context` slash command missing**: Users cannot see detailed token breakdown.\n\n7. **`/tools`, `/skip-all`, `/dev` commands missing**: These toggles cannot be changed at runtime.\n\n8. **Exec panel scrolling broken**: `PageUp`/`PageDown` now scroll the chat panel instead of the exec panel (`exec_scroll_offset` is never modified by the event loop).\n\n9. **Auto-scroll not re-enabled on `End` key**: Old behavior: pressing End jumps to end and re-enables auto-scroll. New behavior: cursor moves but auto-scroll stays off.\n\n10. **No bracketed paste support**: The old handler inserted pasted text at the cursor position. No paste handling exists in the new event loop.\n\n11. **No auto-balance query on startup**: The old code queried API balance asynchronously on startup. New code does not.\n\n12. **No `auto_scroll` field in `RenderContext`?** — Checking RenderContext fields... actually `auto_scroll` IS in RenderContext (line 406). OK, that's fine.\n\n13. **Tool progress displays only latest instead of all**: Old code iterated all `stream_tool_progress` entries. New code only shows the last entry via `.last()`.</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>98877</total_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>127541</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"4f4a811b-6245-41e7-b6f2-bdb1b00423b1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:45:05.202Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"4f4a811b-6245-41e7-b6f2-bdb1b00423b1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx/crates/dsx-agent/src/config.rs","snippet":"1\tpub use crate::prompt::system_prompt;\n2\tpub use crate::tui_text::{tui_text, TuiText};\n3\t\n4\tuse dsx_types::PersistentConfig;\n5\tuse std::collections::HashMap;\n6\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n7\t\n8\t#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n9\tpub struct Config {\n10\t    pub api_key: String,\n11\t    pub base_url: String,\n12\t    pub model: String,\n13\t    pub max_tokens: u32,\n14\t    pub context_limit: u32,\n15\t    pub effort: Option<String>,\n16\t    pub prompt_lang: String,\n17\t    pub profiles: HashMap<String, dsx_types::ProfileConfig>,\n18\t    pub active_profile: String,\n19\t    pub auto_mode: bool,\n20\t    pub max_tool_rounds: Option<u32>,\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\timpl Default for Config {\n24\t    fn default() -> Self {\n25\t        let mut profiles = HashMap::new();\n26\t        profiles.insert(\"default\".into(), dsx_types::ProfileConfig {\n27\t            model: \"deepseek-v4-flash\".into(), max_tokens: 16000,\n28\t            effort: None, context_limit: 1_000_000,\n29\t            base_url: \"https://api.deepseek.com\".into(), prompt_lang: \"en\".into(),\n30\t        });\n31\t        Self {\n32\t            api_key: String::new(), base_url: \"https://api.deepseek.com\".into(),\n33\t            model: \"deepseek-v4-flash\".into(), max_tokens: 16000, context_limit: 1_000_000,\n34\t            effort: None, prompt_lang: \"en\".into(),\n35\t            profiles, active_profile: \"default\".into(),\n36\t            auto_mode: true,\n37\t        }\n38\t    }\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\timpl Config {\n42\t    pub fn load() -> anyhow::Result<Self> {\n43\t        let mut cfg = Self::default();\n44\t\n45\t        if let Some(path) = config_path() {\n46\t            if path.exists() {\n47\t                if let Ok(data) = std::fs::read_to_string(&path) {\n48\t                    if let Ok(pc) = serde_json::from_str::<PersistentConfig>(&data) {\n49\t                        // 1. Load profiles\n50\t                        if let Some(profiles) = pc.profiles {\n51\t                            cfg.profiles = profiles;\n52\t                        }\n53\t                        // 2. Apply active profile\n54\t                        if let Some(ref active) = pc.active_profile {\n55\t                            cfg.active_profile = active.clone();\n56\t                            if let Some(profile) = cfg.profiles.get(active) {\n57\t                                cfg.model = profile.model.clone();\n58\t                                cfg.max_tokens = profile.max_tokens;\n59\t                                cfg.effort = profile.effort.clone();\n60\t                                cfg.context_limit = profile.context_limit;\n61\t                                cfg.base_url = profile.base_url.clone();\n62\t                                cfg.prompt_lang = profile.prompt_lang.clone();\n63\t                            }\n64\t                        }\n65\t                        // 3. Overlay flat fields (backward compat — take precedence)\n66\t                        if let Some(k) = pc.api_key { cfg.api_key = k; }\n67\t                        if let Some(m) = pc.model { cfg.model = m; }\n68\t                        if let Some(u) = pc.base_url { cfg.base_url = u; }\n69\t                        if let Some(mt) = pc.max_tokens { cfg.max_tokens = mt; }\n70\t                        if let Some(cl) = pc.context_limit { cfg.context_limit = cl; }\n71\t                        if pc.effort.is_some() { cfg.effort = pc.effort; }\n72\t                        if let Some(pl) = pc.prompt_lang { cfg.prompt_lang = pl; }\n73\t                        if let Some(am) = pc.auto_mode { cfg.auto_mode = am; }\n74\t                    }\n75\t                }\n76\t            }\n77\t        }\n78\t\n79\t        // 4. Env vars (highest priority)\n80\t        if let Ok(k) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_API_KEY\") { let k = k.trim().to_string(); if !k.is_empty() { cfg.api_key = k; } }\n81\t        if let Ok(m) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_MODEL\") { cfg.model = m; }\n82\t        if let Ok(u) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL\") { cfg.base_url = u; }\n83\t        if let Ok(mt) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_MAX_TOKENS\") { if let Ok(v) = mt.parse() { cfg.max_tokens = v; } }\n84\t        if let Ok(cl) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_CONTEXT_LIMIT\") { if let Ok(v) = cl.parse() { cfg.context_limit = v; } }\n85\t        if let Ok(e) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_EFFORT\") { let e = e.to_lowercase(); if e == \"high\" || e == \"max\" { cfg.effort = Some(e); } }\n86\t        if let Ok(pl) = std::env::var(\"DEEPSEEK_PROMPT_LANG\") { let pl = pl.to_lowercase(); if pl == \"zh\" || pl == \"en\" { cfg.prompt_lang = pl; } }\n87\t\n88\t        // Ensure default profile exists\n89\t        if !cfg.profiles.contains_key(\"default\") {\n90\t            cfg.profiles.insert(\"default\".into(), dsx_types::ProfileConfig {\n91\t                model: cfg.model.clone(), max_tokens: cfg.max_tokens,\n92\t                effort: cfg.effort.clone(), context_limit: cfg.context_limit,\n93\t                base_url: cfg.base_url.clone(), prompt_lang: cfg.prompt_lang.clone(),\n94\t            });\n95\t        }\n96\t\n97\t        Ok(cfg)\n98\t    }\n99\t\n100\t    pub fn save(&self) {\n101\t        if let Some(path) = config_path() {\n102\t            let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(path.parent().unwrap());\n103\t            // Sync current values into active profile\n104\t            let mut profiles = self.profiles.clone();\n105\t            profiles.insert(self.active_profile.clone(), dsx_types::ProfileConfig {\n106\t                model: self.model.clone(), max_tokens: self.max_tokens,\n107\t                effort: self.effort.clone(), context_limit: self.context_limit,\n108\t                base_url: self.base_url.clone(), prompt_lang: self.prompt_lang.clone(),\n109\t            });\n110\t            let pc = PersistentConfig {\n111\t                api_key: if self.api_key.is_empty() { None } else { Some(self.api_key.clone()) },\n112\t                model: Some(self.model.clone()),\n113\t                base_url: Some(self.base_url.clone()),\n114\t                max_tokens: Some(self.max_tokens),\n115\t                context_limit: Some(self.context_limit),\n116\t                thinking: None,\n117\t                effort: self.effort.clone(),\n118\t                prompt_lang: Some(self.prompt_lang.clone()),\n119\t                profiles: Some(profiles),\n120\t                active_profile: Some(self.active_profile.clone()),\n121\t                preferences: None,\n122\t                auto_mode: Some(self.auto_mode),\n123\t            };\n124\t            let _ = std::fs::write(&path, serde_json::to_string_pretty(&pc).unwrap_or_default());\n125\t        }\n126\t    }\n127\t\n128\t    pub fn apply_profile(&mut self, name: &str) -> Option<String> {\n129\t        let profile = self.profiles.get(name)?.clone();\n130\t        self.model = profile.model;\n131\t        self.max_tokens = profile.max_tokens;\n132\t        self.effort = profile.effort;\n133\t        self.context_limit = profile.context_limit;\n134\t        self.base_url = profile.base_url;\n135\t        self.prompt_lang = profile.prompt_lang;\n136\t        self.active_profile = name.to_string();\n137\t        self.save();\n138\t        Some(name.to_string())\n139\t    }\n140\t\n141\t    pub fn save_profile(&mut self, name: &str) {\n142\t        self.profiles.insert(name.to_string(), dsx_types::ProfileConfig {\n143\t            model: self.model.clone(), max_tokens: self.max_tokens,\n144\t            effort: self.effort.clone(), context_limit: self.context_limit,\n145\t            base_url: self.base_url.clone(), prompt_lang: self.prompt_lang.clone(),\n146\t        });\n147\t        self.active_profile = name.to_string();\n148\t        self.save();\n149\t    }\n150\t\n151\t    pub f