{"parentUuid":"0e21aea1-4ba1-4ed8-86a4-68636413fbea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"f62b0e5c-aca1-4869-8a68-4a309b9836ce","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to dispatch subagents to fix the missing feature groups one by one. Let me organize the missing features into groups that can be worked on in parallel, then dispatch agents.\n\nThe key missing feature groups are:\n\n1. **Exec handling** - ExecDone, ExecStarted, ExecProgress frames handling in TUI + agent\n2. **Sudo flow** - Password actually used for sudo exec\n3. **Gate/error/retry/rate-limit display** - Wire the frame handlers\n4. **Missing slash commands** - /tools, /skip-all, /dev, /context, /fix, /balance\n5. **Session persistence timer** - Periodic snapshots\n6. **Keyboard fixes** - PageUp/Down for exec, End for auto_scroll, bracketed paste\n7. **Auto balance query on startup**\n\nLet me dispatch these as parallel agents. I'll group them into a few larger work items to keep the number manageable:\n\n1. **Exec + Sudo** - Fix the entire exec pipeline (ExecDone/ExecStarted/ExecProgress handling) and sudo flow\n2. **Slash commands + keyboard** - Missing slash commands (9+ commands) + keyboard fixes\n3. **Gate/error/retry/rate-limit** - Wire the frame handlers in TUI event loop\n4. **Session + startup** - Snapshot timer + auto balance + session save on exit\n\nActually, let me be more focused. The user said \"一大块一大块功能恢复\" - restore feature by feature block. Let me pick the 3 most impactful blocks:\n\n1. **Exec + Sudo pipeline** - Most critical for tool usage\n2. **Slash commands + keyboard regressions** - Most visible to user\n3. **Gate/error/health display** - Important for usability\n\nLet me dispatch these.","signature":"f62b0e5c-aca1-4869-8a68-4a309b9836ce"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":549,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":484096,"output_tokens":2992,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"cbc02a31-1201-4baf-987e-8b2c77772dcc","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:46:13.238Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"cbc02a31-1201-4baf-987e-8b2c77772dcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"f62b0e5c-aca1-4869-8a68-4a309b9836ce","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_obe70lkcevFpsP0Z8Ve38335","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix exec and sudo pipeline","model":"sonnet","name":"fix-exec-sudo","prompt":"Fix three connected features in the DSX project at `/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx`.\n\n## 1. Exec pipeline broken\n\nThe TUI event loop in `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs` receives frames from the agent via raw pipe (stdout). It currently handles: content_delta, tool_progress, api_response, error, done, tool_confirm_req. But it does NOT handle:\n\n- `ExecStarted(id, pid)` — stores child PID for cancellation\n- `ExecDone(id, result)` — finalizes exec, updates tool_code, pushes result\n- `ExecProgress(output)` — streams exec output lines\n\nThese frames come from the agent (game from HP's StreamEvent). The TUI needs to handle them.\n\n**Fix in lib.rs** (in the `while awaiting` loop, add these branches after the existing frame handlers):\n\nFor `exec_started`: set `state.exec_started_at = Some(Instant::now())` and increment `state.exec_pending`.\n\nFor `exec_done` or similar: decrement `state.exec_pending`, update `state.tool_code_content`\n\nFor `exec_progress`: accumulate `state.tool_code_content` with the output.\n\nAlso need to handle `SudoDone` - send sudo results to agent.\n\nRead the existing frame handling code first (around line 220-270), then add these handlers.\n\n## 2. Sudo password actually used\n\nIn `crates/dsx-tui/src/lib.rs`, the `InputAction::SubmitSudo` handler (around line 340+) sends a generic `tool_confirm_resp` with `approved: true`. But for Sudo, the password should be sent along with the approval.\n\nFix: change the SubmitSudo handler to include the sudo password in the response frame:\n```rust\nInputAction::SubmitSudo => {\n    if let Some((tc, _, _)) = state.pending_tools.first() {\n        let pw = &state.sudo_password;\n        let _ = writeln!(agent_writer, r#\"{{\"type\":\"tool_confirm_resp\",\"id\":\"{}\",\"approved\":true,\"sudo_password\":\"{}\"}}\"#, tc.id, pw);\n    }\n    state.pending_tools.clear();\n    state.sudo_password.clear();\n    state.mode = Mode::Chat;\n}\n```\n\n## 3. PageUp/PageDown exec scroll\n\nCurrently `PageUp`/`PageDown` in `input/chat.rs` return `ScrollPageUp`/`ScrollPageDown` actions. These adjust `state.scroll_offset` (chat scrolling). But they should adjust `state.exec_scroll_offset` when the exec panel is focused.\n\n**Fix in lib.rs**: Keep the current ScrollPageUp/ScrollPageDown handlers for chat, but also handle exec_panel scrolling separately. Since there's no exec panel focus state, the simplest fix: bind `Shift+PageUp`/`Shift+PageDown` to exec scroll. Or just add the handlers and let them control `state.exec_scroll_offset`.\n\n**Fix in input/chat.rs**: The Up/Down keys at lines 190-191 return `ScrollUp(3)`/`ScrollDown(3)`. The old code used Up/Down for chat HISTORY navigation (previous messages), not scrolling. Since we don't have chat history in the new architecture, keep current behavior but also add `End` to re-enable auto-scroll.\n\nAdd in input/chat.rs:\n```rust\nKeyCode::End => { NO_ACTION } // handled in lib.rs directly\n```\n\nActually, the End key is already handled at line 186-188 in chat.rs. Change it to also enable auto-scroll by checking the state. Or better: handle it in lib.rs.\n\n**Simplest fix**: In lib.rs, add a match arm for `End` (alongside Ctrl+C) that enables auto-scroll:\n```rust\n// In keyboard handler:\nif key.code == KeyCode::End {\n    state.auto_scroll = true;\n    continue;\n}\n```\n\n## 4. Auto balance query on startup\n\nIn `run_impl`, after the terminal is set up, spawn a thread that queries the balance via the agent. Since the TUI talks to agent via pipes, send a special frame:\n```rust\nlet _ = writeln!(agent_writer, r#\"{{\"type\":\"balance_query\"}}\"#);\n```\n\nThen in the while awaiting loop, handle the response frame `balance_result` if the agent sends it back.\n\nOr simpler: just send a `/balance` command to the agent via the normal user_input path.\n\n## Build\n`cargo build --release` must pass. Do NOT run cargo test.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"general-purpose"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":549,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":484096,"output_tokens":2992,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7e680dd1-8190-4938-bf8c-d21289cbd9d5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:46:25.259Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
