{"parentUuid":"08642a7a-26f9-4e7e-bae2-6fbd12ddf3eb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eaad5a83-cd2a-4446-a54b-6c02fa94aba5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"应该不是不支持原生tool_use,可能是用法错了||   Anthropic API\n为了满足大家对 Anthropic API 生态的使用需求，我们的 API 新增了对 Anthropic API 格式的支持，其 base_url 为 https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic。\n\n通过简单的配置，即可将 DeepSeek 的能力，接入到 Anthropic API 生态中。\n\n将 DeepSeek 模型接入 Claude Code\n请参考接入 Agent 工具\n\n通过 Anthropic API 调用 DeepSeek 模型\n安装 Anthropic SDK\npip install anthropic\n\n配置环境变量\nexport ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=${YOUR_API_KEY}\n\n调用 API\nimport anthropic\n\nclient = anthropic.Anthropic()\n\nmessage = client.messages.create(\n    model=\"deepseek-v4-pro\",\n    max_tokens=1000,\n    system=\"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n    messages=[\n        {\n            \"role\": \"user\",\n            \"content\": [\n                {\n                    \"type\": \"text\",\n                    \"text\": \"Hi, how are you?\"\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n)\nprint(message.content)\n\n注意：当您给 DeepSeek 的 Anthropic API 传入不支持的模型名时，API 后端会自动将其映射到 deepseek-v4-flash 模型。\n\nAnthropic API 兼容性细节\nHTTP Header\nField    Support Status\nanthropic-beta    Ignored\nanthropic-version    Ignored\nx-api-key    Fully Supported\nSimple Fields\nField    Support Status\nmodel    Use DeepSeek Model Instead\nmax_tokens    Fully Supported\ncontainer    Ignored\nmcp_servers    Ignored\nmetadata    Ignored\nservice_tier    Ignored\nstop_sequences    Fully Supported\nstream    Fully Supported\nsystem    Fully Supported\ntemperature    Fully Supported (range [0.0 ~ 2.0])\nthinking    Supported (budget_tokens is ignored)\noutput_config    Only effort is supported\ntop_k    Ignored\ntop_p    Fully Supported\nTool Fields\ntools\nField    Support Status\nname    Fully Supported\ninput_schema    Fully Supported\ndescription    Fully Supported\ncache_control    Ignored\ntool_choice\nValue    Support Status\nnone    Fully Supported\nauto    Supported (disable_parallel_tool_use is ignored)\nany    Supported (disable_parallel_tool_use is ignored)\ntool    Supported (disable_parallel_tool_use is ignored)\nMessage Fields\nField    Variant    Sub-Field    Support Status\ncontent    string        Fully Supported\narray, type=\"text\"    text    Fully Supported\ncache_control    Ignored\ncitations    Ignored\narray, type=\"image\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"document\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"search_result\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"thinking\"        Supported\narray, type=\"redacted_thinking\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"tool_use\"    id    Fully Supported\ninput    Fully Supported\nname    Fully Supported\ncache_control    Ignored\narray, type = \"tool_result\"    tool_use_id    Fully Supported\ncontent    Fully Supported\ncache_control    Ignored\nis_error    Ignored\narray, type = \"server_tool_use\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"web_search_tool_result\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"code_execution_tool_result\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"mcp_tool_use\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"mcp_tool_result\"        Not Supported\narray, type = \"container_upload\"        Not Supported"},"uuid":"64d478e3-e293-40d4-944d-54eef86ce243","timestamp":"2026-05-15T11:00:58.627Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"64d478e3-e293-40d4-944d-54eef86ce243","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"dcdfb2ba-8883-4775-8871-d7e7e426553d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is showing me the official DeepSeek Anthropic API documentation. Let me analyze what they're trying to tell me.\n\nLooking at the Tool Fields section:\n\n**tools:**\n- name: Fully Supported\n- input_schema: Fully Supported\n- description: Fully Supported\n\n**Message content types:**\n- type = \"tool_use\": Fully Supported (id, input, name)\n- type = \"tool_result\": Fully Supported (tool_use_id, content)\n\nSo the DeepSeek Anthropic API DOES support native `tool_use` and `tool_result` content blocks! The user was right — it's fully supported. The issue we had earlier (model outputting XML instead of tool_use blocks) was NOT because the API doesn't support it. It was because:\n\n1. We didn't have `tools` in the api_chat request initially (tools: None)\n2. After we fixed that, the model DID generate tool_use blocks (we saw tool_progress events)\n3. But the error was the API responding with tool_use, then the agent forwarding to tools process, which failed with \"Unknown tool\"\n\nWait, but earlier when we tested with the Anthropic endpoint directly (via Python), the response had tool calls as text content, not tool_use blocks. Let me re-check...\n\nActually, looking back at the Python test earlier, the HP test with the Anthropic endpoint showed content_delta frames with reasoning but no tool_use blocks. The tool_calls only appeared when we used the OpenAI endpoint.\n\nBut the documentation says `tool_use` IS supported. The issue might have been:\n1. The model receiving tools but not having a great system prompt\n2. Or we were testing with `deepseek-v4-flash` which might not support tool_use in the Anthropic format\n\nWait, the docs say: \"当您给 DeepSeek 的 Anthropic API 传入不支持的模型名时，API 后端会自动将其映射到 deepseek-v4-flash 模型。\" But `deepseek-v4-flash` is a valid model. The docs also show `model=\"deepseek-v4-pro\"` as the example.\n\nActually, looking at the docs more carefully: `tool_use` IS fully supported in the Anthropic API. So our Anthropic endpoint should work if:\n1. We send `tools` in the request (we do now)\n2. The message format is correct (Anthropic format, not OpenAI)\n3. The response is parsed as Anthropic SSE events\n\nBut our Anthropic gateway (`anthropic.rs`) already handles this — it converts the raw JSON messages to AnthropicMessage format and sends them to the API. The API should return `tool_use` content blocks.\n\nWait — let me re-check. When we tested the Anthropic endpoint earlier, the model DID NOT return tool_use blocks. But looking at our system prompt, we had told the model to use XML format! After I removed the XML format from the prompt, maybe the Anthropic endpoint would work correctly now.\n\nLet me think about what's different. The user is saying: the API DOES support `tool_use`, maybe we were just using it wrong. They're right — we assumed it doesn't work and added XML parsing as a workaround. But the actual issue might have been that:\n\n1. We had `tools: None` in the api_chat (so the model didn't know about tools)\n2. Or our message format was wrong when sending tool results back\n\nNow that tools are properly sent, and the gateway handles conversion, the Anthropic endpoint might work correctly.\n\nThe user wants to use Anthropic endpoint. Let me validate by testing with the Anthropic endpoint now (after all our fixes) and see if tool calls work.","signature":"dcdfb2ba-8883-4775-8871-d7e7e426553d"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1073,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":503936,"output_tokens":1172,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"spee