{"parentUuid":"dfed3b3b-bfcc-4150-bea4-410e42e65b53","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"bf69e64d-fcef-4e76-8529-8dd71eb399df","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the actual request format. Round 0 is correct: `[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"read /tmp/test.txt\"}]`.\n\nRound 1 (the second api_chat with tool result):\n```json\n[\n  {\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"read /tmp/test.txt\"},\n  {\"role\":\"assistant\",\"reasoning_content\":\"...\",\"thinking_signature\":\"...\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"function\":{\"arguments\":\"...\",\"name\":\"read_file\"},\"id\":\"call_00_...\",\"type\":\"function\"}]},\n  {\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"[OK] read_file:\\n[PARTIAL] 1 lines...\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_00_...\"}\n]\n```\n\nThis looks correct! The assistant message has `tool_calls` (no `tool_call_id`), and the tool message has `role: \"tool\"` with `tool_call_id`.\n\nThe Anthropic gateway should:\n1. Message 0 → role: \"user\", content: [Text]\n2. Message 1 → role: \"assistant\", content: [ToolUse] (because tool_calls exists)\n3. Message 2 → role: \"user\", content: [ToolResult] (because role == \"tool\")\n\nBut the API says it got a tool_result at messages.1.content.0. The \"thinking_signature\" field might be causing issues? Or the \"reasoning_content\"?\n\nActually, wait — the Anthropic API might not recognize `thinking_signature` and `reasoning_content` as valid fields for the assistant message. Let me check the Anthropic API spec...\n\nLooking at the doc: the Anthropic API supports `thinking` content blocks. But the way we send `reasoning_content` as a field in the JSON might not match the expected Anthropic format.\n\nThe message JSON has:\n```json\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"reasoning_content\":\"...\",\"thinking_signature\":\"...\",\"tool_calls\":[...]}\n```\n\nIn the Anthropic gateway, message 1 enters the `tool_calls` branch (first if). It creates `ToolUse` blocks. The `reasoning_content` and `thinking_signature` fields are NOT part of the AnthropicMessage struct — they're just ignored by the gateway.\n\nBut wait — the message at the Anthropic API level is serialized from `AnthropicMessage`. The `AnthropicMessage` struct is:\n```rust\npub struct AnthropicMessage {\n    pub role: String,\n    pub content: Vec<AnthropicContent>,\n}\n```\n\nIt doesn't have `reasoning_content` or `thinking_signature`. So these extra fields from the original JSON are dropped during conversion.\n\nBut the API error says the content has a `tool_use_id`. Where does this come from?\n\nOH! I think I finally understand. The issue might be with how `content` is handled when it's `null` in the RAW JSON.\n\nLooking at the raw JSON for message 1:\n```json\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"reasoning_content\":\"...\",\"thinking_signature\":\"...\",\"tool_calls\":[...]}\n```\n\nThere's NO `content` field! (Because `content: None` in the Message struct.)\n\nIn the anthropic gateway:\n```rust\nlet content = m.get(\"content\")?;\n```\n\n`m.get(\"content\")` returns `None` (the field doesn't exist). The `?` operator returns `None` from the `filter_map`. So the assistant message is SKIPPED!\n\nThat's the bug! The `content` field doesn't exist (because `content: None` in the Message), so `filter_map` returns `None` and the assistant message is filtered out. Then message 2 (role: \"tool\") becomes message 1 (index 1), and it's a `tool_result` block.\n\nWait, but `\"\"` content should have `content: Some(\"\")` which serializes as `\"content\": \"\"`. But `content: None` serializes with skip, so no `content` field.\n\nLet me check: does the agent set `content` to `None` for tool-call-only responses?\n\nLooking at the agent code:\n```rust\nlet assistant_msg = Message {\n    role: \"assistant\".into(),\n    content: if content.is_empty() && !parsed.is_empty() { None } else { Some(content.clone()) },\n    ...\n};\n```\n\nIf `content` is empty AND `parsed` (tool_calls) is not empty, `content` is set to `None`. This means the `content` field is absent from the JSON, and the anthropic gateway skips the message entirely.\n\nThat's the root cause! When the content field is missing, the `content = m.get(\"content\")?` returns None, and `filter_map` drops the message.\n\nThe fix: in the anthropic gateway, don't require `content` to exist. Handle the case where `content` is None (Value::Null or missing).\n\nLet me check the anthropic gateway code structure:\n\n```rust\n.filter_map(|m| {\n    let role = m.get(\"role\")?.as_str()?;\n    let content = m.get(\"content\")?;  // ← BUG! None if missing\n    if let Some(tcs) = m.get(\"tool_calls\").and_then(|t| t.as_array()) {\n        // handle tool_calls\n    }\n    if role == \"tool\" || role == \"tool_result\" {\n        // handle tool result\n    }\n    ...\n})\n```\n\nThe fix: `let content = m.get(\"content\").or(Some(&serde_json::Value::Null))?;`","signature":"bf69e64d-fcef-4e76-8529-8dd71eb399df"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":521088,"output_tokens":1495,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7cb3632f-ba01-4202-9f2d-61dc853ff407","timestamp":"2026-05-15T11:08:30.310Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
