{"parentUuid":"c9640ade-bdc0-425a-807e-4bdbbad8e0c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"fc716958-a562-4801-b2df-eea80c299e9a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Exit code 124 (timeout) again. The tool progress shows the model built up the exec command character by character over 40+ frames. But the timeout fired before the tool could actually be executed.\n\nThe fundamental issue: `deepseek-v4-flash` streams tool call arguments character by character via the OpenAI streaming format. Each character of the command is a separate frame. The model thinks (reasoning) before generating the tool call. This takes a lot of time.\n\nThe actual execution time from user input to tool execution is probably 30-45 seconds just for the streaming/thinking part. Then the tool execution itself is fast (a few ms). The timeout needs to be generous.\n\nBut 120-180 seconds is already generous and still timing out. Let me check: does the tool actually get executed after the streaming finishes? The 124 error means the shell timeout killed the dsx process. The dsx agent was still in the middle of processing.\n\nLet me try with an EVEN LONGER timeout, or just skip the streaming output and see if the tool executes.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that the agent is stuck in the streaming loop — it reads content_delta and tool_progress frames, but the api_response never comes because the model is still reasoning. The agent is waiting for the api_response which signals the end of tool call construction. Meanwhile, the stdin pipe closes (because the heredoc ends), and the agent exits.\n\nWait, actually the timeout is the OUTER shell timeout (`timeout 180`). This kills the `dsx agent` process. The process was in the middle of streaming. Let me check if the tool WAS actually dispatched but the process was killed before it could report.\n\nLet me check if any files were created despite the timeout:","signature":"fc716958-