{"parentUuid":"bc92d74b-284f-477e-8bb3-8ce6e125f205","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"2da25b79-6f4b-4f60-bd2e-883d5d00b7a0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tool wasn't executed. The timeout killed the process before the tool could be dispatched. The streaming of the tool call arguments takes too long.\n\nThe core problem: with deepseek-v4-flash + OpenAI streaming, tool call arguments are streamed character by character. This is the API behavior, not something we can easily change.\n\nThe user said \"openAi也无所谓了\" - they're OK with OpenAI. But the issue isn't which protocol — it's the streaming nature of tool calls. Each character is a separate API event.\n\nHowever, I notice something: we're streaming CONTENT from the API. For tool calls, the arguments are built incrementally. But for a SIMPLE request like \"run this command\", the model first does reasoning (streamed as content_delta with reasoning), then starts the tool call. This takes time because:\n1. Reasoning: 10-20 content_delta frames\n2. Tool call construction: 40+ tool_progress frames \n\nThe solution: use `tool_choice: \"required\"` to force the model to immediately call a tool instead of reasoning first. Or use a simpler prompt.\n\nActually, the REAL issue is that the agent needs to process all these frames in the streaming loop. The streaming loop processes content_delta and tool_progress, and then the api_response. But the tool_progress being 40+ frames means the agent spends a lot of time reading and forwarding these before it can actually execute the tool.\n\nFor the demo: let me try with `exec hello_world.c` instead of Rust — C doesn't need a Cargo.toml. Or just try a simpler command first.\n\nActually wait — the user's test included cargo build AND apt update. That's a LOT of tool calls. Even if each tool call takes 20 seconds (reasoning + streaming + execution), 5+ tool calls would be 100+ seconds.\n\nFor the demo to work, I should either:\n1. Accept the latency and use a very long timeout\n2. Or simplify the test to fewer steps\n\nLet me just try with a 5-minute timeout and see if it completes.","signature":"2da25b79-6f4b-4f60-bd2e-883d5d00b7a0"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":546176,"output_tokens":619,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"4ed995ea-af0e-4c0b-b62a-c0b1723698a1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T11:33:51.945Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
