{"parentUuid":"8c8c83e5-8332-47a2-8348-fa8e84f29736","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"222bf534-236d-4996-8662-96e3317419ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to switch to a local model. This means we need to support running a local LLM (like through Ollama, llama.cpp, or similar) and point the DSX HP/gateway at it.\n\nThe key change is simple: just change the base_url to point to the local model server. For example, if running Ollama locally (default port 11434), the OpenAI-compatible endpoint would be `http://localhost:11434/v1`.\n\nBut we need to consider:\n1. The gateway's URL construction for local models\n2. Whether the local model supports tool calling (Ollama supports OpenAI-compatible tool calling)\n3. How to configure it easily\n\nThe simplest approach: the user can set the base_url to their local endpoint. Let me check if our gateway handles this correctly.\n\nFor OpenAI protocol: `{base_url}/chat/completions` (e.g., `http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions`)\nFor Anthropic protocol: `{base_url}/anthropic/messages`\n\nBut our current URL construction for OpenAI already handles the case where base_url ends with `/v1` — it appends `chat/completions`. So `http://localhost:11434/v1` → `http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions`.\n\nWait actually, looking at the current code:\n```rust\nlet origin = match raw.find(\"://\") {\n    Some(scheme_end) => {\n        let after_scheme = &raw[scheme_end + 3..];\n        match after_scheme.find('/') {\n            Some(slash_pos) => format!(\"{}/chat/completions\", &raw[..scheme_end + 3 + slash_pos]),\n            None => format!(\"{raw}/chat/completions\"),\n        }\n    }\n    None => format!(\"{raw}/chat/completions\"),\n};\n```\n\nThis EXTRACTS the ORIGIN and appends `/chat/completions`. So:\n- `http://localhost:11434/v1` → origin = `http://localhost:11434` → URL = `http://localhost:11434/chat/completions`\n\nBut Ollama's 