{"parentUuid":"c20d9036-46ae-41e3-b7f8-caed73a3c6d7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5cf5f944-0872-47ff-95b5-0a5ebbf455fc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"不是直接关闭think mode就行了吗"},"uuid":"a1ef817d-4504-404a-8b3b-4228d34acd9d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:14:23.681Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"a1ef817d-4504-404a-8b3b-4228d34acd9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"016b11da-b569-4bb7-8c85-a8e49da5c145","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying \"just turn off think mode\" - they're referring to the fact that in LM Studio / llama.cpp, you can disable the model's thinking/reasoning by setting a parameter. \n\nFor Qwen 3.5-9B models served via llama.cpp (which LM Studio uses), the thinking/reasoning behavior is controlled by:\n1. The system prompt\n2. Model parameters like `temperature`, `top_p`, etc.\n3. Whether you explicitly request reasoning via the API\n\nBut actually, what the user might be referring to is that some Qwen models have a specific thinking mode that can be toggled. Actually, looking at the log output more carefully:\n\n```\nLlamaV4: server assigned slot 3 to task 163\n```\n\nThe model is being served via llama.cpp through LM Studio. The thinking/reasoning is a model-level behavior, not an API parameter. The model's architecture includes thinking tokens internally.\n\nHowever, I think the user might be right in a simpler sense - rather than modifying the system prompt (which changes the model's behavior), they might want to just not include the `reasoning_effort` parameter in the API call. But we already checked - `reasoning_effort` is only sent to DeepSeek API, not local models.\n\nWait, maybe the user is thinking about a different thing entirely. In the context of Qwen models served by llama.cpp or LM Studio, there is no \"think mode\" toggle in the API. The model either thinks (outputs reasoning tokens) or doesn't, based on its training.\n\nBut actually, I think the user might be right - the system prompt change I made is the wrong approach. The real fix might be simpler. Let me think...\n\nActually, the user might be talking about the fact that Qwen 3.5 models have a built-in thinking mechanism. In the llama.cpp server, when you send a chat completion request, the model may output `reasoning_content` in the response. If we just tell the system prompt \"don't think\", the model might ignore it since it's baked into the model's behavior.\n\nBut there's actually another approach - some models support a `\"thinking\"` parameter or you can set the model's generation parameters to discourage thinking. But I'm not sure LM Studio exposes this.\n\nHmm, maybe the user is just saying that the system prompt change is overkill and they just want a simpler toggle. Let me re-read their message: \"不是直接关闭think mode就行了吗\"\n\nThey're asking \"can't we just turn off think mode?\" - implying there should be a simpler toggle, perhaps:\n1. A config flag\n2. An API parameter\n3. Or just reverting the prompt change and doing something else\n\nActually, I think I might have over-engineered this. The user's point is valid - instead of modifying the system prompt (which affects model behavior), we should look at whether there's a way to simply not request/display thinking.\n\nBut actually, let me reconsider. The Qwen model outputs reasoning tokens because that's how it was trained. We can't \"turn it off\" via an API parameter on LM Studio/llama.cpp. The system prompt approach IS the right way to discourage it.\n\nHowever, the user might not want me to touch the system prompt at all. They might want a config-level flag.\n\nActually, you know what, I think the user is just pointing out that the simple fix is to not set `reasoning_effort` anywhere, and the system prompt change is unnecessary. They're right that the system prompt already doesn't encourage thinking - the model does it on its own.\n\nLet me just revert the prompt change and tell them the real situation: Qwen 3.5-9B's thinking is baked into the model, not something we control via API parameters for local models. The `reasoning_effort` is only for DeepSeek API. The system prompt change won't help much.\n\nActually wait, I already made the change and rebuilt. Let me just be straightforward and say: \"你说的对，系统提示词其实没让模型思考，是模型自己内置的。改提示词效果有限。`reasoning_effort` 只对 DeepSeek API 生效，本地模型不受影响。所以本质上我们改不了模型的内置行为。\"\n\nBut actually, re-reading the conversation more carefully, the user's original complaint was:\n1. Model is slow (14 tok/s)\n2. Thinking chain takes forever (4000+ tokens)\n3. \"关掉思考链路看看\" - \"turn off thinking chain and see\"\n\nThey want to know if disabling thinking makes it faster. The system prompt change might help a bit but won't fundamentally change the model's behavior since Qwen 3.5 is trained to think.\n\nLet me just be honest and pragmatic.","signature":"016b11da-b569-4bb7-8c85-a8e49da5c145"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":50432,"output_tokens":1203,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2ba13a62-e047-4618-8298-f693f35fc0d7","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:14:38.174Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"2ba13a62-e047-4618-8298-f693f35fc0d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"016b11da-b569-4bb7-8c85-a8e49da5c145","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你确实说得对。`reasoning_effort` 只对 DeepSeek API 才设（第 260 行），本地模型根本不发这个参数。\n\nQwen 3.5-9B 的思考是模型**训练内置的**，不是我们请求的。改 system prompt 效果很有限——模型还是会自己输出 reasoning token，只是表现形式不同而已。\n\n所以实际上对于本地模型，**没有\"关闭思考\"的 API 开关**。真想让本地模型跑得快：\n- 换小模型（Qwen 2.5-Coder 7B 或 DeepSeek-Coder 6.7B）\n- 或者用远端 API（DeepSeek/Anthropic），那边 `reasoning_effort: \"high\"` 可以关\n\n要不要把刚才的 prompt 改回去？然后下次你发消息给模型试试简单指令，看它是不是还走长思考链。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":50432,"output_tokens":1203,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d88fd90f-3b6c-49fc-902f-80e59e37ad20","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:14:40.700Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
