{"parentUuid":"250ae149-1272-41af-88d0-3ecf086dfbbb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9314bc85-d83c-4615-a3e9-3094fffaf797","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"25token每秒算是起飞了，现在连2.5token每秒都没有。而且还一直在跑prompt processing progress ，这是啥"},"uuid":"c3920212-0c1e-43d2-acce-64a3c1b46b2b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:18:06.050Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"c3920212-0c1e-43d2-acce-64a3c1b46b2b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"35f6f454-bcad-4665-8cea-7db04ba6d53a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying they're getting only ~2.5 tok/s and seeing \"prompt processing progress\" messages. This means the model is spending most of its time on prompt processing (ingesting the context), not on generation.\n\nThis is actually a critical insight. The \"prompt processing progress\" means LM Studio/llama.cpp is busy processing the prompt (KV cache fill), not generating tokens. The issue is:\n\n1. The prompt is very large (system prompt + 10 tool definitions + messages = probably ~4-5K tokens)\n2. On Vulkan, prompt processing (prefill) is slow\n3. The \"eval time\" in the log shows 49 tokens at 20 tok/s for prompt processing, then only 2 tokens of generation\n\nWait, looking at the log again from earlier:\n```\nprompt eval time = 2441.42 ms / 49 tokens (49.82 ms per token, 20.07 tokens per second)\neval time = 139.80 ms / 2 tokens (69.90 ms per token, 14.31 tokens per second)\ntotal time = 2581.22 ms / 51 tokens\n```\n\n49 tokens prompt eval seems too low for our full system prompt + tools. That 49 tokens might just be the initial processing. Then:\n\n```\nn_tokens = 4095, truncated = 1\n```\n\nThis means the model generated 4095 tokens total but was truncated at 1 (maybe the context limit). Actually wait, the log format from llama.cpp is a bit confusing. Let me re-read:\n\n`slot release: id 3 | task 163 | stop processing: n_tokens = 4095, truncated = 1`\n\nThis might mean the slot processed 4095 tokens (prompt + generation combined) and truncated 1. Or it could mean something different.\n\nAnyway, the user is now saying they're seeing \"prompt processing progress\" - which is a progress bar during the prompt evaluation phase. This means the prompt is being processed (KV cache being computed) and it's taking a long time.\n\nThe root cause: **prompt too large for local model**. Our system prompt + 10 tools + conversation history is probably too big for a 12K context model to process quickly on Vulkan. The model spends a long time ingesting the context before it can start generating.\n\nWhat can we do:\n1. **Reduce the prompt size**: trim tool descriptions, shorten system prompt\n2. **Use a smaller model** that fits better in GPU memory\n3. **Check if context is already way over 12K** - the model might be swamped\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - the user mentioned \"一直在跑prompt processing progress\" which means each request triggers a full re-processing of the prompt. This is because llama.cpp doesn't cache the KV cache between requests for context reuse (or it does but it still takes time).\n\nFor a local model at 2.5 tok/s, I suspect the issue is that:\n1. The prompt is very long (let's check how many tokens we're actually sending)\n2. The GPU can't fit the full model + KV cache, so some layers run on CPU\n3. Vulkan performance for prompt prefill is particularly bad\n\nLet me think about what practical suggestions to give.","signature":"35f6f454-bcad-4665-8cea-7db04ba6d53a"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":50688,"output_tokens":984,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"27550dc1-acf1-41c0-a446-9cabd6fceed7","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:18:14.703Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"27550dc1-acf1-41c0-a446-9cabd6fceed7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"35f6f454-bcad-4665-8cea-7db04ba6d53a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"这就是症结了。\n\n**\"prompt processing progress\" = 模型在「吃提示词」**，还没开始生成答案。每次你发消息，它都要重新消化整个上下文：\n\n- System prompt (~500 tokens)\n- 10 个工具定义 (~3000 tokens)\n- 历史消息 (~2000+ tokens)\n- **总共可能 5000-8000 tokens**\n\nVulkan 下做这种长序列的 prompt prefill（attention 计算）特别慢，因为是密集矩阵计算。GPU 被大块 context 塞满，生成阶段反而分不到资源。\n\n**简单验证** — 发个极短的 prompt 试试，发 `hi` 看它还跑不跑 processing：\n\n```\nhi\n```\n\n如果 hi 秒回，那就是 context 太大。如果还慢，那是模型本身的问题。\n\n**解决方向**（按见效速度排序）：\n\n1. **减少携带的工具数量** — 本地模式没必要暴露 10 个工具，留 4-5 个核心的就行（explore/exec/read_file/write_file）。工具定义是 context 大头。\n2. **缩短 system prompt** — 现在两句就够了\n3. **启用 KV cache 复用** — LM Studio 有 \"cache prompt\" 选项，打开后相同前缀不重新计算\n\n要先试减工具吗？改这行 `context_compactor.rs` 里的过滤逻辑就行。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":50688,"output_tokens":984,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fb9a766a-6d27-43f9-a7b7-9e6d038ff044","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:18:18.664Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
