{"parentUuid":"0d73b11b-e0c6-4b0e-ab0c-c6bfbc62f5d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"4c411017-463b-43a3-a3ff-106d5a3bff34","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the GPU is an **AMD Radeon RX 6600** (10GB, actually shows up on lspci as Navi 23). The vulkaninfo shows:\n- GPU 0: `AMD Radeon RX 6750 GRE 10GB (RADV NAVI22)` — this is the actual AMD GPU\n- GPU 1: `llvmpipe (LLVM 21.1.8, 256 bits)` — this is the software CPU fallback renderer (llvmpipe)\n\nSo Vulkan IS installed and detects the AMD GPU. The issue is that LM Studio is not using it. LM Studio might be:\n1. Defaulting to the llvmpipe (CPU) device instead of the AMD RADV device\n2. Or not detecting AMD GPUs properly in its build\n\nLet me check if LM Studio might need the ROCm stack or if the issue is just that we need to tell LM Studio to use the right device.\n\nThe AMD GPU shows up as `Radeon RX 6750 GRE 10GB` via RADV (open source Vulkan driver for AMD). This should work with Vulkan in LM Studio.\n\nProbably LM Studio is defaulting to device 1 (llvmpipe / CPU) because it can't find AMD GPU. Let me check if there's a way to specify the device in LM Studio settings, or if we need to use a different backend.\n\nActually, the issue might be simpler. Let me check if the `mesa-vulkan-drivers` is installed (it should be since vulkaninfo works) but perhaps LM Studio is using the Snap or Flatpak version which has sandboxing issues with GPU access.\n\nOr maybe LM Studio needs the ROCm stack. AMD has two Vulkan drivers:\n1. RADV (open source, from Mesa) — detected as GPU 0\n2. AMDVLK / ROCm (official AMD) — not installed\n\nLM Studio (using llama.cpp) might need ROCm for AMD GPUs on Linux. Let me check if there's a ROCm installation or if we should try installing it.\n\nActually wait, llama.cpp supports Vulkan on AMD. The issue might be just that LM Studio needs to be configured to use Vulkan backend AND select the right device. Let me check the current LM Studio configuration.\n\nLet me look at LM Studio's config or ask where it's installed.","signature":"4c411017-463b-43a3-a3ff-106d5a3bff34"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1621,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":52096,"output_tokens":871,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"02fba31d-7983-49bb-a51d-a10a389405a8","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:23:22.937Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
