{"parentUuid":"1a9004eb-ef2e-4b3f-b974-16ab37b89794","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"815f951e-ebd8-47e9-ad84-a01a000d6d11","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to look into ROCm for their AMD Radeon RX 6600/6750 GRE. This card is based on RDNA 2 (Navi 22/23), and officially ROCm doesn't support RDNA 2 on Linux (ROCm only officially supports their high-end compute cards like Radeon Pro and Instinct, plus some RDNA 3 cards).\n\nHowever, there's a community fork called `rocm-legacy` or there are ways to get ROCm working on RDNA 2 cards through:\n1. The `rocm-hip-sdk` community builds\n2. Or sticking with the Vulkan backend which is already working\n\nSince the user asked me to use context7 to look up ROCm compatibility, let me fetch the docs.\n\nActually, Vulkan is working fine - we just enabled the Vulkan backend. The user already has 10GB AMD card and Vulkan is detected. The real question is whether switching to ROCm would give better performance.\n\nFor llama.cpp specifically:\n- Vulkan backend on AMD RDNA 2 works and is well-maintained\n- ROCm backend (HIP/ROCm) technically isn't officially supported for RDNA 2, but community has patches\n- Performance-wise, for inference (not training), Vulkan is often close to ROCm on RDNA 2\n\nBut the user is asking about community ROCm patches, which would be about trying to get the official ROCm stack working on this card. Let me use context7 to look up current info on ROCm compatibility for RDNA 2 cards and then make a recommendation.\n\nActually, wait - the Vulkan switch I made might already solve the problem. Let me first confirm that the Vulkan backend works by having them restart LM Studio and test. If the speed is acceptable, ROCm isn't necessary.\n\nBut the user explicitly asked about ROCm community patches - they want to go further. Let me use context7 to look into it.\n\nActually, thinking more carefully - the user said \"amd按理来说用的是rocm\" meaning \"AMD normally uses ROCm\" - they're wondering if ROCm would be better. Let me check and advise.\n\nFor the RX 6600/6750 GRE specifically:\n- The RX 6600 XT (Navi 23) detected by lspci but vulkaninfo shows RX 6750 GRE (NAVI22)\n- Both are RDNA 2 cards\n- ROCm officially supports: gfx900 (Vega), gfx906 (Vega 7nm), gfx908 (CDNA1), gfx90a (CDNA2), gfx940 (CDNA3), gfx1030 (Navi 21 / RX 6800+), gfx1100 (RDNA 3)\n- Note: Navi 22 (RX 6750 GRE) and Navi 23 (RX 6600) are NOT in that list\n- Community has `rocm-hip-sdk` or you can build from source with `gfx1031` or `gfx1032` target flags\n\nLet me search for the latest info.","signature":"815f951e-ebd8-47e9-ad84-a01a000d6d11"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":60928,"output_tokens":784,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d89ba574-cfa8-47c5-aaed-ec106b4a8cd3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:25:30.673Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
