{"parentUuid":"cc123be0-b9c4-4639-a553-0a66bfde5e7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"de5fa138-8977-44cc-95bc-00703db2cc92","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the agent's flow clearly:\n\n1. Line 336-338: Sets up the tool-calling loop\n2. Line 380-430: Reading HP response in streaming loop:\n   - `ContentDelta { delta, reasoning }` → forwards to TUI as `AgentToTui::ContentDelta { delta, reasoning }`\n   - `ToolCallProgress` → forwards as `ToolProgress`\n   - `ApiResponse` → stores content, tool_calls, reasoning_content, etc.\n3. Line 436-498: After HP response, process tool calls:\n   - If there are tool calls → execute tools → **clear `stream_reasoning`** (line 498) → loop back\n   - If no tool calls → forward final ApiResponse to TUI and done\n\nSo the agent DOES clear `stream_reasoning` between turns (line 498). But the TUI doesn't know about turns - it just sees a continuous stream of ContentDelta events with reasoning and content.\n\nThe fix should be at the agent level: between turns, the agent should send some kind of \"reasoning segment complete\" signal, or structure the reasoning differently for the TUI.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the agent code:\n\nLine 396-403: On `ContentDelta`, the agent forwards to TUI immediately:\n```rust\nHpToAgent::ContentDelta { delta, reasoning } => {\n    let _ = dsx_proto::write_frame(tui_writer, &AgentToTui::ContentDelta {\n        delta: delta.clone(),\n        reasoning: reasoning.clone(),\n    });\n}\n```\n\nLine 410: On `ToolCallProgress`, forwards to TUI.\n\nLine 414-428: On `ApiResponse`, stores the data and loops.\n\nLine 481-483: When there ARE tool calls, it DOESN'T forward the ApiResponse to TUI yet - it stores it for the next loop iteration:\n```rust\ntool_calls: if parsed.is_empty() { None } else { Some(parsed.clone()) },\nreasoning_content,\n```\n\nLine 498: `agent.stream_reasoning.clear();` — this clears the local reasoning tracker, but since HP sends new reasoning for the next turn, the TUI will see it as a continuation.\n\nThe issue is that in the TUI, all `ContentDelta` events with `reasoning` get appended to `stream.reasoning` regardless of turn boundaries. The agent doesn't send any \"turn end\" marker.\n\nThe simplest fix: After the agent processes tool calls and is about to loop back for the next API call, it should send a signal to the TUI. I can:\n\n1. **Agent side (easiest)**: After executing tools and before calling HP again, send a `ContentDelta` with an empty delta and an explicit marker. Or send a new frame type like `{\"type\": \"reasoning_end\"}`.\n\nActually, the simplest approach might be to have the TUI detect turn boundaries based on tool_progress entries. When tool execution is happening, reasoning from the NEXT turn should be a new block.\n\nOR, I can take a different approach: add `reasoning_blocks: Vec<String>` to the StreamBuffer. When:\n1. A new `content_delta` with `reasoning` arrives after we've seen tool_progress entries → save current reasoning as a block, start new\n2. When tool execution is ongoing → this is a SEPARATE block\n\nWait, let me think about this differently. The TUI currently has:\n- `stream.content`: the full assistant response (accumulated from ContentDelta.delta)\n- `stream.reasoning`: all reasoning accumulated from ALL turns\n\nWhen the agent finishes all turns and sends the final `api_response`, the TUI should have:\n- content: just the final answer\n- reasoning: ALL thinking from ALL turns concatenated\n\nBut the user wants to see each thinking block separately. So the fix should be:\n\n**Option A: Agent sends turn boundaries**\n- After processing tool calls and before next HP call, agent sends a `ContentDelta { delta: \"\", reasoning: Some(\"\\n---\\n\".to_string()) }` or a new frame type\n\n**Option B: TUI splits by tool_progress**\n- When `content_delta` with `reasoning` arrives and there are pending `tool_progress` entries, save current reasoning as a completed block\n\n**Option C: Agent sends reasoning blocks separately**\n- Store reasoning in the final ApiResponse as separate blocks\n\nActually, the most natural approach: change the StreamBuffer to store reasoning as `Vec<String>` (blocks) instead of `String`. When a new tool execution starts between reasoning blocks, the TUI pushes the current reasoning as a completed block.\n\nBut this is complex because the TUI doesn't know when a turn ends - it only receives deltas. The tool_progress events are interleaved with reasoning.\n\nLet me re-think. The actual sequence from the agent to TUI looks like:\n\nTurn 1:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning=\"I need to explore...\")  ← thinking\n- ToolProgress(name=\"explore\", args=\".\")          ← tool call starts\n- ContentDelta(delta=\"Explored directory...\")     ← maybe some content\n- ContentDelta(reasoning=\"Now I need to...\")      ← next thinking (turn 2?)\n\nWait, actually in the HP streaming flow, thinking content comes first (as `reasoning_content` in SSE), then the content+tool_calls arrive. So:\n\nTurn 1:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning=\"I need to explore first...\")\n- ContentDelta(delta=\"\") and/or ContentDelta(delta=\"I'll examine the structure\")\n- ToolProgress(name=\"explore\", args=\".\")\n- api_response with tool_calls=[{name: \"explore\", args: \".\"}]\n\n(tool execution happens)\n\nTurn 2:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning=\"The explore shows a Rust project...\")\n- ContentDelta(delta=\"Let me continue with...\")  \n- ToolProgress(name=\"read_file\", args=\"Cargo.toml\")\n- api_response with tool_calls=[{name: \"read_file\", args: \"Cargo.toml\"}]\n\n...\n\nFinal turn:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning=\"The project structure is clear\")\n- ContentDelta(delta=\"Here's what I found...\")\n- api_response with no tool_calls (final answer)\n\nSo the TUI sees this sequence:\n1. ContentDelta(reasoning=\"...\") ← thinking block 1 starts\n2. ContentDelta(delta=\"...\")     ← maybe some content\n3. ToolProgress(...)             ← tool call\n4. ContentDelta(reasoning=\"...\") ← thinking block 2 starts (new turn)\n5. ContentDelta(delta=\"...\")\n6. ToolProgress(...)\n7. ContentDelta(reasoning=\"...\") ← thinking block 3 starts\n8. ContentDelta(delta=\"Here's the answer\") ← final\n9. api_response (no tool_calls)\n\nThe current TUI just appends all reasoning to one string, so the user sees it as one block.\n\nTo fix this properly, I should:\n\n1. Track when reasoning arrives after a tool_progress → it's a new block\n2. OR: the agent could send a clear boundary between turns\n\nThe simplest approach: modify the agent to send a `ContentDelta { delta: \"\\n\\n\", reasoning: None }` or similar boundary before starting a new turn. But that's hacky.\n\nA better approach: In the agent, between turns, send the accumulated content+reasoning as a \"segment\" to the TUI, along with the tool calls that were made in that turn. Then the TUI can display each segment separately.\n\nActually, I think the CLEANEST approach is:\n- When the STREAMED reasoning comes, store each turn's reasoning as a separate block\n- When `tool_progress` is emitted, mark a boundary\n- When the next `ContentDelta` with `reasoning` arrives, start a new block\n\nLet me implement this in the TUI's StreamBuffer:\n\n1. Add `reasoning_blocks: Vec<String>` (completed blocks) and `current_reasoning: String` (in-progress)\n2. On `apply_payload`, if reasoning is present and we have pending tool progress: push current_reasoning to reasoning_blocks, clear current_reasoning, start new\n3. On `stream.clear()`, push current_reasoning to reasoning_blocks\n4. In the render, show reasoning_blocks separated\n\nWait, but the tool_progress is part of the SAME turn. The flow is:\n- reasoning starts\n- content starts\n- tool_progress appears as the model builds up the tool call\n- then api_response with the actual tool call\n\nSo reasoning → content → tool_progress is ONE turn. The next turn starts with new reasoning AFTER tools execute.\n\nActually, let me look at this more carefully. The agent's flow is:\n\n1. Read HP response (streaming)\n   - ContentDelta events → forward to TUI\n   - ToolCallProgress events → forward to TUI\n   - ApiResponse → store data\n2. If there are tool calls:\n   - Execute tools\n   - Build the next API request with tool results\n   - Send new request to HP\n   - Loop back to step 1\n\nBetween step 2 looping to step 1, the agent clears `stream_reasoning` locally but doesn't tell the TUI about the boundary.\n\nThe key issue: in the agent, after executing tools and before calling HP again, there's no signal to TUI saying \"new thinking cycle starting\".\n\n**Best solution**: Add a `ReasoningBoundary` or similar concept. But to avoid new frame types, I can just have the agent send a `ContentDelta { delta: \"\", reasoning: Some(\"\") }` between turns - empty reason signals the boundary.\n\nActually, no, even simpler: the agent already sends `ToolProgress` for each tool call. The user can SEE tool progress entries in the TUI. The issue is just that the reasoning display in the final message shows everything concatenated.\n\nI think the real fix should be: in the TUI, when we store the message (on done frame), we can reconstruct reasoning blocks by looking at tool_progress entries. Or: the agent should include structured reasoning in the ApiResponse.\n\nActually, let me step back. What does the user WANT to see? They want something like:\n\n```\n┌─ Reasoning turn 1 ──────────────────────────┐\n│ I need to explore the project structure...   │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  → explore(\".\")\n┌─ Reasoning turn 2 ──────────────────────────┐\n│ The project is a Rust workspace with...      │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  → read_file(\"Cargo.toml\")\n┌─ Reasoning turn 3 + Answer ────────────────┐\n│ Based on the analysis, here's what I found: │\n│ ...content...                               │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nNOT all the thinking in one big block.\n\nSo the fix involves:\n1. Store reasoning as separate blocks per turn\n2. Display them separated by tool calls\n\nThe simplest approach for now: in the agent, send the accumulated reasoning+content+tool_calls as a \"segment\" before each new turn. But this requires restructuring the agent's output stream.\n\nActually, here's a simpler approach: In the agent, capture the streaming for each turn, and at the end of each turn (when we get api_response with tool_calls), send a structured segment to TUI:\n\n```\nTurn 1:\n- Streaming: ContentDelta(reasoning=\"...\"), ToolProgress(...), ContentDelta(delta=\"...\")\n- At api_response: \n  - ApiResponse { reasoning: \"...\", tool_calls: [...], content: \"...\" }\n  - Then don't forward the api_response yet\n  - Execute tools\n  - Send \"turn\" with content+reasoning+tool_calls to TUI as an intermediate response\n\nTurn 2:\n- Same pattern\n\nFinal turn:\n- ApiResponse with no tool_calls → forward as final api_response\n```\n\nHmm, but this would require changing the streaming model significantly.\n\nLet me think of the SIMPLEST fix. Actually, the user said the agent handles the multi-turn internally. The TUI just gets the stream. What if, when the agent starts a NEW turn (sending a new API request to HP), it first sends the previous turn's accumulated content+reasoning to TUI as an `api_response`, then starts fresh streaming?\n\nLet me look at the agent code more carefully to find the right insertion point.","signature":"de5fa138-8977-44cc-95bc-00703db2cc92"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":89216,"output_tokens":2781,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"ass