(one token or small chunk).\n    #[serde(rename = \"content_delta\")]\n    ContentDelta {\n        delta: String,\n        #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n        reasoning: Option<String>,\n    },\n\n    /// Streaming tool progress.\n    #[serde(rename = \"tool_progress\")]\n    ToolProgress {\n        id: String,\n        content: String,\n        stream_type: String,\n    },\n\n    /// Full API response (non-streaming fallback or final).\n    #[serde(rename = \"api_response\")]\n    ApiResponse {\n        content: String,\n        #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n        tool_calls: Option<Vec<dsx_types::ToolCall>>,\n        #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n        stop_reason: Option<String>,\n        #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n        usage: Option<dsx_types::UsageInfo>,\n    },\n\n    /// Echo back a raw frame (passthrough mode, no HP).\n    #[serde(rename = \"echo\")]\n    Echo { data: serde_json::Value },\n\n    /// End of a turn (agent ready for next input).\n    #[serde(rename = \"done\")]\n    Done,\n\n    /// Error during processing.\n    #[serde(rename = \"error\")]\n    Error { message: String },\n\n    /// Shutdown acknowledgement.\n    #[serde(rename = \"shutdown_ack\")]\n    ShutdownAck,\n}\n\n// ── Agent ↔ Tools ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/// Agent → Tools frames (stdin pipe).\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(tag = \"type\")]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e346d85d-b7ec-489b-a7a5-9be87d715fe0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/qaqtamsy/Desktop/dsx","sessionId":"40da231b-9053-442b-b857-d081c20c78fb","version":"2.1.142","gitBranch":"master","slug":"gentle-orbiting-karp"}
{"parentUuid":"9b02d8ce-4251-4ab9-b65b-59cd36ade15f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"8cafd721-c8ad-4fd2-8a88-50f5efd23115","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the full picture. I need to modify the approach. The best solution:\n\n**Add `TurnBoundary` to AgentToTui proto**, and have the agent send it between turns. Then the TUI can close the current reasoning block, push it as completed, and start fresh.\n\nBut that adds a new frame type which requires changes to proto, TUI, and agent.\n\nA simpler approach: **Have the agent send `Done` between turns and use a variant.** Wait, `Done` means the agent is done completely.\n\nActually, let me approach this differently. Looking at the code flow again:\n\nBetween rounds (line 525+), the agent has already streamed content_delta events to TUI. The TUI has:\n- `stream.reasoning` accumulated for the CURRENT turn\n- `stream.content` accumulated\n- `stream.tool_progress` showing tool calls\n\nWhen the agent starts a new round (line 348 loop iteration), it sends new ContentDelta with reasoning. The TUI appends to the same `stream.reasoning`.\n\nThe simplest fix that doesn't require proto changes:\n\n**In the agent, between rounds, send a `ContentDelta { delta: \"\", reasoning: Some(\"\".into()) }`** — this is an empty reasoning segment that the TUI can interpret as \"flush current reasoning block, start new one.\" No, that's ambiguous since it could just be an empty chunk.\n\nOK, another approach: **Use the existing `api_response` frame between turns.** \n\nIn the agent, when there are tool calls, send an `ApiResponse` to TUI with the current content and tool_calls, then clear the stream buffers and continue. The TUI already handles `api_response` frames.\n\nBut the TUI's handling of `api_response` is minimal — it just applies content if stream is empty. It doesn't create a message. Only `done` creates a message.\n\nLet me look at what happens when the TUI receives `api_response` in the streaming loop more carefully:\n\n```rust\n// Line 261: first loop\nif trimmed.contains(\"\\\"api_response\\\"\") {\n    if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(trimmed) {\n        if let Some(content) = v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            if stream.content.is_empty() {\n                stream.apply_payload(content, None, &[]);\n            }\n        }\n        // ...usage capture...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `api_response` only applies content if `stream.content.is_empty()`. During streaming, `stream.content` won't be empty. So the handler is a no-op during active streaming.\n\nAnd in the second loop:\n```rust\n// Line 790\nif trimmed.contains(\"\\\"api_response\\\"\") {\n    if let Ok(v) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(trimmed) {\n        if let Some(content) = v.get(\"content\").and_then(|c| c.as_str()) {\n            stream.apply_payload(content, None, &[]);\n        }\n        // ...usage capture...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis just applies content unconditionally, overwriting or extending `stream.content`. It doesn't create a message.\n\nSo `api_response` alone won't work for creating segments.\n\n**The best approach: Add `TurnBoundary` to the proto, or use the existing `Done` frame differently.**\n\nWait, let me re-think. What does the user actually want to see? They want:\n- Reasoning block 1 (show this)\n- Tool calls that were made\n- Reasoning block 2 (show this)\n- Tool calls that were made\n- Final answer\n\nCurrently, all reasoning is in one blob, shown in one place. The streaming TUI renders `stream.reasoning` in a reasoning box. The content is shown below. Tool progress is shown as it happens.\n\nFor the user's request: they want the reasoning boxes to be per-turn, not all combined.\n\nThe simplest thing I can do without restructuring the streaming model:\n\n**Send `ApiResponse` with tool_calls between turns, and modify the TUI to create a message from it.**\n\nLet me