ss → forward to TUI, ApiResponse → break)\n4. Agent processes ApiResponse (parses tool calls)\n5. If tool calls → executes tools → loops back to step 2\n6. If no tool calls → sends final `ApiResponse` to TUI → returns\n\nDuring step 3, the TUI is in the first loop receiving the stream. After step 3 breaks (agent got ApiResponse from HP), and before step 5 loops back, we can send an interim ApiResponse to TUI.\n\nBut WAIT - the TUI's first loop processes all frames. After the first streaming finishes (when the agent sends Done or finishes), the TUI exits the first loop and enters the second loop. But the agent is still running and will loop back for the next turn.\n\nThe issue: the TUI reads frames synchronously from the agent in the first loop. If the agent sends `ApiResponse` (between turns) then starts streaming again (next turn's ContentDelta), the TUI will process them all in the first loop.\n\nLet me trace the flow more carefully:\n\n**TUI first loop (line 230-330):**\n```\nloop {\n    line = agent_reader.read_line();\n    if line contains \"content_delta\" → stream.apply_payload(delta, reasoning, &[]); render\n    if line contains \"tool_progress\" → stream.tool_progress.push(...); render\n    if line contains \"api_response\" → stream.apply_payload(content) [if stream empty]; capture usage; render NEW: if tool_calls present → create message\n    if line contains \"done\" → create final message, clear stream, set mode=Chat; break?\n    etc.\n}\n```\n\nWait, looking at line 329:\n```rust\n_ => { break; }\n```\nNo wait, let me re-read the first loop structure.","signature":"8cafd721-c8ad-4fd2-8a88-50f5efd23115"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":404,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":97664,"output_tokens":2316,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iter