{"parentUuid":"f8f6c7ea-2007-4dc8-919a-ebbdbc72b38d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"b74a308c-3a68-4622-9c6d-bf3c0174df76","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the agent sends `Done` after `ApiResponse`. The agent's flow at the end of `handle_user_input`:\n1. Sends `ApiResponse` with content + usage (line 515)\n2. Returns from `handle_user_input`\n3. The caller (the agent's main loop) sends `Done` (line 915/940)\n\nSo the TUI gets:\n1. Streaming: ContentDelta (with reasoning), ToolProgress, etc.\n2. `api_response` (with usage)\n3. `done`\n\nWhen the TUI gets `done`, it calls `stream.to_message()` and pushes to messages.\n\nNow, for multi-turn with tool calls, the agent:\n1. Streams ContentDelta with reasoning (turn 1 thinking)\n2. Streams ToolProgress (tool call building)\n3. Gets ApiResponse from HP with tool_calls\n4. Sends ApiResponse to TUI? NO - currently it doesn't!\n5. Executes tools\n6. Loops back to step 1 (new HP request)\n7. Streams ContentDelta with new reasoning (turn 2 thinking)\n8. ...\n9. Final: ApiResponse then Done\n\nSo the TUI appends ALL reasoning from step 1-9 into one `stream.reasoning` because there's no boundary between the turns.\n\nThe fix is clear now: **I need the agent to send an intermediate frame that tells the TUI to save the current stream as a message before continuing.**\n\nThe approach: When the agent has tool calls and is about to execute them (between rounds), send what the TUI needs to create a segment.\n\nLooking at the TUI's frame handler, the simplest approach:\n1. Agent sends `ApiResponse` between turns (with tool_calls info but no usage, or with usage from that turn)\n2. Then sends a `Done` frame to signal the TUI to finalize that segment\n3. TUI creates a message from the stream\n4. Then agent continues with the next turn\n\nWait but `Done` also sets `awaiting = false`, which exits the streaming loop and goes back to keyboard input. The TUI would think the entire response is done and wait for user input. That's wrong.\n\nOK so the cleanest way without major restructuring:\n\n**Just add the intermediate reasoning as a rendered separator, not as separate messages.**\n\nWhat if I modify the StreamBuffer and render to show reasoning blocks separated by tool calls?\n\nIn the StreamBuffer, I add:\n- `reasoning_blocks: Vec<String>` — each completed turn's reasoning\n- `tool_block: Vec<(String, String)>` — tool calls made between reasoning blocks\n\nWhen rendering:\n1. Show reasoning block 1\n2. Show tool calls from that turn\n3. Show reasoning block 2\n4. Show tool calls from that turn\n5. ...etc\n\nTo know when a turn boundary happens:\n- The TUI can detect that after receiving a `content_delta` with `reasoning`, if we've previously seen `tool_progress` entries (meaning a tool call was made in the previous turn), that's a boundary.\n\nWait, but that's fragile. Tool_progress happens WITHIN a turn.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The sequence of frames TUI gets is:\n```\n[Turn 1]\nContentDelta(reasoning=\"I need to...\")\nContentDelta(delta=\"Let's explore\")\nToolProgress(name=\"explore\", args=\".\")\nToolProgress(name=\"explore\", args=\".\")\nToolProgress(name=\"explore\", args=\"{path: '.'}\")\n[agent executes tools, no frames to TUI]\n\n[Turn 2]\nContentDelta(reasoning=\"The explore shows...\")\nContentDelta(delta=\"Now I see the structure\")\nToolProgress(name=\"read_file\", args=\".\")\nToolProgress(name=\"read_file\", args=\"{path: 'Cargo.toml'}\")\n[agent executes tools]\n\n[Turn 3 - final]\nContentDelta(reasoning=\"Based on what I found...\")\nContentDelta(delta=\"Here is the summary\")\n[no tool calls]\napi_response {content: \"Here is the summary\"}\ndone\n```\n\nSo the boundary between turns is: after tool_progress entries and a GAP (no frames while agent executes tools), a new ContentDelta with reasoning arrives.\n\nI CAN detect this: when we receive a `ContentDelta` with `reasoning` and we already have `tool_progress` entries → save current reasoning as block, start new.\n\nWait, but in turn 1, the reasoning arrives FIRST, then tool_progress. So:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning) → tool_progress is empty, this is current reasoning\n- ToolProgress(...) → tool_progress is now non-empty\n\nThen for turn 2:\n- ContentDelta(reasoning) → tool_progress is non-empty (from turn 1) → SAVE turn 1 reasoning, start new\n\nYes! This works. The boundary detection:\n\n```\nOn ContentDelta(reasoning):\n  if tool_progress is non-empty:\n    push current_reasoning to reasoning_blocks\n    clear current_reasoning\n    clear tool_progress (they were for the previous turn)\n  append reasoning to current_reasoning\n```\n\nWait, but tool_progress also needs to be saved per turn. Let me think...\n\nActually, for the UI display, what we want is:\n- [Reasoning Block 1]\n  → explore(\".\")  [tool call from this turn]\n- [Reasoning Block 2]\n  → read_file(\"Cargo.toml\")  [tool call from this turn]\n- [Reasoning Block 3 + Final Content]\n\nSo we need:\n1. `reasoning_blocks: Vec<String>` — each turn's reasoning text\n2. `tool_calls_per_turn: Vec<Vec<(String, String)>>` — each turn's tool calls\n\nWhen turn boundary detected:\n1. Push current_reasoning to reasoning_blocks\n2. Push current tool_progress snapshot to tool_calls per turn\n3. Clear both for next turn\n\nWhen the stream is finalized (on `done`):\n1. Push remaining current_reasoning to reasoning_blocks (last turn)\n2. Push remaining tool_progress\n\nIn the render:\n- Show each reasoning block with its tool calls\n\nLet me implement this. It's all in the TUI, no agent changes needed!\n\nLet me modify `StreamBuffer` in state.rs and the rendering.","signature":"b74a308c-3a68-4622-9c6d-bf3c0174df76"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":218,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":103296,"output_tokens":1527,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"ser